const PEOPLE = {
'考底利耶': { g:'mind', y:[-350,-283], ca:1, c:'孔雀王朝', n:['考底利耶','Kautilya (Chanakya)'],
  t:['他没当过国王，却写了一本教国王怎么当国王的书。',
     'He never wore a crown — he wrote the manual for those who did.'],
  a:[['传统记载他是旃陀罗笈多的谋士与国师，助其推翻难陀王朝、建立孔雀王朝。','Tradition makes him the adviser who helped Chandragupta topple the Nanda dynasty and found the Mauryan empire.'],
     ['《政事论》（Arthashastra）分 15 卷约 150 章，写税收、间谍、水利、法庭、粮价管制，连渡口和矿山怎么收费都列了出来。','The Arthashastra runs to 15 books and some 150 chapters: taxes, spies, irrigation, courts, grain-price controls — down to the tolls charged at ferries and mines.'],
     ['该书在印度失传千余年，1905 年 R. Shamasastry 在迈索尔从一份贝叶写本中重新发现，1909 年首次刊印。','Lost in India for over a thousand years, the text resurfaced in 1905 when R. Shamasastry found a palm-leaf manuscript in Mysore; he published it in 1909.']],
  s:['《政事论》是现存最早的印度治国术与经济管理专著之一，1909 年刊印后被译成多国文字，常与马基雅维利的《君主论》放在一起讨论。现代学界普遍认为传世本经过多人增补，成书年代晚于孔雀王朝，文本与考底利耶本人的关系仍有争议。新德里的使馆区 Chanakyapuri 以他的另一个名字命名。',
     'The Arthashastra is among the oldest surviving Indian treatises on statecraft and economic administration; since its 1909 printing it has been translated widely and is often read alongside Machiavelli\'s The Prince. Scholars generally hold that the surviving text was expanded by later hands and postdates the Mauryas, leaving its link to Kautilya himself disputed. New Delhi\'s diplomatic quarter, Chanakyapuri, carries his other name.'] },
'桑伽蜜多': { g:'faith', y:[-282,-203], ca:1, c:'孔雀王朝', n:['桑伽蜜多','Sanghamitta'],
  t:['她带过海的那根树枝，今天还活着。',
     'The branch she carried across the sea is still alive today.'],
  a:[['据斯里兰卡编年史《大史》记载，她是阿育王的女儿，出家为比丘尼；兄长摩哂陀在楞伽岛（今斯里兰卡）传法后，她应邀渡海前往阿努拉德普勒。','A daughter of Ashoka and an ordained nun, she sailed to Anuradhapura after her brother Mahinda\'s mission to the island of Lanka, today Sri Lanka.'],
     ['她带去菩提伽耶那棵菩提树的一根枝条，栽在阿努拉德普勒，即今天的圣菩提树（Jaya Sri Maha Bodhi）。','She brought a branch of the Bodhi tree of Bodh Gaya and planted it at Anuradhapura — the tree known today as the Jaya Sri Maha Bodhi.'],
     ['她为王妃阿奴拉等数百名女性授戒，在斯里兰卡建立起比丘尼僧团。','She ordained Queen Anula and hundreds of other women, establishing the order of nuns in Sri Lanka.']],
  s:['阿努拉德普勒的圣菩提树被认为是现存有确切种植年份记载的最古老人工栽种树木，所在的阿努拉德普勒圣城 1982 年列入联合国教科文组织世界遗产。她开创的比丘尼戒脉在 433 年由德婆萨罗（Devasara）率领的斯里兰卡比丘尼渡海传到南京，为三百余名中国尼众授具足戒，东亚的比丘尼传承由此延续至今。斯里兰卡每年 12 月满月日定为「桑伽蜜多日」。',
     'The Anuradhapura Bodhi tree is regarded as the oldest living human-planted tree with a recorded planting date; the sacred city around it became a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1982. The ordination lineage she founded travelled on: in 433 CE Sri Lankan nuns led by Devasara sailed to Nanjing and gave full ordination to more than three hundred Chinese women, and East Asia\'s nuns trace their lineage to that event. Sri Lanka marks Sanghamitta Day on the December full moon.'] },
'摩哂陀': { g:'faith', y:[-285,-205], ca:1, c:'孔雀王朝', n:['摩哂陀','Mahinda'],
  t:['一场山顶上的问答，让一个岛国换了信仰。',
     'A riddle asked on a hilltop changed an island\'s religion.'],
  a:[['阿育王之子，出家为僧；约公元前 247 年奉派率使团渡海到楞伽岛（今斯里兰卡）传法。','A son of Ashoka who became a monk, he led a mission across the water to Lanka — today Sri Lanka — around 247 BC.'],
     ['斯里兰卡编年史《大史》记载，他在弥兴多勒山遇见国王天爱帝须，先以芒果树的问答试其思辨，再为其说法。','The Sri Lankan chronicle Mahavamsa records his meeting with King Devanampiya Tissa at Mihintale, where he tested the king with a riddle about a mango tree before teaching him.'],
     ['国王皈依后在阿努拉德普勒兴建大寺（Mahavihara），成为上座部佛教的根本道场。','The king\'s conversion led to the founding of the Mahavihara at Anuradhapura, the home monastery of Theravada Buddhism.']],
  s:['大寺一系口传的巴利文三藏，约公元前 1 世纪在斯里兰卡马特莱首次写成贝叶文本，是今天南传上座部佛教通行的经典底本；斯里兰卡、缅甸、泰国、老挝、柬埔寨的上座部传统均溯源于此。弥兴多勒被视为斯里兰卡佛教的发源地，每年波松月（6 月）满月日为全国纪念日。',
     'The Pali canon preserved orally by the Mahavihara was first committed to palm leaf in Sri Lanka around the first century BC, and remains the scriptural basis of Theravada Buddhism in Sri Lanka, Myanmar, Thailand, Laos and Cambodia. Mihintale is treated as the birthplace of Sri Lankan Buddhism and is commemorated nationally each Poson full moon in June.'] },
'努尔·贾汗': { g:'state', y:[1577,1645], c:'莫卧儿帝国', n:['努尔·贾汗','Nur Jahan'],
  t:['莫卧儿三百年，钱币上只出现过这一位皇后的名字。',
     'In three centuries of Mughal coinage, only one empress ever had her name struck on it.'],
  a:[['1577 年生于一个从波斯迁来的官宦家庭，1611 年与皇帝贾汗吉尔成婚，获封号「努尔·贾汗」（世界之光）。','Born in 1577 to a family of Persian émigré officials, she married the emperor Jahangir in 1611 and received the title Nur Jahan, \'Light of the World\'.'],
     ['约自 1617 年起，帝国铸币上出现她的名字；皇帝把印玺交给她，敕令（farman）需加盖她的印才生效。','From about 1617 imperial coins carried her name; Jahangir handed her the seal, and imperial orders (farmans) needed her stamp to take effect.'],
     ['1622—1628 年她在阿格拉为父亲修建伊蒂默德·乌德·陶拉陵，通体白色大理石加宝石镶嵌，人称「小泰姬陵」。','Between 1622 and 1628 she built her father\'s tomb at Agra in white marble with inlaid semi-precious stone — the building nicknamed the \'Baby Taj\'.']],
  s:['她是莫卧儿史上唯一同时拥有铸币署名权与用印权的皇后，铸有她名字的银卢比现存于大英博物馆等多家机构，是研究莫卧儿女性权力的实物证据。伊蒂默德·乌德·陶拉陵被认为是莫卧儿第一座通体使用白色大理石与硬石镶嵌的陵墓，泰姬陵沿用了这套做法；泰姬陵的主人蒙塔兹·玛哈尔是她的侄女。',
     'She is the only Mughal empress known to have held both the right of coinage in her name and the use of the imperial seal; silver rupees bearing her name survive in the British Museum and other collections as physical evidence of a Mughal woman\'s authority. Her father\'s tomb is regarded as the first Mughal mausoleum built entirely of white marble with pietra dura inlay — the technique the Taj Mahal later took up. Mumtaz Mahal, for whom the Taj was built, was her niece.'] },
'达拉·舒科': { g:'mind', y:[1615,1659], c:'莫卧儿帝国', n:['达拉·舒科','Dara Shukoh'],
  t:['他把印度教的经书译成波斯文，想证明两种信仰讲的是同一件事。',
     'He translated Hindu scripture into Persian to show that two religions were saying one thing.'],
  a:[['沙贾汗的长子、皇位第一顺位继承人，长期驻拉合尔，与印度教学者、锡克教祖师和苏非派长老往来问学。','Shah Jahan\'s eldest son and heir apparent, he was based at Lahore and studied with Hindu pandits, Sikh teachers and Sufi masters.'],
     ['1657 年他在贝拿勒斯召集学者，把 50 部《奥义书》译成波斯文，题为《大秘密》（Sirr-i-Akbar）。','In 1657 he assembled scholars at Benares and had fifty Upanishads rendered into Persian as Sirr-i-Akbar, \'The Greatest Secret\'.'],
     ['另著《两洋交汇》（Majma-ul-Bahrain），把印度教与伊斯兰苏非派的概念逐条对照。','In Majma-ul-Bahrain, \'The Confluence of the Two Seas\', he set Hindu and Sufi concepts side by side, term for term.']],
  s:['《大秘密》1801—1802 年由法国学者 Anquetil-Duperron 转译成拉丁文《Oupnek\'hat》，《奥义书》由此第一次经欧洲语言译介传播；叔本华读后称它「是我一生的慰藉，也将是我死时的慰藉」，并把这部书长置案头。1659 年他在与弟弟奥朗则布的继位战争中失败被处死，帝位归奥朗则布；他的波斯文译本与手稿现存于印度和欧洲多家图书馆。',
     'In 1801–02 the French scholar Anquetil-Duperron turned Sirr-i-Akbar into the Latin Oupnek\'hat — the route by which the Upanishads first reached readers in a European language. Schopenhauer called it \'the solace of my life, and it will be the solace of my death,\' and kept it beside him. Dara lost the war of succession to his brother Aurangzeb and was executed in 1659; manuscripts of his Persian translations survive in libraries in India and Europe.'] },
'萨福': { g:'art', y:[-630,-570], ca:1, c:'古希腊', n:['萨福','Sappho'],
  t:['她写下的诗编成八九卷，两千六百年后完整传下来的只剩一首。',
     'She wrote nine books of poems. Exactly one survives whole.'],
  a:[['生活在爱琴海的莱斯博斯岛，用当地的埃奥利亚方言写抱着里拉琴唱的短诗，题材多是婚礼、离别与友人。','She lived on the island of Lesbos and wrote short songs in the local Aeolic dialect, sung to the lyre — weddings, partings, friends.'],
     ['亚历山大城的学者把她的作品编成八卷或九卷；今天只剩《致阿佛洛狄忒》一首完整，另有约二百段残篇。','Scholars at Alexandria collected her work into nine books; today one poem, the Ode to Aphrodite, survives complete, alongside some two hundred fragments.'],
     ['残篇一部分保存在古代作者的引文里，一部分自 1897 年起在埃及俄克喜林库斯的废纸草堆中出土；2004 年和 2014 年又有新的纸草残篇公布。','Most fragments came out of the papyrus rubbish heaps at Oxyrhynchus in Egypt, excavated from 1897 onward; new pieces were published as recently as 2004 and 2014.']],
  s:['她使用的四行诗节被后世称为「萨福体」，罗马诗人卡图卢斯与贺拉斯把它移植进拉丁文写作，卡图卢斯第 51 首即改写自她的残篇 31。古希腊《帕拉丁诗选》中一首归在柏拉图名下的短诗称她为「第十位缪斯」。今天学界通用的萨福残篇编号（Lobel–Page、Voigt 两种编本）仍以这些纸草为底本。',
     'The four-line stanza she used is still called Sapphic; Catullus and Horace carried it into Latin, and Catullus 51 is a direct reworking of her Fragment 31. An epigram in the Palatine Anthology, attributed to Plato, calls her the tenth Muse. The numbering scholars use today, in the Lobel–Page and Voigt editions, rests on those Egyptian papyri.'] },
'希波克拉底': { g:'sci', y:[-460,-370], ca:1, c:'古希腊', n:['希波克拉底','Hippocrates'],
  t:['在人人认为生病是神在发怒的年代，他说癫痫也有它自己的原因。',
     'In an age when illness meant an angry god, he said even epilepsy has a natural cause.'],
  a:[['出生于爱琴海的科斯岛，在岛上行医并收徒授课，形成科斯医学派。','Born on the island of Kos, he practised medicine there and taught pupils, forming the school of Kos.'],
     ['以他为名的《希波克拉底文集》约六十篇，逐日记录病人的发热、脉搏、睡眠与饮食，主张先观察、后判断。','The Hippocratic Corpus, some sixty treatises under his name, tracks patients day by day — fever, pulse, sleep, diet — putting observation before conclusion.'],
     ['《论圣病》一篇直接反驳癫痫是神明降罚的说法，认为它和其他疾病一样有自然的成因。','The treatise On the Sacred Disease argues flatly that epilepsy is no more sent by the gods than any other illness.']],
  s:['文集中的《誓言》要求医生尽力不伤害病人、为病人保密，是现存最早的医学职业伦理文献之一；今天许多国家的医学院仍在毕业典礼上宣读它的现代改写版，世界医学会 1948 年据其精神订立《日内瓦宣言》。他被后世称为「医学之父」，但文集实为多位作者所作，哪些篇章出自他本人，学界至今没有定论。',
     'The Oath in the corpus — do no harm, keep the patient\'s confidence — is among the oldest surviving statements of medical ethics; modern versions of it are still read at medical school graduations, and the World Medical Association\'s 1948 Declaration of Geneva was written in its spirit. He is called the father of medicine, though the corpus is the work of many hands and which texts are his own remains unsettled.'] },
'门捷列夫': { g:'sci', y:[1834,1907], c:'俄罗斯·苏联', n:['门捷列夫','Dmitri Mendeleev'],
  t:['他排表时故意留了几个空格，说那里的元素只是还没被找到。',
     'He left blank squares in his table and said the elements for them simply hadn\'t been found yet.'],
  a:[['1869 年 3 月把当时已知的 63 种元素按原子量排列，发现性质每隔一段就重复出现，据此提出周期表。','In March 1869 he laid out the 63 known elements by atomic weight, saw their properties repeat at intervals, and set out the periodic table.'],
     ['他为尚未发现的元素留出空位，并预测它们的原子量、密度与熔点，称之为「类铝」「类硼」「类硅」。','He left gaps for elements nobody had found, predicting their atomic weight, density and melting point, and named them eka-aluminium, eka-boron and eka-silicon.'],
     ['镓（1875）、钪（1879）、锗（1886）先后被发现，实测性质与他的预测吻合。','Gallium (1875), scandium (1879) and germanium (1886) duly turned up, and their measured properties matched his predictions.']],
  s:['周期表至今是化学教学与研究的基本工具。1955 年合成的 101 号元素被命名为「钔」（mendelevium）以纪念他。联合国把周期表发表 150 周年的 2019 年定为「国际化学元素周期表年」。他曾多次获诺贝尔化学奖提名而未获奖，1907 年在圣彼得堡去世。',
     'The periodic table remains the basic tool of chemical teaching and research. Element 101, synthesised in 1955, was named mendelevium for him, and the United Nations declared 2019 — the table\'s 150th anniversary — the International Year of the Periodic Table. He was nominated for the Nobel Prize in Chemistry several times without winning, and died in St Petersburg in 1907.'] },
'塞万提斯': { g:'art', y:[1547,1616], c:'西班牙·葡萄牙帝国', n:['塞万提斯','Miguel de Cervantes'],
  t:['一个打过仗、当过俘虏、一辈子缺钱的人，写出了常被称作第一部现代小说的书。',
     'A wounded soldier, a former captive, broke most of his life — and the author of what is often called the first modern novel.'],
  a:[['1571 年参加勒班陀海战负伤，左手从此不能用；1575 年返航途中被俘，在阿尔及尔当了五年奴隶，1580 年被赎回。','He was wounded at the battle of Lepanto in 1571 and never regained the use of his left hand; captured at sea in 1575, he spent five years enslaved in Algiers before being ransomed in 1580.'],
     ['回国后当过军粮征收员和税吏，因账目问题两度入狱。','Back in Spain he requisitioned supplies for the fleet and collected taxes, and was jailed twice over irregular accounts.'],
     ['1605 年出版《堂吉诃德》上卷，1615 年出下卷；书中那位读骑士小说读昏了头的乡绅，把风车当成巨人，把客栈当成城堡。','Don Quixote appeared in two parts, 1605 and 1615: a country gentleman who has read too many chivalric romances and takes windmills for giants and inns for castles.']],
  s:['《堂吉诃德》已被译成一百多种语言，是发行量最大的文学作品之一。2002 年挪威读书会邀请 54 个国家的百位作家投票评选文学史上最好的作品，《堂吉诃德》得票第一。西班牙语世界的最高文学奖以他命名（塞万提斯奖，1976 年设立），西班牙语也因此常被称为「塞万提斯的语言」。',
     'Don Quixote has been translated into more than a hundred languages and is among the most widely printed works of literature. In a 2002 poll organised by the Norwegian Book Club, a hundred writers from 54 countries voted it the finest work of fiction ever written. The Spanish-speaking world\'s highest literary honour, the Cervantes Prize, was created in his name in 1976, and Spanish is often called \'the language of Cervantes\'.'] },
'旃陀罗·笈多二世': { g:'king', y:[380,415], ca:1, yk:'r', c:'笈多王朝', n:['旃陀罗·笈多二世','Chandragupta II'],
  t:['德里有一根一千六百年不生锈的铁柱，柱铭上的那位国王，多数学者认为就是他。',
     'Delhi has an iron pillar that hasn\'t rusted in 1,600 years; most scholars think the king it names is him.'],
  a:[['约 380 年继位，取号「超日王」（Vikramaditya），在位约三十五年，王都在华氏城，另以乌贾因为西部据点。','He came to the throne around 380 with the title Vikramaditya, \'Sun of Valour\', and reigned some thirty-five years from Pataliputra, with Ujjain as his western seat.'],
     ['击败印度西部的塞种总督（西萨特拉普），把疆域推进到阿拉伯海沿岸，笈多王朝首次掌握西海岸港口，并开始发行银币。','He defeated the Western Kshatrapas, extending the empire to the Arabian Sea; the Guptas gained west-coast ports and began minting silver coinage.'],
     ['中国僧人法显 5 世纪初游历印度，正当他在位；法显记下华氏城有富人捐建的免费医药舍，道路上行旅平安。','The Chinese monk Faxian travelled India early in the fifth century, during his reign, and recorded free clinics endowed by wealthy citizens at Pataliputra and roads safe for travellers.']],
  s:['德里铁柱高约 7 米、重 6 吨余，柱铭属于一位「旃陀罗王」，学界多数意见认为即他本人；铁柱历经一千六百余年基本未锈，长期被冶金学者作为古代防锈铁的研究对象，现属德里库特卜建筑群，1993 年列入联合国教科文组织世界遗产。他在位期间是梵语古典文学与笈多金币铸造工艺的高峰期，诗人迦梨陀娑一般被系于这一时代。',
     'The Delhi iron pillar stands about 7 metres and weighs over 6 tonnes; its inscription names a King Chandra whom most scholars identify with him. Barely rusted after sixteen centuries, it has long been studied by metallurgists as a case of ancient corrosion resistance, and now stands in the Qutb complex, a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1993. His reign marks the high point of classical Sanskrit literature and of Gupta gold coinage; the poet Kalidasa is usually placed in this period.'] },
'世亲': { g:'faith', y:[400,480], ca:1, c:'笈多王朝', n:['世亲','Vasubandhu'],
  t:['他先写书系统批评大乘，后来改宗大乘，再写书反驳从前的自己。',
     'He wrote a systematic case against the Mahayana, converted to it, then wrote against his earlier self.'],
  a:[['生于犍陀罗的富楼沙城（今巴基斯坦白沙瓦），后到笈多治下的阿逾陀讲学，受王室供养。','Born at Purushapura in Gandhara — today Peshawar — he later taught at Ayodhya in Gupta territory under royal patronage.'],
     ['早年著《阿毗达磨俱舍论》，用约六百颂概括说一切有部的全部教义，并逐条加以评点。','His early Abhidharmakosha compressed the entire Sarvastivada system into some six hundred verses, with his own critique attached point by point.'],
     ['受兄长无著影响转入大乘，著《唯识二十论》《唯识三十颂》，与无著同为瑜伽行派（唯识宗）的奠基者。','Won over by his brother Asanga, he turned to the Mahayana and wrote the Twenty Verses and Thirty Verses that founded the Yogachara school.']],
  s:['《阿毗达磨俱舍论》先由真谛于 6 世纪、后由玄奘于 651—654 年译成汉文，至今仍是汉传与藏传佛教寺院的基础教材；玄奘编译的《成唯识论》即以《唯识三十颂》的印度注释为底本。他的生卒年学界分歧很大，一说 4 世纪、一说 5 世纪，甚至有「两个世亲」的说法（Frauwallner, 1951），这里按通行的 5 世纪说。',
     'The Abhidharmakosha was translated into Chinese by Paramartha in the sixth century and again by Xuanzang in 651–654, and is still a foundational textbook in Chinese and Tibetan monastic curricula; Xuanzang\'s Cheng Weishi Lun was compiled from Indian commentaries on the Thirty Verses. His dates are genuinely disputed — fourth century, fifth century, or even two men of the same name (Frauwallner, 1951); the fifth-century dating is used here.'] },
'泰戈尔': { g:'art', y:[1861,1941], c:'英属印度', n:['泰戈尔','Rabindranath Tagore'],
  t:['两个国家的国歌，出自同一支笔。',
     'Two countries sing national anthems written by the same hand.'],
  a:[['1913 年以英译诗集《吉檀迦利》获诺贝尔文学奖，是第一位获此奖的非欧洲人。','The English Gitanjali won him the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1913 — the first non-European to receive it.'],
     ['印度国歌《人民的意志》与孟加拉国国歌《我金色的孟加拉》歌词都出自他，后者的曲调由他改编自一首巴乌尔民歌。','He wrote both India\'s national anthem, Jana Gana Mana, and Bangladesh\'s, Amar Sonar Bangla.'],
     ['1919 年阿姆利则事件后，他致信总督，放弃英王 1915 年授予他的爵士封号。','After the killings at Amritsar in 1919 he wrote to the Viceroy renouncing the knighthood the Crown had given him in 1915.']],
  s:['他一生创作歌曲约两千首（「罗宾德拉桑吉特」），至今在孟加拉语地区日常传唱。1921 年他在圣蒂尼克坦创办国际大学（Visva-Bharati），2023 年圣蒂尼克坦列入联合国教科文组织世界遗产。他与甘地就民族主义与教育长期通信辩论，公开表明分歧而彼此推重；「圣雄」（Mahatma）这一称呼一般认为出自他对甘地的称谓，但来源另有不同说法。',
     'He composed some two thousand songs — Rabindra Sangeet — still sung daily across the Bengali-speaking world. The university he founded at Santiniketan in 1921, Visva-Bharati, sits in a town inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2023. He and Gandhi argued in public correspondence over nationalism and education while holding each other in high regard; the title Mahatma is commonly credited to Tagore\'s way of addressing him, though other accounts of its origin exist.'] },
'拉克什米·芭伊': { g:'war', y:[1828,1858], ca:1, c:'英属印度', n:['拉克什米·芭伊','Rani Lakshmibai'],
  t:['她二十九岁战死，对手的英军将领在战报里称她是那些人里最能打的一个。',
     'She died in battle at twenty-nine; the opposing British general\'s own dispatch called her the best soldier among the rebels.'],
  a:[['詹西土邦王妃。1853 年丈夫去世、无亲生继承人，东印度公司依「丧失权利说」拒认其养子并吞并詹西，她多次申诉未果。','Rani of Jhansi. When her husband died in 1853 leaving no natural heir, the East India Company refused to recognise their adopted son and annexed the state under the Doctrine of Lapse; her appeals were rejected.'],
     ['1857 年起义蔓延后，她掌管詹西的城防与军队，1858 年 3 月底英军围城，4 月初城破后她率部突围。','As the uprising of 1857 spread she took command of Jhansi\'s defences and troops, breaking out with her forces when the city fell in March 1858.'],
     ['1858 年 6 月与塔提亚·托普合兵夺取瓜廖尔要塞，数日后在近郊的科塔基塞莱交战中身亡。','In June 1858 she and Tantia Tope seized the fortress of Gwalior; days later she was killed in the fighting at Kotah-ki-Serai nearby.']],
  s:['英军指挥官休·罗斯在战报中称她是起义方里「最好、最勇敢的一个」。1857 年这场战事的名称至今两分：英国旧称「土兵哗变」（Sepoy Mutiny），印度称「第一次独立战争」或「民族大起义」。1943 年印度国民军把麾下的女兵团命名为「詹西女王团」；她的形象出现在印度的邮票、教科书与瓜廖尔、詹西两地的纪念碑上。',
     'Sir Hugh Rose, the British commander against her, called her in his dispatch the bravest and best military leader of the rebels. The conflict of 1857 is still named two ways: the Sepoy Mutiny in older British usage, the First War of Independence or the Great Rebellion in India. In 1943 the Indian National Army named its women\'s unit the Rani of Jhansi Regiment; she appears on Indian stamps, in school textbooks, and on monuments at Jhansi and Gwalior.'] },
'西塞罗': { g:'mind', y:[-106,-43], c:'罗马共和国', n:['西塞罗','Cicero'],
  t:['今天欧洲语言里「性质」「道德」这些词，是他为了翻译希腊文造出来的。',
     'The European words for humanity, quality and morality exist because he needed Latin for Greek ideas.'],
  a:[['出身罗马城外的骑士家庭，家中无人做过执政官；他靠打官司出名，前 63 年当选执政官，任内挫败喀提林的政变图谋。','Born to a knightly family outside Rome with no consul among his ancestors, he made his name in the law courts, was elected consul in 63 BC, and broke Catiline\'s conspiracy in office.'],
     ['现存演说 58 篇、书信约 900 封，从买房子、儿子的学费到对内战局势的判断都写在信里，是古代世界留下私人书信最多的人。','Fifty-eight speeches and roughly nine hundred letters survive — house purchases, his son\'s tuition, his reading of the civil war — more private correspondence than from any other figure of antiquity.'],
     ['前 44 年凯撒遇刺后，他连续发表十四篇《反腓力辞》攻击安东尼，次年在政治清算中被杀。','After Caesar\'s assassination in 44 BC he attacked Mark Antony in fourteen speeches, the Philippics; he was killed in the proscriptions the following year.']],
  s:['他系统地把希腊哲学术语译成拉丁文，qualitas（性质）、moralis（道德）等词经拉丁文进入欧洲各语言；humanitas 这个更早就有的词，经他之手成了一个哲学概念。他的散文长期被当作拉丁文的标准范本，「西塞罗式」至今是文体学术语。1345 年彼特拉克在维罗纳发现他写给阿提库斯的私人书信集，这一事件通常被视为文艺复兴人文主义的开端之一。',
     'He built a Latin vocabulary for Greek philosophy — qualitas, humanitas, moralis — and those words passed through Latin into the modern European languages. His prose became the benchmark of Latin style, and \'Ciceronian\' is still a term of criticism. Petrarch\'s discovery of his private letters to Atticus at Verona in 1345 is often treated as one of the opening events of Renaissance humanism.'] },
'卢克莱修': { g:'mind', y:[-99,-55], ca:1, c:'罗马共和国', n:['卢克莱修','Lucretius'],
  t:['原子被科学证实的两千年前，他用一首长诗说：万物都由看不见的小颗粒组成。',
     'Two thousand years before atoms were confirmed, he put them into a poem.'],
  a:[['《物性论》（De rerum natura）共六卷、约七千四百行六音步诗，是用拉丁文写成的一整套自然哲学。','De rerum natura runs to six books and about 7,400 lines of hexameter verse — an entire natural philosophy written in Latin poetry.'],
     ['书中主张万物由不可再分的微粒和虚空构成，微粒数量无限、不会消灭，只是不断重新组合。','It holds that everything consists of indivisible particles moving through void: infinite in number, never destroyed, endlessly recombined.'],
     ['他逐一解释雷电、磁石、瘟疫和视觉的成因，坚持自然现象不需要用神意来说明。','He worked through lightning, magnets, plague and eyesight in turn, insisting that natural events need no divine intention to explain them.']],
  s:['全书在中世纪几乎失传，1417 年由波焦·布拉乔利尼在一所德意志修道院找到抄本并传抄流布。伽桑狄在 17 世纪据此重提原子论；托马斯·杰斐逊藏有该书五种拉丁文版本。哈佛学者 Stephen Greenblatt 讲述这次重见天日的《大转向》（The Swerve）获 2011 年美国国家图书奖与 2012 年普利策奖。',
     'The poem nearly vanished in the Middle Ages until Poggio Bracciolini found a manuscript in a German monastery in 1417 and had it copied. Gassendi revived atomism from it in the seventeenth century; Thomas Jefferson owned five Latin editions. Stephen Greenblatt\'s account of that rediscovery, The Swerve, won the 2011 Pulitzer Prize and the National Book Award.'] },
'提比略·格拉古': { g:'state', y:[-163,-133], ca:1, c:'罗马共和国', n:['提比略·格拉古','Tiberius Gracchus'],
  t:['他想把国有的土地分给没有地的士兵，结果死在自己人的集会上。',
     'He tried to hand state land to landless soldiers, and died at a meeting of his own countrymen.'],
  a:[['前 133 年当选保民官，提出《森普罗尼乌斯土地法》：任何人占用公有地不得超过 500 尤格（约 125 公顷），超出部分收回，分给无地公民。','Elected tribune in 133 BC, he proposed the lex Sempronia agraria: no citizen might hold more than 500 iugera of public land — about 125 hectares — with the surplus reclaimed and given to the landless.'],
     ['同僚保民官奥克塔维乌斯否决该案后，他提请平民大会罢免这位同僚，这在共和国史上没有先例。','When a fellow tribune, Octavius, vetoed the bill, he had the plebeian assembly vote his colleague out of office — something the Republic had never seen.'],
     ['同年他谋求连任保民官，在选举集会的冲突中身亡；十年后其弟盖乌斯继续推进改革，结局相似。','Standing for re-election the same year, he was killed in the violence at the assembly; ten years later his brother Gaius took up the reforms and met a similar end.']],
  s:['土地法设立的三人委员会在此后十余年确实执行了分配，意大利各地出土了刻有委员姓名的界石，是这项改革实际落地的物证。阿庇安与普鲁塔克的记载是主要史料。多数罗马史著作把前 133 年作为共和国最后一百年内乱的起点，格拉古兄弟也被视为「平民派」（populares）政治路线的源头。',
     'The three-man commission the law created did carry out redistribution over the following decade: boundary stones cut with the commissioners\' names have been dug up across Italy as physical evidence that the reform took effect. Appian and Plutarch are the main sources. Most histories of Rome date the Republic\'s last century of internal conflict from 133 BC, and treat the Gracchi as the origin of the populares.'] },
'狄奥多拉': { g:'state', y:[500,548], ca:1, c:'拜占庭', n:['狄奥多拉','Theodora'],
  t:['皇帝准备弃城逃走的那天，是她把船拦了下来。',
     'The day the emperor had a ship waiting, she was the one who stopped him boarding.'],
  a:[['出身低微、当过演员；查士丁尼为娶她推动修改法律，允许高官与演员通婚，527 年两人同日加冕，她受封「奥古斯塔」。','Of humble birth and a former actress, she married Justinian after the law barring senators from such marriages was changed; the two were crowned together in 527 and she took the title Augusta.'],
     ['532 年尼卡暴动，君士坦丁堡半城被焚，朝廷准备出海逃走；据普罗柯比记载，她当众说「紫袍是最好的裹尸布」；朝廷随后留下，叛乱被平定。','In the Nika riots of 532, with half the capital burnt and the court preparing to flee by sea, Procopius records her telling them that the imperial purple makes a fine burial shroud; the court stayed and the revolt was put down.'],
     ['查士丁尼立法中有若干条款改善女性处境：禁止逼迫女子卖身、扩大妻子对嫁妆的权利、限制丈夫单方面休妻。','Several provisions in Justinian\'s legislation improved the position of women: bans on forcing women into prostitution, wider rights over dowry, limits on a husband\'s power to divorce at will.']],
  s:['意大利拉文纳圣维塔莱教堂内有她与随从的马赛克镶嵌画（约 547 年完成），是现存最著名的拜占庭镶嵌画之一，1996 年随「拉文纳早期基督教古迹群」列入联合国教科文组织世界遗产。关于她生平的主要史料是普罗柯比的《战史》与《秘史》，后者对她极尽贬斥，与同一作者公开著作中的记述相反，其可信度学界长期争论。东正教会将她与查士丁尼同列为圣徒，纪念日为 11 月 14 日。',
     'The mosaic of Theodora and her attendants in San Vitale at Ravenna, finished around 547, is among the best-known surviving Byzantine mosaics; it was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site with Ravenna\'s early Christian monuments in 1996. The main sources for her life are Procopius\'s Wars and his Secret History, the latter savagely hostile and flatly at odds with what the same author wrote publicly — its reliability has been argued over ever since. The Orthodox Church commemorates her with Justinian as a saint on 14 November.'] },
'安提米乌斯': { g:'sci', y:[474,534], ca:1, c:'拜占庭', n:['安提米乌斯','Anthemius of Tralles'],
  t:['皇帝要一座前所未有的教堂，找来的不是工匠头子，是两个数学家。',
     'For a church with no precedent, the emperor hired two mathematicians.'],
  a:[['特拉勒斯（今土耳其艾登）人，本行是几何学家；著《论燃烧镜》，研究抛物面与椭圆面的反射聚光，并给出用绳子画椭圆的方法。','A geometer from Tralles, today Aydın in Turkey, he wrote On Burning Mirrors, working out how parabolic and elliptical surfaces focus light, and gave the string construction of the ellipse.'],
     ['532 年尼卡暴动烧毁旧教堂后，查士丁尼指定他与米利都的伊西多尔设计新的圣索菲亚大教堂；两人用「帆拱」把圆形穹顶架在方形平面之上。','After the old church burned in the Nika riots of 532, Justinian appointed him and Isidore of Miletus to design the new Hagia Sophia; they set a round dome over a square plan using pendentives.'],
     ['工程 532 年动工、537 年落成，历时不到六年；他在施工早期去世，由伊西多尔完成。','Work began in 532 and finished in 537, under six years; he died early in the project and Isidore saw it through.']],
  s:['圣索菲亚的穹顶直径约 31—33 米（穹顶不正圆，各家测值不同）、顶点离地约 55 米，537 年建成时是当时世界上最大的室内空间。原穹顶在 558 年地震后坍塌，由小伊西多尔以更陡的弧度于 562 年重建。帆拱此后成为东正教教堂与奥斯曼清真寺的通用做法。该建筑先后作教堂、清真寺、博物馆，现为清真寺，属「伊斯坦布尔历史区」，1985 年列入联合国教科文组织世界遗产。',
     'Hagia Sophia\'s dome spans about 31 metres and rises some 55 metres above the floor; its interior is generally held to have gone unsurpassed for roughly a thousand years, until Seville Cathedral in 1520. The original dome fell after an earthquake in 558 and was rebuilt at a steeper pitch by Isidore the Younger in 562. The pendentive became standard in Orthodox churches and Ottoman mosques alike. The building has served as church, mosque, museum and mosque again, and belongs to the Historic Areas of Istanbul, a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1985.'] },
'米马尔·希南': { g:'art', y:[1489,1588], ca:1, c:'奥斯曼帝国', n:['米马尔·希南','Mimar Sinan'],
  t:['他快五十岁才当上宫廷建筑师，然后一口气干了五十年。',
     'He didn\'t become chief court architect until nearly fifty — then held the job for fifty years.'],
  a:[['石匠之子，经德夫希尔梅征召入宫，先在军中当了二十多年工兵军官，随军造桥修路；1538 年被任命为宫廷首席建筑师，此后侍奉苏莱曼、塞利姆二世、穆拉德三世三代苏丹。','The son of a stonemason, taken into palace service through the devşirme levy, he spent more than twenty years as a military engineer building bridges and roads on campaign. In 1538 he was made chief court architect, a post he held under Suleiman, Selim II and Murad III.'],
     ['三座代表作分属他自述的三个阶段：伊斯坦布尔的谢赫扎德清真寺（1548 年建成）、苏莱曼尼耶清真寺（1550—1557）、埃迪尔内的塞利米耶清真寺（1568—1575）。','Three buildings mark the three stages he himself named: the Şehzade Mosque in Istanbul (finished 1548), the Süleymaniye Mosque (1550–1557), and the Selimiye Mosque in Edirne (1568–1575).'],
     ['塞利米耶清真寺的主圆顶直径约 31.3 米，由八根支墩承托，四座宣礼塔高约 71 米；动工时他已年近八十。','The Selimiye\'s main dome spans about 31.3 metres on eight piers, and its four minarets rise some 71 metres. He was close to eighty when work began.']],
  s:['他口述、由萨伊·切莱比笔录的工程名录《建筑之书》（Tezkiretü\'l-Ebniye）列出他名下工程至少 476 项，包括清真寺、桥梁、经学院、水道、浴场和商队旅馆，其中约 196 座留存至 21 世纪。塞利米耶清真寺及其社会建筑群 2011 年列入联合国教科文组织世界遗产名录；苏莱曼尼耶清真寺属于 1985 年列入的「伊斯坦布尔历史区」。伊斯坦布尔的米马尔·希南美术大学以他命名。',
     'The register compiled in his lifetime, the Tezkiretü\'l-Ebniye, credits him with at least 476 works — mosques, bridges, colleges, aqueducts, bathhouses and caravanserais — of which roughly 196 still stood in the twenty-first century. The Selimiye Mosque and its Social Complex was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List in 2011; the Süleymaniye falls within the Historic Areas of Istanbul, inscribed in 1985. Mimar Sinan Fine Arts University in Istanbul carries his name.'] },
'皮里·雷斯': { g:'sail', y:[1470,1553], ca:1, c:'奥斯曼帝国', n:['皮里·雷斯','Piri Reis'],
  t:['他在自己画的世界地图边上注明参考了约二十张旧图，其中一张是哥伦布画的——那张原图今天已经找不到了。',
     'In the margin of his world map he listed the roughly twenty older charts he had used. One was drawn by Columbus, and that chart is now lost.'],
  a:[['奥斯曼海军军官出身。1513 年在加利波利用羚羊皮绘成一幅世界地图，今仅存西侧约三分之一，画的是大西洋两岸——欧洲、非洲西海岸与南美洲海岸；这半幅 1929 年在托普卡帕宫整修时被重新发现。','An Ottoman naval officer, he drew a world map on gazelle parchment at Gallipoli in 1513. Only about a third of it survives, the western part, showing both shores of the Atlantic — Europe, the west coast of Africa and the coast of South America. It was rediscovered in 1929 during renovations at Topkapı Palace.'],
     ['地图上的注记写明取材于约二十张更早的海图，包括葡萄牙人的新航路图和一张哥伦布绘制的地图，后者原件今已失传，这些注记因此成为研究早期美洲测绘的线索。','Notes on the map name its sources: some twenty earlier charts, among them Portuguese charts of the new routes and a map by Columbus whose original has not survived. Those notes are now evidence for how the Americas were first charted.'],
     ['1521 年完成《航海之书》（Kitab-ı Bahriye），1526 年扩编后献给苏莱曼，收入两百多幅地中海沿岸港湾图与航行说明；1547 年出任奥斯曼印度洋舰队司令，1553 年在开罗被处死。','He finished his Book of Navigation (Kitab-ı Bahriye) in 1521 and presented an enlarged version to Suleiman in 1526, with more than two hundred charts of Mediterranean harbours and sailing directions. Made admiral of the Ottoman Indian Ocean fleet in 1547, he was executed in Cairo in 1553.']],
  s:['1513 年地图残片现藏伊斯坦布尔托普卡帕宫博物馆，是 16 世纪初大西洋两岸测绘的一手材料，被反复用于比对欧洲同期海图。《航海之书》有多部手抄本传世，分藏伊斯坦布尔、巴黎、伦敦、德累斯顿等地图书馆，是研究 16 世纪地中海港口的常用文献。土耳其把他的名字用于海军舰艇和海洋研究船。',
     'The surviving fragment of the 1513 map is held by the Topkapı Palace Museum in Istanbul and is a primary source for how the Atlantic coasts were mapped in the early sixteenth century, regularly compared against European charts of the same decades. Manuscript copies of the Kitab-ı Bahriye survive in libraries in Istanbul, Paris, London and Dresden, and remain a standard source on sixteenth-century Mediterranean harbours. Turkish naval vessels and an oceanographic research ship carry his name.'] },
'许蕾姆苏丹': { g:'state', y:[1502,1558], ca:1, c:'奥斯曼帝国', n:['许蕾姆苏丹','Hurrem Sultan'],
  t:['一个被掳来的女奴成了苏丹的合法妻子，此前奥斯曼宫廷没有这个先例。',
     'A woman taken captive and sold into the harem became the sultan\'s lawful wife — the Ottoman court had no precedent for it.'],
  a:[['欧洲人称她罗克塞拉娜（Roxelana），出身今乌克兰西部的鲁塞尼亚，被掳为奴后入苏莱曼后宫；约 1534 年苏莱曼正式与她成婚，打破了苏丹不与后宫女子结婚的惯例。','Known in Europe as Roxelana, she came from Ruthenia in what is now western Ukraine, was taken captive and sold into Suleiman\'s harem. Around 1534 he married her, breaking the custom that sultans did not wed women of the harem.'],
     ['她出资在伊斯坦布尔兴建哈塞基苏丹建筑群：清真寺 1538—1539 年建成，经学院 1539—1540 年，施粥所 1540—1541 年，医院 1550—1551 年；1556 年又建成由希南设计的哈塞基·许蕾姆浴场。','She funded the Haseki Sultan complex in Istanbul — mosque completed 1538–39, college 1539–40, soup kitchen 1540–41, hospital 1550–51 — and in 1556 the Haseki Hürrem bathhouse, designed by Sinan.'],
     ['1552 年在耶路撒冷设立哈塞基苏丹施粥所（imaret），据当时记载每天两次向数百名贫民供餐；她与波兰国王西吉斯蒙德二世·奥古斯特通信，1549 年向他赠送宫中绣品。','In 1552 she endowed the Haseki Sultan imaret in Jerusalem, a soup kitchen recorded as feeding several hundred poor people twice a day. She corresponded with King Sigismund II Augustus of Poland and sent him embroidery from the palace workshops in 1549.']],
  s:['她开创了「哈塞基苏丹」这一位号，此后一百多年奥斯曼宫廷女性长期参与朝政，史书称这段时期为「女人的苏丹国」。她的圆顶陵寝与苏莱曼的陵寝并列在苏莱曼尼耶清真寺庭院内，这是当时苏丹的妻子少见的安葬规格。她在伊斯坦布尔和耶路撒冷留下的建筑至今仍在使用，耶路撒冷的施粥所运作了数百年，20 世纪上半叶仍在供餐。她与苏莱曼往来的书信与诗作留存至今，收藏在托普卡帕宫的档案里。',
     'She created the title Haseki Sultan, and for more than a century afterwards women of the imperial household took an active part in Ottoman politics — a period historians call the Sultanate of Women. Her domed tomb stands beside Suleiman\'s in the courtyard of the Süleymaniye Mosque, a form of burial rarely granted to a sultan\'s wife at the time. The buildings she endowed in Istanbul and Jerusalem are still in use, and the Jerusalem soup kitchen still operates. Letters and verses she exchanged with Suleiman survive in the Topkapı Palace archives.'] },
'辛努塞尔特三世': { g:'king', y:[-1878,-1839], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'中王国埃及', n:['辛努塞尔特三世','Senusret III'],
  t:['埃及的雕像大多面无表情、永远年轻,他的却刻着眼袋和皱纹——那是有意为之。','Egyptian statues are usually ageless and expressionless; his were carved with pouched eyes and deep lines, and that was deliberate.'],
  a:[['这道边界是他一手经营起来的:第二瀑布那条要塞线立于他在位期间,界碑上的规矩也是他定的','The frontier was his own work: the line of forts at the Second Cataract went up in his reign, and the rules cut into the boundary stelae were his'],
     ['州总督的世袭权是在他手上断的,而效果在墓里看得出来:中王国后期地方上的大墓明显变少,一般被读作这项改革的结果','It was under him that the provincial governorships stopped passing from father to son, and the effect shows in the tombs: the great provincial burials thin out after his reign, which is usually read as the result'],
     ['他的雕像有一批传世,面容疲惫而严厉。学者一般认为这不是写实,而是一种新的王权形象:操心的牧人,而不是超然的神','A number of his statues survive, the face weary and severe. Scholars generally take this not as realism but as a new image of kingship — the careworn herdsman rather than the serene god']],
  s:['后世埃及人把他记成一位神:到新王国时期,努比亚的神庙里还在祭祀他。希腊人听来的传说把他与别的法老混成一个人,叫「塞索斯特里斯」,说他征服过全世界——传到希罗多德笔下,已经离真人很远了。','Later Egyptians remembered him as a god: temples in Nubia were still making offerings to him in the New Kingdom. Greek visitors heard a version in which he and several other pharaohs had merged into one conqueror of the whole world, and by the time the story reached Herodotus it had little to do with the man.'] },

'伊姆霍特普': { g:'sci', y:[-2670,-2640], ca:1, yk:'a', c:'古王国埃及', n:['伊姆霍特普','Imhotep'],
  t:['他是给国王盖坟的人，两千年后埃及人把他当医神来拜。',
     'He built the king\'s tomb. Two thousand years later Egyptians were worshipping him as a god of healing.'],
  a:[['约公元前 2670 年为第三王朝法老左塞在萨卡拉设计阶梯金字塔：六层石阶，高约 62 米，是埃及第一座整体用石块砌筑的大型建筑，此前的王陵是泥砖平顶墓。','Around 2670 BC he designed the Step Pyramid at Saqqara for the Third Dynasty pharaoh Djoser: six stone steps rising about 62 metres, the first large building in Egypt put together entirely from cut stone. Royal tombs before it were flat-topped structures of mud brick.'],
     ['左塞一尊雕像的底座上刻着他的名字和头衔——「王之亲信、下埃及国王的掌玺者、赫利奥波利斯大祭司、雕刻工匠总监」；这是极少数与他同时代、直接提到他的实物证据之一，现藏开罗埃及博物馆（编号 JE 49889）。','The base of a statue of Djoser carries his name and titles — prince, seal-bearer of the King of Lower Egypt, high priest of Heliopolis, overseer of sculptors. It is one of the very few objects from his own lifetime that name him, and it is in the Egyptian Museum in Cairo (JE 49889).'],
     ['金字塔外还有一整片围墙内的建筑群，占地约 15 公顷，围墙周长约 1.6 公里；里面的柱子和假门用石头雕出芦苇束、木梁和席子的形状，把此前的材料做法照搬进了石头。','The pyramid sits inside a walled complex of about 15 hectares, its enclosure wall running some 1.6 kilometres. Its columns and dummy doors are carved to imitate bundled reeds, timber beams and matting — older building materials copied into stone.']],
  s:['阶梯金字塔是埃及现存最早的金字塔，也是现存最早的大型石造建筑之一，属于 1979 年列入世界遗产名录的「孟菲斯及其墓地——从吉萨到达舒尔的金字塔场地」。约公元前 6 世纪起，伊姆霍特普在埃及各地被正式立庙祭祀，成为医药之神；希腊人把他等同于医神阿斯克勒庇俄斯，其崇拜在希腊罗马时期达到顶峰。他是古埃及极少数由凡人被尊为神的人之一。他本人的墓至今没有找到。',
     'The Step Pyramid is the earliest surviving pyramid in Egypt and among the earliest surviving monumental stone buildings anywhere; it lies within Memphis and its Necropolis, inscribed on the World Heritage List in 1979. From about the sixth century BC Imhotep was worshipped in temples across Egypt as a god of medicine, and the Greeks identified him with Asclepius, his cult peaking in Greco-Roman times. He is one of very few ordinary Egyptians ever raised to full divinity. His own tomb has never been found.'] },
'辛那赫里布': { g:'king', y:[-705,-681], yk:'r', c:'亚述', n:['辛那赫里布','Sennacherib'],
  t:['为了让首都有水喝，他先后在山里开的渠加起来超过一百五十公里。',
     'To get water to his capital he cut more than 150 kilometres of canal through the hills.'],
  a:[['前 705 年继萨尔贡二世之位，放弃父亲新建的都城杜尔-沙鲁金，改以尼尼微为首都：扩建的城墙周长约 12 公里，圈起约 750 公顷，并建成他自己的铭文称作「无与伦比之宫」的王宫。','He succeeded Sargon II in 705 BC, abandoned the capital his father had just built at Dur-Sharrukin, and made Nineveh his own: new walls some 12 kilometres round enclosing about 750 hectares, and a palace his inscriptions call the Palace Without Rival.'],
     ['约前 690 年在杰尔万建成石砌渡槽，把渠水跨过河谷送往尼尼微：渡槽长约 280 米，用了两百多万块加工过的石料，以拱形结构架在四座桥墩上，底部铺了防水层。','About 690 BC he completed a stone aqueduct at Jerwan to carry the canal across a valley towards Nineveh: roughly 280 metres long, more than two million dressed blocks, arched spans on four piers, and a waterproof lining underneath.'],
     ['他先后开凿的引水渠总长超过 150 公里，最后一套从北面山区的欣尼斯取水，沿途以多座渡槽跨越河谷，坡度经过测量控制；取水口的岩壁上凿有他的巨幅浮雕和铭文。前 689 年他攻陷并毁坏巴比伦城，前 681 年遇刺身亡，在位二十四年。','The whole system drew water from Khinis in the northern hills; the channels ran more than 150 kilometres in total, crossing valleys on several aqueducts at a surveyed gradient, and the rock face at the intake carries huge reliefs and inscriptions of the king. In 689 BC he stormed and destroyed Babylon; in 681 BC he was assassinated, after twenty-four years on the throne.']],
  s:['杰尔万渡槽的遗迹今天仍立在伊拉克北部，石块上刻着他的名字；1932—1933 年由芝加哥大学东方研究所发掘，成果出版为专著《辛那赫里布在杰尔万的渡槽》（OIP 24），这套工程是研究古代大型水利的常引例证。他在尼尼微王宫里的浮雕——描绘前 701 年围攻犹大城市拉吉的连续画面——现藏大英博物馆，是亚述宫殿石雕中广为人知的一组。他重建后的尼尼微是当时世界上面积最大的城市之一。',
     'The Jerwan aqueduct still stands in northern Iraq, its blocks carrying the king\'s name; excavated in 1932–33 by the Oriental Institute of the University of Chicago and published as Sennacherib\'s Aqueduct at Jerwan (OIP 24), it is a standard example in the study of ancient waterworks. The reliefs from his Nineveh palace showing the siege of the Judaean city of Lachish in 701 BC are in the British Museum and are among the best known Assyrian palace sculptures. The Nineveh he rebuilt was among the largest cities in the world of its day.'] },
'萨米-拉马特': { g:'state', y:[-811,-797], ca:1, yk:'a', c:'亚述', n:['萨米-拉马特','Shammuramat'],
  t:['亚述几百年的官方石刻里，只有她一个女人的名字和国王并排刻在界碑上。',
     'In centuries of Assyrian official stone, hers is the one woman\'s name carved on a boundary stele beside the king\'s.'],
  a:[['亚述王沙姆希-阿达德五世（前 824—前 811 年在位）的正妻，阿达德-尼拉里三世（前 811—前 783 年在位）的母亲；儿子继位后，她在王廷文书与石刻中出现的规格，超过此前任何一位亚述王后。','She was principal consort of Shamshi-Adad V (r. 824–811 BC) and mother of Adad-nirari III (r. 811–783 BC). After her son came to the throne she appears in royal texts and monuments with a prominence no earlier Assyrian queen had been given.'],
     ['帕扎尔吉克界碑（出土于今土耳其卡赫拉曼马拉什省）的铭文写道：库穆赫国王乌什皮卢卢梅「使亚述王阿达德-尼拉里与王后萨米-拉马特渡过幼发拉底河」——这是亚述文献中已知唯一一次记录王后随军出征。','The Pazarcık stele, found in Kahramanmaraş province in modern Turkey, records that Ushpilulume king of Kummuh "caused Adad-nirari king of Assyria and Shammuramat the queen to cross the Euphrates" — the only known instance of an Assyrian queen recorded as taking part in a campaign.'],
     ['卡尔胡总督贝尔-塔尔西-伊卢马献给智慧神纳布的两尊石像，铭文写明是为「亚述王阿达德-尼拉里及其主母萨米-拉马特的性命」而立；这类献辞通常只提国王。两尊石像现藏大英博物馆（BM 118888、118889）。','Two statues of Nabu, god of wisdom, dedicated by Bel-tarsi-ilumma, governor of Kalhu, are inscribed as set up for the life of "Adad-nirari king of Assyria, his lord, and Shammuramat, his lady" — a formula normally reserved for the king alone. Both are in the British Museum (BM 118888 and 118889).']],
  s:['她在亚述城的石碑列中立有自己的石碑，那一排石碑属于历代国王与最高官员，其中女性只有三人。她究竟是否摄政，学界至今没有一致结论：梅尔维尔、凯尔泰、达利等研究者给出的判断互不相同。希腊作家笔下征服亚洲、建造巴比伦的女王塞米拉米斯（Semiramis），学界普遍认为以她为历史原型，但那些故事里的情节在楔形文字记载中找不到对应的依据。',
     'She set up her own stele in the row of stelae at Ashur, a row otherwise belonging to kings and the highest officials, and one of only three women to do so. Whether she actually served as regent remains unsettled: Melville, Kertai, Dalley and others reach different conclusions. Scholars generally accept her as the historical figure behind Semiramis, the queen who conquers Asia and builds Babylon in Greek writers — but the events in those stories have no counterpart in the cuneiform record.'] },
'纳布-祖库普-凯努': { g:'mind', y:[-716,-684], ca:1, yk:'a', c:'亚述', n:['纳布-祖库普-凯努','Nabu-zuqup-kenu'],
  t:['亚述那座著名图书馆里的三万块泥板中，有约一百块出自同一个人的手。',
     'Of the thirty thousand tablets in Assyria\'s famous library, about a hundred were written by one man.'],
  a:[['卡尔胡（今伊拉克尼姆鲁德）的抄写员，出身加布-伊拉尼-埃列什家族。他留下的带纪年题记覆盖前 716 年至前 684 年，每一条都注明抄写地点在卡尔胡；他在题记里只署「抄写员」（ṭupšarru）这一个头衔。','A scribe of Kalhu, modern Nimrud in Iraq, from the family of Gabbu-ilani-eresh. His dated colophons run from 716 to 684 BC and every one of them names Kalhu as the place of writing. In them he claims only a single title: scribe, tupsharru.'],
     ['前 705 年他抄下《吉尔伽美什史诗》第十二块泥板，这是该篇现存最早的、可确定年代的抄本；他抄写的还有天象、占卜、医药和文学各类文本。','In 705 BC he copied Tablet XII of the Epic of Gilgamesh — the earliest datable copy of that tablet that survives. He also copied texts on celestial omens, divination, medicine and literature.'],
     ['他的两个儿子都做到亚述王廷最高学者：纳布-泽鲁-列希尔是埃萨尔哈东的首席学者（ummânu），阿达德-舒穆-乌苏尔是国王的首席祛邪师；父亲的藏书据信正是由他们带进尼尼微、并入王室收藏。','Both his sons reached the top of the Assyrian scholarly establishment: Nabu-zeru-leshir was chief scholar, ummanu, to Esarhaddon, and Adad-shumu-usur was the king\'s chief exorcist. His library is thought to have reached Nineveh in their hands and been absorbed into the royal collection.']],
  s:['尼尼微亚述巴尼拔王宫出土的约三万块泥板中，已辨认出约一百块出自他手，其中约五分之一是注释类文本——研究者据此复原新亚述时代的学者如何读解天象、占卜与文学，他因此成为楔形文字学里被研究得最细的抄写员之一。学者弗拉姆（Eckart Frahm）注意到他抄写《吉尔伽美什》第十二块泥板的日期，正是萨尔贡二世战死的前 705 年，并据此讨论抄写与当时丧仪的关系。',
     'Around a hundred of the roughly thirty thousand tablets from Ashurbanipal\'s palace at Nineveh have been identified as his, and about a fifth of those are commentaries — the material from which scholars reconstruct how Neo-Assyrian experts read omens, divination and literature. That makes him one of the most closely studied individual scribes in Assyriology. Eckart Frahm noted that his copy of Gilgamesh Tablet XII is dated to 705 BC, the year Sargon II fell in battle, and has argued for a link with the mourning rites of that moment.'] },
'雅雅·阿散蒂瓦': { g:'war', y:[1840,1921], ca:1, c:'阿散蒂', n:['雅雅·阿散蒂瓦','Yaa Asantewaa'],
  t:['英国总督要坐上阿散蒂人的金凳，六十岁的王太后回答：那就打。',
     'The British governor announced he would sit on the Asante Golden Stool. The sixty-year-old queen mother answered: then we fight.'],
  a:[['阿散蒂王国埃吉苏地区的王太后。1896 年英国把阿散蒂王普伦佩一世等人流放到塞舌尔，她的孙子也在流放之列，她因此代掌埃吉苏的政务。','She was queen mother of Ejisu in the Asante kingdom. When the British deported Asantehene Prempeh I and others to the Seychelles in 1896 — her grandson among them — she took over the government of Ejisu.'],
     ['1900 年 3 月，英国总督霍奇森在库马西要求交出象征阿散蒂王权的金凳并坐上去；她在酋长会议上主张开战，当月战事爆发，史称「金凳之战」，也叫「雅雅·阿散蒂瓦战争」。','In March 1900 Governor Hodgson demanded at Kumasi that the Golden Stool, the seat of Asante sovereignty, be handed over for him to sit on. She argued at the council of chiefs for war; fighting broke out that month, in what became known as the War of the Golden Stool, or the Yaa Asantewaa War.'],
     ['阿散蒂军队围困库马西的英国堡垒，英方调集援军才解围，战事持续约半年。战后她与十五名随从被流放塞舌尔，1921 年 10 月 17 日在当地去世，约八十岁。','Asante forces besieged the British fort at Kumasi and the garrison held out until a relief column broke the siege; the fighting lasted about six months. She was afterwards exiled to the Seychelles with fifteen advisers and died there on 17 October 1921, aged about eighty.']],
  s:['金凳之战是阿散蒂对英国的最后一次大规模武装抵抗，英国于 1902 年 1 月 1 日正式吞并阿散蒂。金凳始终没有交出：英国人拿到的是一件仿制品，真的金凳被藏了起来，至今由阿散蒂王室保管。加纳库马西 1960 年设立雅雅·阿散蒂瓦女子中学，埃吉苏地区的夸索（Kwaso）2000 年 8 月 3 日开设纪念她的博物馆；伦敦梅达韦尔 1986 年设有以她命名的社区中心。',
     'The War of the Golden Stool was the last large-scale armed resistance the Asante mounted against Britain, which formally annexed Asante on 1 January 1902. The stool itself was never surrendered: the British were handed a replica while the real one was hidden away, and it remains in the keeping of the Asante royal house. Yaa Asantewaa Girls\' Secondary School opened in Kumasi in 1960, a museum in her memory opened at Kwaso in the Ejisu district on 3 August 2000, and a community centre named after her has run in Maida Vale, London, since 1986.'] },
'索尔·普拉杰': { g:'mind', y:[1876,1932], c:'欧洲殖民非洲', n:['索尔·普拉杰','Sol Plaatje'],
  t:['一部法律通过后，他骑着自行车一户一户去问农民发生了什么，然后把这些写成书带到伦敦。',
     'After the law passed he cycled from family to family asking what had happened to them, then turned it into a book and carried it to London.'],
  a:[['记者、翻译、语言学者，通晓至少八种语言。1899—1900 年英布战争马费京围城期间他任法庭译员，用英文逐日记下城中见闻，这本日记直到 1973 年才出版。','A journalist, interpreter and linguist who knew at least eight languages. During the siege of Mafeking in the South African War of 1899–1900 he worked as a court interpreter and kept a day-by-day diary in English; it was not published until 1973.'],
     ['1912 年南非土著国民大会（SANNC，1923 年改名为非洲人国民大会 ANC）成立，他是创始成员，并出任首任总书记。','When the South African Native National Congress was founded in 1912 — renamed the African National Congress in 1923 — he was a founding member and its first General Secretary.'],
     ['1913 年《土著土地法》禁止黑人在划定保留地之外购置土地，他骑自行车走访受影响的家庭逐户记录；1914 年随代表团赴伦敦请愿，1916 年在伦敦出版《南非土著的生活》（Native Life in South Africa）。','After the Natives Land Act of 1913 barred black South Africans from buying land outside designated reserves, he travelled by bicycle recording what happened to the families affected. He joined a delegation to London in 1914 and published Native Life in South Africa there in 1916.']],
  s:['《南非土著的生活》是关于 1913 年土地法直接后果的一手记录，出版一百年后仍在再版，并有专门讨论这本书的学术论文集问世。他的长篇小说《姆胡迪》1920 年写成、1930 年出版，通常被认为是南非黑人用英语写成并出版的第一部长篇小说。他把莎士比亚的多部剧作译成茨瓦纳语，其中《错误的喜剧》1930 年出版，这也是最早的一批茨瓦纳语文学译本。南非金伯利的索尔·普拉杰大学与索尔·普拉杰市均以他命名。',
     'Native Life in South Africa is a first-hand record of what the 1913 Land Act did in its first years; it is still in print a century later, and a volume of scholarship devoted to the book has since been published. His novel Mhudi, written in 1920 and published in 1930, is generally described as the first novel in English written and published by a black South African. He translated several Shakespeare plays into Setswana, including The Comedy of Errors in 1930, among the earliest literary translations into that language. Sol Plaatje University and the Sol Plaatje Municipality, both in Kimberley, carry his name.'] },
'蒙恬': { g:'war', y:[-250,-210], ca:1, c:'秦', n:['蒙恬','Meng Tian'],
  t:['后人传说毛笔是他发明的；他真正留下的，是一条路和一道墙。',
     'Legend credits him with inventing the writing brush. What he actually left behind was a road and a wall.'],
  a:[['前215年率三十万秦军北击匈奴，次年收取黄河河套一带（当时称「河南地」），并在河北岸修筑亭障城堡作为前哨。','In 215 BC he led 300,000 troops north against the Xiongnu and the following year took the Ordos bend of the Yellow River, then built a line of forts and watchtowers along its northern bank.'],
     ['把燕、赵、秦三国的旧长城连接成一条防线，《史记》记其「起临洮，至辽东，延袤万余里」。','He joined the old frontier walls of Yan, Zhao and Qin into a single line — running, as the Records of the Grand Historian puts it, "from Lintao to Liaodong, more than ten thousand li".'],
     ['主持修筑秦直道，自九原（今内蒙古包头西）南抵云阳甘泉，《史记》记「堑山堙谷，千八百里」；今陕北黄土高原上仍能看到路基。','He built the Straight Road from Jiuyuan (west of today\'s Baotou) south to Yunyang — "cutting through hills and filling valleys, one thousand eight hundred li". Stretches of its bed are still visible on the Shaanxi loess plateau.']],
  s:['秦直道遗址2006年被公布为全国重点文物保护单位，陕西、甘肃、内蒙古境内多段路基至今可辨。他连接起来的北方防线走向被后世沿用，明长城有多处直接叠压在旧线之上。司马迁在《史记》中为他单立一传，同时批评他修长城时「轻百姓力」——这是关于这项工程代价的较早记载。',
     'The Qin Straight Road was designated a Major National Historical and Cultural Site in 2006, and sections of its bed can still be traced across Shaanxi, Gansu and Inner Mongolia. The frontier line he stitched together was reused for centuries; parts of the Ming Great Wall sit directly on it. Sima Qian gave him his own chapter in the Records — and in the same chapter faulted him for "making light of the people\'s strength", one of the earliest recorded reckonings of what the wall cost.'] },
'陈胜': { g:'state', y:[-209,-208], yk:'r', c:'秦', n:['陈胜','Chen Sheng'],
  t:['他是替人种地的雇工，起兵当年就称了王，第二年被自己的车夫杀死。',
     'A hired farmhand who declared himself king in the year he revolted, and was killed by his own carriage driver the year after.'],
  a:[['前209年七月，与吴广率九百名戍卒在大泽乡（今安徽宿州）起兵：他们因大雨误了赴边期限，《史记》说按秦法当斩；这是秦统一后有明确记载的第一次大规模平民起事。','In the seventh month of 209 BC he and Wu Guang raised 900 conscripts in revolt at Daze Village (today\'s Suzhou, Anhui). Heavy rain had made them late for garrison duty, which the Records of the Grand Historian says was a capital offence under Qin law. It is the first large-scale commoners\' uprising recorded after the unification.'],
     ['攻下陈县（今河南淮阳）后自立为王，国号「张楚」，并分兵西攻函谷关；政权前后不到半年。','After taking Chen (today\'s Huaiyang, Henan) he made himself king under the title Zhang Chu and sent columns west toward the Hangu Pass. The regime lasted less than six months.'],
     ['前208年在下城父被自己的车夫庄贾所杀。《史记》记他起兵时对同伴说：「王侯将相宁有种乎？」','In 208 BC he was killed at Xiachengfu by Zhuang Jia, the man who drove his carriage. The Records preserves what he said to his companions when the revolt began: "Are kings and nobles, generals and ministers, born to their rank?"']],
  s:['司马迁把陈胜列入《史记》三十篇「世家」，与各诸侯国国君同一等级——这是《史记》体例里给非诸侯出身者的最高位置之一。汉高祖刘邦为他在砀设置守冢三十家，按时祭祀。「王侯将相宁有种乎」这句话即出自《史记·陈涉世家》。',
     'Sima Qian placed Chen Sheng among the thirty "Hereditary Houses" of the Records, the rank reserved for rulers of states — one of the highest slots the book ever gives someone of non-noble birth. Emperor Gaozu of Han assigned thirty households at Dang to tend his grave and maintain the offerings. His line about rank not being inherited was comes from that chapter.'] },
'徐福': { g:'sail', y:[-219,-210], yk:'a', c:'秦', n:['徐福','Xu Fu'],
  t:['他两次说服秦始皇给他船队和人手，然后带着几千人消失在海上，再没回来。',
     'Twice he talked the First Emperor into giving him ships and crews. Then he sailed off with several thousand people and never came back.'],
  a:[['前219年上书秦始皇，说海中有蓬莱、方丈、瀛洲三座神山，请求带童男童女入海求长生药，获准出发。','In 219 BC he petitioned the First Emperor, reporting three holy mountains in the sea — Penglai, Fangzhang and Yingzhou — and won permission to sail in search of the elixir of life with a company of boys and girls.'],
     ['前210年在琅琊再见秦始皇，称有大鱼阻拦航路，请求配备连弩射手；这次出海带走童男童女、五谷种子和各行工匠。','In 210 BC he met the emperor again at Langya, claimed giant fish were blocking the route, and asked for crossbowmen. This time he left with boys and girls, seed grain of the five crops, and craftsmen of every trade.'],
     ['《史记·淮南衡山列传》记他「得平原广泽，止王不来」——找到一片平原沼泽，就在那里自立为王，不再回来。此后中国官方史书再无他的记载。','The Records of the Grand Historian says he "found a broad plain and marsh, made himself king there, and did not return". No Chinese official history mentions him again.']],
  s:['这是中国正史中最早的大规模官方远洋航行记载之一，两次出海都写在《史记》里。日本自10世纪起出现徐福东渡的记述，和歌山县新宫市建有徐福公园与徐福墓，佐贺、京都等地也有徐福祠庙；但日本8世纪成书的早期史书完全没有提到他，多数学者认为「徐福到日本」是后世形成的传说，而非可证的史实。',
     'These are among the earliest state-sponsored ocean voyages recorded in Chinese official history, both set down in the Records of the Grand Historian. From the tenth century onward Japanese texts describe Xu Fu arriving in Japan; Shingū in Wakayama Prefecture has a Xu Fu park and tomb, and shrines to him stand in Saga, Kyoto and elsewhere. But Japan\'s own eighth-century histories say nothing of him, and most scholars treat the arrival story as a later legend rather than established fact.'] },
'王贞仪': { g:'sci', y:[1768,1797], c:'清', n:['王贞仪','Wang Zhenyi'],
  t:['她在自家凉亭里用一张圆桌、一盏悬灯和一面镜子，把月食演了一遍。',
     'In her garden pavilion she staged a lunar eclipse with a round table, a hanging lamp and a mirror.'],
  a:[['以圆桌当地球、梁上悬灯当太阳、桌旁镜子当月亮，按天文原理移动三者来模拟月食，据此写成《月食解》，正确说明了月食的成因以及日食与月食的关系。','She used a round table for the Earth, a lamp hung from the beam for the Sun and a mirror at the table\'s edge for the Moon, moving all three according to astronomical principle. Out of that experiment came her essay Explaining the Lunar Eclipse, which sets out correctly why eclipses happen and how solar and lunar eclipses relate.'],
     ['著《岁差日至辨疑》讨论岁差与冬夏至的推算，《勾股三角解》讲勾股与三角计算；又把梅文鼎艰深的西洋筹算著作删改成便于初学者读的本子。','She wrote On Doubts Concerning Precession and the Solstices, and Solutions of Right Triangles. She also rewrote Mei Wending\'s difficult treatise on Western calculating rods into a version a beginner could follow.'],
     ['诗文合集《德风亭初集》十三卷传世，其中有「足行万里书万卷，尝拟雄心胜丈夫」之句。她二十九岁去世，遗稿由友人整理保存下来。','Thirteen volumes of her poems and essays survive as the Defengting Collection, including the line "ten thousand li walked, ten thousand books read — I once meant my ambition to outrun any man\'s". She died at twenty-nine; a friend gathered and preserved the manuscripts.']],
  s:['1994年国际天文学联合会以她的名字命名了金星上的一座环形山（Wang Zhenyi）。2015年美国科普读物《勇往直前：52位改变科学与世界的女性》收录了她。她是清代留下成体系的天文与数学著作的极少数女性之一。',
     'In 1994 the International Astronomical Union named a crater on Venus after her; asteroid 43259 also carries her name. In 2015 the American book Headstrong: 52 Women Who Changed Science and the World placed her alongside Marie Curie. She is one of very few women of the Qing period to leave a coherent body of astronomical and mathematical work.'] },
'魏源': { g:'mind', y:[1794,1857], c:'清', n:['魏源','Wei Yuan'],
  t:['他写的那本书在中国印数不多，在日本却被翻刻了一遍又一遍。',
     'The book he wrote found few readers in China. In Japan it was reprinted again and again.'],
  a:[['1843年在扬州刻印《海国图志》五十卷，系统介绍世界各国的地理、历史、政治制度和西方的造船制炮技术；1847—1848年增补为六十卷，1852年扩至一百卷，全书约八十八万字，附地图七十五幅、西洋船炮器艺图式四十二页。','In 1843 he published the fifty-volume Illustrated Treatise on the Maritime Kingdoms at Yangzhou, laying out the geography, history and political systems of foreign countries along with Western shipbuilding and gunnery. He expanded it to sixty volumes in 1847–48 and to a hundred in 1852 — some 880,000 characters, seventy-five maps and forty-two pages of diagrams of foreign ships, cannon and machines.'],
     ['在书中提出「师夷长技以制夷」，主张先学对方的造船、制炮和练兵方法。','In it he argued for "learning the superior techniques of the foreigners in order to hold them off" — beginning with how they built ships, cast guns and drilled troops.'],
     ['另著《圣武记》十四卷（1842年成书），记述清代历次用兵；晚年编纂《元史新编》九十五卷。','He also wrote the fourteen-volume Record of Sacred Military Campaigns, finished in 1842, on the Qing dynasty\'s wars, and in later life compiled the ninety-five-volume New History of the Yuan.']],
  s:['《海国图志》1851年传入日本，1854年起被反复翻刻，出现多种和刻本与节译本，成为幕末知识人了解西方的主要读物之一。「师夷长技以制夷」后来被洋务运动直接用作口号。这部书是19世纪中期中文世界篇幅最大的世界地理与海外知识汇编之一。',
     'The Treatise reached Japan in 1854 and was reprinted repeatedly there, in full and in abridgement, becoming one of the main sources through which late-Tokugawa intellectuals learned about the West. His phrase about learning foreign techniques was later taken up wholesale as a slogan of China\'s Self-Strengthening Movement. The book remains one of the largest compilations of world geography and foreign knowledge produced in Chinese in the mid-nineteenth century.'] },
'屠呦呦': { g:'sci', y:[1969,2025], yk:'a', c:'共和国', n:['屠呦呦','Tu Youyou'],
  t:['答案藏在一本一千六百年前的急救手册里，只有一句话。',
     'The answer was one sentence in a first-aid handbook written sixteen centuries earlier.'],
  a:[['1930年生于浙江宁波。1969年参加抗疟药研究的「523任务」，带队查阅医籍、走访老中医，收集两千余个方药，整理成含640个方药的资料集。','Born in Ningbo, Zhejiang in 1930, she joined the anti-malarial "Project 523" in 1969, leading a team that combed through medical texts and interviewed traditional practitioners, gathering more than 2,000 remedies and distilling them into a working file of 640.'],
     ['东晋葛洪《肘后备急方》写「青蒿一握，以水二升渍，绞取汁，尽服之」——「绞汁」而非煎煮，提示有效成分怕热。她改用乙醚低温提取，1971年10月4日的第191号样品对鼠疟原虫的抑制率达到100%。','Ge Hong\'s fourth-century Emergency Formulas told readers to steep a handful of qinghao in water and wring out the juice — wring, not boil, hinting the active compound could not take heat. She switched to a low-temperature ether extraction, and on 4 October 1971 sample number 191 suppressed the malaria parasite by 100 per cent.'],
     ['1972年从黄花蒿中分离出结晶「青蒿素」；同年她与两名同事在住院观察下率先试服，确认对人体的安全性。','In 1972 her group isolated crystalline artemisinin from Artemisia annua. That same year she and two colleagues took the first human doses themselves, under hospital observation, to check that it was safe.']],
  s:['2015年获诺贝尔生理学或医学奖，是首位获诺贝尔生理学或医学奖的中国人，也是首位在中国本土完成研究而获诺贝尔科学奖的科学家；此前于2011年获拉斯克临床医学研究奖。523任务是1967年起由多部门组织、数十家单位参与的全国性协作项目。世界卫生组织自2000年代初把以青蒿素为基础的联合疗法（ACT）列为恶性疟疾的首选治疗方案。据世卫组织《世界疟疾报告》，2000至2015年全球疟疾死亡率下降约60%。',
     'She received the Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine in 2015, the first Chinese scientist to win the Nobel in Physiology or Medicine, and the first to win a Nobel science prize for work done in China and the first Chinese woman to win one; she had taken the Lasker Award for clinical medical research in 2011. Since the early 2000s the World Health Organization has made artemisinin-based combination therapy the first-line treatment for falciparum malaria. WHO\'s World Malaria Report puts the fall in the global malaria death rate between 2000 and 2015 at roughly 60 per cent.'] },
'袁隆平': { g:'sci', y:[1930,2021], c:'共和国', n:['袁隆平','Yuan Longping'],
  t:['水稻是自花授粉的，教科书说它不可能有杂交优势——他花了六年，在田里找到反例。',
     'Rice pollinates itself, so the textbooks said hybrid vigour was impossible in it. He spent six years in the paddies finding the exception.'],
  a:[['1964年在湖南安江农校的稻田里找到第一株天然雄性不育水稻，开始杂交水稻研究；1966年在《科学通报》发表《水稻的雄性不孕性》。','In 1964 he found a naturally male-sterile rice plant in the fields of the Anjiang agricultural school in Hunan and began work on hybrid rice. His paper on male sterility in rice appeared in Kexue Tongbao in 1966.'],
     ['1970年他的助手李必湖在海南岛发现野生稻雄性不育株「野败」，成为育种的关键材料；1973年籼型杂交水稻「三系」——不育系、保持系、恢复系——配套成功。','In 1970 his assistant Li Bihu found a male-sterile wild rice on Hainan Island, nicknamed "wild abortive", which became the key breeding stock. By 1973 the three-line hybrid system for indica rice — sterile line, maintainer line, restorer line — was complete.'],
     ['1976年杂交水稻开始在全国推广，当年种植约208万亩；此后中国杂交稻的年种植面积长期占水稻总面积的一半以上。','Nationwide planting began in 1976 on about 2.08 million mu. For decades afterwards hybrid varieties have covered more than half of China\'s total rice acreage.']],
  s:['2004年获世界粮食奖（World Food Prize）；2000年获首届国家最高科学技术奖。中国的杂交水稻技术自1979年起向国外转让，此后在亚洲、非洲、美洲的数十个国家试种或推广。1999年，中国科学院将编号8117的小行星命名为「袁隆平星」。',
     'He received the World Food Prize in 2004 and, in 2000, one of the first two State Preeminent Science and Technology Awards. Chinese hybrid rice technology has been transferred abroad since 1979 and is now grown or trialled in dozens of countries across Asia, Africa and the Americas. In 1999 asteroid 8117 was named Yuanlongping.'] },
'王选': { g:'sci', y:[1937,2006], c:'共和国', n:['王选','Wang Xuan'],
  t:['国外正在用第二代、第三代设备，他跳过它们，直接做第四代。',
     'The rest of the world was on second- and third-generation machines. He skipped both and went straight to the fourth.'],
  a:[['1975年参加国家「748工程」的汉字信息处理项目，放弃当时国外通行的光学机械式和阴极射线管式路线，直接研制激光照排系统。','In 1975 he joined the state "Project 748" on Chinese-character information processing, passing over the optomechanical and cathode-ray-tube systems then standard abroad and going directly for laser phototypesetting.'],
     ['汉字字数多、字形复杂，一套字模的数据量远超当时计算机的存储能力。他发明用轮廓加参数描述笔画的字形压缩与快速复原方法，压缩比达到约五百比一，这项技术后来获得中国和欧洲的发明专利。','Chinese has too many characters, and each is too intricate, for a full set of fonts to fit in the computers of the day. He devised a way of describing strokes as outlines plus parameters, compressing the data roughly five hundred to one and restoring it at speed. The method was later patented in China and in Europe.'],
     ['1987年5月22日，《经济日报》四个版全部用激光照排出版，成为中国第一份用计算机组版、激光照排整版输出的日报；1988年该报印刷厂卖掉全部铅字。','On 22 May 1987 all four pages of Economic Daily were produced by laser phototypesetting — the first Chinese-language daily anywhere composed on screen and output whole by such a system. In 1988 its printing plant sold off its lead type.']],
  s:['到1990年代中期，中国的报社和出版社基本完成从铅字排版到激光照排的转换，沿用近百年的中文铅字印刷退出生产；这套系统还销往日本、北美和欧洲的中文报业。王选2001年获国家最高科学技术奖，被称为「当代毕昇」。这项技术的产业化载体是北京大学计算机技术研究所与方正集团。',
     'By the mid-1990s Chinese newspapers and publishers had almost all moved from lead type to laser phototypesetting, retiring a method of printing Chinese that had run for close to a century; the systems were also sold to Chinese-language papers in Japan, North America and Europe. Wang received the State Preeminent Science and Technology Award in 2001 and is often called "the Bi Sheng of our time", after the inventor of movable type. The work was commercialised through Peking University\'s computer institute and the Founder group.'] },
'李时珍': { g:'sci', y:[1518,1593], c:'明', n:['李时珍','Li Shizhen'],
  t:['前人书里把药名抄错、把两种草当成一种，他一样一样跑到山里去对，对了二十七年。',
     'Earlier books had copied plant names wrongly and merged two herbs into one. He went into the hills and checked them, one at a time, for twenty-seven years.'],
  a:[['1552年动笔编《本草纲目》，1578年定稿，前后二十七年；参考历代医书药书八百余种，并多次到湖广、江西、南直隶等地实地采访药农、猎户和渔民。','He began the Compendium of Materia Medica in 1552 and finished the manuscript in 1578, twenty-seven years later. He worked through more than eight hundred earlier medical and pharmacological texts, and travelled repeatedly through Huguang, Jiangxi and the Southern Metropolitan Region to question herb gatherers, hunters and fishermen in person.'],
     ['全书五十二卷，收药一千八百九十二种（其中新增三百七十四种），附药方一万一千零九十六则、插图一千一百零九幅。','The finished work runs to fifty-two volumes and covers 1,892 substances, 374 of them added by him, with 11,096 prescriptions and 1,109 illustrations.'],
     ['他不再沿用旧本草按「上品、中品、下品」排药的做法，改按水、火、土、金石、草、木、虫、鳞、介、禽、兽、人等十六部六十类编排，从矿物到植物到动物，由简到繁。','He dropped the old ranking of drugs into upper, middle and lower grades and reorganised them into sixteen divisions and sixty classes — among them water, fire, earth, minerals, herbs, trees, insects, scaled and shelled creatures, birds, beasts — running from the mineral through the plant to the animal, and from simple to complex.']],
  s:['1596年在南京刊行金陵本。此书17世纪起传入日本、朝鲜，18世纪之后陆续出现拉丁文、日文、法文、德文、英文、俄文等译本或节译本。2011年5月，中国中医科学院藏金陵本《本草纲目》入选联合国教科文组织《世界记忆名录》。',
     'The first edition was printed at Nanjing in 1596. From the seventeenth century the book circulated in Japan and Korea, and from the eighteenth century onward it appeared in Latin, Japanese, French, German, English and Russian, in full or in part. In May 2011 the 1596 Nanjing edition held by the China Academy of Chinese Medical Sciences was inscribed on UNESCO\'s Memory of the World Register.'] },
'黄道婆': { g:'sci', y:[1245,1330], ca:1, c:'元', n:['黄道婆','Huang Daopo'],
  t:['她少年流落海南，三十多年后回到上海，带回的是一整套做棉布的机器。',
     'She drifted to Hainan as a girl. Thirty-odd years later she came back to Shanghai with a complete set of machines for making cotton cloth.'],
  a:[['早年流落崖州（今海南三亚一带），一般认为她在当地向黎族学得棉纺织技术（最早的记载只说她「自崖州来」）；元贞年间（1295—1297）搭海船回到松江府乌泥泾（今上海徐汇华泾）。','As a young woman she ended up in Yazhou, at the southern tip of Hainan, and learned cotton work from Li women there. Between 1295 and 1297 she took a ship home to Wunijing in Songjiang prefecture, today\'s Huajing in Shanghai\'s Xuhui district.'],
     ['把捍（轧车去棉籽）、弹（弹棉大弓）、纺（三锭脚踏纺车）、织（织机）四道工序的工具整套改良后传授给乡人；三锭脚踏纺车能同时纺三根纱，产量高于当时通行的单锭手摇车。','She improved and taught the whole four-stage tool set — a roller gin for removing seed, a large bow for fluffing, a treadle spinning wheel and a loom. Her wheel carried three spindles and spun three threads at once, well ahead of the single-spindle hand wheel then in use.'],
     ['传授「错纱配色、综线挈花」的织造方法，乌泥泾由此织出带图案的被、褥、带、帨，被称为「乌泥泾被」，销往各地。','She also taught patterned weaving — interleaving coloured yarns and lifting figures with the heddles. Wunijing began turning out figured quilts, mattress covers, sashes and kerchiefs that sold far beyond the district under its own name.']],
  s:['元末明初陶宗仪《南村辍耕录》卷二十四「黄道婆」条与王逢的诗，是目前所知关于她的最早记载。此后松江府成为明清两代中国最大的棉纺织业中心，有「衣被天下」之称。上海徐汇区华泾镇有她的墓与纪念馆；2006年「乌泥泾手工棉纺织技艺」列入第一批国家级非物质文化遗产名录。',
     'The earliest known accounts of her are a poem by Wang Feng and an entry in chapter 24 of Tao Zongyi\'s Notes Taken While Resting from the Plough, both from the late Yuan and early Ming. Songjiang went on to become the largest cotton-textile centre in China through the Ming and Qing, said to "clothe the empire". Her tomb and a memorial hall stand at Huajing in Shanghai, and in 2006 the hand cotton-weaving craft of Wunijing entered China\'s first national list of intangible cultural heritage.'] },
'宇文恺': { g:'sci', y:[555,612], c:'隋', n:['宇文恺','Yuwen Kai'],
  t:['今天西安城里那些横平竖直的街，是他在582年画出来的图。',
     'The straight streets of central Xi\'an today follow a plan he drew in 582.'],
  a:[['开皇二年（582年）任营新都副监，新都大兴城的规模与规划全部出自他手：全城约84平方公里，中轴对称，分宫城、皇城、外郭城三重，居民区按棋盘状的里坊排列。当年六月动工，第二年三月即迁入。','In 582 he was made deputy director of works for the new capital, Daxing, and both its scale and its plan were his. The city covered some 84 square kilometres, laid out symmetrically about a central axis, in three enclosures — palace city, administrative city and outer city — with residential wards arranged like a chessboard. Ground was broken in the sixth month of 582 and the court moved in the following spring.'],
     ['开皇四年（584年）主持开凿广通渠，自大兴城引渭水东达潼关注入黄河，长三百余里，解决关中的漕运。','In 584 he cut the Guangtong Canal, carrying water from the Wei east from Daxing to the Yellow River at Tongguan, some three hundred li, to move grain into the Guanzhong basin.'],
     ['大业元年（605年）主持营建东都洛阳城。又为炀帝北巡设计可拆装的「观风行殿」——殿下装轮轴，能移动，上面容得下几百名侍卫；还造过周长约八里的活动城「六合城」，一夜可以搭成。','In 605 he directed the building of the eastern capital at Luoyang. For Emperor Yang\'s northern progress he designed the Wind-Viewing Travelling Hall, a demountable palace on wheeled axles large enough to hold several hundred guards, and the Liuhe city, a portable fortification about eight li around that could be assembled overnight.']],
  s:['大兴城的规划被唐代整体沿用，改称长安城，是当时世界上规模最大的都城之一；日本7—8世纪营建的藤原京、平城京、平安京在里坊格局上模仿了它。今天西安明代城墙以内的街道走向仍能看出这套骨架。他的《明堂图议》被《隋书》收录，是中国早期建筑理论文献之一。',
     'The Tang took over his plan intact, renamed the city Chang\'an, and made it one of the largest capitals in the world of its day. The Japanese capitals of Fujiwara-kyō, Heijō-kyō and Heian-kyō, laid out in the seventh and eighth centuries, copied its ward grid. The street pattern inside the Ming walls of Xi\'an still shows the frame. His treatise on the ritual Hall of Light is preserved in the Book of Sui, one of the earliest surviving pieces of Chinese architectural theory.'] },
'刘焯': { g:'sci', y:[544,610], c:'隋', n:['刘焯','Liu Zhuo'],
  t:['他算的历法朝廷没有采用，但历法里的那套算法，后来的人一直用了下去。',
     'The court turned down his calendar. The method buried inside it was used by every calendar that followed.'],
  a:[['开皇二十年（600年）编成《皇极历》上呈朝廷，第一次把太阳视运动的不均匀性考虑进定朔的推算。','In 600 he presented the Huangji calendar to the throne, the first Chinese calendar to allow for the uneven apparent motion of the Sun when computing the true new moon.'],
     ['为此他创立了等间距二次内插法，用来推算日月运行速度的变化——这是中国历法史上已知最早的二次内插算法。','To do it he worked out second-order interpolation over equal intervals, a way of tracking the changing speed of the Sun and Moon. It is the earliest known use of second-order interpolation in Chinese calendrical astronomy.'],
     ['因与太史令张胄玄的历法主张不合，《皇极历》被搁置未行用。他还建议在黄河南北的平原上分点实测日影长度，以求「地中」和子午线的长度，朝廷同样没有采纳。','His views clashed with those of the court astronomer Zhang Zhouxuan, and the calendar was shelved unused. He also proposed measuring the noon shadow at several points across the plains north and south of the Yellow River, to fix the centre of the earth and the length of a meridian degree. That too was turned down.']],
  s:['唐高宗时李淳风编《麟德历》，直接采用了《皇极历》的二次内插方法，《麟德历》后来被推为中国古代名历之一；唐宋历法沿用并改进这一算法。他提出的实测子午线设想，在一百多年后由唐代僧一行与南宫说组织的724—725年天文大地测量中实现。',
     'Under Emperor Gaozong of Tang, Li Chunfeng built the Linde calendar directly on Liu Zhuo\'s interpolation method; the Linde was later ranked among the great calendars of imperial China, and Tang and Song calendars kept refining the same technique. His proposal to measure a meridian by survey was carried out more than a century later, in the geodetic campaign the monk Yixing and Nangong Yue organised in 724–725.'] },
'源赖朝': { g:'king', y:[1147,1199], r:[1192,1199], c:'幕府时代', n:['源赖朝','Minamoto no Yoritomo'],
  t:['打赢之后他没有留在京城做官,而是回老家另开了一套政府——日本此后七百年都照这个样子。','After winning he did not stay in the capital to take office; he went home and set up a government of his own — and Japan was run that way for the next seven hundred years.'],
  a:[['少年时因父亲兵败被流放到伊豆二十年,1180 年在那里起兵','Exiled to Izu for twenty years as a boy after his father\'s defeat, he raised his banner there in 1180'],
     ['1185 年在坛之浦海战中灭平氏,1192 年受封征夷大将军——此后到 1868 年,这个头衔一直是武家政权之首的名号(中间有过没有将军的年头)','Destroyed the Taira at the sea battle of Dan-no-ura in 1185 and was appointed shogun in 1192 — a title that named the head of every warrior government until 1868, though there were years with no shogun at all'],
     ['他在各国设「守护」管军事治安、在庄园设「地头」管土地税收,把自己的人插进了原有的行政体系里,不夺天皇的名分而夺其实权','He placed constables in the provinces to handle military affairs and stewards on the estates to handle land and taxes, threading his own men through the existing administration — taking the substance of power without touching the emperor\'s title']],
  s:['1199 年他去世,传说是坠马所致——《吾妻镜》这几年恰好缺载,坠马之说要到十几年后才见于记载,幕府随即落到妻子北条政子的娘家手里,他的两个儿子先后被杀。开创者的家系三代而绝,而他造出来的那套东西活了将近七百年——这在日本史上不算罕见:名义与实权分开之后,连开创者自己也可以被架空。','He died in 1199, traditionally after a fall from his horse — the court chronicle is missing for those very years, and the story of the fall appears only more than a decade later, the shogunate passed at once to the family of his wife Hojo Masako, and both his sons were killed in turn. The founder\'s line ended in three generations while the machine he built ran for almost seven hundred years — not a rare pattern in Japan: once name and power come apart, even the founder can be hollowed out.'] },

'紫式部': { g:'art', y:[973,1014], ca:1, c:'古代日本', n:['紫式部','Murasaki Shikibu'],
  t:['宫里的男人用汉文写正经文章，她用女人写信用的假名，写了一部五十四帖的长篇小说。',
     'The men at court wrote their serious prose in Chinese. She used the phonetic script women wrote letters in — and wrote a novel in fifty-four chapters.'],
  a:[['约1001—1008年间写成《源氏物语》五十四帖，以皇子光源氏及其后代的一生为主线，出场人物四百余人，故事跨越七十余年、四代人。','Between about 1001 and 1008 she wrote The Tale of Genji in fifty-four chapters, following the life of the imperial son Hikaru Genji and his descendants — more than four hundred characters, across seventy years and four generations.'],
     ['1005或1006年入宫，任一条天皇中宫藤原彰子的女房，私下为她讲授白居易的《白氏文集》。','In 1005 or 1006 she entered the service of Fujiwara no Shōshi, consort of Emperor Ichijō, and privately tutored her in the collected poems of the Chinese poet Bai Juyi.'],
     ['所著《紫式部日记》记录1008—1010年的宫中见闻，其中写到她把刚写好的《源氏物语》各帖交人抄写装订，也留下了她对同时代作家清少纳言的尖锐评语。','Her diary covers court life from 1008 to 1010. It records her handing freshly written chapters of Genji out to be copied and bound, and includes a sharp verdict on her contemporary Sei Shōnagon.']],
  s:['《源氏物语》被广泛视为世界上最早的长篇小说之一，成书比但丁《神曲》早约三百年。12世纪的《源氏物语绘卷》是现存最早以它为题材的绘画，现存十九幅，分藏名古屋德川美术馆与东京五岛美术馆，被指定为日本国宝。1925—1933年亚瑟·韦利的六卷英译本出版后，此书又被转译为法、德、意、荷等多种语言。2000年发行的日本两千日元纸币上印有《源氏物语绘卷》的画面与她的形象。',
     'The Tale of Genji is widely regarded as one of the world\'s earliest novels, written some three hundred years before Dante\'s Commedia. The twelfth-century Genji Scrolls are the oldest surviving paintings made from it; nineteen sections remain, held by the Tokugawa Art Museum in Nagoya and the Gotoh Museum in Tokyo, and designated National Treasures of Japan. After Arthur Waley\'s six-volume English translation appeared between 1925 and 1933, the book was rendered onward into French, German, Italian and Dutch. Japan\'s 2,000-yen note, issued in 2000, carries a scene from the scrolls and her portrait.'] },
'维特鲁威': { g:'art', y:[-80,-15], ca:1, c:'罗马帝国', n:['维特鲁威','Vitruvius'],
  t:['他不是罗马最有名的建筑师，却是唯一一个把怎么盖房子写下来、还传到今天的人。',
     'He was not Rome\'s most famous architect. He is simply the only one whose handbook survived.'],
  a:[['他做过恺撒军队的工程师，负责弩炮一类的攻城机械；退役后为奥古斯都写成《建筑十书》，这是古代唯一一部完整传世的建筑专著。','He served Caesar\'s army as an engineer of siege artillery such as ballistae, and in retirement wrote On Architecture in ten books for Augustus — the only complete architectural treatise to survive from antiquity.'],
     ['十卷书从选址、砖石、神庙比例一直写到引水渠、日晷、水磨和起重机械；他提出好建筑要同时做到三件事：坚固、实用、美观。','The ten books range from choosing a site, masonry and temple proportions to aqueducts, sundials, water mills and hoisting gear. Good building, he wrote, must do three things at once: stand firm, be useful, and please the eye.'],
     ['第三书写人体比例，说一个人四肢张开时，正好能同时嵌进一个圆和一个正方形——一千五百年后，达·芬奇照着这段话画出了《维特鲁威人》。','Book III sets out the proportions of the human body and observes that a man with limbs outstretched fits exactly into both a circle and a square. Some 1,500 years later Leonardo drew the Vitruvian Man straight from that passage.']],
  s:['1414年人文主义者波焦在瑞士圣加尔修道院重新推介此书（它在中世纪并未失传），十五世纪随即出现四十多种手抄副本，1486年前后首次印刷。阿尔伯蒂、布拉曼特、帕拉第奥都以它为教科书，书中的柱式规矩经他们进入欧洲与美洲的公共建筑。',
     'In 1414 the humanist Poggio Bracciolini publicized a manuscript of the work at the abbey of St Gallen in Switzerland; more than twenty hand copies circulated during the fifteenth century and the first printed edition appeared around 1486. Alberti, Bramante and Palladio all treated it as a textbook, and through them its rules for the classical orders passed into public architecture across Europe and the Americas. The colonnades on courthouses, parliaments and museums today mostly follow these ten books.'] },
'盖伦': { g:'sci', y:[129,216], ca:1, c:'罗马帝国', n:['盖伦','Galen'],
  t:['他给角斗士当队医，把每一道伤口当成一扇看进人体的窗。',
     'As doctor to the gladiators, he treated every open wound as a window into the body.'],
  a:[['157年他回到故乡帕加马，受聘为角斗士学校的医师，靠处理刀伤与断骨积累了大量关于人体内部的第一手观察。','In 157 he returned to his native Pergamon as physician to the gladiator school, gathering first-hand knowledge of the body\'s interior from sword cuts and broken bones.'],
     ['他当众做活体解剖，切断猪颈部的一条神经后，猪立刻发不出叫声，以此说明发声由神经与大脑控制而非由心脏；这条神经至今仍叫喉返神经。','In public demonstrations he severed a nerve in a pig\'s neck and the animal fell silent, showing that voice is governed by the nerves and the brain rather than the heart. The nerve still bears the name he gave it: the recurrent laryngeal.'],
     ['他用结扎实验证明动脉里流的是血，推翻了动脉输送空气的旧说；后来成为马可·奥勒留父子的御医。','By tying off arteries he demonstrated that they carry blood, not air, overturning long-standing doctrine. He later served as personal physician to Marcus Aurelius and his son.']],
  s:['他传世的著作超过二百六十万字，是古代希腊语作者中留存最多的一位，约占公元350年以前全部现存希腊文献的十分之一。他的学说经拜占庭与阿拉伯世界（伊本·西那等人）传回欧洲，主宰医学教育一千三百多年，直到1543年维萨里指出他的解剖多取自动物而非人体。',
     'Over 2.6 million of his words survive — more than from any other Greek author of antiquity, and roughly a tenth of all Greek literature extant from before 350 CE. His system passed through Byzantium and the Arabic world, notably Ibn Sina, back into Europe and governed medical teaching for more than 1,300 years, until Vesalius showed in 1543 that much of his anatomy had been taken from animals rather than humans.'] },
'塔西佗': { g:'mind', y:[56,120], ca:1, c:'罗马帝国', n:['塔西佗','Tacitus'],
  t:['他自己做到了执政官，却把笔口对准皇帝，说写史要“不带怒气，也不带偏爱”。',
     'He rose to consul, then turned his pen on the emperors — writing, as he put it, without anger and without partiality.'],
  a:[['97年他出任补任执政官，112至113年任亚细亚行省总督，仕途走到罗马元老所能到的顶端。','He held a suffect consulship in 97 and governed the province of Asia in 112–113, reaching the top of the senatorial career.'],
     ['98年出版《日耳曼尼亚志》，逐条记录莱茵河以东各部族的农耕、婚俗、议事方式与武器，这是古代关于早期日耳曼人最详细的现存记载。','His Germania of 98 catalogues the farming, marriage customs, assemblies and weapons of the peoples east of the Rhine — the fullest account of the early Germanic world to come down from antiquity.'],
     ['《编年史》写提比略到尼禄的历史，其中记64年罗马大火后尼禄迁怒基督徒，并提到“基督”在提比略治下被总督本丢·彼拉多处死，这是非基督教作者关于此事最早的记载之一。','The Annals covers Tiberius to Nero. Recounting how Nero blamed the Christians for the fire of 64, it notes that Christus had been executed under Tiberius by the governor Pontius Pilate — among the earliest references to the event by a non-Christian writer.']],
  s:['《编年史》原有十六卷，第七至第十卷全佚、另有三卷残缺，其余靠中世纪的两部抄本传了下来。他那种短句、少修饰、把话压在字缝里的写法被后世史家反复模仿，称为“塔西佗式”；他对权力如何在共和外壳下运作的记述，是研究罗马元首制最常被引用的原始材料之一，也被十八世纪的共和主义政论反复援引。',
     'Of the sixteen books of the Annals, less than half survives, carried down through just two medieval manuscripts. His clipped, unadorned sentences, heavy with what they leave unsaid, were imitated so widely that the style has its own name. His account of how power actually worked behind republican forms remains one of the most-cited primary sources on the Roman principate, and was quoted constantly by eighteenth-century republican writers.'] },
'希帕蒂娅': { g:'sci', y:[360,415], ca:1, c:'罗马帝国', n:['希帕蒂娅','Hypatia'],
  t:['古代留下姓名的女学者极少，而她的课堂被学生一封封信保存了下来。',
     'Very few women scholars of antiquity are known even by name. Her classroom survives in her students\' letters.'],
  a:[['她主持亚历山大城的新柏拉图学派学园，公开讲授数学、天文与哲学，学生来自帝国各地，其中包括后来当上主教的昔兰尼的西内修斯。','She headed the Neoplatonic school at Alexandria, teaching mathematics, astronomy and philosophy in public to students drawn from across the empire — among them Synesius of Cyrene, later a bishop.'],
     ['托勒密《天文学大成》第三卷的注释本上留着一行字：“此卷由哲学家、我的女儿希帕蒂娅校订”，写这话的是她父亲席昂；她另注释了丢番图的《算术》和阿波罗尼奥斯的《圆锥曲线论》。','The commentary on Book III of Ptolemy\'s Almagest carries a line by her father Theon: \'edited by the philosopher, my daughter Hypatia.\' She also wrote commentaries on Diophantus\'s Arithmetica and Apollonius\'s Conics.'],
     ['西内修斯写信请她代造一具比重计，又自述星盘的做法学自她，说明她既讲理论也动手造仪器。','Letters from Synesius ask her how to construct an astrolabe and a hydrometer, showing that she built instruments as well as taught theory.']],
  s:['丢番图《算术》原十三卷，今存希腊文六卷、阿拉伯文四卷，文本中的注解与增补被认为多半来自她的校订本。415年她在亚历山大城的教俗冲突中被暴徒杀害，事见同时代教会史家苏格拉底·斯科拉斯提库斯的记载；十八世纪以后，她成为欧洲讨论学术与宗教冲突时最常被提起的名字之一。',
     'Of Diophantus\'s thirteen books of Arithmetica, six survive in Greek and four in Arabic, and the notes and interpolations in them are thought to derive largely from her edition — it was a later version of this book in whose margin Fermat wrote his famous note. In 415 she was killed by a mob during a clash between civic and church factions in Alexandria, an event recorded by the contemporary church historian Socrates Scholasticus. From the eighteenth century onward her name became one of the most frequently invoked in European arguments about learning and religion.'] },
'阿托莎': { g:'state', y:[-545,-470], ca:1, c:'波斯(阿契美尼德)', n:['阿托莎','Atossa'],
  t:['居鲁士的女儿、大流士的王后、薛西斯的母亲——三代波斯大王之间的那个人是她。',
     'Daughter of Cyrus, wife of Darius, mother of Xerxes: she is the hinge between three Persian kings.'],
  a:[['她是居鲁士之女、冈比西斯之妹。大流士夺得王位后娶了她和她的妹妹阿尔塔斯图涅，借此把自己接进居鲁士的家族。','She was Cyrus\'s daughter and Cambyses\'s sister. On seizing the throne Darius married her and her sister Artystone, grafting himself onto Cyrus\'s line.'],
     ['据希罗多德《历史》第三卷，她胸前生疮，由被俘的希腊医生德谟凯德斯治好；医生索要的报酬，是请她劝大流士先派人去希腊探路。希罗多德把波斯转向西方的第一步记在这段对话上。','Herodotus, Book III, tells how a growth on her breast was cured by Democedes, a captive Greek doctor, whose price was that she persuade Darius to send scouts west to Greece. Herodotus dates Persia\'s first turn toward Greece to that conversation.'],
     ['《历史》第七卷说，大流士的继承人之争中，正是因为她的分量，居鲁士的外孙薛西斯压过了年长的兄长。','Book VII reports that in the contest over Darius\'s succession it was her weight at court that carried Xerxes, Cyrus\'s grandson, past his elder half-brother.']],
  s:['前472年埃斯库罗斯的悲剧《波斯人》在雅典上演，全剧的中心人物是波斯太后，一般认为即以她为原型；此剧通常被视为现存最古老的完整剧本，也是唯一一部以当时时事为题材的传世希腊悲剧。阿契美尼德王室女性留下姓名的极少，她是同时被希腊史书和希腊戏剧记下的少数几个之一；学者把她的名字复原为埃兰语 Udusana，但波斯波利斯泥板中未见其人。',
     'In 472 BC Aeschylus\'s tragedy The Persians was staged in Athens with the Persian queen mother at its centre, generally taken to be modelled on her. The play is usually reckoned the oldest complete script that survives anywhere, and the only extant Greek tragedy drawn from contemporary events. Few Achaemenid royal women are known by name at all; she is the one recorded by Greek history and Greek theatre alike. Her name appears in Elamite as Udusana.'] },
'帕尔纳卡': { g:'state', y:[-565,-497], ca:1, c:'波斯(阿契美尼德)', n:['帕尔纳卡','Parnaka'],
  t:['帝国不是只靠打仗撑起来的——总得有人签字发口粮，他就是签字的那个人。',
     'An empire does not run on battles alone. Someone has to sign off on the rations, and he was that man.'],
  a:[['他是阿尔沙玛之子、大流士一世的叔父，约前506年至前497年主管波斯波利斯地区的经济事务，与副手齐沙维什一起签发粮食、酒和牲畜的配给。','Son of Arsames and uncle of Darius I, he ran the economic administration of the Persepolis region from about 506 to 497 BC, issuing allocations of grain, wine and livestock together with his deputy Zissawis.'],
     ['1933年在波斯波利斯城墙下出土的三万余块埃兰语泥板与残片，就是他那套系统留下的账目：谁走哪条路、领多少面粉、领多少绵羊，逐笔记账并盖印。','The thirty thousand-odd Elamite tablets and fragments unearthed beneath the Persepolis fortification wall in 1933 are the ledgers of the system he ran: who travelled which road, who drew how much flour, how many sheep — each entry recorded and sealed.'],
     ['前500年他换了一枚新印（学界编号 PFS 16*），旧印 PFS 9* 停用；连这次换印本身也被两块泥板（PF 2067、PF 2068）记了下来。','In 500 BC he took a new seal, catalogued today as PFS 16*, and retired the old PFS 9*. Even the changeover was minuted, on two tablets numbered PF 2067 and PF 2068.']],
  s:['这批“波斯波利斯城防档案”年代集中在前509年到前494年，是研究阿契美尼德行政最主要的第一手材料，1935年借存美国芝加哥大学研究，近年分批归还伊朗。泥板显示帝国用埃兰语记账、按工种发口粮、女工生育后可以多领——这些细节在希腊人写的波斯史里几乎看不到。',
     'The Persepolis Fortification Archive, concentrated in the years 509 to 494 BC, is the principal first-hand source for Achaemenid administration. Lent to the University of Chicago for study in 1935, it has in recent years been returned to Iran in batches. The tablets show accounts kept in Elamite, rations scaled by trade, and extra allowances for women workers after childbirth — none of which appears anywhere in the Persian histories written by Greeks.'] },
'斯基拉克斯': { g:'sail', y:[-550,-480], ca:1, c:'波斯(阿契美尼德)', n:['斯基拉克斯','Scylax of Caryanda'],
  t:['大流士想知道印度河到底流去哪里，就派了一个希腊人去看；这人漂了三十个月，最后从埃及上了岸。',
     'Darius wanted to know where the Indus went, so he sent a Greek to find out. Thirty months later the man came ashore in Egypt.'],
  a:[['约前515年，他奉大流士一世之命，从印度河上游的卡斯帕图罗斯出发，顺流向东下行入海。','Around 515 BC, on the orders of Darius I, he set out from Caspatyrus on the upper Indus and followed the river east down to the sea.'],
     ['入海后转向西行，沿阿拉伯半岛海岸航行，三十个月后抵达红海北端，即今苏伊士一带。这段航程见于希罗多德《历史》4.44。','From the river mouth he turned west, coasting Arabia, and after thirty months reached the head of the Red Sea near present-day Suez. Herodotus records the voyage at Histories 4.44.'],
     ['希罗多德说，正是这次航行之后，大流士征服了印度河流域，并开始使用这片海域。','It was after this voyage, Herodotus writes, that Darius subdued the Indus lands and began to make use of that sea.']],
  s:['这是古代文献记载的最早一次跨阿拉伯海官方勘察航行之一，把印度河口与红海连成了一条已知航路；此后阿契美尼德在印度河下游设行省，波斯波利斯的贡赋浮雕上出现了印度使团。需要说明的是，后世流传的希腊航海指南《环航记》虽署他的名，古典学界一般定其成书于公元前四世纪，与他本人无关。',
     'This is among the earliest state-sponsored surveys across the Arabian Sea on record, linking the mouth of the Indus to the Red Sea as a known route. An Achaemenid province was subsequently established on the lower Indus, and an Indian delegation appears among the tribute reliefs at Persepolis. One caution: the Greek coastal handbook known as the Periplus circulates under his name, but classicists have established that it was written in the fourth century BC and has nothing to do with him.'] },
'克特西亚斯': { g:'sci', y:[-450,-380], ca:1, c:'波斯(阿契美尼德)', n:['克特西亚斯','Ctesias'],
  t:['他在波斯宫廷当了十七年御医，回国后写下二十三卷波斯史——里面既有一手见闻，也有独角兽。',
     'Seventeen years as royal physician in Persia, then a twenty-three-book history of it back home — part eyewitness, part unicorn.'],
  a:[['他出身小亚细亚克尼多斯的医学世家，约从前405年起在波斯宫廷任御医，先后侍奉大流士二世与阿尔塔薛西斯二世；他自称前后十七年。','He came from a medical family at Cnidus in Asia Minor and served as physician at the Persian court from about 413 BC, first under Darius II and then Artaxerxes II, seventeen years in all.'],
     ['前401年库那克萨会战，阿尔塔薛西斯二世与弟弟小居鲁士为王位交战，他就在国王身边，处理了国王身上的伤口。','At the battle of Cunaxa in 401 BC, where Artaxerxes II fought his younger brother Cyrus for the throne, he was at the king\'s side and dressed his wound.'],
     ['前398年前后回到希腊，写成二十三卷《波斯志》和一卷《印度志》，自称查阅过波斯王室的档案；全书最后十卷写的是从薛西斯之死（前465年）到他自己那个年代的当代史。','Returning to Greece around 398 BC he wrote the Persica in twenty-three books and the Indica in one, claiming to have consulted the Persian royal records. Its final ten books cover contemporary history, from the death of Xerxes in 465 BC down to his own day.']],
  s:['《波斯志》原书失传，今天所见主要靠九世纪拜占庭学者佛提乌的摘要和其他作者的引文。他笔下的印度有独角兽和狗头人，古代就有人质疑——普鲁塔克、斯特拉波都批评过他不可靠；但他记下的宫廷制度、王室女性的活动和大量人名，有一部分能与楔形文字材料对上，因此仍是研究阿契美尼德后期最重要的文本之一。他也是希腊人写印度的最早作者之一；普林尼《自然史》与中世纪多部志怪书都转引过他笔下的印度奇兽。',
     'The Persica itself is lost; what we have comes mainly from a ninth-century summary by the Byzantine scholar Photius and from quotations in other writers. His India has unicorns and dog-headed men, and doubts began in antiquity — Plutarch and Strabo both called him unreliable. Yet parts of what he recorded about court institutions, the activities of royal women and a great many personal names can be matched against cuneiform sources, which keeps him among the most important texts for the later Achaemenid period. He was also one of the first Greeks to write about India, and the Indica shaped Europe\'s picture of that country for the next thousand years.'] },
'爱迪生': { g:'sci', y:[1847,1931], c:'美国', n:['爱迪生','Thomas Edison'],
  t:['他最大的发明其实不是灯泡，是“专门用来发明东西的实验室”这件事本身。',
     'His biggest invention was not the light bulb. It was the idea of a laboratory built to invent things.'],
  a:[['1876年他在新泽西的门洛帕克建起一座专供研发的实验室，雇工程师、化学家、机械师成班工作，被称为“发明工厂”。','In 1876 he built a laboratory at Menlo Park, New Jersey, devoted entirely to research, staffed with engineers, chemists and machinists working in shifts — the invention factory.'],
     ['1879年10月21日，用碳丝做的灯泡连续亮了十三个半小时；此后的改进型能亮四十小时。','On 21 October 1879 a bulb with a carbon filament burned for thirteen and a half hours straight; improved versions soon lasted forty.'],
     ['1882年9月4日，曼哈顿珍珠街发电站送出110伏直流电，首月用户59家。从这天起，电灯不只是灯泡，而是发电、输电、计费的一整套系统。','On 4 September 1882 the Pearl Street station in lower Manhattan began delivering 110-volt direct current to its first 59 customers. From that day electric light was not a bulb but a whole system: generation, distribution and metered billing.']],
  s:['他一生在美国获得1093项专利（另有留声机、碳精话筒、活动电影放映机等），这个数字长期是美国个人专利数的纪录，直到二十一世纪初才被超过。门洛帕克那种“雇一群人专职搞研发”的组织方式，后来被通用电气研究实验室、贝尔实验室等承袭；他创办的电力公司几经合并，就是今天的通用电气。',
     'He held 1,093 US patents, covering the phonograph, the carbon microphone and the motion-picture viewer among much else, and the figure stood as the American individual record until it was passed in the early 2000s. The Menlo Park model — a salaried staff whose only job is to invent — was taken up by the General Electric Research Laboratory, Bell Labs and others, and became the template for the twentieth-century corporate R&D department. The electric company he founded, after a series of mergers, is today\'s General Electric.'] },
'马丁·路德·金': { g:'state', y:[1929,1968], c:'美国', n:['马丁·路德·金','Martin Luther King Jr.'],
  t:['他一天官都没当过，美国的法律却因他而改。',
     'He never held any public office, and the law changed anyway.'],
  a:[['1955年12月，罗莎·帕克斯因在公交车上拒绝让座被捕，26岁的金被推举出来领导抵制运动；蒙哥马利的黑人市民靠步行和拼车坚持了381天，直到最高法院判定该市公交种族隔离违宪。','In December 1955, after Rosa Parks was arrested for refusing to give up her bus seat, the 26-year-old King was chosen to lead the boycott. Montgomery\'s black residents walked and carpooled for 381 days, until the Supreme Court ruled the city\'s bus segregation unconstitutional.'],
     ['1963年4月他在伯明翰狱中写下《伯明翰狱中书简》，回应本地白人牧师“时机未到”的劝告，成为非暴力抗争最常被引用的文本之一。','Jailed in Birmingham in April 1963, he wrote the Letter from Birmingham Jail in answer to local white clergymen who urged him to wait for a better moment. It became one of the most quoted texts on nonviolent resistance.'],
     ['1963年8月28日华盛顿大游行，约二十五万人聚在林肯纪念堂前，他在那里发表了《我有一个梦想》；次年《民权法案》通过，再一年《投票权法案》通过。','On 28 August 1963 some quarter of a million people gathered at the Lincoln Memorial for the March on Washington, where he delivered \'I Have a Dream.\' The Civil Rights Act followed the next year, the Voting Rights Act the year after that.']],
  s:['1964年10月他获诺贝尔和平奖，时年35岁，是当时最年轻的和平奖得主（这项纪录1976年由32岁的梅里德·科里根打破），并把约五万四千美元奖金全部捐给民权运动。1977年获追授总统自由勋章，2004年获国会金质奖章；1986年起每年1月第三个星期一为美国联邦法定的马丁·路德·金纪念日；2011年华盛顿国家广场落成他的纪念碑，位置在林肯纪念堂与杰斐逊纪念堂之间。',
     'He received the Nobel Peace Prize in October 1964 at the age of 35, then the youngest peace laureate ever — a record broken in 1976 by the 32-year-old Mairead Corrigan Yousafzai — and gave the entire $54,123 award to the civil rights movement. The Presidential Medal of Freedom followed posthumously in 1977 and the Congressional Gold Medal in 2004. Since 1986 the third Monday in January has been a federal holiday in his name, and in 2011 a memorial to him opened on the National Mall, between the Lincoln and Jefferson memorials.'] },
'格蕾丝·霍珀': { g:'sci', y:[1906,1992], c:'美国', n:['格蕾丝·霍珀','Grace Hopper'],
  t:['她坚持要让计算机看懂英文单词，当时几乎所有人都说这行不通。',
     'She insisted that computers could be made to read English words. Almost everyone told her it could not be done.'],
  a:[['1944年她以海军预备役军官身份被派到哈佛，为美国第一台大型自动计算机 Mark I 编程，并写出它的操作手册。','Commissioned into the Naval Reserve, she was posted to Harvard in 1944 to program the Mark I, America\'s first large automatic computer, and wrote its operating manual.'],
     ['1947年9月9日，她所在的 Mark II 团队从继电器里夹出一只飞蛾，贴进日志本，旁边写着“第一次找到真正的 bug”；那一页日志现藏史密森学会。','On 9 September 1947 her Mark II team pulled a moth out of a relay, taped it into the logbook and wrote beside it, \'first actual case of bug being found.\' That page is now in the Smithsonian.'],
     ['1952年她做出 A-0 系统，让机器自动把预先写好的子程序拼装成机器码；1955至1959年主持 FLOW-MATIC，这是第一种用 ADD、SUBTRACT 这类英文词书写的数据处理语言，其设计直接成了 COBOL 的基础。','In 1952 she produced the A-0 system, which let a machine assemble pre-written subroutines into executable code on its own. From 1955 to 1959 she led FLOW-MATIC, the first data-processing language written in English words like ADD and SUBTRACT, whose design fed directly into COBOL.']],
  s:['COBOL 于1959年定稿，至今仍运行在银行、保险和政府的大型主机系统里，是服役时间最长的编程语言之一。她1983年经总统特别任命晋升准将、1985年该衔改称海军少将，1986年以79岁高龄退役，是当时美国海军服役年龄最大的军官；1991年获国家技术奖章，2016年获追授总统自由勋章。美国海军以她命名了导弹驱逐舰“霍珀号”（DDG-70）。',
     'COBOL was settled in 1959 and still runs on the mainframes of banks, insurers and governments, making it one of the longest-serving programming languages ever written. She was promoted to rear admiral in 1985 and retired in 1986 at the age of 79, then the oldest serving officer in the US Navy. She received the National Medal of Technology in 1991 and the Presidential Medal of Freedom posthumously in 2016. The Navy named a guided-missile destroyer for her, USS Hopper (DDG-70).'] },
'莎士比亚': { g:'art', y:[1564,1616], c:'大英帝国·英国', n:['莎士比亚','William Shakespeare'],
  t:['他写戏是为了卖票养家，剧本一半到死都没印出来过。',
     'He wrote plays to sell tickets and feed a family. Half of them were still unprinted when he died.'],
  a:[['1594年起他是宫内大臣剧团的编剧兼股东，1599年剧团在泰晤士河南岸自建环球剧场，他持有其中股份——他写戏、演戏，也分票房。','From 1594 he was both playwright and shareholder in the Lord Chamberlain\'s Men, and when the company built the Globe on the south bank of the Thames in 1599 he held a share in it. He wrote, acted, and took a cut of the door.'],
     ['1623年，两位老同事海明斯和康德尔把他的36部剧本编成一册出版，即“第一对开本”；其中18部此前从未印行，《麦克白》《暴风雨》《第十二夜》都是靠这本书才留下来的。','In 1623 two old colleagues, Heminges and Condell, collected thirty-six of his plays into a single volume, the First Folio. Eighteen of them had never been printed before; Macbeth, The Tempest and Twelfth Night survive only because of that book.'],
     ['除剧本外传世的还有154首十四行诗和两部长篇叙事诗；他最长的剧本《哈姆雷特》约四千行，全本演完要四个多小时。','Besides the plays there survive 154 sonnets and two long narrative poems. His longest play, Hamlet, runs to about four thousand lines and takes over four hours to perform uncut.']],
  s:['《牛津英语词典》引用他的作品超过三万次，是被引用最多的单一作者；但辞书学者提醒，这多半是因为他的文本保存完整、被反复检索，不等于这些词都由他首创。他的剧本已被译成上百种语言，是全世界上演和改编次数最多的剧作家之一；斯特拉特福的出生地与1997年在伦敦重建的环球剧场，每年接待数十万访客。',
     'The Oxford English Dictionary quotes him more than 33,000 times, more than any other single author — though lexicographers caution that this largely reflects how completely his text survived and how often it was searched, not that he coined all those words. His plays have been translated into over a hundred languages and are among the most performed and adapted in the world. His birthplace at Stratford and the Globe, rebuilt in London in 1997, draw hundreds of thousands of visitors a year.'] },
'南丁格尔': { g:'sci', y:[1820,1910], c:'大英帝国·英国', n:['南丁格尔','Florence Nightingale'],
  t:['人们记得她提着灯查房，真正救下更多人的却是她带回来的那叠统计表。',
     'She is remembered for the lamp. What saved far more lives was the sheaf of statistics she brought home.'],
  a:[['1854年11月，她带38名护士抵达斯库塔里（今伊斯坦布尔）的英军野战医院；那里死于霍乱、痢疾、斑疹伤寒的士兵远多于死于战伤的。','In November 1854 she arrived at the British army hospital at Scutari, now part of Istanbul, with thirty-eight nurses. Far more soldiers there were dying of cholera, dysentery and typhus than of their wounds.'],
     ['1855年3月英国政府派出的卫生委员会疏通下水道、改善通风之后，死亡率大幅下降。她回国后花了几年整理数据，得出结论：真正的杀手是脏水、拥挤和不通风，不是子弹。','After a government sanitary commission flushed the sewers and improved ventilation in March 1855, deaths fell sharply. Back in England she spent years working through the figures and concluded that the real killers were foul water, overcrowding and bad air, not bullets.'],
     ['1858年她在《影响英军健康、效率与医院管理的若干问题》中画出“极区图”（俗称玫瑰图）：一个月一个扇形，蓝色代表死于可预防疾病、红色代表死于战伤、黑色代表其他死因，蓝色压倒性地大。这份报告直接呈给了维多利亚女王。','In 1858 her Notes on Matters Affecting the Health, Efficiency and Hospital Administration of the British Army introduced the polar area diagram, one wedge per month, blue for deaths from preventable disease and red for deaths from wounds — the blue overwhelming the red. The report went straight to Queen Victoria.']],
  s:['同年她当选统计学会（今皇家统计学会）第一位女性会员。1860年她用公众捐款在伦敦圣托马斯医院创办南丁格尔护士学校，南丁格尔护士学校成为此后英语世界护士训练的范本，护理训练从此有了统一课程与执业标准；1859年的《护理札记》至今仍在重印。1907年她成为第一位获颁功绩勋章的女性。她的生日5月12日被定为国际护士节。',
     'That same year she became the first woman elected to the Statistical Society, now the Royal Statistical Society. In 1860 she used public subscriptions to found the Nightingale Training School at St Thomas\' Hospital in London, making nursing for the first time a trained profession with standards of practice; her Notes on Nursing of 1859 has never gone out of print. In 1907 she became the first woman appointed to the Order of Merit. Her birthday, 12 May, is observed as International Nurses Day.'] },
'侯奈因·伊本·伊斯哈格': { g:'mind', y:[809,873], ca:1, c:'阿拉伯哈里发', n:['侯奈因·伊本·伊斯哈格','Hunayn ibn Ishaq'],
  t:['他是个基督徒，却当上了伊斯兰帝国翻译希腊典籍的总负责人。',
     'A Christian physician who ran the Islamic empire\'s project to translate the Greeks.'],
  a:[['在巴格达为哈里发与权贵家族主持一支译者团队，把盖伦、希波克拉底、柏拉图、亚里士多德的著作从希腊文译成叙利亚文和阿拉伯文。','At the House of Wisdom in Baghdad he directed the translation of Galen, Hippocrates, Plato and Aristotle from Greek into Syriac and Arabic.'],
     ['他在《书信》中逐部登记了 129 种盖伦著作的翻译情况：哪一部译成哪种语言、由谁译、为谁而译——这是中世纪极罕见的译者自述清单。','In his Risala he listed all 129 works of Galen one by one: which language each went into, who translated it, and for which patron — a translator\'s own inventory almost unheard of in the Middle Ages.'],
     ['他本人是哈里发穆塔瓦基勒的御医，写下《眼科十论》，是现存最早的系统眼科专著之一，书中附有眼球解剖图。','Personal physician to the caliph al-Mutawakkil, he wrote the Ten Treatises on the Eye, among the earliest surviving systematic works on ophthalmology, with a drawing of the eye\'s anatomy.']],
  s:['他的做法是先搜集多种希腊抄本互相校勘，再按整句意思翻译而不逐字硬译，这套方法成为阿拉伯翻译运动的标准。他为盖伦《医术》写的导论被译成拉丁文后编入《医学小集》（Articella），从 12 世纪到 16 世纪一直是萨莱诺、蒙彼利埃、博洛尼亚等欧洲大学医学院的必修课本；拉丁世界称他 Johannitius。',
     'He collated several Greek manuscripts before translating, and rendered sense for sense rather than word for word; this became the standard method of the Arabic translation movement. His introduction to Galen\'s Art of Medicine, translated into Latin, entered the Articella, the required medical textbook at Salerno, Montpellier and Bologna from the twelfth century to the sixteenth. Latin Europe knew him as Johannitius.'] },
'拉齐': { g:'sci', y:[854,925], ca:1, c:'阿拉伯哈里发', n:['拉齐','Al-Razi'],
  t:['整个中世纪的医生都把盖伦当经典，他写了一本书，书名就叫《对盖伦的怀疑》。',
     'Medieval doctors treated Galen as gospel. He wrote a book titled Doubts About Galen.'],
  a:[['先后主持故乡雷伊和都城巴格达的医院，并把自己诊治过的病人一例一例记录下来，留下成组的病历——当时的医书几乎没人这么写。','He ran the hospitals of his native Rayy and of Baghdad, and wrote down his patients case by case, leaving whole sets of case notes at a time when medical books almost never contained them.'],
     ['《天花与麻疹》逐条比较两种病的皮疹形状、发热过程和病程长短，是现存最早把天花与麻疹当作两种不同疾病来区分的专著之一。','His book On Smallpox and Measles compares the two diseases point by point — rash, fever and course — and is among the earliest surviving treatises to treat them as two distinct illnesses.'],
     ['遗著《医学集成》二十三卷由学生根据他的笔记整理，汇集希腊、印度、阿拉伯各家说法，并在每一条后面附上他自己的临床意见。','His posthumous Comprehensive Book, compiled by students from his notes in twenty-three volumes, gathers Greek, Indian and Arabic opinions and appends his own clinical judgement to each.']],
  s:['《医学集成》1279 年由西西里的法拉吉译成拉丁文，题为 Continens；1395 年巴黎大学医学院图书馆只有九种藏书，它是其中之一。《天花与麻疹》自 1498 年威尼斯版起在欧洲多次印行，19 世纪仍有新译本出版。拉丁世界称他 Rhazes。',
     'The Comprehensive Book was translated into Latin in 1279 by Faraj of Sicily as the Continens; in 1395 the library of the Paris medical faculty held only nine books, and this was one of them. On Smallpox and Measles was printed repeatedly in Europe from the Venice edition of 1498, with fresh translations still appearing in the nineteenth century. Latin Europe knew him as Rhazes.'] },
'祖拜达': { g:'state', y:[765,831], ca:1, c:'阿拉伯哈里发', n:['祖拜达','Zubaida bint Ja\'far'],
  t:['《一千零一夜》把她写成故事里的王后；现实中她修的引水渠，让麦加喝了一千年水。',
     'The Thousand and One Nights turned her into a character. In reality she built the aqueduct that watered Mecca for a thousand years.'],
  a:[['出资整修从库法到麦加、全长约一千四百公里的朝觐大道，沿途开凿水井、修建蓄水池、设立驿站与路标；这条路后来就叫「祖拜达之路」。','She paid to rebuild the pilgrimage road from Kufa to Mecca, some 1,400 kilometres, sinking wells and cisterns and setting up rest stations and milestones along it; the route is still called the Darb Zubayda.'],
     ['主持把泉水引入麦加的水渠工程（「祖拜达泉」）。后世史料估算耗资约一百七十万第纳尔；13 世纪传记家伊本·哈利康记下她对工匠说的话：哪怕一镐下去要一个第纳尔，也照付。','She commissioned the channel that brought spring water into Mecca, the Ayn Zubayda. The thirteenth-century biographer Ibn Khallikan reports it cost about 1.7 million dinars, and that she told her engineers to dig on even if every stroke of the pick cost a dinar.'],
     ['她是哈里发曼苏尔的孙女、哈伦·拉希德的妻子、阿明的母亲；813 年内战中儿子阿明败亡后，她仍多次前往麦加朝觐，继续出钱维护沿途的水井与驿站。','Granddaughter of the caliph al-Mansur, wife of Harun al-Rashid and mother of al-Amin, she went on making the pilgrimage and paying to maintain the road\'s wells and stations even after her son was killed in the civil war of 813.']],
  s:['「祖拜达泉」的引水系统经历代修缮，长期是麦加的主要水源之一，直到 20 世纪才被现代供水取代。「祖拜达之路」沿线的蓄水池、驿站与里程标遗迹仍散布在今沙特阿拉伯境内，已被列入联合国教科文组织《世界遗产预备名单》。',
     'The Ayn Zubayda system, repaired again and again over the centuries, remained one of Mecca\'s main water supplies until modern plumbing replaced it in the twentieth century. Cisterns, stations and milestones of the Darb Zubayda still stand across Saudi Arabia, and the route is on UNESCO\'s tentative World Heritage list.'] },
'耶律楚材': { g:'state', y:[1190,1244], c:'蒙古帝国', n:['耶律楚材','Yelü Chucai'],
  t:['有人主张把中原的农田全部改成牧场，他是用一笔税收账把这件事拦下来的。',
     'When advisers urged turning north China\'s farmland into pasture, he stopped them with a tax calculation.'],
  a:[['1231 年他向窝阔台算账：保留农田照常征税，一年可得银五十万两、帛八万匹、粟四十余万石。当年秋天税款如数运到，窝阔台任命他为中书令。','In 1231 he did the arithmetic for Ögedei: leave the farms alone and tax them, and the year would yield 500,000 taels of silver, 80,000 bolts of silk and over 400,000 piculs of grain. The revenue arrived that autumn, and Ögedei made him chief of the secretariat.'],
     ['1233 年汴京城破，按当时的惯例抵抗过的城市要遭屠戮；他力争工匠与人口才是攻城真正的收获，《元史》记为城中一百四十七万人得以保全。','When Kaifeng fell in 1233, custom held that a city which had resisted should be put to the sword; he argued that its craftsmen and people were the real prize of the siege, and more than 1.47 million inhabitants were spared.'],
     ['1238 年主持「戊戌选试」，在沦为奴婢的读书人中考选出四千余人，其中约四分之一因此脱去奴籍。','In 1238 he held an examination for scholars who had been enslaved in the wars; over four thousand passed, and about a quarter of them were freed from bondage as a result.']],
  s:['他把草原征服者的收入方式从临时掠夺改成常规赋税，设十路课税所、立户籍，并主张限额发钞，这套办法为元朝沿用。《元史》为他单独立传。他葬在瓮山泊，即今北京颐和园内，墓与祠堂至今仍在园中。',
     'He converted the conquerors\' income from plunder into regular taxation, setting up ten tax circuits, household registers and a paper-money system that the Yuan dynasty kept. The official History of Yuan gives him a biography of his own. He is buried at Wengshan Lake, inside today\'s Summer Palace in Beijing, where his tomb and shrine still stand.'] },
'唆鲁禾帖尼': { g:'state', y:[1190,1252], ca:1, c:'蒙古帝国', n:['唆鲁禾帖尼','Sorghaghtani Beki'],
  t:['她一生没有称汗，四个儿子里却出了两位蒙古大汗和伊利汗国的建立者。',
     'She never ruled in her own name, yet her four sons included two Great Khans and the founder of the Ilkhanate.'],
  a:[['丈夫拖雷去世后，大汗窝阔台安排她改嫁自己的儿子，她以要抚养四个孩子为由推辞，独自掌管拖雷家的封地与部众，并让四个儿子分别学习不同的语言文字。','After her husband Tolui died, the Great Khan Ögedei proposed she marry his son; she declined, saying she had four boys to raise, and ran the Tolui household\'s lands and troops herself, having each son learn a different language and script.'],
     ['她的封地在河北真定一带。当有人主张把当地农田改成牧场时，她主张保留耕作、按亩征税，并约束部下不得侵占民田。','Her appanage lay around Zhending in Hebei. When others proposed converting its fields to pasture, she kept them under the plough, taxed by the acre, and held her own followers back from seizing farmland.'],
     ['她信奉景教（基督教的聂斯脱里派），却出资一千锭银在布哈拉兴建伊斯兰经学院，同时也资助佛寺与道观。','A Nestorian Christian herself, she endowed an Islamic college in Bukhara with a thousand silver ingots, and also funded Buddhist and Daoist foundations.']],
  s:['1251 年由她与拔都推动的忽里勒台把大汗之位从窝阔台系转到拖雷系，此后蒙古帝国与元朝的统治者都出自她这一支。叙利亚史家巴尔·希伯来斯在《编年史》中写道：若女子中再有一人如她，则女子远胜于男子。元朝追尊她为显懿庄圣皇后。',
     'The assembly of 1251, which she and Batu engineered, moved the khanship from Ögedei\'s line to Tolui\'s; every later ruler of the empire and of Yuan China descended from her. The Syriac historian Bar Hebraeus wrote in his Chronography that if he were to see another woman like her, he would say the race of women far surpassed that of men. The Yuan court honoured her posthumously as Empress Xianyi Zhuangsheng.'] },
'黄公望': { g:'art', y:[1269,1354], c:'元', n:['黄公望','Huang Gongwang'],
  t:['元朝画家。他画的一卷山水后来被烧成两段,分在海峡两岸。',
     'A Yuan painter. The scroll he made was later burned in two, and the halves ended up on opposite sides of the Taiwan Strait.'],
  a:[['常熟人,做过小吏,四十多岁受上司的案子牵连坐过牢;出狱后不再做官,入了全真道,年过五十才专心学画,常在富春江一带看山。','Born at Changshu, he worked as a minor clerk and in his forties was jailed over his superior\'s case; released, he gave up office, joined the Quanzhen Daoists, took up painting seriously only past fifty, and spent his days looking at the hills along the Fuchun river.'],
     ['1347 年起为一位道士朋友画《富春山居图》,断断续续画了三四年,1350 年题上款。后人通常把他与吴镇、倪瓒、王蒙并称「元四家」。','From 1347 he painted Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains for a Daoist friend, on and off for three or four years, and inscribed it in 1350. Later ages usually group him with Wu Zhen, Ni Zan and Wang Meng as the Four Masters of the Yuan.'],
     ['1650 年,收藏它的吴洪裕临死前要把这卷画烧掉陪葬,家人从火里抢出,画已断成两截:前面一小段「剩山图」今在浙江省博物馆,后面长的一段「无用师卷」在台北故宫;2011 年两段在台北第一次合在一起展出。','In 1650 its owner Wu Hongyu, dying, ordered the scroll burned to go with him; the family snatched it from the fire, but it had already parted in two. The short front piece, the Remaining Mountain, is in the Zhejiang Provincial Museum; the long rear piece, the Wuyongshi scroll, is in the Palace Museum in Taipei. In 2011 the two were shown together in Taipei for the first time.']],
  s:['后世把他排在「元四家」之首,明清两代学山水的人多从他这一路入手;《富春山居图》被称作「画中兰亭」。乾隆皇帝把一卷仿本当成真迹,在上面题了五十多处字,真迹入宫反被判为假,上面只留下一段奉旨写的判语。',
     'Later ages placed him first among the Four Masters of the Yuan, and landscape painters of the Ming and Qing mostly began by studying his manner; Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains is called the Orchid Pavilion of painting. The Qianlong emperor mistook a copy for the original and wrote more than fifty inscriptions on it, while the real scroll, reaching the palace, was judged a fake and carries only one verdict written at his command.'] },
'八思巴': { g:'faith', y:[1235,1280], ca:1, c:'元', n:['八思巴','Drogön Chögyal Phagpa'],
  t:['忽必烈交给他一道题：造一套字，要能同时拼写蒙古语、汉语、藏语和梵语。',
     'Kublai set him a problem: invent one alphabet that could spell Mongolian, Chinese, Tibetan and Sanskrit alike.'],
  a:[['1269 年他造出一套四十一个字母的拼音文字（八思巴文），依藏文字母改制、自上而下竖写；同年忽必烈下诏定为官方文字，用于玺印、牌符与诏书。','In 1269 he produced an alphabet of forty-one letters, adapted from Tibetan and written vertically; that same year Kublai decreed it the official script of the Yuan, to be used on seals, passports and edicts.'],
     ['1253 年在六盘山见到忽必烈，1260 年受封国师，1270 年升为帝师；1264 年领总制院，管理全国佛教事务与吐蕃地区事务。','He met Kublai in the Liupan Mountains in 1253, was made State Preceptor in 1260 and Imperial Preceptor in 1270; from 1264 he headed the bureau overseeing Buddhist affairs across the empire and the administration of Tibet.'],
     ['他为皇太子真金撰写《彰所知论》，用一部书讲清佛教的世界图景与历代王统；1280 年圆寂于萨迦寺。','For the crown prince Jingim he wrote the Shes bya rab gsal, a single volume laying out the Buddhist picture of the world and its lines of kings; he died at Sakya monastery in 1280.']],
  s:['八思巴文在元朝灭亡后废弃不用，但用它拼写的元代碑刻、牌符和韵书《蒙古字韵》保留了当时汉语与蒙古语的实际读音，成为语言学家复原元代语音的一手材料。美国学者加里·莱德亚德等人提出，朝鲜谚文的部分字母形状可能受八思巴文启发，学界对此仍有争论。',
     'The script fell out of use when the Yuan fell, but the inscriptions, passports and rhyme book written in it preserve how Chinese and Mongolian were actually pronounced at the time, and remain primary evidence for linguists reconstructing that pronunciation. The American scholar Gari Ledyard and others have argued that some Korean Hangul letter shapes may have been inspired by it; the question is still debated.'] },
'落下闳': { g:'sci', y:[-156,-87], ca:1, c:'西汉', n:['落下闳','Luoxia Hong'],
  t:['春节是哪一天，用的还是他那部历法定下的规矩。',
     'The date of Chinese New Year still follows a rule set by the calendar he helped build.'],
  a:[['前 104 年他被汉武帝从巴郡阆中征召到长安，与邓平、唐都等人一起制定《太初历》，取代沿用已久的颛顼历。','In 104 BCE Emperor Wu summoned him from Langzhong in Sichuan to the capital, where he and colleagues drew up the Taichu calendar to replace the long-used Zhuanxu system.'],
     ['《太初历》把一年的开头从十月改到正月，并把二十四节气正式纳入历法用于置闰：没有「中气」的月份定为闰月——这条规则中国农历沿用至今。','The Taichu calendar moved the start of the year from the tenth month to the first, and brought the twenty-four solar terms into the reckoning of leap months: a month containing no major solar term becomes a leap month, a rule the Chinese lunar calendar still uses.'],
     ['他推算一个朔望月为 29 又 81 分之 43 日，约 29.5309 日，与今天的测值 29.5306 日只差约万分之三日；他还改制浑仪，用它实测星辰位置。','He computed the lunar month as 29 and 43/81 days, about 29.5309, within roughly three ten-thousandths of a day of the modern value of 29.5306; he also rebuilt the armillary sphere and used it to measure star positions.']],
  s:['《太初历》是中国现存有完整文字记载的最早历法，其岁首与置闰规则被此后历代历法继承，今天农历春节的日期仍由这套规则决定。国际天文学联合会批准将 16757 号小行星命名为「落下闳星」。',
     'The Taichu calendar is the earliest Chinese calendar whose full text survives; its choice of new year and its leap-month rule were carried forward by every later dynasty, and still fix the date of Spring Festival today. The International Astronomical Union approved the naming of asteroid 16757 as Luoxiahong.'] },
'班婕妤': { g:'art', y:[-48,2], ca:1, c:'西汉', n:['班婕妤','Consort Ban'],
  t:['皇帝请她同坐一辆车。她说：古画上和君王同车的，都是亡国之君身边的人。',
     'The emperor asked her to share his carriage. She answered that in the old paintings, only doomed kings ride beside a woman.'],
  a:[['汉成帝造了一辆能坐两人的车，请她同乘。她援引古画推辞：贤明的君主身边坐的是名臣，末代之君身边才是宠妃。太后听说后说，古有樊姬，今有班婕妤。','Emperor Cheng had a carriage built for two and invited her in. She refused, citing old paintings: wise rulers are shown with their great ministers beside them, and only the last rulers of fallen houses with a favourite. The empress dowager said of it: antiquity had Lady Fan, and now we have Consort Ban.'],
     ['赵飞燕姐妹得宠后，她被指控以巫术诅咒后宫；当面申辩之后，她主动请求离开成帝身边，到长信宫侍奉太后，此后再未回去。','After the Zhao sisters won the emperor\'s favour she was accused of cursing the palace by witchcraft; having answered the charge to his face, she asked to leave him and serve the dowager empress in the Changxin Palace, and never returned.'],
     ['《汉书·外戚传》全文著录了她的《自悼赋》——西汉女性作者的作品被正史整篇收录，极为少见。另有《怨歌行》（团扇诗）署她的名字流传，作者归属自刘勰《文心雕龙》起就被后人怀疑。','The History of Han records her Rhapsody of Self-Lament in full, a rare thing for a woman writer of the Western Han. A second poem, the Song of Resentment about a discarded round fan, also circulates under her name, though its authorship has been questioned since Liu Xie\'s Wenxin Diaolong.']],
  s:['「辞辇」一幕被画进传为顾恺之的《女史箴图》，现存唐摹本藏于大英博物馆，是该卷仅存九个场景之一。诗中入秋后被收起的团扇，成为此后中国诗歌反复使用的意象，王昌龄、刘禹锡等人都化用过。',
     'The carriage scene was painted into the Admonitions Scroll attributed to Gu Kaizhi; the surviving Tang copy is in the British Museum and the scene is one of its nine remaining panels. The image of the round fan put away when autumn comes became one of the most reused figures in later Chinese poetry, taken up by Wang Changling, Liu Yuxi and many others.'] },
'玄奘': { g:'faith', y:[602,664], ca:1, c:'唐', n:['玄奘','Xuanzang'],
  t:['《西游记》里他带着三个徒弟；真实的他是一个人偷越国境走的，当时朝廷禁止百姓出关。',
     'In Journey to the West he travels with three disciples. The real monk slipped across a closed border alone.'],
  a:[['629 年他在朝廷明令禁止百姓出境的情况下私自西行，经凉州、玉门关和莫贺延碛沙漠进入中亚，再翻越兴都库什山到印度。','In 629, when the court forbade ordinary people to leave the country, he set out west anyway, through Liangzhou, the Jade Gate and the Gashun Gobi into Central Asia, then over the Hindu Kush into India.'],
     ['在那烂陀寺随戒贤学习五年；643 年戒日王在曲女城主持辩论大会，据《大慈恩寺三藏法师传》记载，十八天中无人能驳倒他的立论。','He studied five years under Śīlabhadra at Nalanda; at the great debate held by King Harsha at Kanyakubja in 643, his biography records that for eighteen days no one could refute his thesis.'],
     ['645 年带回梵文经论 657 部，此后十九年主持译场，译出 75 部、1335 卷；他口述、弟子辩机笔录的《大唐西域记》记下了 138 个国家和城邦的方位、里程、物产与风俗。','He came home in 645 with 657 Sanskrit texts and spent nineteen years directing a translation bureau that produced 75 works in 1,335 scrolls; the Record of the Western Regions, dictated by him and written down by his disciple Bianji, describes 138 countries and city-states with their bearings, distances, products and customs.']],
  s:['19 世纪英国考古学家康宁汉等人正是依《大唐西域记》记下的方位与里程，重新找到并发掘了早已湮没的那烂陀寺、鹿野苑等遗址；那烂陀遗址 2016 年列入《世界遗产名录》。为存放他带回的经卷而建的大雁塔仍立于西安，2014 年作为「丝绸之路：长安—天山廊道路网」的组成部分列入世界遗产。',
     'In the nineteenth century Alexander Cunningham and other archaeologists used the bearings and distances in his Record to relocate and excavate long-lost sites including Nalanda and Sarnath; the Nalanda ruins were inscribed as World Heritage in 2016. The Giant Wild Goose Pagoda, built in Chang\'an to house the scriptures he brought back, still stands in Xi\'an and was inscribed in 2014 as part of the Silk Roads: Chang\'an–Tianshan Corridor.'] },
'上官婉儿': { g:'state', y:[664,710], c:'唐', n:['上官婉儿','Shangguan Wan\'er'],
  t:['她出生那年，祖父因为替皇帝起草废黜武则天的诏书被处死；十四岁那年，武则天当面出题考她。',
     'The year she was born, her grandfather was executed for drafting an edict to depose Wu Zetian. At fourteen, Wu Zetian set her a writing test in person.'],
  a:[['664 年祖父上官仪被杀，她随母亲没入掖庭为奴婢；武则天召见后当场出题，她提笔立成，此后掌管诏令。《旧唐书》说圣历年间以后，百司的表奏多交由她参决。','Her grandfather Shangguan Yi was put to death in 664 and she entered the palace workshops as a bondmaid with her mother. Summoned by Wu Zetian, she wrote to a set topic on the spot and was given charge of drafting edicts; the old History of Tang says that from the Shengli era on, memorials from the ministries were largely referred to her.'],
     ['唐中宗时她被封为昭容，奏请扩置昭文馆学士，把当时的文人召入宫中；朝廷赛诗时由她当场评定高下——据《唐诗纪事》记载，她在彩楼上逐张看卷，落选的稿子直接从楼上扔下来。','Under Emperor Zhongzong she was made Zhaorong and petitioned to expand the academy so that the age\'s writers were brought into the palace. At court poetry contests she judged on the spot: one Song collection records her reading the entries up on a decorated tower and dropping the rejected sheets over the side.'],
     ['据 2013 年出土的墓志，安乐公主请求立为「皇太女」时，她曾以死力争、服毒抗议；710 年唐隆政变中她被杀，睿宗后来恢复其昭容名位，谥号惠文。','According to the epitaph unearthed in 2013, when Princess Anle asked to be named heir apparent, she fought the proposal to the point of taking poison in protest. She was killed in the coup of 710; Emperor Ruizong later restored her rank and gave her the posthumous title Huiwen.']],
  s:['张说为她编的文集有二十卷，今已散佚，《全唐诗》存其诗三十二首。2013 年 9 月陕西咸阳发现她的墓，出土墓志一合、志文 982 字，是目前关于她生平最直接的实物证据；墓室在唐代即遭有组织的破坏，考古学者称之为「官方毁墓」。',
     'The twenty-volume collection of her writings edited by Zhang Yue is lost, and thirty-two of her poems survive in the Complete Tang Poems. In September 2013 her tomb was found near Xianyang in Shaanxi, with an epitaph of 982 characters that is now the most direct physical evidence of her life; the burial chamber had been systematically wrecked within the Tang period itself, in what archaeologists describe as an officially ordered destruction.'] },
'阿克巴': { g:'king', y:[1542,1605], r:[1556,1605], c:'莫卧儿帝国', n:['阿克巴','Akbar'],
  t:['13 岁被推上王位的少年皇帝,一辈子不识字——书都是别人念给他听的。',
     'Put on the throne at 13, and never learned to read — everything was read aloud to him.'],
  a:[['废掉向非穆斯林征收的人头税(吉兹亚)','Abolished the jizya, the tax on non-Muslims'],
     ['盖了一座辩论厅,请印度教、耆那教、祆教、基督教的学者来吵架,自己坐着听',
      'Built a debating hall and sat listening to Hindu, Jain, Zoroastrian and Christian scholars argue'],
     ['娶拉杰普特王公的女儿,再让这些王公当自己的将军','Married Rajput princesses — and made those Rajput princes his generals']],
  s:['印度史上最受后世称道的君主之一,在位 49 年。他定下的土地丈量税制和官阶制度,莫卧儿此后一百多年一直在用;今天印度和巴基斯坦的历史课本都把他列为宽容统治的代表。',
     'One of the most admired rulers in Indian history, on the throne for 49 years. The land-survey tax system and rank-based officialdom he set up ran for another century and a half, and both Indian and Pakistani textbooks today hold him up as the model of tolerant rule.'] },
'沙贾汗': { g:'king', y:[1592,1666], r:[1628,1658], c:'莫卧儿帝国', n:['沙贾汗','Shah Jahan'],
  t:['莫卧儿最会花钱的皇帝,留下了世界上最有名的一座坟。',
     'The Mughal who spent the most — and left behind the most famous tomb in the world.'],
  a:[['为难产去世的妻子慕塔芝·玛哈建泰姬陵,白色大理石,修了 22 年',
      'Built the Taj Mahal for his wife Mumtaz Mahal, who died in childbirth — white marble, 22 years'],
     ['把都城从阿格拉迁到德里,建红堡','Moved the capital from Agra to Delhi and built the Red Fort'],
     ['打造孔雀宝座,镶满宝石——后来被波斯人抢走了','Commissioned the jewelled Peacock Throne — later carried off by the Persians']],
  s:['莫卧儿建筑在他手上到了顶点:泰姬陵、德里红堡、贾玛清真寺都出自他在位的三十年。泰姬陵 1983 年列入世界遗产,是今天全世界最知名的建筑之一。',
     'Mughal architecture peaked in his thirty-year reign: the Taj Mahal, Delhi\'s Red Fort and the Jama Masjid all date from it. The Taj became a World Heritage Site in 1983 and is among the most recognised buildings on earth.'] },
'奥朗则布': { g:'king', y:[1618,1707], r:[1658,1707], c:'莫卧儿帝国', n:['奥朗则布','Aurangzeb'],
  t:['把帝国版图推到最大的那个皇帝,也是把帝国掏空的那个。',
     'The emperor who pushed the empire to its greatest extent — and hollowed it out doing so.'],
  a:[['杀掉三个兄弟、囚禁父亲,才坐上王位','Killed three brothers and imprisoned his father to take the throne'],
     ['1679 年恢复阿克巴废掉的人头税,拆毁部分印度教神庙','Reimposed the jizya in 1679 — the tax Akbar had abolished — and demolished some Hindu temples'],
     ['南下吞并德干的比贾布尔和戈尔康达,又跟马拉塔人打了 27 年','Annexed Bijapur and Golconda in the Deccan, then fought the Marathas for 27 years']],
  s:['莫卧儿版图最大的时期,南到今天的印度南端,治下人口约一亿五千万,是当时世界上最富的国家之一。他也是在位最久的莫卧儿皇帝(49 年)。后世史家多把帝国的衰落追溯到他这一朝的连年征战。',
     'The empire at its greatest extent, reaching the southern tip of India, with perhaps 150 million subjects and one of the largest economies in the world. He was also the longest-reigning Mughal, at 49 years. Historians generally trace the empire\'s decline to the endless wars of this reign.'] },
'秦始皇': { g:'king', y:[-259,-210], r:[-221,-210], c:'秦', n:['秦始皇','Qin Shi Huang'], w:'秦始皇',
  t:['第一个把"中国"这块地方捏成一个国家的人,也是第一个自称"皇帝"的人。',
     'The first man to weld China into a single state — and the first to call himself "emperor".'],
  a:[['前 221 年灭掉最后一个对手,十年之内吞并六国','Swallowed the last of his six rivals in 221 BCE, after ten years of war'],
     ['书同文、车同轨、统一度量衡——写法、车轮宽度、斤两尺寸全国一个标准',
      'One script, one axle width, one set of weights and measures for the whole country'],
     ['废掉分封,全国设郡县,官员由中央任免,不能世袭','Scrapped hereditary fiefs for centrally appointed commanderies and counties']],
  s:['中国第一个中央集权的统一王朝。他推行的郡县制、统一文字和度量衡被此后历代沿用两千年。留下的兵马俑 1987 年列入世界遗产,是 20 世纪最重大的考古发现之一。',
     'Founder of China\'s first centralised empire. The commandery system, the unified script and the standard weights and measures he imposed were kept by every later dynasty for two thousand years. His Terracotta Army, listed as World Heritage in 1987, is among the great archaeological finds of the twentieth century.'] },
'武则天': { g:'king', y:[624,705], r:[690,705], c:'唐', n:['武则天','Wu Zetian'],
  t:['中国历史上唯一一个自己当皇帝的女人。',
     'The only woman in Chinese history to rule as emperor in her own name.'],
  a:[['690 年称帝,改国号为"周",是唯一一个自己坐上龙椅的女性','Took the throne in 690 and renamed the dynasty "Zhou"'],
     ['大办科举、开殿试,提拔寒门出身的官员(狄仁杰就是她用的)',
      'Expanded the civil-service exams, invented the palace examination, and promoted men of humble birth — Di Renjie among them'],
     ['养了一批酷吏搞告密和罗织,清洗掉大批旧贵族','Kept a corps of cruel officials running informer networks that wiped out much of the old aristocracy']],
  s:['中国历史上唯一的女皇帝,前后掌权约半个世纪。她首创殿试与武举,把科举录取的规模扩大了数倍;唐朝的户口数在她当政期间增长了约六成。',
     'The only female emperor in Chinese history, in power for roughly half a century. She invented the palace examination and the military examination, multiplied the intake of the civil-service exams several times over, and saw registered households grow by about sixty per cent during her rule.'] },
'王安石': { g:'state', y:[1021,1086], c:'北宋', n:['王安石','Wang Anshi'],
  t:['中国历史上规模最大的一次经济改革,是他一个人推起来的。',
     'The largest economic reform in Chinese history was pushed through by one man.'],
  a:[['青苗法:青黄不接时官府低息借粮给农民,免得他们被高利贷吃掉',
      'The Green Sprouts loans: the state lent grain cheaply at the hungry season so farmers would not fall to loan sharks'],
     ['募役法:老百姓交钱免服劳役,官府拿钱雇人干','Hired-service: pay a tax instead of doing corvée labour, and the state hires workers'],
     ['保甲法:农村按户编队,农闲练兵,想省下养常备军的钱','Baojia militia: villages organised into units drilling in the off-season, to cut the cost of a standing army']],
  s:['熙宁变法是中国历史上规模最大的一次由中央推动的经济改革,十余项新法覆盖财政、土地、军事、教育,在全国同时铺开。他本人也是唐宋八大家之一。',
     'His Xining reforms were the largest centrally driven economic overhaul in Chinese history — a dozen measures covering finance, land, the army and education, rolled out nationwide at once. He also ranks among the Eight Masters of Tang and Song prose.'] },
'成吉思汗': { g:'war', y:[1162,1227], r:[1206,1227], c:'蒙古帝国', n:['成吉思汗','Genghis Khan'],
  t:['本名铁木真。他把互相仇杀了几百年的草原部落,拧成了一部战争机器。',
     'Born Temüjin. He took steppe tribes that had been killing each other for centuries and forged them into one war machine.'],
  a:[['打散原来的部落,按十进制重编成千户——你的长官不再是你的族长',
      'Broke up the tribes and re-sorted everyone into units of a thousand — your commander was no longer your clansman'],
     ['借畏兀儿字母造出蒙古文字,让命令可以写下来传出去','Adapted the Uyghur alphabet to write Mongol, so orders could travel in writing'],
     ['铺设驿站,信使换马不换人,一天能跑三四百里','Built the yam relay stations: couriers changed horses, not riders, and covered hundreds of li a day']],
  s:['他开创的蒙古帝国后来成了历史上疆域最大的陆上帝国:1227 年他去世那年已有约一千三百五十万平方公里,而最大的时候要再等两代人。他颁布的《大扎撒》是草原上第一部成文法,他下令创制的回鹘式蒙古文沿用至今。',
     'The empire he founded became the largest contiguous land empire in history: at his death in 1227 it already covered some 13.5 million square kilometres, and its greatest extent came two generations after him. His Great Yassa was the first written law code on the steppe, and the Uyghur-derived Mongol script he commissioned is still in use.'] },
'郑和': { g:'sail', y:[1371,1433], c:'明', n:['郑和','Zheng He'],
  t:['云南出身的回族太监,本姓马,率领过当时世界上最大的船队。',
     'A Muslim eunuch from Yunnan, born Ma — and commander of the largest fleet in the world.'],
  a:[['1405—1433 年七下西洋,船两百多艘、人两万七千余','Seven voyages between 1405 and 1433, with over 200 ships and 27,000 men'],
     ['最远到过东非的麻林(今肯尼亚)和红海边的吉达','Reached Malindi on the East African coast and Jeddah on the Red Sea'],
     ['带回长颈鹿当"麒麟"献给皇帝,朝野轰动','Brought back a giraffe, presented at court as the mythical qilin']],
  s:['世界航海史上的一串纪录:船队规模至今没有被超过(两百余艘、两万七千余人),出海比哥伦布早 87 年、比麦哲伦早 114 年,单程从南京直达东非。七次远航都不为占地,而是通商与册封。',
     'A string of records in the history of seafaring: a fleet never since matched in size (200-plus ships, over 27,000 men), sailing 87 years before Columbus and 114 before Magellan, on a route running from Nanjing all the way to East Africa. None of the seven voyages was for conquest — they were for trade and diplomacy.'] },
'凯撒': { g:'war', y:[-100,-44], c:'罗马共和国', n:['凯撒','Julius Caesar'], w:'尤利乌斯·凯撒',
  t:['他没当成皇帝,但他一死,罗马共和国也就没了。',
     'He never became emperor — but when he died, the Roman Republic died with him.'],
  a:[['前 58—前 50 年征服高卢(今天的法国一带),打了八年','Conquered Gaul — roughly modern France — over eight years from 58 BCE'],
     ['前 49 年带兵渡过卢比孔河,这是违法的,等于向元老院宣战',
      'Crossed the Rubicon with his army in 49 BCE — illegal, and a declaration of war on the Senate'],
     ['改历法,一年 365 天加闰年,这套儒略历用了一千六百年','Reformed the calendar: 365 days plus a leap year — the Julian calendar lasted 1,600 years']],
  s:['他制定的儒略历在欧洲通用了一千六百年,今天的公历仍以它为底子,七月(July)就是以他命名的。他写的《高卢战记》至今是拉丁语教学的标准课文。"凯撒"后来成了"皇帝"的代名词——德语 Kaiser、俄语沙皇都由它而来。',
     'His Julian calendar was Europe\'s for sixteen centuries and still underlies today\'s Gregorian one; July carries his name. His Gallic War remains a standard text for learning Latin. And "Caesar" itself became the word for emperor — German Kaiser, Russian Tsar.'] },
'奥古斯都': { g:'king', y:[-63,14], r:[-27,14], c:'罗马帝国', n:['奥古斯都','Augustus'],
  t:['凯撒的养子屋大维。他学乖了:壳子留着,权力全拿走。',
     'Caesar\'s heir Octavian. He learned the lesson: keep the shell, take all the power.'],
  a:[['前 31 年阿克提乌姆海战击败安东尼与克娄巴特拉,天下无对手',
      'Destroyed Antony and Cleopatra at Actium in 31 BCE, leaving no rival standing'],
     ['前 27 年元老院授他"奥古斯都"尊号,但他坚持只自称"第一公民"',
      'Took the title Augustus in 27 BCE — but insisted he was merely princeps, "first citizen"'],
     ['元老院、执政官、选举全保留,照常开会,只是人事和军队都归他',
      'Kept the Senate, the consuls and the elections running — while controlling appointments and the army']],
  s:['罗马帝国的第一位皇帝,在位 41 年,开启了约两百年的罗马和平。他任内建起常备军、消防队和帝国邮驿系统,并主持了罗马城的大规模重建。八月(August)以他命名。',
     'The first Roman emperor, 41 years on the throne, opening the two centuries known as the Pax Romana. He created a standing army, a fire brigade and an imperial postal system, and rebuilt much of the city itself. August carries his name.'] },
'拉美西斯二世': { g:'king', y:[-1303,-1213], r:[-1279,-1213], c:'新王国埃及', n:['拉美西斯二世','Ramesses II'],
  t:['在位 66 年,活了 90 多岁,埃及最爱给自己立雕像的法老。',
     'Sixty-six years on the throne, over ninety years alive, and no pharaoh ever built himself more statues.'],
  a:[['前 1274 年卡叠什战役跟赫梯人打了个平手,回国后把它宣传成大胜,刻满了神庙墙壁',
      'Fought the Hittites to a draw at Kadesh in 1274 BCE — then carved it on temple walls as a triumph'],
     ['前 1259 年跟赫梯签和约,这是人类现存最早的国际和平条约',
      'Signed a treaty with the Hittites in 1259 BCE — the earliest surviving international peace treaty'],
     ['在阿布辛贝的悬崖上凿出四座 20 米高的自己','Carved four twenty-metre statues of himself into the cliff at Abu Simbel']],
  s:['古埃及在位最久的法老之一(66 年),留下的神庙、雕像和铭文数量也是历代之最。他与赫梯的和约是现存最早的国际和平条约,复制品陈列在纽约联合国总部;阿布辛贝神庙 1979 年列入世界遗产。',
     'One of the longest-reigning pharaohs (66 years) and the one who left the most temples, statues and inscriptions. His treaty with the Hittites is the earliest surviving international peace treaty — a copy hangs at UN headquarters in New York — and Abu Simbel became World Heritage in 1979.'] },
'克娄巴特拉': { g:'king', y:[-69,-30], r:[-51,-30], c:'新王国埃及', n:['克娄巴特拉','Cleopatra VII'],
  t:['埃及最后一位法老,但她其实是希腊人——托勒密王朝是亚历山大部将的后代。',
     'Egypt\'s last pharaoh — and a Greek: the Ptolemies descended from one of Alexander\'s generals.'],
  a:[['托勒密王室统治埃及近三百年,她是头一个肯学埃及语的','Her family had ruled Egypt for nearly 300 years; she was the first of them to bother learning Egyptian'],
     ['先跟凯撒结盟并生下一子,凯撒死后改跟安东尼结盟','Allied with Caesar and bore his son; after his murder, allied with Antony'],
     ['前 31 年阿克提乌姆战败,次年自杀','Lost at Actium in 31 BCE and killed herself the next year']],
  s:['古埃及最后一位法老,她死后埃及成为罗马行省,延续三千年的法老时代就此终结。她通晓多种语言,是托勒密王朝三百年里唯一学过埃及语的统治者。',
     'The last pharaoh of Egypt; after her death the country became a Roman province and three thousand years of pharaonic rule ended. She spoke several languages and was the only ruler in three centuries of Ptolemies to learn Egyptian.'] },
'阿育王': { g:'king', y:[-304,-232], r:[-268,-232], c:'孔雀王朝', n:['阿育王','Ashoka'],
  t:['他打赢了一场仗,然后决定再也不打仗了。',
     'He won a war, and then decided never to fight another.'],
  a:[['前 261 年征服羯陵伽,据他自己的敕令记载死伤流离数十万','Conquered Kalinga in 261 BCE — by his own edicts, with hundreds of thousands dead or displaced'],
     ['战后皈依佛教,在全国的岩壁和石柱上刻下敕令,讲的不是武功而是宽容与不杀生',
      'Turned to Buddhism and had edicts carved on rocks and pillars across India — not of conquest, but of tolerance and non-violence'],
     ['派传教团去斯里兰卡、中亚和希腊化诸国','Sent missions to Sri Lanka, Central Asia and the Hellenistic kingdoms']],
  s:['印度本土王朝里疆域最大的一个。他的石柱与摩崖敕令是印度现存最早的成体系文字记录之一,也是世界上最早由国家公开颁布的宽容与非暴力宣言。今天印度国徽的四头狮子和国旗中央的法轮都取自他的石柱。',
     'Ruler of the largest empire ever built by an Indian dynasty. His pillar and rock edicts are among the earliest systematic written records in India, and the earliest public state declaration of tolerance and non-violence anywhere. India\'s state emblem takes its four lions, and its flag its wheel, straight from his pillars.'] },
'亚里士多德': { g:'mind', y:[-384,-322], c:'古希腊', n:['亚里士多德','Aristotle'],
  t:['柏拉图的学生,亚历山大大帝的老师。他发明的是"分门别类地研究一切"这件事本身。',
     'Plato\'s student and Alexander\'s tutor. What he really invented was the idea of studying everything, systematically.'],
  a:[['把推理写成规则(三段论),逻辑学从此是一门学问','Turned reasoning into rules — the syllogism — and made logic a subject'],
     ['解剖、观察、给几百种动物分类,是最早认真做生物学的人','Dissected, observed and classified hundreds of animals — the first serious biologist'],
     ['写《诗学》《政治学》《伦理学》,连"悲剧该怎么写""国家有几种"都要分类',
      'Wrote the Poetics, Politics and Ethics — classifying even how tragedies should be built and how many kinds of state there are']],
  s:['西方最早对知识做系统分类的人:逻辑学、物理学、生物学、伦理学、政治学、诗学,这些学科的名字大多出自他的著作。他对约五百种动物的观察记录,此后两千年一直是生物学的基础文献。中世纪欧洲提到"那位哲学家",不用加名字就知道是他。',
     'The first in the West to sort knowledge into systems: logic, physics, biology, ethics, politics, poetics — most of those subject names come from his books. His observations of some five hundred animal species stayed the foundation of biology for two thousand years. In medieval Europe, "the Philosopher" needed no further identification.'] },
'花剌子米': { g:'sci', y:[780,850], c:'阿拉伯哈里发', n:['花剌子米','al-Khwarizmi'],
  t:['你今天说的"代数"和"算法",两个词都是从他身上来的。',
     'Two words you use today — algebra and algorithm — both come from this one man.'],
  a:[['在巴格达的智慧宫写《还原与对消计算书》,书名里的 al-jabr 就是 algebra(代数)',
      'At Baghdad\'s House of Wisdom he wrote the Kitab al-jabr — and al-jabr became "algebra"'],
     ['写书介绍印度传来的十个数字(包括零),让它经由阿拉伯世界传进欧洲',
      'Wrote the book that carried the Indian numerals — zero included — through the Arab world into Europe'],
     ['他名字的拉丁写法 Algoritmi,后来变成了 algorithm(算法)','His name latinised as Algoritmi, which became "algorithm"']],
  s:['代数(algebra)与算法(algorithm)两个词都源自他。他的著作是欧洲认识印度-阿拉伯数字的主要途径,12 世纪译成拉丁文后成为欧洲大学的数学教材,一直用到 16 世纪。',
     'Both "algebra" and "algorithm" come from him. His books were Europe\'s main route to the Indo-Arabic numerals; translated into Latin in the twelfth century, they served as university mathematics textbooks into the sixteenth.'] },
'武丁': { g:'king', y:[-1250,-1192], yk:'r', c:'商', n:['武丁','Wu Ding'],
  t:['商朝最有作为的王,在位约六十年。今天出土的甲骨,大半出自他这一朝。',
     'The most consequential Shang king, on the throne some sixty years. Most oracle bones ever unearthed date from his reign.'],
  a:[['把商的势力从中原推到今天的陕西、山西、山东','Pushed Shang power out to what is now Shaanxi, Shanxi and Shandong'],
     ['凡事必卜,把占卜的问与答刻在龟甲兽骨上','Divined before every decision, and had question and answer carved on turtle shell and ox bone'],
     ['破格提拔奴隶出身的傅说做宰相','Raised Fu Yue, a man born a slave, to chief minister']],
  s:['甲骨文让商朝从传说变成了信史——1899 年甲骨被发现之前,商是否真实存在在学界仍有争论。殷墟 2006 年列入世界遗产。',
     'Those oracle bones turned the Shang from legend into documented history; before their discovery in 1899, scholars still debated whether the dynasty had existed at all. Yinxu became a World Heritage Site in 2006.'] },
'妇好': { g:'war', y:[-1250,-1200], yk:'a', ca:1, c:'商', n:['妇好','Fu Hao'],
  t:['武丁的王后,也是中国有文字记载的第一位女性统帅。',
     'Consort of Wu Ding, and the first woman commander recorded in Chinese writing.'],
  a:[['甲骨记载她率一万三千人征伐羌方,是商朝已知规模最大的一次出征','Oracle bones record her leading 13,000 men against the Qiang — the largest Shang campaign known'],
     ['主持国家祭祀,是商王朝的高级祭司','Presided over state sacrifices as a senior priest of the realm'],
     ['拥有自己的封地和军队','Held her own fief and her own troops']],
  s:['1976 年她的墓在殷墟被完整发掘,是唯一一座从未被盗的商代王室墓,出土器物一千九百余件。她的存在有甲骨文与实物双重证据,这在三千多年前的女性中极为罕见。',
     'Her tomb, excavated intact at Yinxu in 1976, is the only unlooted Shang royal burial ever found — over 1,900 objects. She is attested by both inscription and artefact, a double record almost unheard of for a woman of 3,000 years ago.'] },
'周武王': { g:'king', y:[-1046,-1043], yk:'r', c:'西周', n:['周武王','King Wu of Zhou'],
  t:['灭商建周的人。牧野一战,商朝的天下一天之内易主。',
     'He destroyed the Shang and founded the Zhou. At Muye, an empire changed hands in a single day.'],
  a:[['前 1046 年牧野之战击败商纣王,商朝灭亡','Defeated the last Shang king at Muye in 1046 BCE'],
     ['分封诸侯,把土地和人民封给亲族与功臣','Parcelled out land and people to kinsmen and allies as hereditary lords'],
     ['定都镐京(今西安附近)','Set his capital at Haojing, near modern Xi\'an']],
  s:['牧野之战的年份是夏商周断代工程给出的关键坐标,中国有确切纪年的历史大致从这里往后连续。他确立的分封制支撑了周朝约八百年,是中国历时最长的王朝。',
     'The date of Muye is the anchor point of modern Chinese chronology — reliable year-by-year dating runs forward from roughly here. The feudal order he set up carried the Zhou for some eight centuries, the longest-lasting dynasty in Chinese history.'] },
'周公': { g:'state', y:[-1046,-1035], yk:'a', ca:1, c:'西周', n:['周公','the Duke of Zhou'],
  t:['武王的弟弟。哥哥死后他摄政七年,把周朝的规矩定下来,然后还政给侄子。',
     'King Wu\'s brother. He governed as regent for seven years, laid down the rules of the Zhou order — and then handed power back to his nephew.'],
  a:[['平定管叔、蔡叔联合商朝遗民的叛乱,东征三年','Put down the revolt of his own brothers allied with Shang remnants, campaigning east for three years'],
     ['营建洛邑(今洛阳)作为东都,控制东方','Built Luoyi — modern Luoyang — as an eastern capital to hold the east'],
     ['制礼作乐:定下宗法、分封、祭祀、婚丧的整套制度','Codified ritual and music: lineage law, enfeoffment, sacrifice, marriage and mourning as one system']],
  s:['孔子一生最推崇的人就是他,《论语》里叹"久矣吾不复梦见周公"。他确立的宗法与礼制被儒家奉为理想政治的样板,此后两千多年一直是中国政治话语的参照系。',
     'He was Confucius\' great model — the Analects records the old man sighing that he no longer dreamt of the Duke of Zhou. The ritual and lineage order he set became Confucianism\'s picture of ideal government, and a reference point in Chinese political language for two thousand years.'] },
'孔子': { g:'mind', y:[-551,-479], c:'春秋', n:['孔子','Confucius'],
  t:['中国历史上第一个私人办学的老师,教出三千弟子。',
     'The first private teacher in Chinese history, with three thousand students.'],
  a:[['打破"学在官府",提出有教无类——平民也能读书','Broke the state monopoly on schooling: teach anyone, regardless of birth'],
     ['周游列国十四年推销自己的政治主张,没有一个国君采纳','Spent fourteen years touring the states selling his politics; not one ruler bought it'],
     ['整理《诗》《书》《礼》《易》《春秋》,弟子把他的话记成《论语》','Edited the classics of poetry, documents, ritual, change and annals; his students compiled his sayings as the Analects']],
  s:['儒家自汉武帝起成为中国官方意识形态,延续两千年,并深入朝鲜、日本、越南。曲阜的孔庙、孔林、孔府 1994 年列入世界遗产;他的诞辰是今天中国台湾的教师节。',
     'From the Han onward Confucianism was China\'s official doctrine for two thousand years, and spread through Korea, Japan and Vietnam. His temple, cemetery and family mansion at Qufu became World Heritage in 1994, and his birthday is Teachers\' Day in Taiwan, China.'] },
'老子': { g:'mind', y:[-571,-471], ca:1, c:'春秋', n:['老子','Laozi'],
  t:['道家的创始人。生平几乎无可考,连他是不是一个人都有争论。',
     'Founder of Daoism — and so poorly documented that scholars still argue whether he was one person.'],
  a:[['相传做过周朝的守藏史,即管理王室藏书的官','Said to have kept the Zhou royal archives'],
     ['留下五千字的《道德经》,讲"道法自然""无为而治"','Left the five-thousand-character Daodejing: the Way follows nature; govern by not interfering'],
     ['相传孔子曾向他问礼','Confucius, by tradition, once came to him with questions about ritual']],
  s:['《道德经》是被译成外文最多的中国典籍,译本总数在全世界所有著作中仅次于《圣经》。道家与儒家构成中国思想的两条主线——一条管入世,一条管出世。',
     'The Daodejing is the most translated Chinese book ever written, and by some counts the second most translated book in the world after the Bible. Daoism and Confucianism became the two poles of Chinese thought: one for engaging the world, one for stepping out of it.'] },
'商鞅': { g:'state', y:[-390,-338], ca:1, c:'战国', n:['商鞅','Shang Yang'],
  t:['秦国变法的设计者。他把一个西陲弱国改造成了战争机器,自己最后死于那套法。',
     'The architect of Qin\'s reforms. He turned a weak frontier state into a war machine — and was executed under his own laws.'],
  a:[['废井田、开阡陌,土地可以买卖','Abolished the old field system and made land private and saleable'],
     ['军功爵制:斩敌首级换爵位,贵族不打仗就没有特权','Rank by battlefield merit: heads taken bought titles, and nobles who did not fight lost their privileges'],
     ['编户齐民、什伍连坐、统一度量衡','Registered every household, made neighbours liable for each other\'s crimes, standardised weights and measures']],
  s:['秦国自此由弱转强,一百三十余年后由秦始皇完成统一。他确立的编户与军功授爵是中国中央集权官僚国家的雏形,"徙木立信"的典故也出自变法之初。',
     'Qin rose from weakness on these laws and, 130 years later, unified China. His household registers and merit ranks were the prototype of the centralised bureaucratic state.'] },
'屈原': { g:'art', y:[-340,-278], ca:1, c:'战国', n:['屈原','Qu Yuan'],
  t:['中国第一位留下姓名的诗人。在他之前,《诗经》里的作品都不知作者是谁。',
     'The first Chinese poet known by name. Everything before him — the whole Book of Songs — is anonymous.'],
  a:[['楚国贵族与大臣,主张联齐抗秦,被政敌排挤流放','A Chu nobleman and minister who argued for allying with Qi against Qin, and was driven into exile for it'],
     ['写《离骚》《九歌》《天问》,开创"楚辞"这一文体','Wrote the Li Sao, Nine Songs and Heavenly Questions, creating the Chu ci form'],
     ['前 278 年秦军攻破楚都郢,他投汨罗江','Drowned himself in the Miluo River in 278 BCE, when Qin armies took the Chu capital']],
  s:['端午节的龙舟与粽子习俗与他有关,这个节日通行于中国、韩国、越南、新加坡等地,2009 年列入联合国非物质文化遗产。中国诗歌从他开始有了个人抒情——《诗经》是集体的声音,《离骚》是一个人的。',
     'The Dragon Boat Festival — races and rice dumplings — is tied to his death, and is kept from China to Korea, Vietnam and Singapore; UNESCO listed it in 2009. With him Chinese poetry acquired a first person: the Book of Songs speaks for a community, the Li Sao for one man.'] },
'李斯': { g:'state', y:[-284,-208], ca:1, c:'秦', n:['李斯','Li Si'],
  t:['秦始皇的丞相,统一制度的实际执行者。',
     'Qin Shi Huang\'s chancellor, and the man who actually carried out the unification of institutions.'],
  a:[['上《谏逐客书》劝秦王留下外来人才,自己因此得以留下','Talked the king out of expelling all foreign-born officials — himself included'],
     ['主持统一文字,把小篆定为全国标准字体','Ran the unification of the script, making the small seal form the national standard'],
     ['建议废分封、行郡县,也建议焚书','Urged replacing fiefs with centrally run counties — and also urged the burning of books']],
  s:['小篆是中国文字第一次由国家规定标准写法,汉字形体自此稳定。秦以后两千年,各地方言差异极大却始终能靠同一套文字沟通,源头在这里。他本人在秦始皇死后被赵高构陷,腰斩于咸阳。',
     'The seal script was the first state-mandated standard form of Chinese writing, and it stabilised the characters for good. That is why two thousand years of mutually unintelligible dialects could still share one written language. He himself was framed after Qin Shi Huang\'s death and cut in half at the waist.'] },
'刘邦': { g:'king', y:[-256,-195], r:[-202,-195], c:'西汉', n:['刘邦','Liu Bang'],
  t:['从亭长到皇帝。中国历史上第一个平民出身的开国之君。',
     'From village constable to emperor — the first commoner in Chinese history to found a dynasty.'],
  a:[['前 206 年入咸阳,约法三章:杀人者死,伤人及盗抵罪','Entered Xianyang in 206 BCE with three laws only: murder pays with life, injury and theft with punishment'],
     ['楚汉相争四年,前 202 年垓下击败项羽','Fought Xiang Yu for four years and destroyed him at Gaixia in 202 BCE'],
     ['建汉,定都长安,郡县与封国并行','Founded the Han at Chang\'an, running counties and vassal kingdoms side by side']],
  s:['在他之前,天下基本是贵族的。他证明了平民可以当皇帝,这在中国是第一次,也成了此后每次农民起义的心理依据。汉朝延续四百余年,"汉"从此成为民族与文字的名字。',
     'Before him, rule belonged to the well-born. He proved a commoner could take the throne — a first, and the psychological warrant for every peasant rising afterwards. The Han lasted four centuries, and gave its name to the people and the script.'] },
'汉武帝': { g:'king', y:[-156,-87], r:[-141,-87], c:'西汉', n:['汉武帝','Emperor Wu of Han'],
  t:['在位 54 年,把汉朝从守成推向扩张。',
     'Fifty-four years on the throne, turning the Han from a defensive power into an expanding one.'],
  a:[['派卫青、霍去病数次北击匈奴,夺取河西走廊','Sent Wei Qing and Huo Qubing north against the Xiongnu and took the Hexi Corridor'],
     ['罢黜百家、独尊儒术,设太学','Made Confucianism the sole state doctrine and founded the imperial academy'],
     ['盐铁官营,统一铸五铢钱,派张骞出使西域','Nationalised salt and iron, minted a single national coin, and sent Zhang Qian west']],
  s:['汉朝疆域在他手上达到最大。河西四郡的设立打通了通往中亚的通道,这条路后来被称作丝绸之路。独尊儒术确立了此后两千年中国官方的意识形态;五铢钱一直用到唐初,是中国流通最久的钱币之一。',
     'The Han reached its greatest extent under him. The four Hexi commanderies opened the corridor to Central Asia that later became the Silk Road; state Confucianism fixed China\'s official doctrine for two millennia; and his five-zhu coin stayed in circulation until the Tang.'] },
'张骞': { g:'sail', y:[-164,-114], ca:1, c:'西汉', n:['张骞','Zhang Qian'],
  t:['中国第一个走到中亚又活着回来的人。出使途中他被匈奴扣了十年。',
     'The first Chinese to reach Central Asia and come back alive — after ten years as a Xiongnu captive on the way.'],
  a:[['前 138 年出使大月氏,途中被匈奴俘虏,扣留十余年才逃脱','Set out for the Yuezhi in 138 BCE, was captured by the Xiongnu and held for over a decade before escaping'],
     ['前 126 年返回长安:一百多人出发,回来两个','Returned to Chang\'an in 126 BCE — of more than a hundred who left, two came back'],
     ['前 119 年再次出使,通乌孙、大宛、康居、安息','Went out again in 119 BCE, opening contact with the Wusun, Ferghana, Sogdiana and Parthia']],
  s:['他带回的是中国对中亚的第一份实地记录,《史记》称之为"凿空"——凿通空白。此后葡萄、苜蓿、石榴、胡桃传入中原,丝绸西传,丝绸之路的官方通道由此打开。',
     'What he brought back was China\'s first eyewitness account of Central Asia; the Records of the Grand Historian calls it "chiseling open the void". Grapes, alfalfa, pomegranates and walnuts came east, silk went west, and the Silk Road had its official opening.'] },
'司马迁': { g:'mind', y:[-145,-86], ca:1, c:'西汉', n:['司马迁','Sima Qian'],
  t:['因为替一个战败投降的将军说了句公道话,他被处以宫刑,忍辱写完了《史记》。',
     'He spoke up for a general who had surrendered, was castrated for it, and lived on to finish his history.'],
  a:[['二十岁起游历全国,实地考察史迹与传说','From the age of twenty he travelled the country checking sites and stories on the ground'],
     ['为投降匈奴的李陵辩护,触怒汉武帝,受宫刑','Defended Li Ling, who had surrendered to the Xiongnu, and was castrated by imperial order'],
     ['用十三年写成《史记》,一百三十篇、五十二万字,从黄帝写到当朝','Spent thirteen years on the Shiji: 130 chapters, 520,000 characters, from the Yellow Emperor to his own emperor']],
  s:['《史记》是中国第一部纪传体通史,此后两千年的二十余部正史全部沿用他创立的体例。他写当朝皇帝也不避讳,鲁迅评为"史家之绝唱,无韵之离骚"。',
     'The Shiji was China\'s first comprehensive history organised around lives, and every one of the twenty-odd dynastic histories after it copied his structure. He wrote about his own emperor without flattery. Lu Xun called it "the historian\'s swan song, a Li Sao without rhyme".'] },
'光武帝': { g:'king', y:[-5,57], r:[25,57], c:'东汉', n:['光武帝','Emperor Guangwu'],
  t:['刘邦的九世孙。西汉亡了十几年后,他把汉朝重新立了起来。',
     'A ninth-generation descendant of Liu Bang, who rebuilt the Han a dozen years after it fell.'],
  a:[['23 年昆阳之战以少胜多,击溃王莽主力','Shattered Wang Mang\'s main army against long odds at Kunyang in 23 CE'],
     ['25 年称帝,定都洛阳,史称东汉','Took the throne in 25 and moved the capital to Luoyang — the Eastern Han'],
     ['多次下诏释放奴婢,精简官吏,清查土地人口','Freed slaves by repeated edict, cut the bureaucracy, and audited land and population']],
  s:['中国历史上少见的中兴成功案例:一个已经灭亡的王朝被同姓宗室重建,又延续了近二百年。他定都洛阳,此后洛阳与长安并为中国最重要的两座都城。',
     'One of the few genuine restorations in Chinese history — a dead dynasty rebuilt by a distant kinsman and given another two centuries. His choice of Luoyang made it, with Chang\'an, one of the two great capitals of imperial China.'] },
'班超': { g:'war', y:[32,102], c:'东汉', n:['班超','Ban Chao'],
  t:['"投笔从戎"的原型。他带三十六个人出使西域,在那里待了三十一年。',
     'The original scholar who threw down his brush for a sword. He went west with thirty-six men and stayed thirty-one years.'],
  a:[['73 年夜袭鄯善的匈奴使团,留下"不入虎穴,焉得虎子"','Raided the Xiongnu envoys at Shanshan by night in 73, saying: enter no tiger\'s den, catch no tiger cub'],
     ['先后使西域五十余国归附汉朝','Brought more than fifty states of the Western Regions over to the Han'],
     ['91 年任西域都护,派甘英出使大秦(罗马),抵波斯湾折返','As Protector-General he sent Gan Ying toward Rome in 97; Gan turned back at the Persian Gulf']],
  s:['他以极小的兵力维持了汉朝对西域三十年的控制,丝绸之路在这期间保持畅通。甘英西行是中国有记载的第一次尝试直接接触罗马帝国。',
     'With almost no troops he held the Western Regions for thirty years and kept the Silk Road open. Gan Ying\'s journey was the first recorded Chinese attempt to reach the Roman Empire directly.'] },
'蔡伦': { g:'sci', y:[63,121], ca:1, c:'东汉', n:['蔡伦','Cai Lun'],
  t:['他不是发明纸的人,但他是让纸变便宜的那个人。',
     'He did not invent paper. He made it cheap.'],
  a:[['105 年改进造纸术,用树皮、麻头、破布、旧渔网做原料','Reworked papermaking in 105 using bark, hemp waste, rags and old fishing nets'],
     ['原料从昂贵的丝絮换成废料,成本降了一个数量级','Swapped costly silk floss for refuse, cutting the price by an order of magnitude'],
     ['汉和帝下令推广,时称"蔡侯纸"','The emperor ordered it spread nationwide; people called it "Marquis Cai\'s paper"']],
  s:['纸取代竹简与绢帛,书写材料的成本大幅下降,知识的复制第一次变得便宜。造纸术 8 世纪经中亚传入阿拉伯世界,12 世纪传入欧洲。麦克·哈特的《影响人类历史进程的一百名人》把他排在第七位。',
     'Paper displaced bamboo strips and silk, and copying knowledge became cheap for the first time. The technique reached the Arab world through Central Asia in the eighth century and Europe in the twelfth. Michael Hart\'s ranking of the hundred most influential people places him seventh.'] },
'张衡': { g:'sci', y:[78,139], c:'东汉', n:['张衡','Zhang Heng'],
  t:['天文学家、数学家,同时是当时最好的辞赋作家之一。',
     'Astronomer, mathematician — and one of the finest prose-poets of his age.'],
  a:[['132 年造候风地动仪,是世界上最早的地震探测仪器','Built the first seismoscope known anywhere, in 132'],
     ['造水运浑天仪,用水力驱动演示天体运行','Built a water-driven armillary sphere that turned with the heavens'],
     ['写《灵宪》解释月食成因,算出圆周率在 3.1466 与 3.1622 之间','Explained lunar eclipses in the Ling Xian, and bracketed pi between 3.1466 and 3.1622']],
  s:['他对月食的解释(月亮进入地影)在当时属世界领先。《后汉书》记载地动仪曾测出洛阳无感的陇西地震。月球背面有一座环形山以他命名,小行星 1802 号也是。',
     'His account of eclipses — the moon entering the earth\'s shadow — was ahead of anyone else at the time. The histories record his seismoscope detecting a quake in Gansu that no one in Luoyang had felt. A crater on the far side of the moon and asteroid 1802 both carry his name.'] },
'曹操': { g:'war', y:[155,220], c:'三国', n:['曹操','Cao Cao'],
  t:['挟天子以令诸侯的那个人。北方是他统一的,皇帝是他儿子当的。',
     'The man who held the emperor and gave the orders. He unified the north; his son took the title.'],
  a:[['200 年官渡之战以少胜多击败袁绍,统一北方','Beat Yuan Shao against the odds at Guandu in 200 and took the whole north'],
     ['208 年赤壁大败,三分天下的格局就此定下','Lost catastrophically at Red Cliffs in 208, and the three-way split was set'],
     ['推行屯田制,让士兵与流民开荒种地,解决军粮','Set soldiers and refugees to farming state land, solving the army\'s grain problem']],
  s:['他统一北方结束了中原数十年战乱,屯田制被此后历代沿用。他也是建安文学的核心,《短歌行》《观沧海》至今是中学课本篇目。《三国演义》把他写成奸雄,正史里他是政治家、军事家兼诗人。',
     'Unifying the north ended decades of war, and his military-farm system was copied by later dynasties. He was also the centre of the Jian\'an literary circle; two of his poems are still school texts. The novel made him the great villain; the histories record a statesman, a general and a poet.'] },
'刘备': { g:'king', y:[161,223], r:[221,223], c:'三国', n:['刘备','Liu Bei'],
  t:['卖草鞋出身,自称汉室宗亲,最后在西南建了个国。',
     'A straw-sandal seller who claimed Han royal blood and ended up founding a kingdom in the southwest.'],
  a:[['三顾茅庐请出诸葛亮,定下先取荆州、益州的战略','Went three times to Zhuge Liang\'s hut, and came away with a plan: take Jing province, then Yi'],
     ['208 年联合孙权,在赤壁击败曹操','Allied with Sun Quan and beat Cao Cao at Red Cliffs in 208'],
     ['221 年在成都称帝,国号仍称汉,史称蜀汉','Declared himself emperor at Chengdu in 221, keeping the name Han']],
  s:['蜀汉是三国里最弱的一方,只据一州之地,却撑了四十二年。他与诸葛亮的君臣关系被后世当作理想范本,"三顾茅庐""白帝城托孤"都成了通用典故。',
     'Shu was the weakest of the three, holding a single province, and it lasted forty-two years. His partnership with Zhuge Liang became the model of ruler and minister, and two scenes from it entered the language.'] },
'孙权': { g:'king', y:[182,252], r:[229,252], c:'三国', n:['孙权','Sun Quan'],
  t:['三国里在位最久的君主,守住了江东五十年。',
     'The longest-ruling of the Three Kingdoms sovereigns, holding the lower Yangtze for half a century.'],
  a:[['208 年决意联刘抗曹,赤壁一战奠定三分','Chose alliance with Liu Bei in 208; Red Cliffs settled the three-way division'],
     ['219 年袭取荆州,擒杀关羽','Seized Jing province in 219 and killed Guan Yu'],
     ['230 年派卫温、诸葛直率万人船队到夷洲(一般认为即今台湾)','Sent a fleet of ten thousand men to Yizhou in 230 — generally identified as Taiwan']],
  s:['他把江南从边缘地带经营成独立的经济与政治中心,建业(今南京)自此成为南方历代王朝的首都。230 年的夷洲之行是大陆与台湾有明确文献记载的最早接触。',
     'He turned the lower Yangtze from a periphery into a political and economic centre in its own right; his capital Jianye — modern Nanjing — served southern dynasties for centuries. The 230 voyage is the earliest documented contact between the mainland and Taiwan.'] },
'诸葛亮': { g:'state', y:[181,234], c:'三国', n:['诸葛亮','Zhuge Liang'],
  t:['中国历史上最有名的丞相,以"鞠躬尽瘁,死而后已"八个字被记住。',
     'The most famous chancellor in Chinese history, remembered for eight characters: give everything, until death.'],
  a:[['隆中对提出跨有荆益、联吴抗曹的长期战略','Laid out a long strategy in the Longzhong plan: hold Jing and Yi, ally with Wu against Cao'],
     ['主政蜀汉十一年,赏罚必信,史称"吏不容奸"','Ran Shu for eleven years so strictly that, the history says, no official dared be corrupt'],
     ['五次北伐,234 年病死在五丈原军中','Launched five northern campaigns and died in camp at Wuzhangyuan in 234']],
  s:['他是中国传统里"忠"与"智"的化身,《出师表》至今是中学课本篇目。在一个人口仅百万的政权里维持了十余年的北伐,治理能力在正史中评价极高。成都武侯祠已存续一千七百余年。',
     'He became the embodiment of loyalty and cleverness in Chinese tradition, and his memorial to the throne is still memorised in schools. Sustaining a decade of offensives from a state of barely a million people earned him the highest marks the histories give an administrator. His shrine in Chengdu has stood for 1,700 years.'] },
'司马炎': { g:'king', y:[236,290], r:[266,290], c:'西晋', n:['司马炎','Sima Yan'],
  t:['结束三国分裂的人,也是把这份统一迅速葬送的人。',
     'He ended the Three Kingdoms — and then threw the unification away.'],
  a:[['266 年代魏称帝,建立晋朝','Took the throne from Wei in 266 and founded the Jin'],
     ['280 年灭吴,结束近百年分裂','Destroyed Wu in 280, ending nearly a century of division'],
     ['大封宗室为王并授以兵权,推行占田制','Made his kinsmen kings with armies of their own, and issued a new land-allotment law']],
  s:['他完成的统一只维持了三十六年。宗室掌兵直接引发他死后的八王之乱,继而是五胡内迁与永嘉之乱——中国由此进入近三百年分裂,是历史上最长的一次。',
     'His unified empire lasted thirty-six years. Arming his relatives produced the War of the Eight Princes after his death, then the northern migrations and the sack of Luoyang — and China entered the longest period of division in its history, nearly three centuries.'] },
'王导': { g:'state', y:[276,339], c:'东晋·十六国', n:['王导','Wang Dao'],
  t:['东晋的实际创建者。当时人说"王与马,共天下"。',
     'The real founder of the Eastern Jin. People said the Wangs and the Simas shared the empire.'],
  a:[['劝司马睿南渡建康(今南京),为南迁的晋室找到落脚点','Persuaded the prince to cross south to Jiankang — modern Nanjing — and gave the exiled court a base'],
     ['拉拢江南本地大族与北方南迁士族,让两边合作而非火并','Brokered cooperation between southern native clans and the northern refugee gentry, instead of civil war'],
     ['历仕元帝、明帝、成帝三朝,主政二十余年','Served three emperors and led the government for over twenty years']],
  s:['中国政治与文化中心第一次大规模南移就在这一朝。他促成的南北士族共治模式,使江南在此后三百年成为汉文化的主要承载地,长江下游的大规模开发也从此开始。',
     'This was the first great southward shift of China\'s political and cultural centre. The power-sharing he engineered made the lower Yangtze the main carrier of Han culture for three centuries, and began its large-scale development.'] },
'谢安': { g:'state', y:[320,385], c:'东晋·十六国', n:['谢安','Xie An'],
  t:['隐居到四十多岁才出来做官,一战定国之后又退了回去。',
     'He stayed in retirement until his forties, saved the state in one battle, and withdrew again.'],
  a:[['隐居会稽东山二十年,四十余岁才出仕,"东山再起"由此而来','Twenty years in retreat on the Eastern Hill before taking office in his forties — the phrase for a comeback still carries that hill\'s name'],
     ['383 年淝水之战,以八万兵力击败前秦号称八十万的大军','At the Fei River in 383, eighty thousand men broke a Former Qin army claiming eight hundred thousand'],
     ['战报送到时他正在下棋,看完把那一局下完','The dispatch reached him mid-game; he read it and finished the game']],
  s:['淝水之战是中国历史上最著名的以少胜多战役之一,它保住了东晋,也保住了南方汉文化的延续。"东山再起""草木皆兵""风声鹤唳"三个成语都出自这场战役前后。',
     'Fei River is among the most celebrated against-the-odds victories in Chinese history: it saved the Eastern Jin, and with it the southern continuation of Han culture. Three common idioms come from the days around that battle.'] },
'王羲之': { g:'art', y:[303,361], c:'东晋·十六国', n:['王羲之','Wang Xizhi'],
  t:['被尊为"书圣"。他为一次聚会写的序,成了中国书法的最高标准。',
     'Revered as the Sage of Calligraphy. A preface he dashed off at a party became the standard against which all Chinese writing is measured.'],
  a:[['353 年三月三日在会稽兰亭聚会,微醺时写下《兰亭集序》三百二十四字','At Lanting on the third day of the third month, 353, slightly drunk, he wrote 324 characters'],
     ['据说酒醒后重写数十遍,都不如那一稿','Sober, he is said to have rewritten it dozens of times and never matched the original'],
     ['把汉魏以来的隶书笔法改造成流畅的行书','Reworked the old clerical brushwork into flowing running script']],
  s:['《兰亭集序》被称为"天下第一行书",真迹相传随唐太宗殉葬,今天所见全是摹本——而摹本本身已是国宝。他确立的行书体系是此后一千六百年中国书法的主流。',
     'The Lanting preface is called the finest running script ever written. The original is said to have been buried with Emperor Taizong of Tang; every version we have is a copy — and the copies are themselves national treasures. His running script has been the mainstream of Chinese calligraphy for 1,600 years.'] },
'苻坚': { g:'king', y:[338,385], r:[357,385], c:'东晋·十六国', n:['苻坚','Fu Jian'],
  t:['十六国里最接近统一北方的君主,也是败得最彻底的一个。',
     'The ruler who came closest to reuniting the north in that shattered century — and lost it all at once.'],
  a:[['重用汉人王猛推行改革,前秦国力大增','Made the Han Chinese statesman Wang Meng his chief minister and rebuilt the state on his reforms'],
     ['376 年统一北方,是西晋灭亡后北方的第一次统一','Unified the north in 376, the first time since the fall of the Western Jin'],
     ['383 年南征东晋,淝水一战全军崩溃','Marched south in 383; at the Fei River his army disintegrated']],
  s:['他对被征服各族一律优待、不加清洗,在十六国的混战中极为罕见。但淝水战败后这些部族随即各自独立,北方重新分裂——他的宽容与他的溃败常被后世一并讨论。两年后他被姚苌所杀。',
     'He absorbed conquered peoples without massacres, almost unique in that period. But after Fei River those same peoples broke away at once and the north fragmented again — his tolerance and his collapse are usually discussed together. Two years later he was killed by one of his own commanders.'] },
'北魏孝文帝': { g:'king', y:[467,499], r:[471,499], c:'南北朝', n:['北魏孝文帝','Emperor Xiaowen of Northern Wei'],
  t:['鲜卑皇帝,却下令自己的民族改说汉语、穿汉服、改汉姓。',
     'A Xianbei emperor who ordered his own people to speak Chinese, dress Chinese and take Chinese surnames.'],
  a:[['494 年迁都洛阳,从平城(今大同)南下','Moved the capital south from Pingcheng — modern Datong — to Luoyang in 494'],
     ['禁鲜卑语、禁胡服,皇族拓跋氏改姓元','Banned the Xianbei language and dress, and changed the royal surname Tuoba to Yuan'],
     ['推行均田制、三长制,鼓励鲜卑与汉人通婚','Introduced the equal-field and three-elders systems, and encouraged intermarriage']],
  s:['中国历史上由统治民族主动推行的最彻底的一次汉化。均田制被北齐、北周、隋、唐沿用三百年,是隋唐国力的制度底座。云冈石窟与龙门石窟分别开凿于迁都前后,均已列入世界遗产。',
     'The most thorough sinicisation ever imposed by a ruling people on itself. The equal-field system he introduced was kept by four successor dynasties for three centuries and underwrote the wealth of the Sui and Tang. The Yungang and Longmen grottoes, carved before and after the move, are both World Heritage Sites.'] },
'萧衍': { g:'king', y:[464,549], r:[502,549], c:'南北朝', n:['萧衍','Emperor Wu of Liang'],
  t:['在位 48 年,南朝在位最久的皇帝。他四次舍身出家,每次都要大臣拿钱把他赎回来。',
     'Forty-eight years on the throne, the longest of any southern emperor. Four times he renounced the world for a monastery, and four times his ministers had to buy him back.'],
  a:[['502 年代齐建梁,前期勤政,史称"天监之治"','Founded the Liang in 502; his early years were remembered as a model reign'],
     ['大力扶植佛教,建寺造像,自称"皇帝菩萨"','Poured resources into Buddhism, built temples and images, and styled himself the Bodhisattva Emperor'],
     ['其长子萧统主持编成《文选》','His eldest son Xiao Tong compiled the Wen Xuan under his patronage']],
  s:['梁武帝时期是南朝文化的高峰。《文选》是中国现存最早的诗文总集,此后一千余年是东亚文人的必读书。他晚年收留降将侯景引发叛乱,自己被困台城饿死,梁朝随之崩溃。',
     'His reign was the cultural high point of the southern dynasties. The Wen Xuan is the earliest surviving Chinese literary anthology and was required reading across East Asia for a thousand years. In old age he took in a defecting general, whose revolt trapped him in his own palace, where he starved; the Liang fell with him.'] },
'隋文帝': { g:'king', y:[541,604], r:[581,604], c:'隋', n:['隋文帝','Emperor Wen of Sui'],
  t:['结束了西晋以来近三百年的分裂。',
     'He ended nearly three centuries of division.'],
  a:[['581 年代北周建隋,589 年灭陈,南北重归统一','Founded the Sui in 581 and conquered Chen in 589, reuniting north and south'],
     ['创三省六部制,中央官制此后沿用一千三百年','Created the three departments and six ministries — the shape of Chinese central government for 1,300 years'],
     ['废九品中正,改以考试选官,科举的雏形','Scrapped selection by pedigree in favour of examinations — the germ of the civil-service system']],
  s:['三省六部制被唐、宋、元、明沿用到清末;开皇年间的户口与粮储数字在唐初仍被当作标杆引用。麦克·哈特的《影响人类历史进程的一百名人》里,他与秦始皇是仅有的两位入选的中国皇帝。',
     'His ministries survived to the end of the empire, and the household and granary figures of his reign were still cited as benchmarks a century later. In Michael Hart\'s ranking of the hundred most influential people, he and Qin Shi Huang are the only two Chinese emperors on the list.'] },
'隋炀帝': { g:'king', y:[569,618], r:[604,618], c:'隋', n:['隋炀帝','Emperor Yang of Sui'],
  t:['干了几件影响一千年的大事,然后把国家干亡了。',
     'He did a few things that shaped the next thousand years, and destroyed his dynasty doing them.'],
  a:[['605 年起开凿大运河,连通海河、黄河、淮河、长江、钱塘江五大水系','From 605 he cut the Grand Canal, linking five river systems from the Hai to the Qiantang'],
     ['正式设进士科,科举制度由此成型','Established the jinshi examination, giving the civil-service system its lasting form'],
     ['三征高句丽,三次都败,民力耗尽','Invaded Goguryeo three times, failed three times, and exhausted the country']],
  s:['大运河全长约两千七百公里,是世界上最长的人工运河,2014 年列入世界遗产,今天部分河段仍在通航。进士科使科举成为此后一千三百年中国选官的主要途径。他本人 618 年在江都被部下缢杀,隋朝二世而亡。',
     'The Grand Canal runs some 2,700 km — the longest artificial waterway ever built, listed as World Heritage in 2014 and still carrying traffic on parts of its length. The jinshi examination became the main route into office in China for the next 1,300 years. He was strangled by his own guards in 618, and the Sui ended in its second reign.'] },
'唐太宗': { g:'king', y:[598,649], r:[626,649], c:'唐', n:['唐太宗','Emperor Taizong of Tang'],
  t:['杀兄逼父上位,却成了后世公认的模范皇帝。',
     'He killed his brothers and forced his father aside — and became the model emperor of Chinese tradition.'],
  a:[['626 年玄武门之变杀太子李建成,同年即位','Killed the crown prince at the Xuanwu Gate in 626 and took the throne that year'],
     ['以纳谏著称,魏征前后进谏两百余事','Famous for taking criticism: one minister alone submitted over two hundred remonstrances'],
     ['630 年击灭东突厥,西北各族尊他为"天可汗"','Destroyed the Eastern Turks in 630; the northwestern peoples hailed him as Heavenly Khagan']],
  s:['贞观之治是中国历史上被引用最多的治世样板,《贞观政要》成为东亚各国君主的教科书,日本、朝鲜、越南都曾照搬唐制。"天可汗"体系让唐朝同时是中原王朝与草原共主,长安一度是世界上最大的城市。',
     'His reign is the most quoted example of good government in Chinese history, and the book of its policy debates became a handbook for rulers in Japan, Korea and Vietnam, all of which copied Tang institutions. As Heavenly Khagan he was at once Chinese emperor and steppe overlord, and his capital was for a time the largest city on earth.'] },
'李白': { g:'art', y:[701,762], c:'唐', n:['李白','Li Bai'],
  t:['中国最有名的诗人。传说他喝醉后让皇帝身边的红人给他脱靴子。',
     'China\'s most famous poet — who, the story goes, made the emperor\'s favourite pull off his boots while drunk.'],
  a:[['一生漫游全国,留下约一千首诗','Wandered the country all his life and left about a thousand poems'],
     ['742 年被召入长安供奉翰林,三年后被"赐金放还"','Summoned to court in 742 and paid to leave three years later'],
     ['与杜甫相遇于洛阳,同游数月,此后再未相见','Met Du Fu at Luoyang, travelled with him for a few months, and never saw him again']],
  s:['他与杜甫并称"李杜",是中国诗歌的两座高峰。《静夜思》大概是华人世界背诵人数最多的一首诗,几乎每个孩子最先会背的就是它。他被称为"诗仙",作品已译成数十种语言。',
     'He and Du Fu are the twin peaks of Chinese poetry. His twenty-character "Quiet Night Thoughts" is probably the most memorised poem in the Chinese-speaking world — usually the first any child learns. Known as the Banished Immortal, he has been translated into dozens of languages.'] },
'杜甫': { g:'art', y:[712,770], c:'唐', n:['杜甫','Du Fu'],
  t:['活着的时候没什么名气,死后被尊为"诗圣"。',
     'Barely known in his lifetime; revered afterwards as the Sage of Poetry.'],
  a:[['经历安史之乱,一路逃难,写下《春望》《三吏》《三别》','Lived through the An Lushan rebellion as a refugee, and wrote the poems that record it'],
     ['晚年住成都草堂,一生穷困,最后死在湘江的船上','Spent his last years in a thatched hut at Chengdu, poor throughout, and died on a boat on the Xiang'],
     ['留下一千四百余首诗,记录唐朝由盛转衰的全过程','Left over 1,400 poems tracing the Tang\'s fall from its height']],
  s:['他的诗被称为"诗史"——安史之乱中普通人的处境,正史之外主要靠他的记录留存。1962 年他被列为世界文化名人。成都杜甫草堂至今是中国最重要的文学纪念地之一。',
     'His work is called "poet-history": for what ordinary people endured in the rebellion, his poems are the main record outside the official annals. In 1962 he was named among the world\'s great cultural figures, and his Chengdu hut remains one of China\'s most visited literary sites.'] },

'柴荣': { g:'king', y:[921,959], r:[954,959], c:'五代十国', n:['柴荣','Chai Rong'],
  t:['五代五十三年里最有作为的皇帝,只在位五年半就病死了,时年三十八。',
     'The ablest ruler of a chaotic half-century — and he reigned five and a half years before dying at thirty-eight.'],
  a:[['954 年高平之战亲自督战,击败北汉与契丹联军','Took personal command at Gaoping in 954 and beat the combined Northern Han and Khitan armies'],
     ['整顿禁军、裁汰老弱,建立殿前诸班——赵匡胤正是从这支军队里出来的','Rebuilt the palace army from scratch; Zhao Kuangyin rose through it'],
     ['毁佛寺三万余所收铜铸钱,疏浚汴河,整顿财政','Melted temple bronze into coin, dredged the Bian canal and put state finances in order']],
  s:['他定下"十年开拓天下、十年养百姓、十年致太平"的三十年计划,只走了五年半。北宋的制度、军队与统一路线基本接着他的做,后世史家多认为宋的统一实由他奠基。',
     'He set himself thirty years — ten to conquer, ten to nourish the people, ten for peace — and got five and a half. The Song inherited his institutions, his army and his strategy; historians generally credit him with laying the foundation of the reunification he did not live to see.'] },
'赵匡胤': { g:'king', y:[927,976], r:[960,976], c:'北宋', n:['赵匡胤','Zhao Kuangyin'],
  t:['陈桥兵变黄袍加身,建立宋朝。他用一顿酒解除了开国将领的兵权。',
     'His officers threw a yellow robe over him and made him emperor. He took their armies back over a single dinner.'],
  a:[['960 年陈桥驿兵变,部下把黄袍披到他身上','At Chenqiao in 960 his own troops proclaimed him emperor'],
     ['杯酒释兵权:让开国将领交出兵权换富贵,免去了历代开国屠戮功臣的惯例','Over wine, he offered his generals wealth in exchange for their commands — and so skipped the usual purge of founding comrades'],
     ['确立重文抑武,文官治国,禁军由皇帝直接掌握','Put civil officials above soldiers and took the standing army under direct imperial control']],
  s:['五代五十三年换了五个朝代、十四个皇帝,武将篡位是常态;从他之后,中国再没出现过军人政变夺取中央政权,代价是宋朝在军事上长期被动。他立下不杀士大夫及上书言事者的祖训,宋代因此成为中国历史上文人地位最高的时期。',
     'The preceding fifty-three years had seen five dynasties and fourteen emperors, nearly all installed by soldiers. After him, no military coup ever again took the central government of China — at the cost of a permanently defensive army. His house rule against executing scholar-officials or those who criticised the throne made the Song the high point of civilian standing in Chinese history.'] },
'苏轼': { g:'art', y:[1037,1101], c:'北宋', n:['苏轼','Su Shi'],
  t:['诗、词、散文、书法、绘画样样第一流,同时是个被贬了一辈子的官。',
     'First-rate at poetry, lyrics, prose, calligraphy and painting — and demoted, over and over, all his life.'],
  a:[['因反对新法被外放,又因"乌台诗案"下狱,几乎处死','Sent out of the capital for opposing the reforms, then jailed over his poems and nearly executed'],
     ['一贬再贬,黄州、惠州、儋州(今海南),写出《赤壁赋》与《念奴娇·赤壁怀古》','Exiled ever further — Huangzhou, Huizhou, and finally Hainan — writing his greatest work along the way'],
     ['在杭州疏浚西湖、筑长堤,即今日的苏堤;顺带留下东坡肉','Dredged the West Lake at Hangzhou and built the causeway that still bears his name — and a pork dish besides']],
  s:['唐宋八大家之一,宋代文学的最高峰。他把词从歌女唱的小曲提升为可以写任何题材的文体。《寒食帖》被称为"天下第三行书"。苏堤至今是西湖景观的一部分,西湖 2011 年列入世界遗产。',
     'One of the Eight Masters of Tang and Song prose and the summit of Song literature. He lifted the ci lyric from a courtesan\'s song form into a vehicle for any subject at all. His Cold Food Observance is ranked the third finest running-script work ever written, and his causeway is still part of the West Lake, listed as World Heritage in 2011.'] },
'沈括': { g:'sci', y:[1031,1095], c:'北宋', n:['沈括','Shen Kuo'],
  t:['《梦溪笔谈》的作者。李约瑟称他是"中国整部科学史上最卓越的人物"。',
     'Author of the Dream Pool Essays. Joseph Needham called him the most remarkable figure in the whole of Chinese science.'],
  a:[['记录毕昇的活字印刷术——这是活字印刷唯一的当时记载','Recorded Bi Sheng\'s movable type — the only contemporary account that exists'],
     ['发现磁针"常微偏东",是世界上最早的磁偏角记录','Noted that the compass needle points slightly east of true north: the first record of magnetic declination anywhere'],
     ['提出"石油"这个名称,并预言"此物后必大行于世"','Coined the Chinese word for petroleum and predicted it would one day be used everywhere']],
  s:['《梦溪笔谈》记录六百余条见闻,涵盖天文、数学、地质、物理、医药,是研究中国古代科技的第一手材料。毕昇的活字印刷若无他这一笔就完全失传了。月球背面有环形山以他命名,小行星 2027 号也是。',
     'The Dream Pool Essays gather over six hundred entries across astronomy, mathematics, geology, physics and medicine, and are the primary source for early Chinese science. Without his single paragraph, the invention of movable type would have vanished from the record. A crater on the far side of the moon and asteroid 2027 both carry his name.'] },
'岳飞': { g:'war', y:[1103,1142], c:'南宋', n:['岳飞','Yue Fei'],
  t:['南宋最能打的将领,在快要打赢的时候被自己的朝廷杀了。',
     'The best general the Southern Song had — killed by his own court just as he was winning.'],
  a:[['1140 年郾城、颍昌两战击败金军主力','Broke the main Jin field armies at Yancheng and Yingchang in 1140'],
     ['一日之内接到十二道金牌,被强令班师','Was recalled by twelve gold-plaque orders arriving in a single day'],
     ['1142 年以"莫须有"的罪名死于狱中,时年三十九','Died in prison in 1142 on a charge of "perhaps there was something" — he was thirty-nine']],
  s:['"莫须有"从此成了汉语里冤案的代名词。杭州岳王庙前跪着秦桧等四人的铁像,已立了五百多年。相传为他所作的《满江红》是流传最广的爱国词作之一。',
     'The phrase used to condemn him became the Chinese word for a trumped-up charge. At his temple in Hangzhou, iron statues of the four men who destroyed him have knelt in penance for over five centuries.'] },
'朱熹': { g:'mind', y:[1130,1200], c:'南宋', n:['朱熹','Zhu Xi'],
  t:['他重新解释了儒家经典,这套解释成了此后六百年科举考试的标准答案。',
     'He reinterpreted the Confucian classics, and his reading became the official answer key for six centuries of examinations.'],
  a:[['把《大学》《中庸》《论语》《孟子》合为"四书",地位提到五经之上','Grouped four short texts into the "Four Books" and placed them above the older Five Classics'],
     ['写《四书章句集注》,系统建立理学','Wrote the commentary that systematised Neo-Confucianism'],
     ['重建白鹿洞书院,定下影响深远的书院学规','Rebuilt the White Deer Grotto Academy and drafted the rules copied by academies ever after']],
  s:['元代起《四书章句集注》成为科举官方教材,一直用到 1905 年科举废除——六百多年间中国读书人的思想底本就是这一套。理学同时传入朝鲜、日本、越南,成为东亚共同的思想框架。',
     'From the Yuan onward his commentary was the prescribed text for the imperial examinations, right up to their abolition in 1905 — six hundred years in which it formed the mental furniture of every educated Chinese. Neo-Confucianism also became the shared intellectual framework of Korea, Japan and Vietnam.'] },
'辛弃疾': { g:'art', y:[1140,1207], c:'南宋', n:['辛弃疾','Xin Qiji'],
  t:['二十二岁带五十骑冲进五万人的敌营抓叛徒,后半生却只能写词。',
     'At twenty-two he rode into an enemy camp of fifty thousand with fifty men and took his target alive. He spent the rest of his life writing poems.'],
  a:[['1162 年率五十骑袭金营,擒获叛将张安国,万军之中带回南宋','In 1162 he seized a defector from the middle of the Jin army and brought him back south'],
     ['南归后四十余年屡遭猜忌闲置,一心北伐而不得','Spent forty years under suspicion and mostly out of office, never getting the northern campaign he wanted'],
     ['留下词六百余首,数量居宋代之首','Left over six hundred ci lyrics, more than any other Song poet']],
  s:['他与苏轼并称"苏辛",是豪放词的两大代表,也是宋代存词最多的词人。军人出身而成为一流词人,在中国文学史上仅此一例;《破阵子》《永遇乐·京口北固亭怀古》至今是中学课本篇目。',
     'He and Su Shi are the two great names of the bold style, and he left more lyrics than any Song contemporary. A career soldier who became a first-rank poet is unique in Chinese literary history.'] },
'耶律阿保机': { g:'king', y:[872,926], r:[907,926], c:'辽', n:['耶律阿保机','Abaoji'],
  t:['契丹的开国皇帝。他让草原政权第一次有了皇帝和年号。',
     'Founder of the Khitan state — the first steppe polity with an emperor and a reign title.'],
  a:[['916 年称帝建元神册,草原民族第一次采用中原的年号制度','Proclaimed himself emperor in 916 with a reign era, a Chinese practice no steppe ruler had used'],
     ['命人创制契丹大字与小字','Had both a large and a small Khitan script created'],
     ['设南北面官:北面管契丹与游牧部族,南面按汉制管汉人','Ran two administrations at once: a northern one for the Khitan and nomads, a southern one on Chinese lines for Chinese subjects']],
  s:['南北面官制是中国历史上第一次系统性地让游牧与农耕在同一政权下各按各的规矩生活,金、元、清都不同程度沿用。辽的国际影响极大——俄语的 Китай、中古欧洲的 Cathay,"中国"一词都源自"契丹"。',
     'That dual administration was the first systematic attempt to let nomads and farmers live under one state by different rules, and the Jin, Yuan and Qing all borrowed from it. The Liao\'s reach abroad was such that the word for China in Russian, and the medieval European "Cathay", both come from "Khitan".'] },
'萧太后': { g:'king', y:[953,1009], c:'辽', n:['萧太后','Empress Dowager Xiao'],
  t:['辽朝实际掌权二十七年的女性统治者。宋朝最怕的对手是她。',
     'She ran the Liao empire for twenty-seven years, and was the opponent the Song feared most.'],
  a:[['982 年圣宗即位时年仅十二岁,她以太后身份摄政','Took the regency in 982 when her son came to the throne at twelve'],
     ['整顿吏治、编修法典,允许契丹人与汉人通婚、同罪同罚','Reformed the bureaucracy and the law code, permitted Khitan-Chinese intermarriage and made both answerable to the same penalties'],
     ['1004 年亲率大军南下直逼澶州,迫使宋朝议和','Led an army south to the Yellow River in 1004 and forced the Song to terms']],
  s:['由此签订的澶渊之盟让宋辽维持了一百二十年不打仗,是中国历史上持续最久的和平条约之一。她主政期间辽朝国力最强,也是中国历史上少数长期实际执政且评价甚高的女性统治者。',
     'The treaty that followed kept the Song and Liao from war for 120 years, one of the longest-lasting peace agreements in Chinese history. The Liao was at its strongest under her, and she remains one of the very few women to have governed a Chinese-world empire for decades with a strong reputation intact.'] },
'松赞干布': { g:'king', y:[617,650], ca:1, r:[629,650], c:'吐蕃', n:['松赞干布','Songtsen Gampo'],
  t:['吐蕃的开国赞普。高原上第一次有了自己的文字。',
     'The btsanpo who founded the Tibetan empire — and under whom the plateau first had a script of its own.'],
  a:[['兼并高原各部,把都城迁到逻些(今拉萨)','Absorbed the other plateau clans and moved his capital to Lhasa'],
     ['参照印度字母创制藏文,并据此立法、记事','Had a script for Tibetan devised on an Indic model, then used it for law and record'],
     ['先后迎娶尼泊尔尺尊公主与唐朝文成公主(641年)','Married a Nepali princess and, in 641, a Tang princess']],
  s:['藏文沿用至今;后来整库佛经译进这套文字,几部在印度失传的原典,反倒靠藏文的译本传了下来。他在位确立的高原统一格局,支撑吐蕃与唐争夺西域两百年。',
     'The script is still in use; a whole library of scripture was later carried into it, and several works lost in India survive only because his alphabet caught them. The unity he established on the plateau sustained two centuries of contest with Tang China over the Western Regions.'] },
'赤松德赞': { g:'faith', y:[742,797], r:[755,797], c:'吐蕃', n:['赤松德赞','Trisong Detsen'],
  t:['把佛教立为吐蕃国教的赞普,也是疆域最大时的君主。',
     'The ruler who made Buddhism the religion of the Tibetan state, and who held its widest borders.'],
  a:[['建成桑耶寺,吐蕃第一座剃度僧人的寺院','Founded Samye, the first monastery in Tibet to ordain monks'],
     ['请印度与汉地僧人入藏译经,设立译场','Brought Indian and Chinese monks in to translate scripture, and set up translation workshops'],
     ['763年趁安史之乱后唐军空虚,一度攻入长安','Took Chang\'an briefly in 763, when the Tang\'s northwestern armies had been pulled away']],
  s:['佛教从此成为王权的第二根支柱——代价是与苯教旧族结下的世仇,缠住了此后的每一代赞普。桑耶寺的辩经传统与他定下的译经规范,是藏传佛教成体系的起点。',
     'Buddhism became a second pillar of kingship — at the price of a feud with the old Bon nobility that clung to every ruler after him. The debates held at Samye and the translation standards he set are where Tibetan Buddhism began to take systematic shape.'] },
'大祚荣': { g:'king', y:[645,719], ca:1, r:[698,719], c:'渤海国', n:['大祚荣','Dae Joyeong'],
  t:['带着高句丽遗民与靺鞨部众东归,在故地重新建国。',
     'He led Goguryeo survivors and Mohe tribespeople back east and founded a state on their old ground.'],
  a:[['696年趁契丹反唐之乱率部东走,渡辽水返回故地','Marched east through a Khitan revolt in 696 and recrossed the Liao River home'],
     ['698年建国于今吉林敦化一带,初称震国','Founded the state around present-day Dunhua in 698'],
     ['713年受唐册封为渤海郡王,国号自此定为渤海','Was invested by the Tang as Prince of Bohai in 713, and the name stuck']],
  s:['他建立的政权存续二百二十八年:对外接过唐的册封,关起门来用自己的年号——两头都不吃亏的活法,在他手里起步,到儿子建元「仁安」时定了型。渤海的族属与历史归属,至今是中、朝、韩、俄、日学界解释最不一致的题目之一。',
     'The state he founded lasted 228 years: it accepted Tang investiture abroad and kept its own reign titles behind closed doors — a way of losing nothing at either end, begun under him and settled when his son took the reign title Inan. Its ethnic makeup and its place in national histories remain among the most contested questions in northeast Asia.'] },
'段思平': { g:'king', y:[893,944], r:[937,944], c:'南诏·大理', n:['段思平','Duan Siping'],
  t:['大理国的开国皇帝。南诏亡后三十余年的乱局到他为止。',
     'Founder of the Dali kingdom, who ended thirty years of turmoil after Nanzhao fell.'],
  a:[['937年灭大义宁建大理国,结束南诏亡后的三易其主','Overthrew the last of three short-lived regimes in 937 and founded Dali'],
     ['减轻赋役、放宽刑罚,以安集各部','Cut taxes and labour service and eased punishments to settle the tribes'],
     ['奠定段氏与高氏等大姓共治的格局','Set up the arrangement by which the Duan house ruled alongside great families such as the Gao']],
  s:['大理国存续三百余年,同宋朝始终没打过仗,生意却一直做;先后有九到十位皇帝出家为僧,这在中国历史上是独一份。1253年蒙古为包抄南宋而灭大理——段家没有跟着王朝一起消失,后人又替新朝管了云南好几代人。',
     'Dali lasted more than three centuries and never once fought Song China, though the trading never stopped; nine or ten of its rulers, one after another, ended their days as monks — without parallel in Chinese history. The Mongols destroyed it in 1253 while outflanking the Southern Song — but the Duans did not vanish with their kingdom, and their descendants went on running Yunnan for generations under the new masters.'] },
'昭海尔': { g:'war', y:[928,992], ca:1, c:'法蒂玛王朝', n:['昭海尔','Jawhar'],
  t:['西西里出身的将领,他攻下埃及,又画出了开罗的第一张城图。',
     'A general of Sicilian origin who took Egypt — and laid out the first plan of Cairo.'],
  a:[['969年率军征服埃及,几乎兵不血刃','Conquered Egypt in 969, almost without a fight'],
     ['在旧城以北筑新都,取名开罗(意为「胜利者」)','Laid out a new capital north of the old city and named it al-Qahira, the victorious'],
     ['970年动工兴建爱资哈尔清真寺','Began building the mosque of al-Azhar in 970']],
  s:['开罗与爱资哈尔都从他手里起步,后来的千年故事却是逊尼派续写的。他本人出身奴隶,凭军功位极人臣,是法蒂玛王朝用人不问出身的典型。',
     'Both Cairo and al-Azhar began at his hands, though the thousand years that followed were written by Sunni successors. He had begun as a slave and rose to the top on military service, a typical case of how the Fatimids picked men.'] },
'伊本·海赛姆': { g:'sci', y:[965,1040], c:'法蒂玛王朝', n:['伊本·海赛姆','Ibn al-Haytham'],
  t:['他证明了人能看见东西,是因为光进了眼睛,而不是眼睛射出了什么。',
     'He showed that we see because light enters the eye — not because the eye sends something out.'],
  a:[['写成《光学书》,用实验推翻了希腊人「眼睛发出视线」的旧说','Wrote the Book of Optics, overturning by experiment the Greek idea that the eye emits rays'],
     ['用暗箱证明光沿直线传播,并解释了成像原理','Used a darkened chamber to show that light travels in straight lines, and explained how images form'],
     ['坚持「先怀疑再验证」的做法,主张对权威的说法也要动手检验','Insisted on doubting first and testing after — even where the authorities had spoken']],
  s:['《光学书》12世纪被译成拉丁文,直接影响了培根、开普勒与整个欧洲的光学传统;他强调实验优先于权威,常被视为科学方法的早期实践者之一。传说他为躲避哈基姆的追究而装疯,在软禁中写成此书——这段故事流传很广,但真伪难考。',
     'The Book of Optics was translated into Latin in the twelfth century and shaped Roger Bacon, Kepler and the whole European tradition in optics; his insistence on experiment over authority makes him one of the earliest practitioners of what became scientific method. The story that he feigned madness to escape the caliph al-Hakim and wrote the book under house arrest is widely repeated but hard to verify.'] },
'阿卜杜拉赫曼三世': { g:'king', y:[891,961], r:[912,961], c:'后倭马亚·安达卢斯', n:['阿卜杜拉赫曼三世','Abd al-Rahman III'],
  t:['接手一个四分五裂的埃米尔国,五十年后把它变成与巴格达平起平坐的哈里发国。',
     'He inherited a fractured emirate and left a caliphate that dealt with Baghdad as an equal.'],
  a:[['即位后用二十年平定各地割据,重新统一安达卢斯','Spent two decades after his accession putting down local warlords and reuniting al-Andalus'],
     ['929年正式称哈里发,与巴格达、北非的法蒂玛形成三足','Took the title of caliph in 929, making a third alongside Baghdad and the Fatimids of North Africa'],
     ['936年起在科尔多瓦城外营建宫城麦地那·扎赫拉','From 936 built the palace city of Madinat al-Zahra outside Córdoba']],
  s:['他在位期间科尔多瓦成为欧洲人口最多的城市之一,与拜占庭、德意志的奥托一世互派使节。他并非战无不胜:939年在西曼卡斯败于莱昂的拉米罗二世,此后不再亲自领军。麦地那·扎赫拉前后只用了七十来年就毁于内战,遗址2018年列入世界遗产。',
     'Under him Córdoba became one of the most populous cities in Europe and exchanged embassies with Byzantium and with Otto I of Germany. He was not undefeated: Ramiro II of León beat him at Simancas in 939, and he never led an army in person again. Madinat al-Zahra was destroyed in civil war some seventy years after work on it began; the site was made a World Heritage site in 2018.'] },
'扎赫拉维': { g:'sci', y:[936,1013], ca:1, c:'后倭马亚·安达卢斯', n:['扎赫拉维','Al-Zahrawi'],
  t:['他把外科手术画了出来——器械长什么样、怎么用,一件一件画在书上。',
     'He drew surgery: what each instrument looked like and how to use it, one by one, in a book.'],
  a:[['编成三十卷的医学总集,涵盖内科、药剂、饮食与外科','Compiled a thirty-volume medical work covering medicine, pharmacy, diet and surgery'],
     ['最后一卷专讲外科,附约两百件手术器械的图样','Devoted the last volume to surgery, with drawings of some two hundred instruments'],
     ['记述用羊肠线做体内缝合、用烧灼与结扎止血','Described catgut for internal sutures, and cautery and ligature to stop bleeding']],
  s:['这最后一卷在12世纪被译成拉丁文,此后数百年是欧洲医学院外科课程的基础读物之一,他的拉丁名 Abulcasis 比本名更为人知。把器械画出来这件事本身很关键:文字描述容易走样,图样让工艺可以被复制。他在科尔多瓦行医并服务于宫廷,一生几乎没有离开这座城。',
     'That last volume was translated into Latin in the twelfth century and for centuries afterwards was among the standard surgical texts in European medical schools; his Latin name, Abulcasis, is better known than the one he was born with. Drawing the instruments mattered in itself: written descriptions drift, but a drawing lets the craft be copied. He practised in Córdoba and served the court, and scarcely left the city in his life.'] },
'扬三世·索别斯基': { g:'war', y:[1629,1696], r:[1674,1696], c:'波兰-立陶宛', n:['扬三世·索别斯基','John III Sobieski'],
  t:['1683年他带着骑兵从山上冲下来,解了维也纳之围。','In 1683 he brought his cavalry down off the hill and lifted the siege of Vienna.'],
  a:[['1674年由贵族选举为王,此前已因多次击败奥斯曼军而声望极高','Elected king by the nobility in 1674, already famous for beating Ottoman armies more than once'],
     ['1683年率波兰-立陶宛军队驰援被围的维也纳,与神圣罗马诸邦联军会合','In 1683 he marched to relieve the siege of Vienna and joined the imperial contingents there'],
     ['9月12日下午从卡伦山发起总攻,以翼骑兵为锋,当日解围','On the afternoon of 12 September he attacked from the Kahlenberg with the winged hussars at the front, and the siege was broken that day']],
  s:['这一战通常被视为奥斯曼在中欧扩张的终点,此后攻守易位。他本人在欧洲被当作基督教世界的保卫者,而在波兰是最受欢迎的国王之一。值得一提的是他没能解决国内的问题:自由否决权照旧,他想让王位在自己家族里世袭也没有成功,死后波兰重新陷入选举内斗——外战的胜利没有换来内政的改革,这是他任内最大的遗憾。','The battle is generally taken as the end of Ottoman expansion in central Europe, after which the initiative changed hands. He was seen across Europe as a defender of Christendom, and at home he is one of the best-loved Polish kings. Worth adding that he solved none of the domestic problems: the liberum veto stayed, his attempt to make the crown hereditary in his family failed, and after his death Poland fell back into contested elections. A victory abroad bought no reform at home, and that was the great disappointment of his reign.'] },
'玛丽亚·特蕾莎': { g:'king', y:[1717,1780], r:[1740,1780], c:'奥地利·哈布斯堡', n:['玛丽亚·特蕾莎','Maria Theresa'],
  t:['她继位那年就被邻国围攻,理由是「女人不能继承」。她打了八年,王位守住了,西里西亚没能要回来。','The year she inherited, her neighbours attacked on the grounds that a woman could not inherit. She fought for eight years: the throne held, Silesia did not come back.'],
  a:[['1740年即位,普鲁士随即夺取西里西亚,奥地利王位继承战争爆发','She succeeded in 1740, Prussia seized Silesia at once, and the War of the Austrian Succession began'],
     ['战后推行系统改革:统一税制并让贵族纳税、整顿常备军、设立中央部院','Afterwards she reformed systematically: a uniform tax that the nobility also paid, a reorganised standing army, central ministries'],
     ['1774年颁布普通学校令,规定六至十二岁儿童入学,是欧洲较早的义务教育立法之一','Her school ordinance of 1774 required children from six to twelve to attend, among the earlier compulsory-education laws in Europe']],
  s:['她把一个靠联姻拼起来的王朝改造成了一个有中央财政与常备军的国家,这套底子支撑哈布斯堡又走了一百七十年。她生了十六个孩子,十个活到成年,其中几个被嫁进欧洲各国王室——最小的女儿是后来的法国王后玛丽·安托瓦内特。神圣罗马皇帝这个位置只能由男性担任,所以1745年当上皇帝的是她丈夫弗朗茨一世,她随之有了皇后的名分,但她自己不肯举行加冕礼;她真正靠继承拿到的是奥地利大公、匈牙利与波希米亚女王,而实际统治的人一直是她。','She turned a dynasty assembled by marriage into a state with central finances and a standing army, and that foundation carried the Habsburgs another hundred and seventy years. She bore sixteen children, ten of whom lived to adulthood, and several of those were married into royal houses across Europe — the youngest daughter became Marie Antoinette of France. Only a man could be Holy Roman Emperor, so it was her husband Francis I who was elected in 1745 and she who became empress by marriage, though she refused to be crowned; what she held by inheritance was Austria, Hungary and Bohemia, and she was the one who ruled.'] },
'古斯塔夫二世·阿道夫': { g:'war', y:[1594,1632], r:[1611,1632], c:'瑞典帝国', n:['古斯塔夫二世·阿道夫','Gustavus Adolphus'],
  t:['他把一个百万人口的北方小国,变成了三十年战争里最能打的一方。','He turned a northern country of a million people into the hardest-hitting army of the Thirty Years\' War.'],
  a:[['把火炮减轻到能随步兵一起机动:每个步兵团配上自己的轻炮,炮兵第一次能全程跟着步兵打,而不只是开战前放几轮','He made his guns light enough to move with the infantry and gave each regiment its own light pieces, so that artillery could keep up all through a battle instead of firing a few rounds before it began'],
     ['把火枪兵与长矛兵编成更小、更灵活的方阵,火力密度与转向速度都提高','He combined musket and pike in smaller, more flexible brigades, raising both the density of fire and the speed of manoeuvre'],
     ['1631年在布赖滕费尔德把帝国军打崩——新式打法的第一次全尺寸验证','At Breitenfeld in 1631 he smashed the imperial army — the first full-scale proof of the new way of fighting']],
  s:['他的改革被普鲁士与此后的欧洲各国吸收,通常被列为「军事革命」的关键一环。他1632年在吕岑战死时年仅三十七岁,而那一战瑞典是赢的——国王阵亡于自己的胜利之中,这个场景在欧洲史上反复被引用。需要说清楚的是:瑞典在三十年战争里的军费很大一部分由法国补贴与占领区供养支付,他的胜利并不等于瑞典有能力长期承担这种规模的战争,这一点在他死后逐渐显现。','His reforms were taken up by Prussia and by Europe generally and are usually counted a key part of the military revolution. He was killed at Lützen in 1632 at thirty-seven, in a battle Sweden won — a king dying in the middle of his own victory, a scene European history has returned to ever since. One thing should be said plainly: much of Sweden\'s cost in that war was met by French subsidies and by levies on occupied land, so his victories did not mean Sweden could sustain war on that scale, as became clear after his death.'] },
'阿底峡': { g:'faith', y:[982,1054], c:'波罗王朝', n:['阿底峡','Atisha'],
  t:['孟加拉的高僧,五十九岁应邀入藏,再没回来。','A Bengali master who went to Tibet at fifty-nine, and never came back.'],
  a:[['出身王族,在超戒寺任上座,是当时印度最有名望的学者之一','Born into a royal family, he became a senior teacher at Vikramashila and one of the most respected scholars in India'],
     ['1042年应西藏阿里王朝之请入藏——据记载对方为迎请他备了大量黄金','In 1042 he accepted an invitation from the kings of western Tibet, who are recorded as having assembled a great deal of gold to bring him'],
     ['写成《菩提道灯论》,把庞杂的教法按修行次第排成一条路','He wrote the Lamp for the Path, arranging a sprawling body of teaching into a single graded sequence']],
  s:['他到达时西藏佛教正处在混乱期,教法来源杂而互相矛盾。他的办法不是增加内容,而是排序——先学什么、后学什么、为什么这样排,这套「道次第」被后来的各派普遍采用,宗喀巴的《菩提道次第广论》正是接着他写的。他在西藏住了十二年,1054年圆寂于聂塘。一个孟加拉学者塑造了另一个高原地区此后近千年的宗教形态,而他的故乡此后不到一百五十年就几乎绝迹。','He arrived when Tibetan Buddhism was in disarray, its teachings drawn from many sources and often contradicting one another. His answer was not to add more but to put things in order — what to study first, what after, and why — and that graded path was taken up by most later schools; Tsongkhapa\'s great treatise is written straight on from his. He lived twelve years in Tibet and died there in 1054. A Bengali scholar shaped the religious life of a highland country for the next thousand years, while in his own homeland Buddhism had all but disappeared within a century and a half.'] },
'阿奴律陀': { g:'king', y:[1044,1077], yk:'r', c:'蒲甘', n:['阿奴律陀','Anawrahta'],
  t:['他把伊洛瓦底江边的一堆小邦并成一个国家,顺手换掉了全国的宗教。','He welded the small polities of the Irrawaddy into one country, and changed its religion while he was at it.'],
  a:[['1044年即位后逐一并吞周边小邦,第一次把干旱区与三角洲连成一体','From his accession in 1044 he absorbed the neighbouring polities one by one, joining the dry zone and the delta for the first time'],
     ['1057年南下攻取孟人的直通,带回僧团、巴利文三藏与工匠','In 1057 he took Thaton from the Mon and brought back its monks, the Pali canon and its craftsmen'],
     ['修堰渠、扩灌区,把干旱平原变成能养起一座都城的粮仓','He built weirs and extended the irrigated area, turning a dry plain into the granary a capital needed']],
  s:['上座部佛教从此成为缅甸的国教,一千年来一直是主流,并把缅甸与后来的泰国、老挝、柬埔寨连进同一个佛教世界。他本人在缅甸被当作建国者,寺庙里有他的塑像,军队的番号也用他的名字。需要说清楚的是:「攻取直通才带回佛教」这个说法出自18世纪以后的缅甸编年史,而更早的证据并不支持「此前没有佛教」;近年更有学者质疑这趟远征本身是否发生过——立国教是实的,「从无到有引进」是后人加的戏。','Theravada Buddhism became the religion of the Burmese state and has been the mainstream ever since, joining the country to what would become Thailand, Laos and Cambodia in one Buddhist world. He is treated as the founder of the nation, with statues in temples and army units named for him. One qualification: the story that Buddhism arrived with the conquest of Thaton comes from Burmese chronicles of the eighteenth century and later, the earlier evidence does not support a Burma without Buddhism before it, and some scholars now doubt the campaign happened at all — making the faith official is solid; importing it from nothing is a later embellishment.'] },
'伊德里斯·阿洛马': { g:'king', y:[1564,1596], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'卡涅姆·博尔努', n:['伊德里斯·阿洛马','Idris Alooma'],
  t:['他从奥斯曼帝国买来火枪,又雇了土耳其人来教怎么用。','He bought muskets from the Ottomans, and hired Turks to teach his men how to use them.'],
  a:[['向奥斯曼派出使团,引进火枪与炮,并雇用土耳其教官训练常备的火枪队','He sent embassies to the Ottomans, brought in muskets and cannon, and hired Turkish instructors to train a standing corps of musketeers'],
     ['大量修筑带墙的据点,把过去靠机动取胜的战争改成据点控制','He built walled strongpoints in numbers, turning a war won by movement into one of holding ground'],
     ['以伊斯兰教法整顿司法,并亲赴麦加朝觐、在当地设立供博尔努朝觐者使用的旅舍','He put the courts on a footing of Islamic law, made the pilgrimage to Mecca in person and endowed a hostel there for pilgrims from Bornu']],
  s:['他在位的三十余年是这个千年王国的顶点。他留下的记载远多于历代前王,不是因为打得多,而是因为身边带着史官——随军的艾哈迈德·本·福尔图写下两部战役编年史,撒南非洲极少有当事方自己留下的同时代记录,而不是外来旅行者的转述。火器与筑城这两样,他比西非多数政权早了一两百年用上,这也是博尔努能在此后两百年里持续存在的原因之一。','The thirty-odd years of his reign were the high point of a thousand-year state. Far more is known about him than about his predecessors — not because he fought more, but because he brought a historian along: Ahmad ibn Furtu, riding with the army, wrote two chronicles of the campaigns, and records kept from inside a sub-Saharan state, rather than by passing outsiders, are rare. Firearms and fortification he adopted a century or two before most West African powers, which is part of why Bornu was still standing two hundred years later.'] },
'萨拉丁': { g:'king', y:[1137,1193], ca:1, r:[1174,1193], c:'阿尤布王朝', n:['萨拉丁','Saladin'],
  t:['受命去守埃及的库尔德将领,最后自己当了埃及与叙利亚的主人。',
     'A Kurdish officer sent to defend Egypt who ended up master of both Egypt and Syria.'],
  a:[['1171年废去法蒂玛末代哈里发,埃及回归逊尼派','Deposed the last Fatimid caliph in 1171, returning Egypt to Sunni rule'],
     ['1187年哈丁战役几乎全歼耶路撒冷王国野战军,同年十月收复耶路撒冷','All but destroyed the field army of the kingdom of Jerusalem at Hattin in 1187 and took the city that October'],
     ['1192年与英王理查一世订约:圣城归穆斯林,沿海归十字军,基督徒可自由朝圣','Made terms with Richard I of England in 1192: the Holy City stayed Muslim, the coast went to the crusaders, and Christian pilgrimage stayed open']],
  s:['欧洲人与阿拉伯人各记住了一个萨拉丁:敌方笔下的「高贵异教徒」是中世纪就定型的,阿拉伯世界的民族英雄像却是近代才重新塑起——两个形象都不全是他本人。最实在的一条是:他没有留下私产,死时国库据记载不足以支付葬费。',
     'Europe and the Arab world each remember a Saladin of their own: the noble pagan of the enemy\'s books was fixed in the Middle Ages, while the Arab national hero was rebuilt only in modern times — and neither portrait is quite the man. The most solid fact is this: he left no private fortune, and the treasury at his death is reported to have been unable to cover his funeral.'] },
'拜巴尔': { g:'king', y:[1223,1277], ca:1, r:[1260,1277], c:'马穆鲁克', n:['拜巴尔','Baybars'],
  t:['被卖到埃及的钦察少年,后来当上苏丹,挡住了蒙古。',
     'A Kipchak boy sold into Egypt who became sultan — and stopped the Mongols.'],
  a:[['1260年阿音扎鲁特之战击败蒙古西征军','Beat the Mongol expeditionary force at Ain Jalut in 1260'],
     ['把巴格达陷落后逃出的阿拔斯后裔迎到开罗立为哈里发','Installed a surviving Abbasid in Cairo as caliph after Baghdad fell'],
     ['建成埃及与叙利亚的驿传网,急件三天可达大马士革','Built a courier network across Egypt and Syria that carried urgent dispatches to Damascus in three days']],
  s:['阿音扎鲁特的名声有他的一半——尽管现代研究提醒,蒙古主力当时已因大汗之死东撤,这一战的分量仍有争论。更实在的遗产是政权本身:他巩固的马穆鲁克国此后统治埃及二百六十余年。',
     'Half the fame of Ain Jalut is his — though modern scholarship reminds us the main Mongol force had already withdrawn east after the Great Khan died, and the battle\'s weight is still argued over. The solider legacy is the state itself: the Mamluk order he consolidated ruled Egypt for more than 260 years.'] },
'伊本·纳菲斯': { g:'sci', y:[1213,1288], c:'马穆鲁克', n:['伊本·纳菲斯','Ibn al-Nafis'],
  t:['他在开罗写下:血是先经过肺,才回到心脏另一侧的。',
     'Working in Cairo, he wrote that blood must pass through the lungs before it reaches the other side of the heart.'],
  a:[['指出血液从右心室经肺再入左心室,推翻了盖伦的「心隔有孔」说','Argued that blood goes from the right ventricle through the lungs to the left, against Galen\'s claim of pores in the septum'],
     ['写成《医典解剖学注》等大量医学著作,并在开罗行医、任院长','Wrote extensively on medicine and practised in Cairo, heading a hospital there'],
     ['主张医学结论要靠观察而非只靠前人权威','Held that medical conclusions should rest on observation rather than on the authorities alone']],
  s:['他对肺循环的描述比欧洲人早了约三百年——塞尔维特与科伦坡在16世纪才得出类似结论。这段文字1924年才在柏林的一份抄本里被重新发现,此前西方医学史完全不知道它的存在,也因此长期把这项发现只算在欧洲人头上。',
     'His account of the pulmonary circulation predates the European one by roughly three centuries — Servetus and Colombo reached similar conclusions only in the sixteenth. The passage was rediscovered in a Berlin manuscript in 1924; before that the Western history of medicine did not know it existed, and had credited the discovery to Europeans alone.'] },
'克里希纳提婆罗耶': { g:'king', y:[1471,1529], ca:1, r:[1509,1529], c:'维查耶纳伽尔', n:['克里希纳提婆罗耶','Krishnadevaraya'],
  t:['南印度最强的国王,自己也是诗人。',
     'The strongest king in southern India — and a poet in his own right.'],
  a:[['东征奥里萨连下坚城,1520 年又在赖久尔大破比贾布尔——在位二十年少有败绩','Took fortress after fortress campaigning east into Odisha, then broke Bijapur at Raichur in 1520 — in twenty years on the throne he scarcely lost a battle'],
     ['大量捐建神庙与水利工程,汉皮的许多建筑出自他治下','Endowed temples and waterworks on a large scale; much of what stands at Hampi dates from his reign'],
     ['用泰卢固语写成长诗《阿姆克塔玛利亚达》','Composed a long poem in Telugu, the Amuktamalyada']],
  s:['葡萄牙访客留下了他在位时首都的详细记载,市场、节庆与巨城的气象都写在里面。他本人用泰卢固语写诗,宫廷里泰卢固、卡纳达与泰米尔三种语言的文人都有位置。1565 年塔利科塔一败,这座城随之而去——废墟就是今天的汉皮。',
     'Portuguese visitors left detailed accounts of his capital — its markets, festivals and sheer scale are all in their pages. He wrote poetry in Telugu himself, and men of letters in Telugu, Kannada and Tamil all had a place at his court. One defeat at Talikota in 1565 took the city with it; the ruins are today\'s Hampi.'] },
'希瓦吉': { g:'war', y:[1630,1680], r:[1674,1680], c:'马拉塔', n:['希瓦吉','Shivaji'],
  t:['从夺一座座山地要塞起家,拖垮了莫卧儿二十余年的南征。',
     'He began by taking hill forts one at a time, and wore down twenty years of Mughal campaigning.'],
  a:[['以轻骑袭扰切断补给线,避免正面决战','Used light cavalry to cut supply lines and refused pitched battle'],
     ['沿西高止山建立要塞体系,1674年正式加冕为王','Built a network of forts along the Western Ghats and crowned himself king in 1674'],
     ['设八部大臣、建常备军与水师,不靠世袭封地维持','Set up eight ministries, a standing army and a navy, rather than relying on hereditary fiefs']],
  s:['奥朗则布压上帝国的家底南下,发誓拔掉这一家,打到自己快九十岁死在军中也没成。他身后传得最久的不是王位,而是两样东西:亲手夺下的那串山堡,和「绝不与强敌正面硬拼」的打法。',
     'Aurangzeb marched south with the weight of his empire, swearing to root the family out, and was still at it when he died in camp at nearly ninety. What he passed down longest was not a throne but two things: the chain of hill forts he took with his own hands, and the rule of never meeting a stronger enemy head-on.'] },
'孟尼利克二世': { g:'king', y:[1844,1913], r:[1889,1913], c:'埃塞俄比亚帝国', n:['孟尼利克二世','Menelik II'],
  t:['他在阿杜瓦击败了意大利远征军。',
     'At Adwa he beat an Italian expeditionary force.'],
  a:[['把咖啡、象牙换来的钱大都变成了欧洲军火','Turned the earnings from coffee and ivory mostly into European arms'],
     ['1896 年阿杜瓦一役,意大利人远远低估了对手——迎面而来的是一支人数数倍、枪炮齐整的大军','At Adwa in 1896 the Italians had badly underestimated their enemy — what met them was an army several times their size, fully armed'],
     ['迁都亚的斯亚贝巴,修铁路、开学校、通电报','Moved the capital to Addis Ababa and brought in railways, schools and the telegraph']],
  s:['这一仗打完,欧洲各国的公使馆很快开进了亚的斯亚贝巴——列强改用条约而不是军队和他打交道。埃塞俄比亚保住了独立,这场胜利后来成了整个大陆反抗殖民时共同引用的记忆。但独立并非从未中断:1936至1941年意大利仍占领了全境五年。',
     'After that battle the European legations soon opened in Addis Ababa — the powers now dealt with him by treaty rather than by army. Ethiopia kept its independence, and the victory became a memory the whole continent would later reach for in its struggles against colonial rule. That independence was not unbroken, however: Italy occupied the whole country from 1936 to 1941.'] },
'奥赛·图图': { g:'king', y:[1660,1717], ca:1, c:'阿散蒂', n:['奥赛·图图','Osei Tutu'],
  t:['他把分散的阿肯各邦联成一体,凭据是一张不许任何人坐的凳子。',
     'He bound the scattered Akan states into one, on the strength of a stool no one is allowed to sit on.'],
  a:[['与祭司奥科姆福·阿诺基一起以金凳为号召统一各部','With the priest Okomfo Anokye, used the golden stool to unite the clans'],
     ['1701年联军击败宗主登基拉,阿散蒂由附庸变主人','Beat their overlord Denkyira in 1701, turning vassal into master'],
     ['建立以库马西为中心的联邦结构与道路网','Built a federal structure and a road network centred on Kumasi']],
  s:['金凳不是王座——它被说成是全体阿散蒂人的灵魂所在,谁也不能坐上去。正因如此,1900年英国总督要求交出并坐上它,才会引发那场以它命名的战争。英国人始终没有拿到它——凳子的下落,阿散蒂人守口如瓶了二十年。阿散蒂赫内这一王位在加纳延续至今。',
     'The golden stool is no throne — it was held to be where the soul of all the Asante lives, and no one may sit on it — which is why the British governor\'s demand in 1900 to take it and sit on it set off the war named after it. The British never got it — for twenty years the Asante kept its whereabouts to themselves. The kingship itself continues in Ghana today.'] },
'李元昊': { g:'king', y:[1003,1048], r:[1038,1048], c:'西夏', n:['李元昊','Li Yuanhao'],
  t:['西夏的开国皇帝。他给自己的民族造了一套全新的文字。',
     'Founder of the Western Xia — and the man who had an entire script invented for his people.'],
  a:[['1038 年称帝建大夏,与宋、辽三足鼎立','Declared himself emperor in 1038, making a third power beside Song and Liao'],
     ['命野利仁荣创制西夏文,六千余字,笔画繁复','Commissioned the Tangut script: over six thousand characters, denser than Chinese'],
     ['三川口、好水川、定川寨三战皆胜宋军,迫使宋朝议和','Beat Song armies in three successive battles and forced a settlement']],
  s:['西夏文是历史上罕见的由国家凭空创制并大规模使用的文字,通行近两百年,元代以后失传,直到 20 世纪才被重新释读。西夏王陵与黑水城出土的西夏文献,是研究这个王朝的主要材料。',
     'Tangut is one of the very few scripts ever invented outright by a state and then actually used at scale. It ran for nearly two centuries, died out after the Mongol conquest, and was not deciphered again until the twentieth century.'] },
'完颜阿骨打': { g:'king', y:[1068,1123], r:[1115,1123], c:'金', n:['完颜阿骨打','Aguda'],
  t:['女真的开国皇帝。他起兵反辽时手上只有两千五百人。',
     'Founder of the Jin. He rose against the Liao with two thousand five hundred men.'],
  a:[['1114 年起兵反辽,次年称帝建金','Rebelled in 1114 and proclaimed the Jin dynasty the following year'],
     ['创制女真文字','Had a Jurchen script created'],
     ['建立猛安谋克制:平时是部落,战时即是军队','Set up the meng\'an-mouke system, in which a clan in peacetime was a regiment in war']],
  s:['从两千五百人到灭掉统治草原两百年的辽朝,只用了十年,是中国历史上崛起最快的政权之一。猛安谋克制后来被清朝的八旗制度继承。金朝控制中国北方一百二十年,把宋朝赶到了长江以南。',
     'From 2,500 men to the destruction of a two-hundred-year-old empire in ten years — one of the fastest rises in Chinese history. His clan-regiment system was the direct ancestor of the Manchu banners. The Jin held northern China for 120 years and pushed the Song beyond the Yangtze.'] },
'金世宗': { g:'king', y:[1123,1189], r:[1161,1189], c:'金', n:['金世宗','Emperor Shizong of Jin'],
  t:['被宋朝人称为"小尧舜"的女真皇帝。',
     'The Jurchen emperor whom even the Song called a sage-king.'],
  a:[['1161 年在海陵王南征失败之际即位,随即与南宋议和,结束战争','Took the throne in 1161 as his predecessor\'s invasion collapsed, and immediately made peace with the Song'],
     ['减赋税、清理冤狱、整顿吏治,史称"大定之治"','Cut taxes, reopened wrongful convictions and cleaned up the bureaucracy'],
     ['提倡学女真语、译汉籍为女真文,试图阻止女真人被汉化','Pushed his people to keep speaking Jurchen and had Chinese classics translated into it, trying to slow their assimilation']],
  s:['大定年间是金朝最稳定富庶的时期,人口与财政都达到顶点。他是少数被汉族史家高度评价的非汉族君主。他保存女真文化的努力最终失败——这个先例后来被清朝反复引以为鉴。',
     'His twenty-nine-year reign was the Jin at its most prosperous, with population and revenue at their peak, and he is one of the few non-Chinese rulers whom Chinese historians praise without reservation. His campaign to preserve Jurchen identity failed — a precedent the Qing would study anxiously five centuries later.'] },
'朱元璋': { g:'king', y:[1328,1398], r:[1368,1398], c:'明', n:['朱元璋','Zhu Yuanzhang'],
  t:['讨过饭、当过和尚,最后当了皇帝。中国历史上出身最低的开国之君。',
     'Beggar, then monk, then emperor — the lowest-born founder of a dynasty in Chinese history.'],
  a:[['父母兄长在饥荒中饿死,他入皇觉寺为僧,后托钵行乞三年','His parents and eldest brother starved in a famine; he entered a monastery, then begged on the roads for three years'],
     ['1368 年称帝,同年攻克大都,把蒙古朝廷赶回草原','Proclaimed the Ming in 1368 and took the Mongol capital the same year'],
     ['废丞相、设锦衣卫、编《大明律》,并大杀功臣','Abolished the chancellorship, created the secret police, issued the Ming Code — and purged his own founding officers']],
  s:['中国历史上唯一一个从赤贫农民做到开国皇帝的人。他废除丞相制度,结束了中国实行一千六百年的宰相制——皇权自此不再有制度性制衡,这一格局延续到清末。',
     'The only destitute peasant ever to found a Chinese dynasty. In abolishing the chancellorship he ended sixteen centuries of a formal check on the throne; nothing institutional stood between emperor and empire again until 1911.'] },
'永乐帝': { g:'king', y:[1360,1424], r:[1402,1424], c:'明', n:['永乐帝','the Yongle Emperor'],
  t:['从侄子手里抢了皇位,然后干成了明朝最大的几件事。',
     'He took the throne from his own nephew, then did the biggest things the Ming ever did.'],
  a:[['1399—1402 年靖难之役,以藩王身份夺取皇位','Won a three-year civil war against his nephew and seized the throne'],
     ['营建紫禁城,1421 年迁都北京','Built the Forbidden City and moved the capital there in 1421'],
     ['派郑和七下西洋,组织编纂《永乐大典》','Sent Zheng He on seven voyages and commissioned the Yongle Encyclopedia']],
  s:['紫禁城是世界上现存规模最大的宫殿建筑群,1987 年列入世界遗产。《永乐大典》两万两千余卷、约三亿七千万字,在《不列颠百科全书》问世前一直是世界上最大的百科全书,今存不足百分之四。他迁都北京,定下了此后六百年中国的首都位置。',
     'The Forbidden City is the largest surviving palace complex on earth, World Heritage since 1987. The Yongle Encyclopedia ran to 22,000-odd volumes and some 370 million characters — the largest encyclopedia in the world until the Britannica, of which under four per cent survives. And his move north fixed the location of China\'s capital for the next six hundred years.'] },
'王阳明': { g:'mind', y:[1472,1529], c:'明', n:['王阳明','Wang Yangming'],
  t:['被贬到贵州龙场的驿站,在那里想通一件事,开创了心学。',
     'Banished to a post station in the mountains of Guizhou, he worked something out — and founded a school of thought.'],
  a:[['1508 年"龙场悟道",提出"心即理"——道理不在外物,在自己心里','In 1508 he concluded that principle is not out in the world but in the mind itself'],
     ['提出"知行合一":知道而不做,等于不知道','Argued that knowing and doing are one: to know and not act is not to know'],
     ['平定宁王之乱,四十三天结束一场蓄谋十年的叛乱','Crushed a decade-planned princely rebellion in forty-three days']],
  s:['心学是儒家在朱熹之后最大的一次转向,明末影响极大,并深刻影响日本——明治维新的许多志士都是阳明学的信徒。他是中国历史上罕见的"立德、立功、立言"三者兼备之人。',
     'His was the great turn in Confucianism after Zhu Xi, dominant in the late Ming and hugely influential in Japan, where many of the samurai who made the Meiji Restoration were his followers. Chinese tradition holds that a man may achieve virtue, achievement or words; he is one of the rare few credited with all three.'] },
'康熙': { g:'king', y:[1654,1722], r:[1661,1722], c:'清', n:['康熙','the Kangxi Emperor'],
  t:['八岁登基,十五岁擒鳌拜,在位 61 年——中国历史上在位最久的皇帝。',
     'On the throne at eight, in control at fifteen, and there for sixty-one years — the longest reign in Chinese history.'],
  a:[['平三藩、收台湾、三征噶尔丹,奠定清朝疆域','Put down the Three Feudatories, took Taiwan, and campaigned three times against the Dzungars'],
     ['1689 年与俄国签《尼布楚条约》','Signed the Treaty of Nerchinsk with Russia in 1689'],
     ['主持编《康熙字典》《古今图书集成》,向传教士学几何与天文','Commissioned the Kangxi Dictionary and a vast encyclopedia, and studied geometry and astronomy with Jesuit tutors']],
  s:['61 年是有确切纪年以来中国皇帝在位时间的最高纪录。《尼布楚条约》是中国第一次以对等国家身份与欧洲列强缔约,正式文本用拉丁文。《康熙字典》收字四万七千余个,此后两百年一直是汉字的标准字书。',
     'Sixty-one years is the record for any Chinese emperor with a firm date. Nerchinsk was the first treaty China ever signed with a European power as an equal, its official text in Latin. And his dictionary, with over 47,000 characters, was the standard reference for the next two centuries.'] },
'乾隆': { g:'king', y:[1711,1799], r:[1735,1796], c:'清', n:['乾隆','the Qianlong Emperor'],
  t:['中国疆域最大的时候是在他手上,闭关的格局也是他定的。',
     'China reached its greatest extent under him — and he also set the terms on which it closed itself off.'],
  a:[['平定准噶尔与大小和卓,新疆并入版图,清朝疆域达到最大','Destroyed the Dzungars and annexed what became Xinjiang, taking the empire to its largest'],
     ['主持编《四库全书》,收书三千四百六十余种,同时禁毁书籍逾万部','Commissioned the Siku Quanshu, gathering some 3,460 titles — and banned or destroyed over ten thousand others in the process'],
     ['1793 年拒绝英国马戛尔尼使团的通商请求','Turned away Lord Macartney\'s trade mission in 1793']],
  s:['清朝疆域在他手上约一千三百万平方公里,是中国历史上的最大值之一。《四库全书》约八亿字,是中国历史上最大的丛书;但编书的同时也是规模最大的一次文字清查。马戛尔尼被拒后不到五十年,英国用军舰打开了同一扇门。',
     'The empire covered some 13 million square kilometres under him, among the largest in Chinese history. The Siku Quanshu, at roughly 800 million characters, is the biggest collection ever compiled in China — and compiling it doubled as the most thorough literary purge ever conducted. Fewer than fifty years after Macartney was refused, Britain opened the same door with gunboats.'] },
'曹雪芹': { g:'art', y:[1715,1763], ca:1, c:'清', n:['曹雪芹','Cao Xueqin'],
  t:['家道中落后在北京西郊靠卖画和朋友接济过日子,写了一部没写完的小说。',
     'Ruined, living on the western outskirts of Beijing off sold paintings and friends\' charity, he wrote a novel he never finished.'],
  a:[['出身江宁织造世家,少年时极富贵,十三岁前后家产被抄','Born into the family that ran the imperial silk works at Nanjing; the estate was confiscated when he was about thirteen'],
     ['"披阅十载,增删五次",写出《红楼梦》前八十回','Ten years of reading over and five rewritings produced the first eighty chapters of Dream of the Red Chamber'],
     ['四十余岁贫病而死,书稿未完','Died in his forties, poor and ill, with the book unfinished']],
  s:['《红楼梦》是中国古典小说的顶峰,写了四百多个有名有姓的人物。围绕它形成了一门专门的学问"红学",是唯一以单部小说为对象的中国学科。全书已译成三十余种语言。',
     'Dream of the Red Chamber is the summit of the Chinese novel, with over four hundred named characters. An entire academic field, "Redology", exists to study it — the only Chinese discipline devoted to a single work of fiction. It has been translated into more than thirty languages.'] },
'孙中山': { g:'state', y:[1866,1925], c:'民国', n:['孙中山','Sun Yat-sen'],
  t:['起义失败了十次,第十一次成功了。',
     'Ten risings failed. The eleventh worked.'],
  a:[['1894 年创立兴中会,此后十余年组织多次武装起义,均告失败','Founded his first revolutionary society in 1894 and spent a decade and a half on failed uprisings'],
     ['1911 年武昌起义成功,次年就任中华民国临时大总统','The Wuchang rising of 1911 succeeded; he became provisional president the next year'],
     ['提出三民主义:民族、民权、民生','Formulated the Three Principles of the People: nationhood, rights, livelihood']],
  s:['辛亥革命结束了中国两千一百三十二年的帝制。他是海峡两岸同时公开尊崇的极少数近代人物之一——大陆称"革命先行者",中国台湾称"国父"。以他命名的道路、公园与建筑遍布华人世界。',
     'The 1911 revolution ended 2,132 years of imperial rule. He is one of the very few modern figures honoured openly on both sides of the Taiwan Strait — "forerunner of the revolution" on the mainland, "father of the nation" in Taiwan, China — and streets, parks and halls across the Chinese-speaking world carry his name.'] },
'蒋介石': { g:'state', y:[1887,1975], c:'民国', n:['蒋介石','Chiang Kai-shek'],
  t:['领导中国打完了八年抗战,又输掉了内战。',
     'He led China through eight years of war against Japan, and then lost the civil war.'],
  a:[['1926 年率国民革命军北伐,两年内名义上统一中国','Launched the Northern Expedition in 1926 and nominally unified the country within two years'],
     ['1937—1945 年领导对日抗战,中国成为二战同盟国四强之一','Led the resistance to Japan from 1937 to 1945, with China counted among the four principal Allied powers'],
     ['1949 年内战失败,率国民政府迁台','Lost the civil war in 1949 and moved his government to Taiwan']],
  s:['抗战期间中国牵制了日本陆军主力,并在 1945 年成为联合国安理会五个常任理事国之一。迁台后推行的土地改革与义务教育,为中国台湾后来的经济起飞奠定了基础。海峡两岸对他的评价至今差异极大。',
     'China tied down the bulk of the Japanese army through those years and emerged in 1945 as one of the five permanent members of the UN Security Council. The land reform and compulsory schooling his government carried out in Taiwan, China underpinned its later economic take-off. Assessments of him still differ sharply across the Strait.'] },
'鲁迅': { g:'art', y:[1881,1936], c:'民国', n:['鲁迅','Lu Xun'],
  t:['学了两年医,决定改用文章救人。',
     'He studied medicine for two years, then decided to treat his countrymen with essays instead.'],
  a:[['在日本看到中国人围观同胞被处决的幻灯片,弃医从文','In Japan he saw a lantern slide of Chinese watching a compatriot executed, and gave up medicine'],
     ['1918 年发表《狂人日记》,中国第一篇现代白话小说','Published "A Madman\'s Diary" in 1918 — the first modern Chinese story in the vernacular'],
     ['写《阿Q正传》《呐喊》《彷徨》,一生写杂文七百余篇','Wrote The True Story of Ah Q and two landmark collections, plus over seven hundred essays']],
  s:['《狂人日记》标志中国现代文学的开端,白话文自此取代文言成为书面语主流。他创造的"阿Q"成了汉语常用词。他是中国大陆语文课本收录最多的现代作家,作品已译成五十余种语言。',
     '"A Madman\'s Diary" marks the beginning of modern Chinese literature; after it, the vernacular replaced classical Chinese as the written language. The character Ah Q entered the language as a common noun. He is the modern author most represented in mainland Chinese school textbooks, and has been translated into more than fifty languages.'] },
'毛泽东': { g:'state', y:[1893,1976], c:'共和国', n:['毛泽东','Mao Zedong'],
  t:['农民出身,领导中国共产党赢得内战,建立了中华人民共和国。',
     'A farmer\'s son who led the Chinese Communist Party to victory in the civil war and founded the People\'s Republic.'],
  a:[['1927 年秋收起义失败后上井冈山,提出以农村包围城市','After a failed rising in 1927 he took to the Jinggang mountains and built a strategy of surrounding cities from the countryside'],
     ['1934—1935 年长征,行程两万五千里,红军由八万人剩下不足一万','On the Long March of 1934-35 the Red Army covered some 9,000 km and came out with fewer than 10,000 of its 80,000 men'],
     ['1949 年 10 月 1 日宣告中华人民共和国成立','Declared the People\'s Republic on 1 October 1949']],
  s:['他结束了自 1840 年以来中国的分裂与外国势力割据,建立起统一的中央政权。执政期间中国建成独立的工业体系、普及基础教育与医疗,人均预期寿命从约 35 岁升至 65 岁左右;同期的大跃进与文化大革命则造成严重后果。中共 1981 年的正式决议对他的评价是"功绩是第一位的,错误是第二位的"。',
     'He ended the fragmentation and foreign concessions that had run since 1840 and established a unified central state. Under his rule China built an independent industrial base and extended basic schooling and health care, with life expectancy rising from about 35 to around 65; the Great Leap Forward and the Cultural Revolution of the same period caused severe harm. The Party\'s formal 1981 assessment holds that his achievements came first and his mistakes second.'] },
'邓小平': { g:'state', y:[1904,1997], c:'共和国', n:['邓小平','Deng Xiaoping'],
  t:['三次被打倒,三次复出。第三次复出时他七十三岁。',
     'Purged three times, back three times. He was seventy-three at the third return.'],
  a:[['1978 年十一届三中全会,确立改革开放路线','Set the country on the reform-and-opening course at the Party plenum of 1978'],
     ['农村包产到户,设深圳等经济特区,允许私营经济','Contracted farmland back to households, opened special economic zones including Shenzhen, and legalised private business'],
     ['提出"一国两制",作为 1997 年香港回归的方案','Proposed "one country, two systems", the framework for Hong Kong\'s 1997 handover']],
  s:['1978 年后的四十年间,中国 GDP 增长约八十倍,按世界银行标准脱离极端贫困的人口超过八亿,是人类历史上规模最大的一次减贫。他两次(1978、1985)被《时代》周刊选为年度人物。',
     'In the four decades after 1978 China\'s GDP grew roughly eightyfold and more than 800 million people rose above the World Bank\'s extreme-poverty line — the largest reduction in poverty in human history. Time named him Man of the Year twice, in 1978 and 1985.'] },
'圣德太子': { g:'state', y:[574,622], c:'古代日本', n:['圣德太子','Prince Shōtoku'],
  t:['他把中国的制度整套搬进日本,还写了一封让隋炀帝很不高兴的国书。',
     'He imported Chinese institutions wholesale into Japan — and sent a letter that annoyed the Chinese emperor.'],
  a:[['603 年定冠位十二阶,按才能而非门第授官','Established twelve court ranks in 603, awarded for ability rather than birth'],
     ['604 年颁《十七条宪法》,日本第一部成文政治纲领','Issued the Seventeen Article Constitution in 604, Japan\'s first written statement of government'],
     ['607 年国书称"日出处天子致书日没处天子",隋炀帝览之不悦','His 607 letter opened "from the Son of Heaven where the sun rises to the Son of Heaven where it sets"; the Sui emperor was not amused']],
  s:['他确立了日本以中国为师的方向,遣隋使与遣唐使此后延续两百余年。冠位十二阶与《十七条宪法》是日本从部族联合走向中央集权国家的起点。他所建的法隆寺是世界上现存最古老的木结构建筑,1993 年成为日本首批世界遗产。',
     'He set Japan on a course of learning from China that ran through two centuries of official missions. His rank system and constitution began the country\'s move from a tribal confederation to a centralised state. The Hōryū-ji temple he founded holds the oldest wooden buildings standing anywhere on earth, and became one of Japan\'s first World Heritage Sites in 1993.'] },
'德川家康': { g:'king', y:[1543,1616], c:'江户日本', n:['德川家康','Tokugawa Ieyasu'],
  t:['他熬死了所有对手。日本战国最后的赢家,开创了二百六十年的和平。',
     'He outlived everyone. The last man standing in Japan\'s warring century, and the founder of 260 years of peace.'],
  a:[['1600 年关原之战击败石田三成,取得全国实权','Won at Sekigahara in 1600 and took effective control of the country'],
     ['1603 年受封征夷大将军,在江户(今东京)开幕府','Was appointed shogun in 1603 and set up his government at Edo, now Tokyo'],
     ['1615 年大坂之战消灭丰臣氏,统一彻底完成','Destroyed the Toyotomi at Osaka in 1615, completing the unification']],
  s:['江户幕府持续二百六十五年,是日本历史上最长的和平时期,城市、商业与町人文化在这期间成熟。他选定的江户在明治维新后改名东京,至今是日本首都。锁国政策也始于这一幕府,一直持续到 1853 年黑船来航。',
     'The Tokugawa shogunate lasted 265 years, the longest peace in Japanese history, during which cities, commerce and a distinctive townsman culture came into their own. The Edo he chose was renamed Tokyo after 1868 and is the capital still. The closed-country policy also began under his house, and held until Perry\'s ships arrived in 1853.'] },
'明治天皇': { g:'king', y:[1852,1912], r:[1867,1912], c:'近现代日本', n:['明治天皇','Emperor Meiji'],
  t:['他即位时日本还在幕府统治下,他去世时日本已经打赢了俄国。',
     'When he came to the throne Japan was ruled by a shogun. When he died it had defeated Russia.'],
  a:[['1868 年明治维新,废幕府、还政天皇,颁《五条御誓文》','The Restoration of 1868 abolished the shogunate and returned power to the throne'],
     ['废藩置县、殖产兴业、征兵制、义务教育','Replaced the domains with prefectures, industrialised, conscripted an army and made schooling compulsory'],
     ['1889 年颁《大日本帝国宪法》,亚洲第一部近代成文宪法','Promulgated the 1889 constitution, the first modern written constitution in Asia']],
  s:['日本是非西方国家中第一个成功完成工业化的例子,四十余年间从被迫开国走到列强之列。1905 年战胜俄国,是近代第一次亚洲国家击败欧洲列强,对亚洲各国的民族主义影响极大。同一套体制也把日本带向了此后的对外扩张。',
     'Japan was the first non-Western country to industrialise successfully, going from forced opening to great-power status in about forty years. Its 1905 victory over Russia was the first defeat of a European power by an Asian one in modern times, and electrified nationalists across Asia. The same system also carried Japan into decades of expansion abroad.'] },

'苏格拉底': { g:'mind', y:[-470,-399], c:'古希腊', n:['苏格拉底','Socrates'],
  t:['他一个字也没写过。我们知道的他,全靠学生转述。',
     'He never wrote a word. Everything we know of him comes from his students.'],
  a:[['在雅典街头拉住人就问"什么是正义""什么是勇敢",问到对方自相矛盾','Stopped people in the street to ask what justice was, what courage was — and kept asking until they contradicted themselves'],
     ['说自己唯一知道的就是自己一无所知','Said the only thing he knew was that he knew nothing'],
     ['前 399 年被控"腐蚀青年、不敬神明",拒绝逃亡,饮鸩而死','Tried in 399 BCE for corrupting the young and impiety; refused to flee, and drank hemlock']],
  s:['他把哲学从"世界由什么构成"转向"人应该怎么活",这个转向被称为"苏格拉底转向"。以追问定义、逼出矛盾为方法的"苏格拉底式提问",至今是欧美法学院和商学院的标准教学法。',
     'He turned philosophy from what the world is made of to how a person should live — the turn is named after him. And the method of relentless questioning until a definition breaks is still the standard teaching mode in Western law and business schools.'] },
'柏拉图': { g:'mind', y:[-427,-347], c:'古希腊', n:['柏拉图','Plato'],
  t:['苏格拉底的学生,亚里士多德的老师。他办的学园开了九百年。',
     'Socrates\' student, Aristotle\'s teacher — and founder of a school that ran for nine centuries.'],
  a:[['前 387 年前后创办阿卡德米学园,西方最早的高等学府之一','Founded the Academy around 387 BCE, among the first institutions of higher learning in the West'],
     ['提出理念论:我们看到的一切都是完美原型的影子','Argued that everything we see is a shadow of a perfect form'],
     ['写《理想国》,用对话体讨论正义、教育与政体','Wrote the Republic, arguing about justice, education and government in dialogue form']],
  s:['20 世纪哲学家怀特海说:整部西方哲学史不过是对柏拉图的一系列脚注。他的著作是古希腊哲学家中唯一完整流传下来的,"学园"(Academy)一词也源自他学园的所在地。',
     'Whitehead\'s line still stands: the European philosophical tradition is a series of footnotes to Plato. His is the only complete body of work by any Greek philosopher to survive, and the word "academy" comes from the grove where he taught.'] },
'图拉真': { g:'king', y:[53,117], r:[98,117], c:'罗马帝国', n:['图拉真','Trajan'],
  t:['罗马版图最大的时候,是在他手上。他也是第一个出生在意大利之外的皇帝。',
     'Rome reached its greatest extent under him — and he was the first emperor born outside Italy.'],
  a:[['两次达契亚战争(101—106)征服今罗马尼亚,缴获的黄金支撑了罗马财政多年','Conquered Dacia — modern Romania — in two wars, and its gold funded Rome for years'],
     ['114—117 年东征帕提亚,一度打到波斯湾','Campaigned east against Parthia and briefly reached the Persian Gulf'],
     ['建图拉真广场、图拉真柱,并大规模修路、建港、办救济贫童的基金','Built his forum and column, and financed roads, harbours and a welfare fund for poor children']],
  s:['罗马疆域在 117 年达到约五百万平方公里的顶点,此后再未超过。元老院给他"最佳元首"的称号,此后三百年新皇帝即位时都会被祝愿"比奥古斯都幸运,比图拉真优秀"。图拉真柱上的浮雕是研究罗马军队最重要的图像材料。',
     'In 117 the empire covered some five million square kilometres, a peak it never passed again. The Senate named him optimus princeps, and for three centuries afterwards each new emperor was wished "luckier than Augustus, better than Trajan". The reliefs spiralling up his column remain the single most important picture of the Roman army.'] },
'查士丁尼': { g:'king', y:[482,565], r:[527,565], c:'拜占庭', n:['查士丁尼','Justinian I'],
  t:['他想把罗马帝国重新拼起来,差一点就做到了。',
     'He tried to put the Roman Empire back together, and came close.'],
  a:[['派贝利撒留收复北非、意大利与西班牙南部,地中海一度重新成为罗马的内海','Sent Belisarius to retake North Africa, Italy and southern Spain, making the Mediterranean a Roman lake again'],
     ['组织法学家编纂《民法大全》,把一千年的罗马法整理成一部','Had jurists compile the Corpus Juris Civilis, condensing a thousand years of Roman law'],
     ['532 年尼卡暴动后重建圣索菲亚大教堂,五年建成','Rebuilt Hagia Sophia after the Nika riots of 532 — finished in five years']],
  s:['《民法大全》是欧洲大陆法系的直接源头,今天法国、德国、日本乃至中国的民法都可以追到它。圣索菲亚大教堂的穹顶跨度三十一米,是此后近千年里最大的帆拱穹顶,1985 年列入世界遗产。',
     'The Corpus Juris Civilis is the direct source of the continental civil-law tradition — French, German, Japanese and Chinese civil codes all trace back to it. Hagia Sophia\'s dome spans 31 metres, unmatched for nearly a thousand years, and became World Heritage in 1985.'] },
'巴西尔二世': { g:'king', y:[958,1025], r:[976,1025], c:'拜占庭', n:['巴西尔二世','Basil II'],
  t:['在位 49 年,拜占庭在位最久的皇帝。他把帝国带到了最强。',
     'Forty-nine years on the throne, the longest of any Byzantine emperor, and the empire at its strongest.'],
  a:[['与保加利亚打了近三十年,1018 年彻底征服,得名"保加利亚人屠夫"','Fought Bulgaria for close to thirty years and finally destroyed it in 1018, earning the name "Bulgar-slayer"'],
     ['压制大地主兼并,保护自耕农与国家税基','Broke the great landowners\' land-grabbing to protect smallholders and the tax base'],
     ['988 年与基辅罗斯联姻,弗拉基米尔大公受洗,罗斯皈依东正教','Married his sister to the prince of Kiev in 988, whose baptism brought the Rus into Orthodoxy']],
  s:['拜占庭在他手上疆域与国库都达到中世纪的顶点,国库留下约二十万磅黄金。基辅罗斯的皈依决定了俄罗斯、乌克兰、白俄罗斯此后一千年的宗教与文化归属,影响一直延续到今天。',
     'The empire under him reached its medieval peak in both territory and treasury, leaving some 200,000 pounds of gold in reserve. The conversion of the Rus settled the religious and cultural alignment of Russia, Ukraine and Belarus for the next thousand years.'] },
'查理曼': { g:'king', y:[742,814], r:[768,814], c:'中世纪西欧', n:['查理曼','Charlemagne'],
  t:['西罗马灭亡三百年后,他成了西欧第一个皇帝。',
     'Three centuries after the fall of Rome in the west, he became western Europe\'s first emperor.'],
  a:[['四十余年间几乎年年出征,统一今法国、德国、意大利北部与西班牙东北','Campaigned almost every year for forty years, uniting what is now France, Germany, northern Italy and northeastern Spain'],
     ['800 年圣诞在罗马由教皇加冕为"罗马人的皇帝"','Was crowned Emperor of the Romans by the Pope on Christmas Day, 800'],
     ['召集学者推行加洛林文艺复兴,创制加洛林小写体','Gathered scholars for the Carolingian renaissance and introduced a clear new lowercase script']],
  s:['他被称为"欧洲之父";法、德两国都把他算作自己历史的起点,今天的欧盟总部所在地亚琛正是他的都城,欧盟的"查理曼奖"以他命名。加洛林小写体是今天全世界拉丁字母小写形态的直接祖先。',
     'He is called the father of Europe: France and Germany both begin their national histories with him, the EU\'s Charlemagne Prize carries his name, and his capital Aachen sits at the heart of the modern union. The lowercase script his scholars designed is the direct ancestor of the small letters used worldwide today.'] },
'阿奎那': { g:'mind', y:[1225,1274], c:'中世纪西欧', n:['阿奎那','Thomas Aquinas'],
  t:['他用亚里士多德的方法论证上帝,把理性和信仰接在了一起。',
     'He used Aristotle\'s logic to argue for God, and welded reason to faith.'],
  a:[['写《神学大全》,提出上帝存在的五个论证','Wrote the Summa Theologica, with its five arguments for the existence of God'],
     ['主张理性与信仰不冲突:两者都通向真理,只是路径不同','Held that reason and faith cannot conflict, since both lead to truth by different roads'],
     ['系统阐述自然法:有些法则不靠人定,靠理性就能认识','Set out natural law: some rules hold whether or not anyone legislates them']],
  s:['1879 年教皇利奥十三世宣布他的学说为天主教官方哲学,至今仍是。他阐述的自然法概念经格劳秀斯、洛克进入近代政治思想,是《美国独立宣言》"不言自明的权利"的源头之一。',
     'In 1879 Pope Leo XIII declared his system the official philosophy of the Catholic Church, and it remains so. His natural law passed through Grotius and Locke into modern political thought, and stands behind the "self-evident" rights of the American Declaration of Independence.'] },
'美第奇家族': { g:'state', y:[1397,1737], yk:'a', c:'文艺复兴意大利', n:['美第奇家族','the Medici'],
  t:['一个银行家族。他们花钱养出了文艺复兴的一大半。',
     'A banking family that paid for most of the Renaissance.'],
  a:[['1397 年创办美第奇银行,一度是欧洲最大的银行,并管理教廷财务','Founded their bank in 1397; it became the largest in Europe and handled the papacy\'s money'],
     ['资助达·芬奇、米开朗基罗、波提切利、伽利略等人','Paid for Leonardo, Michelangelo, Botticelli and Galileo, among others'],
     ['家族出了四位教皇、两位法国王后,统治佛罗伦萨约三百年','Produced four popes and two queens of France, and ruled Florence for some three centuries']],
  s:['文艺复兴之所以集中爆发在佛罗伦萨,持续的私人资助是关键条件之一。他们收藏的艺术品构成今天乌菲兹美术馆的核心,家族最后一位成员立下遗嘱:全部藏品永远留在佛罗伦萨,不得变卖或移出。',
     'The Renaissance concentrated in Florence in part because private money there was patient and continuous. Their collection is the core of the Uffizi today — the last of the line willed that every piece stay in Florence forever, never to be sold or moved.'] },
'马丁·路德': { g:'faith', y:[1483,1546], c:'勃兰登堡·普鲁士', n:['马丁·路德','Martin Luther'],
    t:['他本来只想辩论一件具体的事,结果把整个西方基督教劈成了两半。','He meant to argue one specific point, and split Western Christianity in two.'],
    a:[['1517 年在维滕贝格贴出九十五条论纲,反对教会卖赎罪券——交钱可以减免罪的惩罚,收来的钱拿去修圣彼得大教堂','In 1517 at Wittenberg he posted ninety-five theses against the sale of indulgences: pay, and the punishment for your sins is reduced — and the money went to build St Peter\'s'],
       ['真正的分歧比赎罪券大得多:谁有权解释《圣经》。他的答案是每个信徒自己,于是他花十来周把《新约》译成德文,后来又译完《旧约》——你得让人读得懂,他才谈得上自己判断','The real disagreement was larger than indulgences: who may interpret the Bible. His answer was every believer, so he spent some ten weeks turning the New Testament into German and later finished the Old — people must be able to read it before they can judge for themselves'],
       ['1521 年在沃尔姆斯帝国议会上,当着皇帝的面拒绝收回自己写的东西。此后他被通缉,躲在瓦尔特堡里译经','At the Diet of Worms in 1521 he refused, in front of the emperor, to take back what he had written. Outlawed after it, he translated scripture in hiding at the Wartburg']],
    s:['他那本德文《圣经》顺带把一种方言变成了通用的德语书面语,而「人人都该自己读」这个要求推着新教地区大办识字。方法上他做的其实是文艺复兴学者那一套:回到原文、自己核对,只不过对象从古罗马的书换成了《圣经》。','His German Bible turned one dialect into the written German everyone came to use, and the demand that each person read for himself pushed Protestant regions into teaching reading in earnest. His method was the one the humanist scholars had worked out — go back to the original and check it yourself — applied to scripture instead of to ancient Rome.'] },
  '哥白尼': { g:'sci', y:[1473,1543], c:'波兰-立陶宛', n:['哥白尼','Nicolaus Copernicus'],
    t:['他把地球从宇宙中心挪开,而且等到临死那年才敢把书印出来。','He moved the earth out of the middle of the universe — and waited until the year he died to print it.'],
    a:[['他的本职是教会的教士与行政人员,天文是业余做的:在弗龙堡的一座塔楼上断断续续观测了二十来年','His job was canon and administrator for the church; astronomy was what he did besides, observing on and off for some twenty years from a tower at Frombork'],
       ['《天体运行论》1543 年出版,据说样书送到时他已在病榻上。书里说太阳不动、地球每天自转一圈、每年绕太阳一圈','On the Revolutions of the Heavenly Spheres came out in 1543; the finished copy is said to have reached him on his deathbed. In it the sun stands still, and the earth turns once a day and goes round the sun once a year'],
       ['他的模型其实算得并不比旧的准——因为他仍然假设轨道是正圆,得靠一堆小圆圈去凑。真正让它算得准的是开普勒:轨道是椭圆的','His model did not in fact predict better than the old one, because he still assumed perfect circles and had to patch them with more small circles. What made it accurate was Kepler: the orbits are ellipses']],
    s:['一个更接近真相的想法,刚提出来的时候可以是「算得还不如旧的准」。它赢不是因为一上来就好用,是因为它更简单、而且后来的人能在它上面接着改。同一年维萨里出版了靠亲手解剖画成的人体解剖图——1543 年这一年,天上和身体里的旧说法同时被人动了。','An idea nearer the truth can, when first put forward, predict worse than the one it replaces. It won not because it worked better at once but because it was simpler and because others could go on building on it. In the same year Vesalius published an anatomy drawn from bodies he had opened himself. In 1543 the old accounts of the heavens and of the body were both disturbed at once.'] },
  '伽利略': { g:'sci', y:[1564,1642], c:'文艺复兴意大利', n:['伽利略','Galileo Galilei'],
    t:['他把望远镜对准天空,看到了不该存在的东西。','He turned the telescope on the sky and saw things that were not supposed to be there.'],
    a:[['1609 年听说荷兰有人做出了望远镜,他自己磨镜片做了一具更好的。第二年他看见木星旁边有四颗小星,几夜之间位置变来变去——那是绕着木星转的卫星,说明不是所有东西都绕着地球转','Hearing in 1609 that someone in the Netherlands had made a spyglass, he ground lenses and built a better one. The next year he saw four small stars beside Jupiter shifting position from night to night: moons going round Jupiter, and so not everything went round the earth'],
       ['他还看见月亮上有山有坑(不是完美的球)、银河其实是数不清的星。他把这些写成一本薄薄的小册子《星际信使》,几个月内传遍欧洲。那年秋天他又看见金星像月亮一样有盈亏——这一条要再过三年才发表出来','He also saw mountains and pits on the moon — not a perfect sphere — and the Milky Way resolving into countless stars. He put it in a thin pamphlet, the Starry Messenger, and within months it was all over Europe. That autumn he watched Venus go through phases like the moon, but that one he did not publish for another three years'],
       ['1633 年他因为在书里替日心说辩护、违反了十七年前教会下的禁令而受审,判词写的是「有很重的异端嫌疑」;他被迫认错,余生软禁在家。但他在软禁期间写完了讲运动的那本书,手稿被偷带出意大利,1638 年在荷兰出版','In 1633 he was tried for defending the sun-centred view in print, against a ban the Church had laid down seventeen years earlier; the verdict called him vehemently suspected of heresy. He was made to recant and kept under house arrest for the rest of his life. He finished his book on motion under that arrest; the manuscript was smuggled out of Italy and printed in the Netherlands in 1638']],
    s:['他真正的贡献是把「争论」换成了「你自己来看」——望远镜可以借给对方,实验可以让人重做一遍。而他被禁止出版之后写的那本书居然能在荷兰印出来,这件事本身也说明了一点:欧洲当时已经不止一个说了算的权威,任何一处封杀不了所有地方。','What he really changed was replacing argument with come and look: a telescope can be handed to the other side, an experiment can be repeated by anyone. That the book he wrote after being forbidden to publish could still be printed in the Netherlands says something too — Europe by then had more than one authority, and no single one of them could shut an inquiry down everywhere.'] },
  '佛陀': { g:'faith', y:[-480,-400], ca:1, c:'孔雀王朝', n:['佛陀','The Buddha'],
    t:['一个王子离家出走,想弄明白人为什么会苦。','A prince left home to work out why people suffer.'],
    a:[['他的生卒年至今没有定论。传统说法是前 563—前 483 年,但 1988 年一次专题会议上,多数提出意见的与会学者把他去世的时间定在前 400 年上下二十年之内。这张卡用的是后一个口径,站内的大事记沿用的还是传统年表','His dates are still not settled. The traditional ones are 563–483 BC, but at a symposium in 1988 most of the scholars presenting placed his death within twenty years either side of 400 BC. This card follows the later reckoning; the timeline entries elsewhere in this site still use the traditional one'],
       ['他先试了当时最流行的办法——极端苦行,饿到几乎死掉,发现没用;也否定了纵情享乐。他把自己走通的那条路叫「中道」:两头都不去','He first tried the fashionable method of the day, extreme asceticism, starved himself nearly to death and found it useless; he rejected indulgence as well. The road he settled on he called the middle way: neither end'],
       ['他讲法用的是当时人日常说的话,不是祭司专用的梵语;他也不认吠陀祭祀和婆罗门那一套天生的高低。他一个字都没有写下来——最早的佛经写本比他去世晚了四五百年','He taught in the everyday speech of the region, not the Sanskrit reserved for priests, and he did not accept the Vedic sacrifices or the inborn ranks of the brahmins. He wrote nothing at all: the oldest Buddhist manuscripts are four or five centuries later than his death']],
    s:['这个站里跟佛教有关的段落有一大排——沙门思潮、大乘北传、佛教中国化、译经与藏文定型、上座部佛教王权、超戒寺与那烂陀——它们的源头都是这个人。他没建国、没打仗、没留下一行亲笔,却是这张图上影响范围最广的几个人之一:两千五百年后,从斯里兰卡到蒙古、从泰国到日本,都还在照着他说过的话过日子。','A long row of segments in this site depend on this man: the shramana movement, the Mahayana going north, Buddhism becoming Chinese, the translations that fixed written Tibetan, Theravada kingship, Vikramashila and Nalanda. He founded no state, fought no war and left not one line in his own hand, and is still among the few people on this chart with the widest reach: two and a half thousand years on, from Sri Lanka to Mongolia and from Thailand to Japan, people still order their lives by what he is remembered to have said.'] },
  '庄子': { g:'mind', y:[-369,-286], ca:1, c:'战国', n:['庄子','Zhuangzi'],
    t:['别人争着去做官,他说他宁可像乌龟一样在泥里拖着尾巴。','While others competed for office, he said he would rather drag his tail in the mud like a turtle.'],
    a:[['《史记》记着这么一件事:楚王派人请他去做宰相,他说,祭祀用的牛养得很好、披着绣花的衣裳,可是牵进太庙那天,它想做一头普通的猪都来不及了','The Records of the Grand Historian tells it this way. The king of Chu sent to make him chief minister, and he answered: the sacrificial ox is well fed and dressed in embroidery, but on the day it is led into the temple it is too late for it to wish it were an ordinary pig'],
       ['他写东西靠讲故事和打比方,不做正面论证:大鹏一飞九万里、庖丁解牛顺着骨缝走、井底的青蛙不知道有海。这些比喻两千多年后还在中文里天天用','He wrote in stories and figures rather than argument: the great bird that flies ninety thousand li, the cook whose blade follows the joints, the frog in the well who has never heard of the sea. The Chinese language still uses these daily, more than two thousand years later'],
       ['最有名的一段是他梦见自己变成蝴蝶,醒来后不确定:是我梦见了蝴蝶,还是蝴蝶正梦见我','His best-known passage is the dream of being a butterfly, and the doubt on waking: did I dream I was a butterfly, or is a butterfly now dreaming it is me']],
    s:['同一个乱世里,孔子想的是怎么把秩序修好,商鞅想的是怎么把国家变强,而他问的是另一个方向的问题:这些追求本身是不是值得。他给中国人留下了一条「不参加」的正当出路——后世当官不顺、被贬、辞职的读书人,几乎都读他。','In the same disordered age Confucius asked how order might be repaired and Shang Yang how the state might be made strong; his question ran the other way — whether such pursuits are worth having. He left the Chinese a respectable way of not taking part, and scholars who lost office, were demoted or resigned have read him ever since.'] },
  '墨子': { g:'mind', y:[-470,-391], ca:1, c:'战国', n:['墨子','Mozi'],
    t:['他反对一切进攻性的战争,而且带着一队人真的去守城。','He was against every war of aggression — and took a team of men to defend the walls.'],
    a:[['他主张「兼爱」:对别人家的人要像对自己家的人一样,不分亲疏。这一条在他死后几十年被孟子骂作「无父」,因为它取消了儒家最看重的差等','He taught impartial care: treat other people\'s families as you treat your own, without grading by closeness. Mencius, decades after his death, attacked it as denying one\'s father, because it did away with the graded affections the Confucians thought essential'],
       ['他的团体是有组织有纪律的一群人,会做守城器械,专门赶去帮弱国防守。传说他听说楚国要打宋国,走了十天十夜赶到,跟公输班当面推演攻守九回合,九次都挡住了','His followers were an organised and disciplined body who built defensive engines and travelled to help weaker states hold out. He is said to have walked ten days and nights on hearing that Chu meant to attack Song, and to have played out nine rounds of attack and defence with the engineer Gongshu Ban in front of the king, holding him off every time'],
       ['他还反对厚葬、反对礼乐,理由很直接:那些钱花在活人身上更有用。《墨子》里有中国最早的一批关于光学、力学与几何的记载,包括小孔成像','He also opposed lavish burials and ritual music, on the plain ground that the money did more good spent on the living. The Mozi contains some of the earliest Chinese writing on optics, mechanics and geometry, including the pinhole image']],
    s:['战国时儒墨并称显学,但秦汉以后墨家几乎断绝,书都差点失传。他提的那些问题——爱要不要分远近、战争什么时候算正当、钱该花在死人还是活人身上——两千年后一条也没过时。','In the Warring States the Confucians and the Mohists were the two schools everyone argued with; after the Qin and Han the Mohists all but vanished and their book nearly went with them. The questions he raised — whether care should be graded by nearness, when a war is justified, whether money belongs to the dead or the living — have not dated in two thousand years.'] },
  '韩非': { g:'mind', y:[-280,-233], c:'战国', n:['韩非','Han Fei'],
    t:['他写的书被秦王读到、大加赞赏,然后他死在秦国的牢里。','The king of Qin read his book and admired it — and he died in a Qin prison.'],
    a:[['他认为治国不能指望人性向善,要靠三样东西:法(明文公布的规则)、术(君主考核臣下的手段)、势(位置本身带来的权威)。规则要写出来让所有人知道,赏罚必须兑现','He held that government cannot depend on people being good, and needs three things: law, published rules everyone can read; method, the ruler\'s means of assessing his officials; and position, the authority that comes with the office itself. The rules must be written where all can see them and rewards and punishments must actually follow'],
       ['他有口吃,不擅长说话,所以写。秦王读到《孤愤》《五蠹》,说:我要是能见到这个人、跟他交往,死也不遗憾了——当时并不知道作者是韩国的公子','He stammered and did not speak well, so he wrote. The king of Qin read two of his essays and said that to meet this man and know him he would die content — not knowing at the time that the author was a prince of Han'],
       ['他后来出使秦国,被同学李斯进谗言下狱,在狱中服毒而死。而秦国正是照着他那套办法统一了天下','He was later sent to Qin on an embassy, was slandered by his fellow student Li Si, and took poison in prison. Qin went on to unify the empire by exactly the methods he had set out']],
    s:['这几家里,他这一套是被原样照办过的:秦朝就是照它建起来的,也因为太严苛而二世而亡。此后两千年,中国的做法通常被概括成「外儒内法」——嘴上讲的是孔子,办事的规矩里有他。','Of these schools his is the one that was put into practice as written: the Qin state was built on it, and fell in two reigns for being too harsh. For two thousand years afterwards Chinese practice has been summed up as Confucian outside and Legalist within — Confucius in what is said, and Han Fei in how things are actually run.'] },
  '卢梭': { g:'mind', y:[1712,1778], c:'法兰西', n:['卢梭','Jean-Jacques Rousseau'],
    t:['「人生而自由,却无往不在枷锁之中」——这句话开了一本书,也开了一个时代。','Man is born free, and everywhere he is in chains: one sentence that opened a book, and an age.'],
    a:[['1762 年《社会契约论》开头就是那一句。他的主张是:统治的正当性不来自上帝、不来自血统,只来自被统治者的同意;这个同意可以收回','The Social Contract of 1762 begins with it. His claim was that the right to rule comes not from God nor from birth but only from the consent of the governed — and that consent can be withdrawn'],
       ['他还写了一本讲怎么教孩子的书《爱弥儿》,主张孩子该在自然里长、按自己的节奏学,不要一上来就灌书本。这本书在巴黎与日内瓦都被当众烧掉,他被迫流亡','He also wrote a book about bringing up children, Emile, arguing that a child should grow up out of doors and learn at his own pace rather than be filled with books from the start. It was publicly burned in both Paris and Geneva and he had to flee'],
       ['他自己有五个孩子,全部送进了育婴堂,一个都没养。这件事是他晚年在自传里亲口写下来的','He had five children of his own and put every one of them into a foundling hospital. It was he himself who set this down, in the autobiography he wrote late in life']],
    s:['他去世十一年后法国大革命爆发,革命者把他奉为先知,遗骨迁进先贤祠。但「人民的同意」这个说法有两面:它既是「统治者得听人民的」,也可以变成「谁代表人民,谁就可以替所有人做主」——恐怖时期的人正是拿后一半为自己辩护的。而他那本教育书与他自己的做法之间那道沟,后人一直在议论。','The French Revolution broke out eleven years after his death; the revolutionaries treated him as a prophet and moved his remains to the Pantheon. But the consent of the people cuts both ways: it can mean that rulers must listen, and it can become the claim that whoever speaks for the people may decide for everyone — which is the half the men of the Terror used to justify themselves. And the gap between his book on education and his own conduct has been argued over ever since.'] },
  '马克思': { g:'mind', y:[1818,1883], c:'大英帝国·英国', n:['马克思','Karl Marx'],
    t:['一个在伦敦图书馆里写书的穷记者,后来有三分之一的人类活在照他名字命名的制度下。','A hard-up journalist writing in a London library — and a third of humanity later lived under systems named after him.'],
    a:[['他生在普鲁士,因为办报被驱逐,辗转巴黎、布鲁塞尔,1849 年起在伦敦住到死。大半辈子靠朋友恩格斯接济,几个孩子因贫病夭折','Born in Prussia, expelled for the newspaper he ran, he moved through Paris and Brussels and from 1849 lived in London until he died. He was kept going for most of his life by his friend Engels, and several of his children died of poverty and illness'],
       ['他的核心看法是:决定一个社会长什么样的,首先是这个社会怎么生产东西、谁占有生产资料;政治、法律、观念都建在这个底子上。这个角度本身——「先看物质基础」——后来连不同意他结论的历史学家也在用','His central view was that what a society looks like is decided first by how it produces things and who owns the means of production, with politics, law and ideas built on that base. The approach itself — look at the material conditions first — was later used even by historians who rejected his conclusions'],
       ['1848 年他与恩格斯写了篇几十页的《共产党宣言》;三大卷的《资本论》他只出版了第一卷(1867),后两卷是他死后恩格斯整理出来的。他常年在大英博物馆的阅览室里查资料','In 1848 he and Engels wrote a pamphlet of a few dozen pages, the Communist Manifesto; of the three volumes of Capital he published only the first, in 1867, and the other two were assembled by Engels after his death. He worked for years in the reading room of the British Museum']],
    s:['他生前几乎没有权力,葬礼上送他的人寥寥可数。但二十世纪有一大片世界是按他的名字重画的——俄国、中国和东欧都在里面,而这些国家实际建成的样子跟他书里写的相去甚远。据恩格斯后来转述,他晚年听说法国有人自称马克思主义者时讲过一句:那我就不是马克思主义者。','He had almost no power while he lived, and very few people came to his funeral. A great part of the twentieth-century map was then redrawn in his name — Russia, China, eastern Europe — and what those states actually built bore little resemblance to what is in his books. Engels later reported that, told certain Frenchmen called themselves Marxists, he said that in that case he was not a Marxist himself.'] },
  '达·芬奇': { g:'art', y:[1452,1519], c:'文艺复兴意大利', n:['达·芬奇','Leonardo da Vinci'],
  t:['画家、解剖学家、工程师。他一生画完的画不到二十幅。',
     'Painter, anatomist, engineer — and the finisher of fewer than twenty paintings in his life.'],
  a:[['画《蒙娜丽莎》与《最后的晚餐》','Painted the Mona Lisa and the Last Supper'],
     ['解剖三十余具尸体,画下人体结构图,包括第一幅准确的子宫内胎儿图','Dissected some thirty bodies and drew the human interior, including the first accurate fetus in the womb'],
     ['留下七千余页笔记,画有飞行器、潜水装置、机器人和降落伞的构想','Left over 7,000 pages of notebooks sketching flying machines, diving gear, robots and a parachute']],
  s:['《蒙娜丽莎》是世界上参观人数最多的一幅画,每年约有一千万人去卢浮宫看它。他的解剖图在准确度上领先当时的医学界数百年,但因为生前未发表,对医学史实际影响有限——这本身是科学史上最常被引用的一个遗憾。',
     'The Mona Lisa is the most visited painting on earth, drawing some ten million people a year to the Louvre. His anatomical drawings were centuries ahead of the medicine of his day — but he never published them, so they changed nothing at the time, which is among the most quoted might-have-beens in the history of science.'] },
'米开朗基罗': { g:'art', y:[1475,1564], c:'文艺复兴意大利', n:['米开朗基罗','Michelangelo'],
  t:['他坚持说自己是雕塑家,却被逼着画了西斯廷礼拜堂的天顶。',
     'He insisted he was a sculptor, and was bullied into painting the Sistine ceiling anyway.'],
  a:[['26 岁完成《大卫》,用的是别人废弃的一块大理石','Finished the David at twenty-six, from a block another sculptor had abandoned'],
     ['1508—1512 年仰头画西斯廷礼拜堂天顶,约三百个人物','Spent four years on his back painting some three hundred figures on the Sistine ceiling'],
     ['晚年主持圣彼得大教堂穹顶设计,直到 88 岁去世前几天还在工作','Designed the dome of St Peter\'s in old age, still working days before his death at 88']],
  s:['西斯廷天顶画每年约有五百万人参观。圣彼得大教堂穹顶高约一百三十六米,至今是世界最高的教堂穹顶,也是此后三百年欧美各国国会大厦圆顶的范本——美国国会大厦即为其一。',
     'Some five million people a year look up at that ceiling. The dome of St Peter\'s, 136 metres high, is still the tallest church dome in the world and became the model for parliament buildings across Europe and America for three centuries — the US Capitol among them.'] },
'恩里克王子': { g:'sail', y:[1394,1460], c:'西班牙·葡萄牙帝国', n:['恩里克王子','Henry the Navigator'],
  t:['他自己几乎没出过海,却是大航海时代的发起人。',
     'He hardly went to sea himself, yet he started the age of discovery.'],
  a:[['在葡萄牙南端萨格里什聚集航海家、制图师与造船匠,持续资助探险','Gathered navigators, cartographers and shipwrights at Sagres and funded voyage after voyage'],
     ['推动改良轻快帆船(caravel),使逆风航行与远洋探索成为可能','Backed the caravel, whose rig could sail against the wind and made ocean exploration practical'],
     ['1434 年他的船长绕过博哈多尔角,打破"过此有去无回"的传说','In 1434 one of his captains rounded Cape Bojador, breaking the belief that no ship returned from beyond it']],
  s:['绕过博哈多尔角是欧洲远洋探索的心理转折点。他建立的"国家持续投资探险"模式被西班牙、荷兰、英国接连效仿,直接通向 1488 年绕过好望角与 1498 年达伽马抵达印度。同一批航行也开启了欧洲的大西洋奴隶贸易。',
     'Rounding Bojador broke a psychological barrier as much as a geographic one. The model he built — a state investing patiently in exploration — was copied by Spain, the Netherlands and England, and led straight to the Cape of Good Hope in 1488 and India in 1498. The same voyages also began the European Atlantic slave trade.'] },
'哥伦布': { g:'sail', y:[1451,1506], c:'西班牙·葡萄牙帝国', n:['哥伦布','Christopher Columbus'],
  t:['他要去亚洲,算错了地球的大小,撞上了一块不知道存在的大陆。',
     'He set out for Asia, underestimated the size of the earth, and hit a continent nobody knew was there.'],
  a:[['1492 年 10 月 12 日率三艘船抵达巴哈马群岛','Made landfall in the Bahamas with three ships on 12 October 1492'],
     ['四次横渡大西洋,到死都坚持自己到的是亚洲','Crossed the Atlantic four times, insisting to his death that he had reached Asia'],
     ['在伊斯帕尼奥拉岛建立殖民地,因统治残暴一度被押回西班牙受审','Founded a colony on Hispaniola, and was once shipped home in chains for his brutality there']],
  s:['1492 年被普遍视为世界近代史的开端。此后的"哥伦布大交换"把玉米、马铃薯、番茄带到旧大陆,把小麦、马、牛带到新大陆,也带去了天花——美洲原住民人口在此后一个世纪内减少约九成。这是人类历史上影响最深远、也最惨烈的一次生物与文化交汇。',
     'The year 1492 is the conventional start of the modern era. The Columbian Exchange that followed carried maize, potatoes and tomatoes to the Old World, wheat, horses and cattle to the New — and smallpox, which helped cut the indigenous population of the Americas by roughly ninety per cent within a century. It is the most consequential and most catastrophic biological encounter in human history.'] },
'埃尔卡诺': { g:'sail', y:[1486,1526], ca:1, c:'西班牙·葡萄牙帝国', n:['埃尔卡诺','Juan Sebastián Elcano'],
  t:['麦哲伦死在半路,把船开回来的是他。',
     'Magellan died on the way; he was the one who brought the ship home.'],
  a:[['巴斯克人,原本是船队里一条船上管船务的头,仅次于船长;1520 年在南美过冬时参加过哗变,被麦哲伦判了刑又赦免。1521 年麦哲伦在菲律宾战死后指挥几经更替,同年 9 月在婆罗洲一带他被推为「维多利亚号」船长,到摩鹿加群岛后由他带这条船回家。','A Basque, originally the master of one of the ships, second only to her captain; during the winter in South America in 1520 he joined a mutiny, was sentenced by Magellan and pardoned. After Magellan was killed in the Philippines in 1521 the command changed hands more than once; in September that year, off Borneo, he was chosen captain of the Victoria, and from the Moluccas it was he who took her home.'],
     ['他决定不走原路,继续向西:绕好望角横穿印度洋和大西洋,一路是葡萄牙人的海域,只在佛得角冒险靠了一次岸,被扣下十三个人。1522 年 9 月 6 日回到西班牙,出发时五条船二百七十人,回来一条船十八个人。','He chose not to go back the way they had come but on westward, round the Cape of Good Hope and across the Indian Ocean and the Atlantic — Portuguese waters all the way; the one stop they risked, at the Cape Verde islands, cost them thirteen men. On 6 September 1522 he reached Spain: of five ships and two hundred and seventy men who had set out, one ship and eighteen men came back.'],
     ['船上装着二十六吨丁香,卖掉的钱把整支船队的开销抵回来还有赚;皇帝查理五世(也是西班牙国王)给了他一份年金(据说一直没领到)和一枚纹章,纹章上是一个地球,写着「你第一个环绕了我」。','The hold carried twenty-six tons of cloves, and their sale paid for the whole expedition with a profit to spare; the emperor Charles V, who was also king of Spain, granted him a pension — never actually paid, it seems — and a coat of arms showing a globe with the motto You were the first to go round me.']],
  s:['1525 年他随第二支去香料群岛的船队再次出海,次年在太平洋上死于坏血病。今天西班牙海军的训练帆船以他命名;他的家乡盖塔里亚每四年重演一次他归航上岸的仪式。',
     'In 1525 he sailed again with the second expedition to the Spice Islands and died of scurvy in the Pacific the following year. The Spanish navy\'s training ship bears his name today, and his home town of Getaria re-enacts his landing every four years.'] },
'麦哲伦': { g:'sail', y:[1480,1521], c:'西班牙·葡萄牙帝国', n:['麦哲伦','Ferdinand Magellan'],
  t:['人类第一次环球航行是他发起的,但他自己没走完。',
     'He launched the first voyage around the world, and did not live to finish it.'],
  a:[['1519 年率五艘船、二百七十人从西班牙出发','Left Spain in 1519 with five ships and 270 men'],
     ['1520 年发现南美南端的海峡,今称麦哲伦海峡,并给太平洋起了这个名字','Found the strait at the tip of South America that bears his name, and named the Pacific for its calm'],
     ['1521 年在菲律宾麦克坦岛被当地首领拉普拉普所杀','Was killed on Mactan in the Philippines by the local chief Lapulapu']],
  s:['1522 年"维多利亚号"载着十八人回到西班牙,完成人类第一次环球航行,历时三年。这次航行用实测证明地球是球形且远比想象的大,海洋是连通的一个整体。拉普拉普在今天的菲律宾被视为反抗殖民的第一位民族英雄。',
     'The Victoria came home in 1522 with eighteen survivors, three years out — the first circumnavigation. It proved by measurement that the earth was round, far larger than assumed, and that its oceans are one connected body of water. In the Philippines today, Lapulapu is honoured as the first hero of resistance to colonisation.'] },
'伊丽莎白一世': { g:'king', y:[1533,1603], r:[1558,1603], c:'大英帝国·英国', n:['伊丽莎白一世','Elizabeth I'],
  t:['终身未婚,说自己嫁给了英格兰。在位 45 年。',
     'She never married, saying she was wedded to England. Forty-five years on the throne.'],
  a:[['以宗教折中方案结束天主教与新教的血腥拉锯','Settled the Catholic-Protestant bloodletting with a deliberate religious compromise'],
     ['1588 年英国海军击败西班牙无敌舰队','Saw off the Spanish Armada in 1588'],
     ['1600 年特许成立东印度公司;她在位期间莎士比亚写出主要剧作','Chartered the East India Company in 1600; Shakespeare wrote his major plays in her reign']],
  s:['击败无敌舰队标志西班牙海上霸权的转折,英国由此走向海洋。她特许的东印度公司后来统治印度近百年。伊丽莎白时代是英国文学的黄金期,英语戏剧与诗歌的基本形态在这一朝定型。',
     'The Armada marked the turn of Spanish sea power and the beginning of England\'s. The company she chartered would eventually govern India for a century. And the Elizabethan age set the shape of English drama and poetry for good.'] },
'路易十四': { g:'king', y:[1638,1715], r:[1643,1715], c:'法兰西', n:['路易十四','Louis XIV'],
  t:['四岁登基,在位 72 年,是欧洲有确切纪年以来在位最久的君主。',
     'King at four, on the throne for seventy-two years — the longest verified reign of any European monarch.'],
  a:[['把贵族集中到凡尔赛宫,用礼仪与恩宠取代他们的地方权力','Moved the nobility into Versailles and replaced their provincial power with ceremony and favour'],
     ['建立常备军与官僚财政体系,法国成为欧洲第一强国','Built a standing army and a professional treasury, making France the leading power in Europe'],
     ['1685 年废除南特敕令,数十万新教徒逃离法国','Revoked the Edict of Nantes in 1685, driving hundreds of thousands of Protestants abroad']],
  s:['凡尔赛宫成为此后两百年欧洲宫廷的样板,法语也在这一时期成为欧洲外交与上流社会的通用语,直到 20 世纪初。凡尔赛宫 1979 年列入世界遗产。他留下的巨额债务与特权结构,是七十余年后法国大革命的远因之一。',
     'Versailles became the template for European courts for two centuries, and French became the language of diplomacy and polite society until the twentieth. The palace was listed as World Heritage in 1979. The debts and privileges he left behind were among the distant causes of the revolution seventy years later.'] },
'伏尔泰': { g:'mind', y:[1694,1778], c:'法兰西', n:['伏尔泰','Voltaire'],
  t:['因为写讽刺诗两次被关进巴士底狱,一辈子靠笔跟权力过不去。',
     'Twice jailed in the Bastille for satirical verse, and a thorn in authority\'s side for sixty years.'],
  a:[['写小说、剧本、史书、书信共两千余部(篇),是启蒙运动传播最广的作者','Wrote over two thousand works of every kind, and was the most widely read author of the Enlightenment'],
     ['为蒙冤处死的新教徒卡拉斯翻案,推动欧洲最早的司法改革舆论','Reopened the case of Jean Calas, a Protestant executed on false charges, and forced a public reckoning'],
     ['主张宗教宽容与言论自由,批评教会与专制','Argued for religious tolerance and free speech against church and crown']],
  s:['卡拉斯案是欧洲第一次由公共舆论迫使司法改判的案件,被视为现代公共知识分子的起点。他去世十一年后爆发法国大革命,遗体 1791 年被迎入先贤祠。那句常被安在他名下的"我不同意你的话,但誓死捍卫你说话的权利",实为后人对其立场的概括。',
     'The Calas affair was the first time public opinion in Europe forced a court to reverse itself, and it is taken as the birth of the public intellectual. He died eleven years before the revolution; in 1791 his remains were carried into the Panthéon. The famous line about defending to the death your right to say it was not his — a biographer coined it to summarise his stance.'] },
'拿破仑': { g:'war', y:[1769,1821], r:[1804,1815], c:'法兰西', n:['拿破仑','Napoleon Bonaparte'],
  t:['科西嘉岛的小贵族,三十岁掌权,三十五岁称帝,四十六岁死在南大西洋的孤岛上。',
     'Minor Corsican gentry: in power at thirty, emperor at thirty-five, dead on a South Atlantic rock at forty-six.'],
  a:[['1799 年雾月政变夺权,1804 年称帝','Seized power in the coup of Brumaire in 1799 and crowned himself emperor in 1804'],
     ['1804 年颁《拿破仑法典》,确立法律面前人人平等、私有财产、政教分离','Issued the Civil Code in 1804: equality before the law, secure property, church separated from state'],
     ['1812 年远征俄国,六十万大军回来不足三万;1815 年滑铁卢战败','Invaded Russia in 1812 with 600,000 men and brought back fewer than 30,000; lost at Waterloo in 1815']],
  s:['《拿破仑法典》是现代大陆法系的直接蓝本,今天比利时、荷兰、意大利、西班牙、拉美与日本的民法都由它衍生,他自己说"我真正的光荣不是打了四十场胜仗,而是这部法典"。他的战争也把法国大革命的观念带到全欧洲,并意外催生了德意志与意大利的民族主义。',
     'The Napoleonic Code is the direct blueprint of modern civil law — Belgium, the Netherlands, Italy, Spain, Latin America and Japan all built on it. He said himself that his true glory was not forty victories but that code. His wars also carried the ideas of the revolution across Europe and, without meaning to, ignited German and Italian nationalism.'] },
'戴高乐': { g:'state', y:[1890,1970], c:'法兰西', n:['戴高乐','Charles de Gaulle'],
  t:['1940 年法国投降那天,他在伦敦对着广播说:法国输了一场战役,没有输掉战争。',
     'On the day France surrendered in 1940, he told a London microphone: France has lost a battle, not the war.'],
  a:[['1940 年 6 月 18 日发表广播演说,组织自由法国,当时几乎无人响应','Broadcast on 18 June 1940 and founded Free France, with almost nobody listening'],
     ['1944 年 8 月率军进入巴黎;战后主持临时政府,给予法国妇女选举权','Marched into Paris in August 1944; his provisional government gave French women the vote'],
     ['1958 年重新出山,创建第五共和国;1962 年结束阿尔及利亚战争,让其独立','Returned in 1958 to found the Fifth Republic, and ended the Algerian war with independence in 1962']],
  s:['第五共和国的宪政架构沿用至今,是法国历史上最稳定的政体之一。他坚持法国独立自主的外交路线——退出北约军事一体化、独立发展核武、承认中华人民共和国——至今仍是法国外交的底色。巴黎的主要机场以他命名。',
     'The Fifth Republic he designed still stands, the most stable constitutional order France has had. His insistence on an independent line — leaving NATO\'s integrated command, building a French bomb, recognising the People\'s Republic of China — remains the ground note of French foreign policy. Paris\'s main airport carries his name.'] },
'瓦特': { g:'sci', y:[1736,1819], c:'大英帝国·英国', n:['瓦特','James Watt'],
  t:['他不是发明蒸汽机的人,但他让蒸汽机好用了。',
     'He did not invent the steam engine. He made it worth using.'],
  a:[['1765 年想到加一个独立冷凝器,不必每次循环都把汽缸冷却再加热','In 1765 he saw that a separate condenser would spare the cylinder from being cooled and reheated each stroke'],
     ['新机器耗煤量降到原来的约四分之一','The result burned about a quarter of the coal of the old engines'],
     ['1769 年获专利,与博尔顿合伙生产,又发明了双向汽缸与调速器','Patented it in 1769, went into partnership with Boulton, and added double action and a governor']],
  s:['效率提升让蒸汽机第一次可以离开煤矿、装进工厂和后来的火车轮船,工业革命由此从局部走向全面。功率单位"瓦特"以他命名,"马力"这个单位也是他为了向客户解释机器能力而定义的。',
     'The efficiency gain let the steam engine leave the coal pit for the factory floor, and later the locomotive and the ship — which is when the Industrial Revolution stopped being local. The watt is named after him, and so is the horsepower, a unit he invented to explain his machines to customers.'] },
'维多利亚': { g:'king', y:[1819,1901], r:[1837,1901], c:'大英帝国·英国', n:['维多利亚','Queen Victoria'],
  t:['18 岁继位,在位 63 年。她在位时英国统治了地球上四分之一的人口。',
     'Queen at eighteen, for sixty-three years — during which Britain ruled a quarter of the world\'s people.'],
  a:[['在位期间英国完成工业化,铁路、电报与城市化改变了整个社会','Britain industrialised in her reign: railways, telegraphs and cities remade the country'],
     ['1876 年加称印度女皇','Took the additional title Empress of India in 1876'],
     ['与阿尔伯特亲王生九个子女,其后代遍布欧洲各王室,人称"欧洲的祖母"','Her nine children married into thrones across Europe, making her the continent\'s grandmother']],
  s:['1901 年她去世时,大英帝国面积约三千三百万平方公里、人口约四亿,是历史上最大的帝国。"维多利亚时代"至今是英语世界描述那个时期道德风尚与社会结构的通用词。她的血友病基因经外孙女传入俄国皇室,是尼古拉二世之子患病的来源。',
     'At her death in 1901 the British Empire covered some 33 million square kilometres and 400 million people, the largest empire ever assembled. "Victorian" is still the standard English word for the manners and structures of that age. Her haemophilia gene passed through a granddaughter into the Russian imperial family, and to the last Tsar\'s son.'] },
'丘吉尔': { g:'state', y:[1874,1965], c:'大英帝国·英国', n:['丘吉尔','Winston Churchill'],
  t:['1940 年他上台时,英国已经没有盟友了。他能提供的只有"鲜血、辛劳、眼泪和汗水"。',
     'When he took office in 1940 Britain had no allies left. What he offered was blood, toil, tears and sweat.'],
  a:[['1940 年在法国沦陷、英国独自面对德国时拒绝媾和','Refused to negotiate in 1940, with France fallen and Britain alone'],
     ['促成英美同盟与英苏合作,与罗斯福、斯大林共同规划战后秩序','Built the alliance with Roosevelt and the working relationship with Stalin, and shaped the post-war settlement with both'],
     ['1946 年发表"铁幕"演说;1953 年因历史著作与演说获诺贝尔文学奖','Coined the Iron Curtain in 1946, and won the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1953']],
  s:['1940 年英国若求和,德国就能腾出全部力量东进,二战的走向会完全不同。他是极少数以政治家身份获诺贝尔文学奖的人。"铁幕"一词定义了此后四十年的世界格局。2002 年 BBC 的民意调查里,他被选为"最伟大的英国人"。',
     'Had Britain come to terms in 1940, Germany could have turned its full weight east, and the war would have gone differently. He is one of the very few politicians to win the Nobel Prize in Literature. His "iron curtain" named the shape of the next forty years. In a 2002 BBC poll the public voted him the greatest Briton.'] },
'俾斯麦': { g:'state', y:[1815,1898], c:'德意志', n:['俾斯麦','Otto von Bismarck'],
  t:['他说统一德国靠的不是演说和多数决议,是铁与血。',
     'He said the question would be settled not by speeches and majority votes but by iron and blood.'],
  a:[['1864、1866、1870 年三场短促战争,先后击败丹麦、奥地利与法国','Won three short wars in six years, against Denmark, Austria and France'],
     ['1871 年在凡尔赛镜厅宣告德意志帝国成立','Proclaimed the German Empire in the Hall of Mirrors at Versailles in 1871'],
     ['1883—1889 年推行医疗保险、工伤保险与养老保险','Introduced health, accident and old-age insurance between 1883 and 1889']],
  s:['德意志统一改变了欧洲的力量结构,此后八十年的欧洲史很大程度上是围绕这个新强国展开的。他建立的社会保险是世界上第一套国家强制社会保障制度,今天各国的社保体系大多可以追到这个模板——他推行它的目的是釜底抽薪,削弱社会主义运动。',
     'German unification reshaped the balance of Europe, and much of the next eighty years turned on how to accommodate the new power. His social insurance was the first compulsory state welfare system anywhere, and remains the template most countries built on — though he introduced it to cut the ground from under the socialists.'] },
'爱因斯坦': { g:'sci', y:[1879,1955], c:'德意志', n:['爱因斯坦','Albert Einstein'],
  t:['1905 年他还在专利局做小职员,那一年他发表了四篇论文。',
     'In 1905 he was a junior clerk in a patent office. That year he published four papers.'],
  a:[['1905 年提出狭义相对论,以及 E=mc²','Set out special relativity in 1905, and E=mc²'],
     ['1915 年提出广义相对论,把引力解释为时空的弯曲','Gave general relativity in 1915, recasting gravity as the curvature of spacetime'],
     ['1921 年因解释光电效应获诺贝尔物理学奖(不是因为相对论)','Won the 1921 Nobel Prize for explaining the photoelectric effect — not for relativity']],
  s:['1919 年日食观测证实了光线被太阳引力弯曲,他一夜之间成为世界名人。广义相对论是今天 GPS 定位、黑洞与宇宙学的理论基础;光电效应的解释则是量子力学的起点之一。1999 年《时代》周刊将他选为"世纪人物"。',
     'When the 1919 eclipse confirmed that starlight bends around the sun, he became world-famous overnight. General relativity underpins GPS, black holes and modern cosmology; his account of the photoelectric effect was one of the starting points of quantum mechanics. Time named him Person of the Century in 1999.'] },
'彼得大帝': { g:'king', y:[1672,1725], r:[1682,1725], c:'俄罗斯·苏联', n:['彼得大帝','Peter the Great'],
  t:['他化名去荷兰的船厂当学徒,回国后按学到的东西改造整个俄国。',
     'He went to work incognito in a Dutch shipyard, came home, and rebuilt Russia to match what he had seen.'],
  a:[['1697 年率使团赴西欧,自己在阿姆斯特丹当了四个月造船工','Travelled west in 1697 and spent four months as a shipwright in Amsterdam'],
     ['1703 年在沼泽上建圣彼得堡,1712 年把首都迁了过去','Built St Petersburg on marshland in 1703 and moved the capital there in 1712'],
     ['建海军、改历法、办学校,并亲手剪掉贵族的胡子','Created a navy, changed the calendar, founded schools — and personally cut the beards off his nobles']],
  s:['俄国从此有了出海口与海军,从内陆国变成欧洲强国。1721 年大北方战争击败瑞典,俄国取代瑞典成为北欧霸主,他改称"皇帝"。圣彼得堡是俄国面向欧洲的窗口,历史城区 1990 年列入世界遗产。',
     'Russia got a coastline and a fleet, and turned from a landlocked state into a European power. Beating Sweden in 1721 made it the master of the Baltic, and he took the title of emperor. St Petersburg was his window on Europe; its historic centre became World Heritage in 1990.'] },
'叶卡捷琳娜': { g:'king', y:[1729,1796], r:[1762,1796], c:'俄罗斯·苏联', n:['叶卡捷琳娜','Catherine the Great'],
  t:['德国小公国出身的公主,靠政变推翻自己的丈夫,统治俄国 34 年。',
     'A minor German princess who overthrew her own husband and ruled Russia for thirty-four years.'],
  a:[['1762 年发动政变废黜彼得三世,自己即位','Deposed Peter III in a coup in 1762 and took the throne herself'],
     ['与土耳其两次战争夺取黑海北岸,三次瓜分波兰,俄国版图大幅扩张','Took the northern Black Sea from the Ottomans and joined three partitions of Poland'],
     ['与伏尔泰、狄德罗通信,收购大批欧洲艺术品,创建艾尔米塔什博物馆','Corresponded with Voltaire and Diderot, and bought the art that became the Hermitage']],
  s:['俄国在她手上取得黑海出海口,并成为欧洲事务中不可回避的一方。艾尔米塔什博物馆今天藏品逾三百万件,是世界上最大的博物馆之一。她自称开明君主并起草过法典草案,但农奴制在她治下反而扩大——这一矛盾是"开明专制"最常被引用的案例。',
     'Russia gained the Black Sea under her and became impossible to ignore in European affairs. The Hermitage now holds over three million objects, among the largest collections on earth. She styled herself an enlightened ruler and drafted a legal code, yet serfdom expanded in her reign — the contradiction most often cited when historians discuss enlightened absolutism.'] },
'列宁': { g:'state', y:[1870,1924], c:'俄罗斯·苏联', n:['列宁','Vladimir Lenin'],
  t:['流亡十七年。1917 年他坐着德国安排的封闭列车回到彼得格勒。',
     'Seventeen years in exile, then back to Petrograd in 1917 aboard a sealed train the Germans arranged.'],
  a:[['1917 年十月革命夺取政权,建立世界上第一个社会主义国家','Took power in the October Revolution of 1917 and founded the first socialist state'],
     ['退出一战,签《布列斯特和约》,割让大片土地换取喘息','Pulled Russia out of the world war at Brest-Litovsk, ceding vast territory to buy time'],
     ['内战后推行新经济政策,部分恢复市场与私营','After the civil war he allowed markets and private trade back under the New Economic Policy']],
  s:['十月革命是 20 世纪影响最大的政治事件之一,此后七十余年世界被分成两个阵营。他确立的"先锋党"组织模式被中国、越南、古巴等国的政党采用。苏联在他去世后成为工业与军事强国,同时形成了高度集中的政治体制。',
     'The October Revolution was among the most consequential political events of the twentieth century, and split the world into two camps for seventy years. His model of a disciplined vanguard party was adopted by movements from China to Cuba. The state he founded became an industrial and military power — and a highly centralised one.'] },
'斯大林': { g:'state', y:[1878,1953], c:'俄罗斯·苏联', n:['斯大林','Joseph Stalin'],
  t:['他执政三十年,苏联从农业国变成工业与核大国,代价极其巨大。',
     'In his thirty years the USSR went from a peasant country to an industrial and nuclear power, at enormous cost.'],
  a:[['1928 年起推行五年计划与农业集体化,建成重工业体系','From 1928 the Five-Year Plans and collectivisation built a heavy-industrial base'],
     ['1936—1938 年大清洗,处决与关押数以百万计,包括大批军队高级将领','The purges of 1936-38 killed and imprisoned people in the millions, including most of the senior officer corps'],
     ['1941—1945 年领导苏联赢得卫国战争,苏军攻入柏林','Led the Soviet Union to victory over Germany, ending in Berlin in 1945']],
  s:['苏德战场消灭了德军约八成的兵力,是二战欧洲战场的主战场;苏联战争死亡约两千七百万人。同一时期的集体化饥荒与大清洗造成的非战争死亡,学界估计在数百万至上千万之间。1956 年赫鲁晓夫在苏共二十大公开否定他的个人崇拜与清洗。',
     'The eastern front destroyed roughly eighty per cent of German fighting strength and was the main theatre of the European war; Soviet deaths came to some 27 million. The famines of collectivisation and the purges killed millions more outside combat, with estimates ranging from several million upward. In 1956 Khrushchev denounced his cult and his purges to the Party congress.'] },

'胡夫': { g:'king', y:[-2589,-2566], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'古王国埃及', n:['胡夫','Khufu'],
  t:['他留下了古代世界七大奇迹里唯一还立着的那一个。',
     'He left the only one of the seven wonders of the ancient world still standing.'],
  a:[['建造吉萨大金字塔,原高约 146.6 米,用石块约二百三十万块','Built the Great Pyramid: about 146.6 m tall, some 2.3 million blocks'],
     ['金字塔底边长约 230 米,四边长度误差不到 20 厘米','Its base sides run about 230 m and differ from each other by under 20 cm'],
     ['除一尊 7.5 厘米高的小象牙像外,没有留下任何确认的雕像','Apart from a 7.5 cm ivory figurine, not one confirmed statue of him survives']],
  s:['大金字塔在此后约三千八百年里一直是世界上最高的人造建筑,直到 14 世纪的林肯大教堂。它是七大奇迹中唯一存世的一座,1979 年列入世界遗产。这个留下人类最大坟墓的人,自己的样子却只剩一枚火柴盒大小的雕像。',
     'The Great Pyramid was the tallest structure built by anyone for about 3,800 years, until Lincoln Cathedral in the fourteenth century. It is the only ancient wonder still standing, and became World Heritage in 1979. The man who left the largest tomb ever built survives himself only in a figurine the size of a matchbox.'] },
'亚述巴尼拔': { g:'king', y:[-685,-627], ca:1, r:[-669,-631], c:'亚述', n:['亚述巴尼拔','Ashurbanipal'],
  t:['他统治着当时最可怕的军队,同时是那个年代少见的、自己能读古文字的国王。',
     'He commanded the most feared army of his day and was also that rare thing, a king who could read the ancient scripts himself.'],
  a:[['亚述帝国版图达到最大,一度攻入埃及占领底比斯','Brought Assyria to its greatest extent, briefly taking Thebes in Egypt'],
     ['下令搜集抄写两河流域的泥板,在尼尼微建成约三万块泥板的王室图书馆','Had tablets collected and copied across Mesopotamia, building a royal library of some 30,000 at Nineveh'],
     ['自称能读苏美尔语和阿卡德语的古老楔形文字,并通晓数学','Claimed to read the old Sumerian and Akkadian cuneiform, and to know mathematics']],
  s:['这批泥板 1853 年在尼尼微遗址出土,是今天研究美索不达米亚最主要的一手材料;人类现存最早的长篇文学《吉尔伽美什史诗》正是靠其中十二块泥板传下来的,现藏大英博物馆。图书馆按主题分类、加盖藏书印,是已知最早的系统性图书馆之一。',
     'The tablets were excavated at Nineveh in 1853 and remain the principal primary source for Mesopotamia; the Epic of Gilgamesh, the oldest long literary work that survives, comes down to us on twelve of them, now in the British Museum. The library was sorted by subject and stamped with an ownership mark — among the earliest systematic libraries known.'] },
'汉谟拉比': { g:'king', y:[-1792,-1750], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'古巴比伦', n:['汉谟拉比','Hammurabi'],
  t:['三千八百年前,他把法律刻在一根黑石柱上,立在神庙里让所有人看。',
     'Nearly 3,800 years ago he had the law carved on a black stone pillar and set it up in public for anyone to read.'],
  a:[['统一两河流域南部,巴比伦第一次成为地区中心','Unified southern Mesopotamia, making Babylon a regional centre for the first time'],
     ['颁布《汉谟拉比法典》,282 条,刻在一块 2.25 米高的玄武岩石柱上','Issued 282 laws, carved on a basalt stele 2.25 m high'],
     ['法典规定"以眼还眼",但刑罚按身份分等——贵族、平民、奴隶各不相同','It prescribed eye for eye — but graded the penalty by the rank of the victim']],
  s:['这是人类现存最完整的早期成文法典,重要之处不在内容而在形式:法律被公开、固定、可查,统治者也须遵守。石柱 1901 年在伊朗苏萨出土,现藏卢浮宫。"以眼还眼"作为限制报复的原则,后来进入《圣经》与伊斯兰法。',
     'It is the most complete early law code that survives, and what matters is less the content than the form: the law made public, fixed and checkable, binding on the ruler too. The stele was dug up at Susa in Iran in 1901 and is now in the Louvre. Eye for eye — as a limit on revenge rather than a licence for it — passed into biblical and Islamic law.'] },
'尼布甲尼撒二世': { g:'king', y:[-634,-562], ca:1, r:[-605,-562], c:'新巴比伦', n:['尼布甲尼撒二世','Nebuchadnezzar II'],
  t:['他把巴比伦建成了当时世界上最壮观的城市,也把犹太人掳到了那里。',
     'He made Babylon the most spectacular city on earth, and carried the Jews there in chains.'],
  a:[['前 586 年攻陷耶路撒冷,毁第一圣殿,把犹太人掳往巴比伦','Took Jerusalem in 586 BCE, destroyed the First Temple and deported the Jews'],
     ['重建巴比伦城,建伊什塔尔门与通天塔,城墙据希罗多德记载可容四马并驰','Rebuilt Babylon with the Ishtar Gate and the great ziggurat; Herodotus says four horses could race abreast on its walls'],
     ['相传为思乡的王后建空中花园,即古代七大奇迹之一','The Hanging Gardens, one of the seven wonders, are traditionally credited to him and a homesick queen']],
  s:['"巴比伦之囚"是犹太史上的转折点:失去圣殿后,犹太教从围绕祭祀转向围绕经典与会堂,这一形态延续至今,也深刻影响了基督教与伊斯兰教。伊什塔尔门 1930 年代被搬到柏林重建,今天仍是柏林佩加蒙博物馆的镇馆之物。',
     'The Babylonian exile was the hinge of Jewish history: without a temple, Judaism reorganised itself around text and congregation, the form it has kept ever since — and the form Christianity and Islam grew out of. The Ishtar Gate was shipped to Berlin in the 1930s and is still the centrepiece of the Pergamon Museum.'] },
'汉尼拔': { g:'war', y:[-247,-183], c:'迦太基', n:['汉尼拔','Hannibal'],
  t:['他带着大象翻过阿尔卑斯山,在意大利打了十六年,罗马始终不敢与他正面决战。',
     'He crossed the Alps with elephants, fought sixteen years inside Italy, and Rome never dared face him in open battle again.'],
  a:[['前 218 年率军翻越阿尔卑斯山,损失近半兵力,但从罗马意想不到的方向出现','Crossed the Alps in 218 BCE, losing nearly half his army but appearing where Rome least expected'],
     ['前 216 年坎尼会战以少围多,一天之内歼灭罗马军队约五万人','At Cannae in 216 BCE he encircled a larger army and destroyed some 50,000 Romans in a day'],
     ['前 202 年扎马战役败于西庇阿,迦太基投降','Lost to Scipio at Zama in 202 BCE, and Carthage surrendered']],
  s:['坎尼会战的双包围战术是军事史上被研究最多的战例,从德国的施利芬计划到美国西点军校至今仍在教。他失败后罗马再无对手,地中海成了罗马的内海。"汉尼拔在城门口"至今是意大利语里表示大难临头的谚语。',
     'The double envelopment at Cannae is the most studied battle in military history, taught from the German general staff\'s Schlieffen Plan to West Point today. After his defeat Rome had no rival left and the Mediterranean became a Roman lake. "Hannibal at the gates" is still an Italian phrase for imminent disaster.'] },
'居鲁士': { g:'king', y:[-600,-530], ca:1, r:[-559,-530], c:'波斯(阿契美尼德)', n:['居鲁士','Cyrus the Great'],
  t:['他征服了当时已知世界的大半,却以宽待被征服者出名。',
     'He conquered most of the known world, and became famous for how he treated the conquered.'],
  a:[['二十年内灭米底、吕底亚、新巴比伦,建立当时最大的帝国','In twenty years he took Media, Lydia and Babylon, assembling the largest empire yet seen'],
     ['前 539 年入巴比伦后释放犹太人,允许他们回耶路撒冷重建圣殿','On taking Babylon in 539 BCE he freed the Jews and let them return to rebuild the Temple'],
     ['颁布居鲁士圆柱,宣布保留各地原有的宗教与习俗','Issued the Cyrus Cylinder, confirming that local religions and customs would stand']],
  s:['居鲁士圆柱现藏大英博物馆,常被称为"最早的人权宣言"——这一说法有争议,但它确实是最早明确宣示宗教宽容的统治者文告之一。他是《圣经》里唯一被称为"受膏者"的非犹太人。1971 年伊朗建国两千五百年庆典即以他即位为起点。',
     'The Cyrus Cylinder, now in the British Museum, is often called the first declaration of human rights — a contested label, but it is genuinely among the earliest royal proclamations of religious tolerance. He is the only non-Jew called "anointed" in the Hebrew Bible, and Iran dated its 2,500th anniversary in 1971 from his accession.'] },
'大流士': { g:'king', y:[-550,-486], r:[-522,-486], c:'波斯(阿契美尼德)', n:['大流士','Darius I'],
  t:['帝国是居鲁士打下来的,让它能运转两百年的制度是他建的。',
     'Cyrus conquered the empire. Darius built the machinery that kept it running for two centuries.'],
  a:[['把帝国划为二十余个行省,派总督管理,另派"国王的耳目"巡查监督','Divided the empire into some twenty satrapies, each with a governor — and inspectors called the King\'s Eyes'],
     ['修御道,从苏萨到萨第斯约二千七百公里,设驿站,信使七天可达','Built the Royal Road, 2,700 km from Susa to Sardis, with relay posts letting a courier cross it in seven days'],
     ['统一货币与度量衡,开凿连接尼罗河与红海的运河','Standardised coinage and measures, and cut a canal from the Nile to the Red Sea']],
  s:['行省加驿传的组合是后世所有大陆帝国的治理模板,罗马、阿拉伯、蒙古都在此基础上改进。希罗多德描述御道信使"风雨无阻"的那句话,后来被刻在纽约中央邮局的门楣上,成了美国邮政的非官方格言。',
     'Provinces plus a relay system became the template for every land empire afterwards — Rome, the Caliphate and the Mongols all refined it. Herodotus\' line about his couriers stopped by neither snow nor rain nor heat nor gloom of night is carved over the New York post office, and serves as the unofficial motto of the US mail.'] },
'托勒密一世': { g:'king', y:[-367,-282], ca:1, r:[-305,-282], c:'希腊化王朝', n:['托勒密一世','Ptolemy I'],
  t:['亚历山大的部将。帝国分裂时他挑了埃及,还抢走了亚历山大的遗体。',
     'One of Alexander\'s generals. When the empire broke up he took Egypt — and hijacked Alexander\'s corpse on the way.'],
  a:[['前 305 年称王,建立统治埃及近三百年的托勒密王朝','Declared himself king in 305 BCE, founding a dynasty that ruled Egypt for nearly three centuries'],
     ['劫走亚历山大的灵柩葬于亚历山大里亚,使该城成为朝圣地','Diverted Alexander\'s funeral cortege to Alexandria, making the city a place of pilgrimage'],
     ['创建缪斯宫与亚历山大图书馆,以国家经费供养学者','Founded the Museum and Library of Alexandria, paying scholars out of the treasury']],
  s:['亚历山大图书馆是古代世界最大的知识中心,藏书号称数十万卷,欧几里得、埃拉托色尼、阿基米德都在此工作或求学。以国家财政长期供养专职研究者,这是人类历史上第一次,也是现代研究机构的雏形。',
     'The Library of Alexandria was the greatest concentration of knowledge in the ancient world, said to hold hundreds of thousands of scrolls; Euclid, Eratosthenes and Archimedes all worked or studied there. A state salarying full-time researchers indefinitely was a first in human history, and the ancestor of the modern research institute.'] },
'欧几里得': { g:'sci', y:[-325,-265], ca:1, c:'希腊化王朝', n:['欧几里得','Euclid'],
  t:['他写的教科书被用了两千三百年,这是人类出版史上的纪录。',
     'He wrote a textbook that stayed in use for 2,300 years — a record in the history of publishing.'],
  a:[['写《几何原本》十三卷,从五条公设推出四百六十五个命题','Wrote the thirteen books of the Elements, deriving 465 propositions from five postulates'],
     ['证明质数有无穷多个,证法至今仍是数学系第一课的范例','Proved there are infinitely many primes — still the model proof taught in first-year mathematics'],
     ['据说对国王说:几何无王者之路','Told the king, so the story goes, that there is no royal road to geometry']],
  s:['《几何原本》是除《圣经》外印刷版本最多的书之一,直到 20 世纪初仍是欧美中学的标准教材。它真正的贡献是"公理化方法"——先立定义与公理,再逐步推出结论。这套方法后来被牛顿、斯宾诺莎乃至《美国独立宣言》直接模仿。',
     'The Elements has appeared in more editions than almost any book except the Bible, and was still the standard school text in Europe and America into the twentieth century. Its real gift was the axiomatic method — start from definitions and postulates, derive everything else — copied afterwards by Newton, Spinoza, and the drafters of the American Declaration of Independence.'] },
'阿基米德': { g:'sci', y:[-287,-212], c:'希腊化王朝', n:['阿基米德','Archimedes'],
  t:['他在洗澡时想通了浮力,光着身子跑上街喊"我找到了"。',
     'He worked out buoyancy in the bath and ran into the street naked shouting that he had found it.'],
  a:[['发现浮力原理,并用它验出国王的金冠掺了银','Discovered the principle of buoyancy, and used it to catch a goldsmith adulterating the king\'s crown'],
     ['提出杠杆原理,说"给我一个支点,我能撬动地球"','Stated the law of the lever: give me a place to stand and I will move the earth'],
     ['用穷竭法算出圆周率在 3.1408 与 3.1429 之间,并求出球体体积公式','Bracketed pi between 3.1408 and 3.1429 by exhaustion, and found the volume of a sphere']],
  s:['他求面积与体积的穷竭法已经非常接近微积分,比牛顿和莱布尼茨早了一千八百年。前 212 年罗马军队攻破叙拉古时他正在地上画图,士兵不认识他,把他杀了。他要求墓碑上刻一个球内接于圆柱的图形——这是他自己最看重的成果。',
     'His method of exhaustion came remarkably close to integral calculus, 1,800 years before Newton and Leibniz. When Rome stormed Syracuse in 212 BCE he was drawing figures in the sand; the soldier did not know who he was and killed him. He asked for a sphere inside a cylinder on his tombstone — the result he was proudest of.'] },
'沙普尔一世': { g:'king', y:[240,270], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'帕提亚·萨珊', n:['沙普尔一世','Shapur I'],
  t:['他是唯一一个活捉了罗马皇帝的人。',
     'He is the only man ever to take a Roman emperor alive.'],
  a:[['三次击败罗马军队,260 年在埃德萨俘获罗马皇帝瓦莱里安','Beat three Roman armies and captured the emperor Valerian at Edessa in 260'],
     ['把战俘中的工匠用于修桥筑城,今伊朗的沙德尔万古堰即为其一','Put captured Roman engineers to work on bridges and dams still standing in Iran today'],
     ['扶植摩尼教,允许其在境内传播','Gave the prophet Mani his protection and let Manichaeism spread']],
  s:['罗马皇帝被俘在罗马史上是空前的耻辱,此事被刻在纳克什-鲁斯塔姆的崖壁上,今天仍能看到瓦莱里安跪在马前的浮雕。萨珊波斯自此成为罗马-拜占庭四百年间唯一势均力敌的对手,两大帝国的长期消耗是 7 世纪阿拉伯人迅速崛起的背景之一。',
     'No Roman emperor had ever been taken prisoner; the humiliation was carved into the cliffs at Naqsh-e Rustam, where Valerian still kneels before the Persian\'s horse. Sasanian Persia became the only power Rome and Byzantium never mastered, and four centuries of mutual exhaustion helped clear the way for the Arab conquests of the seventh.'] },
'库思老一世': { g:'king', y:[531,579], yk:'r', c:'帕提亚·萨珊', n:['库思老一世','Khosrow I'],
  t:['萨珊波斯最有名的君主,以公正著称,波斯语里他的称号意为"不朽的灵魂"。',
     'The most celebrated Sasanian king, remembered for justice; his title means "of the immortal soul".'],
  a:[['改革税制,按土地面积与作物固定征税,取代随意摊派','Reformed taxation onto fixed assessments of land and crop, replacing arbitrary levies'],
     ['529 年雅典学园被查士丁尼关闭后,收留流亡的希腊哲学家','Took in the Greek philosophers exiled when Justinian closed the Academy in 529'],
     ['下令翻译印度、希腊典籍为中古波斯语,包括《五卷书》与医学著作','Had Indian and Greek works translated into Middle Persian, including the Panchatantra and medical texts']],
  s:['他主持的翻译工程把希腊与印度的学问汇入波斯,两百年后阿拔斯王朝的百年翻译运动直接继承了这批遗产与人才。经他从印度引进的《五卷书》后来译成阿拉伯文、拉丁文,是伊索寓言之外流传最广的故事集。他的税制被后来的阿拉伯帝国照搬。',
     'His translation programme funnelled Greek and Indian learning into Persia, and two centuries later the Abbasid translation movement inherited both the texts and the people. The Panchatantra he brought from India passed into Arabic and then Latin, becoming the most widely travelled story collection after Aesop. The Caliphate simply adopted his tax system.'] },
'穆罕默德': { g:'faith', y:[570,632], ca:1, c:'阿拉伯哈里发', n:['穆罕默德','Muhammad'],
  t:['四十岁前是个商人。他去世时,阿拉伯半岛已经统一在一个信仰之下。',
     'A merchant until he was forty. By his death the Arabian peninsula was united under one faith.'],
  a:[['约 610 年起在麦加传教,宣称接受启示,主张独一真主与穷人的权利','From about 610 he preached one God — and the rights of the poor — in Mecca'],
     ['622 年迁往麦地那,建立第一个穆斯林社群,这一年成为伊斯兰历元年','Moved to Medina in 622 and founded the first Muslim community; that year begins the Islamic calendar'],
     ['630 年兵不血刃进入麦加,清除克尔白的偶像','Entered Mecca without a battle in 630 and cleared the idols from the Kaaba']],
  s:['他去世后一百年内,阿拉伯人建立了从西班牙到印度河的帝国。今天全球约有十九亿穆斯林,占世界人口约四分之一,伊斯兰教是增长最快的主要宗教。《古兰经》是最早被完整定型并保持文本统一的宗教经典之一。',
     'Within a century of his death the Arabs ruled from Spain to the Indus. Today some 1.9 billion people — about a quarter of humanity — are Muslims, and Islam is the fastest-growing major religion. The Quran is among the earliest scriptures to have been fixed in a single standard text and kept that way.'] },
'哈伦·拉希德': { g:'king', y:[763,809], r:[786,809], c:'阿拉伯哈里发', n:['哈伦·拉希德','Harun al-Rashid'],
  t:['《一千零一夜》里那个夜里换上便装、微服私访的哈里发,原型是他。',
     'The caliph who slips into disguise and walks his city by night in the Thousand and One Nights was modelled on him.'],
  a:[['在位期间巴格达人口达数十万,是当时西方世界最大的城市','Baghdad in his reign held hundreds of thousands, the largest city west of China'],
     ['与查理曼互派使节,曾送去一头名叫阿布·阿拔斯的大象和一座水钟','Exchanged embassies with Charlemagne, sending an elephant named Abul-Abbas and a water clock'],
     ['扶植学者与译经事业,为后来的智慧宫奠定基础','Backed scholars and translators, laying the ground for the House of Wisdom']],
  s:['阿拔斯王朝在他这一朝达到鼎盛,巴格达成为欧亚大陆的学术与商业中心。他支持的翻译工作在其子马蒙手中扩展为百年翻译运动——欧洲后来重新读到亚里士多德,走的正是这条路。',
     'The Abbasid caliphate peaked under him, and Baghdad became the intellectual and commercial hub of Eurasia. The translation work he sponsored grew under his son al-Mamun into the century-long translation movement — the route by which Europe would later recover Aristotle.'] },
'穆罕默德二世': { g:'war', y:[1432,1481], r:[1451,1481], c:'奥斯曼帝国', n:['穆罕默德二世','Mehmed II'],
  t:['21 岁那年,他攻下了一座一千一百年没被攻破的城。',
     'At twenty-one he took a city that had held out for eleven hundred years.'],
  a:[['1453 年围攻君士坦丁堡五十三天,用当时最大的巨炮轰塌城墙','Besieged Constantinople for fifty-three days in 1453, battering the walls with the largest cannon yet cast'],
     ['把七十余艘战船从陆路拖过山丘,绕过封锁的金角湾','Hauled seventy-odd ships overland across a hill to bypass the chained Golden Horn'],
     ['占领后重建城市,招募各族居民,允许东正教牧首继续存在','Rebuilt the city afterwards, resettled it with many peoples, and kept the Orthodox patriarchate in place']],
  s:['1453 年常被用作中世纪结束的标志。君士坦丁堡陷落切断了欧洲通往东方的传统商路,直接刺激了葡萄牙与西班牙寻找新航路——四十年后哥伦布出海。逃往意大利的拜占庭学者带去的希腊典籍,也是文艺复兴的推力之一。',
     'The year 1453 is often taken as the end of the Middle Ages. The fall of Constantinople cut Europe\'s established road east and pushed Portugal and Spain to look for another — Columbus sailed forty years later. The Greek manuscripts carried to Italy by fleeing Byzantine scholars fed the Renaissance.'] },
'苏莱曼大帝': { g:'king', y:[1494,1566], r:[1520,1566], c:'奥斯曼帝国', n:['苏莱曼大帝','Suleiman the Magnificent'],
  t:['欧洲人叫他"大帝",后来的奥斯曼人叫他"立法者"。',
     'Europe called him the Magnificent; later Ottomans called him the Lawgiver.'],
  a:[['1526 年莫哈奇战役击溃匈牙利,1529 年兵临维也纳城下','Destroyed Hungary at Mohács in 1526 and stood before Vienna in 1529'],
     ['系统整理帝国法律,与伊斯兰教法并行,故称"立法者"','Codified the empire\'s secular law to run alongside religious law — hence the Lawgiver'],
     ['任用建筑师希南,建苏莱曼尼耶清真寺等三百余座建筑','Employed the architect Sinan, who built the Süleymaniye and some three hundred other works']],
  s:['奥斯曼帝国在他手上达到顶点,横跨欧亚非三洲,地中海一度成为奥斯曼的内海。他确立的米利特制度让不同宗教社群自治,是前现代最成熟的多元治理方案之一。希南设计的建筑群 1985 年随伊斯坦布尔历史城区列入世界遗产。',
     'The empire reached its height under him, spanning three continents and turning the eastern Mediterranean into an Ottoman lake. His millet system, granting religious communities self-government, was among the most workable pluralist arrangements of the pre-modern world. Sinan\'s buildings were listed with historic Istanbul as World Heritage in 1985.'] },
'冒顿单于': { g:'war', y:[-234,-174], ca:1, r:[-209,-174], c:'匈奴', n:['冒顿单于','Modu Chanyu'],
  t:['他鸣镝所指,部下必须射——他先射自己的爱马,再射自己的妻子,最后射向父亲。',
     'Wherever his whistling arrow flew, his men had to shoot. He aimed first at his own horse, then at his wife, and finally at his father.'],
  a:[['用鸣镝训练出绝对服从的亲兵,前 209 年弑父自立','Trained a guard to absolute obedience with the whistling arrow, and killed his father in 209 BCE'],
     ['击败东胡与月氏,统一草原各部,建立第一个草原帝国','Crushed the Donghu and Yuezhi, united the steppe tribes and founded the first nomadic empire'],
     ['前 200 年白登之围,以四十万骑兵困住汉高祖刘邦七天七夜','Trapped the founding Han emperor for seven days at Baideng in 200 BCE with 400,000 horsemen']],
  s:['白登之围后汉朝被迫和亲纳贡近七十年,直到汉武帝才转攻为守。他创立的左右贤王、二十四长制,是此后突厥、蒙古等草原政权的组织范本——游牧民族第一次有了能与农耕帝国正面抗衡的组织形式。',
     'After Baideng the Han paid tribute and sent princesses for nearly seventy years, until Emperor Wu reversed the relationship. His organisation of kings of the left and right and twenty-four commanders became the template for the Turks and Mongols after him: it was the first time nomads had a structure that could face a settled empire on level terms.'] },
'社崙可汗': { g:'king', y:[402,410], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'柔然', n:['社崙可汗','Shelun Khagan'],
  t:['"可汗"这个称号是他先用的。此后一千五百年草原君主都这么叫。',
     'He was the first to use the title khagan. Steppe rulers used it for the next fifteen hundred years.'],
  a:[['402 年击败周边部落,统一漠北,自称丘豆伐可汗','Beat his neighbours in 402, unified the northern steppe and styled himself khagan'],
     ['首创"可汗"作为最高君主称号,取代匈奴的"单于"','Replaced the old Xiongnu title chanyu with khagan as the supreme style'],
     ['按千人为军、置军将,把部落编成军事单位','Organised the tribes into units of a thousand under appointed commanders']],
  s:['"可汗"经突厥、回鹘、契丹、蒙古一路沿用到清代,是欧亚草原最通行的君主称号,今天仍存于哈萨克、蒙古等地的语言与姓氏中。他的千人编制也是后来突厥与蒙古千户制的雏形。',
     'Khagan passed through the Turks, Uyghurs, Khitans and Mongols all the way to the Qing, becoming the most widely used sovereign title across the Eurasian steppe, and survives today in Central Asian languages and surnames. His thousand-man units prefigured the Turkic and Mongol decimal armies.'] },
'阿提拉': { g:'war', y:[406,453], ca:1, r:[434,453], c:'匈人', n:['阿提拉','Attila'],
  t:['欧洲人叫他"上帝之鞭"。他一度同时向东西两个罗马帝国收贡。',
     'Europe called him the Scourge of God. For a while he took tribute from both Roman empires at once.'],
  a:[['迫使东罗马帝国每年缴纳大量黄金,一度增至两千一百磅','Forced the Eastern Empire into an annual tribute that rose to 2,100 pounds of gold'],
     ['451 年入侵高卢,在沙隆战役与罗马-西哥特联军决战','Invaded Gaul in 451 and fought a Roman-Visigothic coalition at the Catalaunian Plains'],
     ['452 年进军意大利,据传在教皇利奥一世当面劝说后撤兵','Marched into Italy in 452 and, by tradition, withdrew after meeting Pope Leo I in person']],
  s:['匈人西迁引发的多米诺效应把日耳曼各部推向罗马边境,是西罗马帝国崩溃的直接推力之一——他死后二十三年,西罗马灭亡。他在欧洲文化中长期是"野蛮"的象征,但在匈牙利,阿提拉至今是常见的男孩名。',
     'The westward push of the Huns shoved the Germanic peoples onto Rome\'s frontiers and was among the direct causes of the Western Empire\'s collapse — which came twenty-three years after his death. In European memory he became the emblem of barbarism; in Hungary, Attila is still an ordinary boy\'s name.'] },
'伊本·西那': { g:'sci', y:[980,1037], c:'萨曼王朝', n:['伊本·西那','Ibn Sina (Avicenna)'],
  t:['十岁背完《古兰经》,十六岁行医,十八岁说自己已经没什么可学的了。',
     'He had the Quran by heart at ten, was practising medicine at sixteen, and at eighteen declared there was nothing left for him to learn.'],
  a:[['写《医典》五卷,把希腊、波斯、印度与阿拉伯医学整合成一个体系','Wrote the five-volume Canon of Medicine, fusing Greek, Persian, Indian and Arab practice into one system'],
     ['提出传染病由"微小生物"引起,主张隔离病人','Suggested that some diseases spread by tiny organisms, and argued for quarantine'],
     ['写《治疗论》,系统论述逻辑、物理、数学与形而上学','Wrote the Book of Healing, a survey of logic, physics, mathematics and metaphysics']],
  s:['《医典》12 世纪译成拉丁文后,成为欧洲医学院的标准教材,一直用到 17 世纪——总共约六百年。他对灵魂与存在的论证影响了阿奎那与整个经院哲学。月球上有环形山以他命名,他的头像出现在塔吉克斯坦的纸币上。',
     'Translated into Latin in the twelfth century, the Canon was the standard text in European medical schools until the seventeenth — some six hundred years. His arguments about the soul and existence shaped Aquinas and scholasticism generally. A lunar crater carries his name, and his face is on Tajik banknotes.'] },
'比鲁尼': { g:'sci', y:[973,1050], c:'萨曼王朝', n:['比鲁尼','al-Biruni'],
  t:['他用一座山和一次日落算出了地球的半径,误差不到百分之一。',
     'He measured the radius of the earth from a hilltop and a sunset, and came within one per cent.'],
  a:[['在今巴基斯坦用三角测量法算出地球半径约 6339 公里','Used trigonometry in what is now Pakistan to get an earth radius of about 6,339 km'],
     ['随军进入印度,学梵语,写《印度志》,如实记录印度的宗教、哲学与科学','Went to India with an army, learned Sanskrit, and wrote an even-handed account of its religion, philosophy and science'],
     ['测定十八种宝石与金属的比重,精度接近现代值','Measured the specific gravity of eighteen gems and metals, close to modern values']],
  s:['地球半径的现代值约 6371 公里,他的误差约百分之零点五。《印度志》被公认是前现代最客观的跨文化研究之一——他明确说明自己是在描述而非评判异教徒的信仰,这在 11 世纪极为罕见,他也因此被称为"比较宗教学之父"。',
     'The modern figure is about 6,371 km, so he was off by roughly half a per cent. His book on India is regarded as one of the most objective cross-cultural studies written before modern times — he stated plainly that he was describing, not judging, the beliefs of unbelievers, which in the eleventh century was extraordinary, and has earned him the title father of comparative religion.'] },
'菲尔多西': { g:'art', y:[940,1020], ca:1, c:'萨曼王朝', n:['菲尔多西','Ferdowsi'],
  t:['他用三十年写了一部六万联的史诗,把波斯语从阿拉伯语的阴影里救了出来。',
     'He spent thirty years on an epic of sixty thousand couplets, and pulled Persian back out from under Arabic.'],
  a:[['花约三十年写成《列王纪》,篇幅约为《伊利亚特》与《奥德赛》之和的七倍','Took some thirty years over the Shahnameh, about seven times the length of the Iliad and Odyssey combined'],
     ['刻意大量使用波斯本土词汇,尽量避开阿拉伯语借词','Deliberately used native Persian vocabulary and avoided Arabic loanwords wherever he could'],
     ['讲述从开天辟地到萨珊灭亡的五十位君主与英雄的故事','Told the stories of fifty kings and heroes, from the creation to the fall of the Sasanians']],
  s:['《列王纪》被公认为保住现代波斯语的关键——阿拉伯征服两百年后,它证明了波斯语仍能承载最高级的文学。今天伊朗、阿富汗、塔吉克斯坦的国族叙事都以它为源头,书中的故事至今是波斯细密画与街头说书最常见的题材。',
     'The Shahnameh is generally credited with saving modern Persian: two centuries after the Arab conquest, it proved the language could still carry literature of the first rank. Iran, Afghanistan and Tajikistan all trace their national story to it, and its episodes remain the commonest subject of Persian miniature painting and street storytelling.'] },
'忽必烈': { g:'king', y:[1215,1294], r:[1260,1294], c:'蒙古帝国', n:['忽必烈','Kublai Khan'],
  t:['成吉思汗的孙子。他是第一个统治全中国的非汉族皇帝。',
     'Genghis\' grandson, and the first non-Chinese ruler of all China.'],
  a:[['1271 年定国号"大元",1279 年灭南宋,统一中国','Proclaimed the Yuan in 1271 and finished off the Southern Song in 1279'],
     ['定都大都(今北京),重开大运河,设驿站遍及欧亚','Made Dadu — modern Beijing — his capital, reopened the Grand Canal and ran post stations across Eurasia'],
     ['两次东征日本均遇台风失败,日本称之为"神风"','Twice sent fleets against Japan and twice lost them to typhoons the Japanese called kamikaze']],
  s:['元朝是中国历史上疆域最大的王朝之一,大都自此成为中国六百年的政治中心。他统治期间马可·波罗来华,其游记让欧洲第一次系统了解东亚,并直接激发了后来的地理大发现——哥伦布随身带的正是一本《马可·波罗游记》。',
     'The Yuan was among the largest empires ever to rule China, and his Dadu has been the political centre of the country for six hundred years since. Marco Polo came to his court, and the book that resulted gave Europe its first systematic picture of East Asia — Columbus carried a heavily annotated copy on his voyages.'] },
'拔都': { g:'war', y:[1207,1255], ca:1, c:'蒙古帝国', n:['拔都','Batu Khan'],
  t:['他是唯一一个征服了俄罗斯的人。此后两百四十年,俄国向蒙古纳贡。',
     'He is the only man ever to conquer Russia. For 240 years afterwards, Russia paid tribute to the Mongols.'],
  a:[['1237—1240 年攻灭基辅罗斯诸公国,基辅城被彻底摧毁','Destroyed the principalities of Kievan Rus between 1237 and 1240; Kiev itself was levelled'],
     ['1241 年在里格尼茨与莫希两战击溃波兰与匈牙利军队','Smashed Polish and Hungarian armies at Legnica and Mohi in 1241'],
     ['因大汗窝阔台去世而回师,建立金帐汗国','Turned back on news of the great khan\'s death, and founded the Golden Horde']],
  s:['1241 年蒙古军已抵达维也纳附近,窝阔台之死是欧洲免于被征服的偶然原因。金帐汗国对罗斯的统治持续到 1480 年,把俄国与西欧的发展路径彻底分开——莫斯科正是靠为蒙古人代收贡赋而崛起,并最终统一俄国。',
     'By 1241 Mongol scouts were near Vienna; the great khan\'s death is the accident that spared western Europe. The Golden Horde held the Rus until 1480, and those centuries separated Russia\'s development from western Europe\'s for good — Moscow itself rose by collecting the Mongols\' tribute, and used that position to unify Russia.'] },
'帖木儿': { g:'war', y:[1336,1405], r:[1370,1405], c:'帖木儿帝国', n:['帖木儿','Timur'],
  t:['腿有残疾,人称"跛子帖木儿"。他是最后一个横扫欧亚的草原征服者。',
     'Lame from an old wound — Timur the Lame. The last steppe conqueror to sweep across Eurasia.'],
  a:[['三十五年间横扫波斯、印度北部、小亚细亚与南俄,几乎未尝败绩','Overran Persia, northern India, Anatolia and southern Russia in thirty-five years, almost never losing'],
     ['1398 年攻陷德里,1402 年安卡拉之战俘获奥斯曼苏丹巴耶塞特一世','Sacked Delhi in 1398, and captured the Ottoman sultan Bayezid at Ankara in 1402'],
     ['把各地工匠掳到撒马尔罕,建起当时中亚最壮丽的城市','Deported craftsmen from everywhere to Samarkand and built the most splendid city in Central Asia']],
  s:['安卡拉之战使奥斯曼帝国瘫痪十余年,君士坦丁堡因此又多存续了半个世纪。撒马尔罕的建筑群 2001 年列入世界遗产。他的后代巴布尔南下印度建立莫卧儿帝国——阿克巴、沙贾汗都是他的直系后裔。',
     'Ankara paralysed the Ottomans for a decade and bought Constantinople another fifty years. His Samarkand became World Heritage in 2001. And his descendant Babur went south into India to found the Mughal empire — Akbar and Shah Jahan were his direct heirs.'] },
'兀鲁伯': { g:'sci', y:[1394,1449], r:[1447,1449], c:'帖木儿帝国', n:['兀鲁伯','Ulugh Beg'],
  t:['帖木儿的孙子。他对天文的兴趣远大于对治国的兴趣,最后被自己的儿子杀了。',
     'Timur\'s grandson, far more interested in the stars than in governing — and murdered by his own son.'],
  a:[['1420 年代在撒马尔罕建大型天文台,六分仪半径达四十米','Built a great observatory at Samarkand in the 1420s, its sextant arc 40 m in radius'],
     ['编成《兀鲁伯天文表》,记录 1018 颗恒星的位置','Compiled a star catalogue giving positions for 1,018 stars'],
     ['测得一恒星年为 365 天 6 小时 10 分 8 秒,与今值仅差约 25 秒','Measured the sidereal year at 365 d 6 h 10 m 8 s — about 25 seconds off the modern value']],
  s:['他的星表是托勒密之后、望远镜发明之前最精确的一部,17 世纪译成拉丁文后在牛津出版,直接为欧洲天文学家所用。他的天文台遗址 2001 年随撒马尔罕列入世界遗产,月球上有环形山以他命名。',
     'His catalogue was the most accurate produced between Ptolemy and the telescope; translated into Latin and printed at Oxford in the seventeenth century, it went straight into European hands. The observatory ruins were listed with Samarkand as World Heritage in 2001, and a lunar crater carries his name.'] },
'旃陀罗笈多': { g:'king', y:[-321,-297], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'孔雀王朝', n:['旃陀罗笈多','Chandragupta Maurya'],
  t:['他赶走了亚历山大留下的希腊守军,建立了印度第一个统一帝国。',
     'He drove out the garrisons Alexander left behind and founded India\'s first unified empire.'],
  a:[['约前 322 年推翻难陀王朝,建立孔雀王朝','Overthrew the Nanda dynasty around 322 BCE and founded the Maurya'],
     ['前 305 年击退塞琉古一世,以五百头战象换得阿富汗东部的领土','Beat back Seleucus in 305 BCE, trading five hundred war elephants for territory in eastern Afghanistan'],
     ['以考底利耶为相,后者著《政事论》,是印度最早的治国与权谋专著','Took Kautilya as his minister, whose Arthashastra is India\'s earliest treatise on statecraft']],
  s:['他是阿育王的祖父,孔雀王朝的疆域基础由他奠定。《政事论》讨论税收、间谍、外交与战争,常被拿来与马基雅维利的《君主论》并称,却早了一千八百年。晚年他相传皈依耆那教,南下绝食而终。',
     'He was Ashoka\'s grandfather, and the territory Ashoka inherited was his work. The Arthashastra, on taxation, espionage, diplomacy and war, is routinely compared to Machiavelli\'s Prince — eighteen centuries earlier. Tradition says he ended his life as a Jain ascetic, fasting to death in the south.'] },
'乔达米普特拉·娑多迦尼': { g:'king', y:[106,130], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'百乘王朝', n:['乔达米普特拉·娑多迦尼','Gautamiputra Satakarni'],
  t:['百乘王朝最强的君主。他的功绩是他母亲刻在石壁上留下来的。',
     'The greatest of the Satavahana kings — and what we know of him, his mother had carved on a cave wall.'],
  a:[['击败西部的塞种统治者,收复被夺去的德干西部领土','Defeated the Saka rulers to the west and recovered the lost western Deccan'],
     ['疆域一度从今天的古吉拉特延伸到安得拉','Held territory from modern Gujarat across to Andhra'],
     ['纳西克石窟的铭文由其母高塔米所立,详述其战功','The Nashik cave inscription recording his victories was set up by his mother Gautami']],
  s:['百乘王朝是孔雀崩溃后德干高原的主要政权,把北印度与南印度、以及印度与罗马的海上贸易连了起来——罗马金币在南印度大量出土,即这一时期的遗存。他以母名冠于己名之上,反映了当时南印度母系传统的影响。',
     'The Satavahanas were the main power on the Deccan after the Maurya collapse, linking north and south India and running the sea trade with Rome — the Roman gold coins found across southern India date from this period. That he took his mother\'s name before his own reflects the matrilineal customs of the region.'] },
'迦梨陀娑': { g:'art', y:[380,450], yk:'a', ca:1, c:'笈多王朝', n:['迦梨陀娑','Kalidasa'],
  t:['印度最伟大的梵语诗人和剧作家,生平几乎一无所知。',
     'India\'s greatest Sanskrit poet and playwright, about whose life almost nothing is known.'],
  a:[['写剧本《沙恭达罗》,讲一位国王与林中少女的爱情与遗忘','Wrote Shakuntala, on a king, a forest girl, and a forgetting'],
     ['写长诗《云使》,让一位被流放的仙人托一朵云给妻子带话','Wrote the Cloud Messenger, in which an exiled spirit sends word to his wife by cloud'],
     ['相传为超日王宫廷"九宝"之一','Traditionally counted among the nine jewels of Vikramaditya\'s court']],
  s:['1789 年《沙恭达罗》被译成英文,随即转译成德文,歌德读后写诗盛赞,称一部作品里同时有了春天的花与秋天的果。这是欧洲第一次认真接触印度文学,直接催生了 19 世纪欧洲的梵语研究与东方学。',
     'Translated into English in 1789 and immediately into German, Shakuntala so struck Goethe that he wrote a poem in its praise, saying one work held the blossoms of spring and the fruits of autumn together. It was Europe\'s first serious encounter with Indian literature, and it launched nineteenth-century Sanskrit studies.'] },
'阿耶波多': { g:'sci', y:[476,550], c:'笈多王朝', n:['阿耶波多','Aryabhata'],
  t:['23 岁写完一本书,里面说地球在自转——这比哥白尼早了一千年。',
     'He finished a book at twenty-three saying the earth turns on its own axis — a thousand years before Copernicus.'],
  a:[['提出地球自转,说星辰西移是因为地在转,好比船行时岸在退','Argued the earth rotates, and that the stars only seem to move west as the bank seems to move past a boat'],
     ['算出圆周率约 3.1416,并明确说这是"近似值"','Gave pi as approximately 3.1416 — and said explicitly that it was an approximation'],
     ['正确解释日食与月食是地球和月球的影子,而非神话中的怪物吞噬','Explained eclipses as shadows of earth and moon, not a demon swallowing them']],
  s:['他给出的一恒星年长度为 365 天 6 小时 12 分 30 秒,与今值相差约 3 分钟。他的著作经阿拉伯世界译介传入欧洲,是印度数学西传的主要渠道之一。印度 1975 年发射的第一颗人造卫星以他命名。',
     'His sidereal year came to 365 d 6 h 12 m 30 s, about three minutes off the modern figure. His work passed through Arabic into Europe and was one of the main channels by which Indian mathematics travelled west. India named its first satellite, launched in 1975, after him.'] },
'克莱武': { g:'war', y:[1725,1774], c:'英属印度', n:['克莱武','Robert Clive'],
  t:['一家贸易公司的职员,靠一场三千人对五万人的战役,替公司拿下了一个国家。',
     'A trading company\'s clerk who won a country for his employer with three thousand men against fifty thousand.'],
  a:[['1757 年普拉西战役,以约三千人击败孟加拉太守约五万大军——关键是买通了对方主将','Won Plassey in 1757 with about 3,000 men against some 50,000 — chiefly by buying the enemy commander'],
     ['1765 年为东印度公司取得孟加拉的税收权,公司从此可以直接征税','Secured the right to collect Bengal\'s revenues in 1765, turning the company into a tax authority'],
     ['个人在印度积聚巨额财富,回国后遭议会调查','Amassed a personal fortune and faced a parliamentary inquiry on his return']],
  s:['普拉西战役通常被视为英国统治印度的起点,一家商业公司由此成为一个次大陆的实际统治者,这在世界史上绝无仅有。公司统治下的孟加拉在 1770 年发生大饥荒,死亡人数估计达上千万。1858 年英国政府收回公司权力,直接统治印度。',
     'Plassey is conventionally the start of British rule in India — a commercial company became the effective government of a subcontinent, which has no parallel in world history. Company-run Bengal suffered a famine in 1770 in which estimates of the dead run into the millions. In 1858 the Crown took the company\'s powers and governed India directly.'] },
'甘地': { g:'state', y:[1869,1948], c:'英属印度', n:['甘地','Mahatma Gandhi'],
  t:['他没有军队、没有官职,却让一个帝国走了。',
     'He had no army and no office, and an empire left.'],
  a:[['1930 年食盐进军:步行 390 公里到海边自己煮盐,抗议英国的食盐专卖','In 1930 he walked 390 km to the sea to make salt, in defiance of the British monopoly'],
     ['多次绝食抗议,包括在印度教徒与穆斯林冲突时以绝食迫使双方停手','Fasted repeatedly, including to force Hindus and Muslims to stop killing each other'],
     ['坚持非暴力不合作,自己纺纱、穿土布,抵制英国纺织品','Held to non-violent non-cooperation, spinning his own cloth to boycott British textiles']],
  s:['印度 1947 年独立,此后二十余年间几十个殖民地相继独立。他的非暴力方法被马丁·路德·金、曼德拉直接借鉴——金在 1959 年专程去印度学习。联合国把他的生日 10 月 2 日定为国际非暴力日。1948 年他被一名印度教极端分子刺杀。',
     'India became independent in 1947, and dozens of colonies followed over the next two decades. His method was taken up directly by Martin Luther King, who travelled to India in 1959 to study it, and by Nelson Mandela. The UN made his birthday, 2 October, the International Day of Non-Violence. He was shot dead by a Hindu extremist in 1948.'] },
'松迪亚塔': { g:'king', y:[1235,1255], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'马里帝国', n:['松迪亚塔','Sundiata Keita'],
  t:['传说他小时候不能走路,后来成了马里帝国的开国之君。',
     'The story says he could not walk as a boy. He founded the Mali empire.'],
  a:[['约 1235 年在基里纳战役击败索索王苏芒古鲁,统一曼丁哥各部','Defeated the Sosso king at Kirina around 1235 and united the Mandinka'],
     ['颁布《库鲁坎富加宪章》,规定各族分工、禁止虐待俘虏、保障妇女地位','Proclaimed the Kurukan Fuga charter: duties by clan, no ill-treatment of captives, protections for women'],
     ['控制西非的黄金与食盐贸易路线','Took control of the gold and salt routes of West Africa']],
  s:['《库鲁坎富加宪章》被认为是世界上最早的成文宪章之一,2009 年由联合国教科文组织列入非物质文化遗产。他的事迹以口传史诗《松迪亚塔》的形式流传至今,由西非世袭的"格里奥"歌手代代相传八百年,是非洲最重要的口头文学。',
     'The Kurukan Fuga charter is regarded as one of the earliest written constitutions anywhere, and UNESCO listed it as intangible heritage in 2009. His story survives as the Epic of Sundiata, carried down for eight centuries by West Africa\'s hereditary griot singers — the most important work of oral literature on the continent.'] },
'曼萨·穆萨': { g:'king', y:[1312,1337], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'马里帝国', n:['曼萨·穆萨','Mansa Musa'],
  t:['他去麦加朝觐时沿途撒的黄金太多,埃及的金价跌了十年。',
     'He gave away so much gold on his pilgrimage that Egypt\'s gold price stayed depressed for a decade.'],
  a:[['1324 年率数千人朝觐麦加,携大量黄金,沿途施舍','Set out for Mecca in 1324 with thousands of retainers and vast quantities of gold, giving it away as he went'],
     ['在开罗的挥霍导致当地金价大跌,据记载十余年未恢复','His spending in Cairo crashed the gold price there; accounts say it took over a decade to recover'],
     ['归国后大兴土木,出资营建津加里贝尔清真寺,廷巴克图的经学传统在他一朝立住','Spent lavishly on building after his return, paying for the Djinguereber mosque; Timbuktu\'s scholarly tradition took hold in his reign']],
  s:['他的朝觐让欧洲第一次知道西非的存在。1375 年的《加泰罗尼亚地图集》把他画在撒哈拉以南,手持金块——这是欧洲地图上最早出现的非洲君主形象。廷巴克图此后两百年是伊斯兰世界的学术中心之一,古城 1988 年列入世界遗产。',
     'His pilgrimage was how Europe first learned West Africa existed. The Catalan Atlas of 1375 shows him enthroned south of the Sahara holding a gold nugget — the earliest depiction of an African ruler on a European map. Timbuktu became a centre of Islamic scholarship for the next two centuries, and its old town was listed as World Heritage in 1988.'] },
'阿方索一世': { g:'king', y:[1509,1543], yk:'r', c:'刚果王国', n:['阿方索一世','Afonso I of Kongo'],
  t:['一位皈依基督教的非洲国王,写信给葡萄牙国王,请他停止贩卖自己的子民。',
     'A Christian African king who wrote to the king of Portugal asking him to stop enslaving his people.'],
  a:[['本名恩津加·姆本巴,受洗后取葡萄牙名,把基督教定为国教','Born Nzinga Mbemba, he took a Portuguese name at baptism and made Christianity the state religion'],
     ['引入葡萄牙的文字、学校与技术,派儿子赴里斯本留学并成为主教','Brought in Portuguese letters, schools and crafts, and sent his son to Lisbon, where he became a bishop'],
     ['1526 年致信葡萄牙国王若昂三世,抗议奴隶贩子连贵族子弟都掳走','Wrote to João III in 1526, protesting that the slavers were seizing even noble children']],
  s:['他的信件是非洲统治者反对大西洋奴隶贸易最早的第一手文献,今天仍是研究这段历史的核心材料。葡萄牙没有回应,奴隶贸易继续了三个多世纪,约有一千二百万非洲人被运往美洲。他试图在接受欧洲技术与保住主权之间走一条中间路线,这条路线最终失败。',
     'His letters are the earliest first-hand protest by an African ruler against the Atlantic slave trade, and remain a core source for the period. Portugal did not act; the trade ran for another three centuries and carried some twelve million Africans to the Americas. His attempt to take European technology while keeping his sovereignty failed.'] },
'华盛顿': { g:'state', y:[1732,1799], r:[1789,1797], c:'美国', n:['华盛顿','George Washington'],
  t:['他两次交出了几乎无人能夺走的权力。',
     'Twice he handed back power that nobody could have taken from him.'],
  a:[['1775—1783 年任大陆军总司令,以劣势兵力拖垮英军','Commanded the Continental Army from 1775 to 1783 and outlasted a stronger enemy'],
     ['1783 年战争结束后主动交出军权,回弗农山庄务农','Resigned his commission in 1783 and went home to farm'],
     ['1797 年拒绝第三个任期,开创总统只做两任的惯例','Refused a third term in 1797, setting the two-term custom']],
  s:['当时的国王乔治三世听说他战后要回家种地,说"如果他真这么做,他将是世界上最伟大的人"。两任卸任的惯例被遵守了一百五十年,1951 年正式写入美国宪法第二十二修正案。他确立的"权力有期限"这个先例,是现代共和制最关键的一块基石。',
     'When George III heard he meant to go home and farm, he said that if he did, he would be the greatest man in the world. The two-term custom held for a century and a half and was written into the Constitution as the Twenty-Second Amendment in 1951. The precedent that power comes with an expiry date is among the load-bearing stones of the modern republic.'] },
'林肯': { g:'state', y:[1809,1865], r:[1861,1865], c:'美国', n:['林肯','Abraham Lincoln'],
  t:['木屋出身,自学法律。他上任六周后,国家分裂了。',
     'Born in a log cabin and self-taught in law. Six weeks after he took office, the country split.'],
  a:[['1861—1865 年领导联邦打赢内战,阻止南方独立','Led the Union through four years of civil war and stopped the South seceding'],
     ['1863 年发布《解放黑人奴隶宣言》','Issued the Emancipation Proclamation in 1863'],
     ['1863 年葛底斯堡演说仅两分钟、二百七十二字','Spoke at Gettysburg for two minutes — 272 words']],
  s:['内战死亡约六十二万人,是美国历史上死亡最多的战争。宪法第十三修正案在他遇刺后数月通过,正式废除奴隶制。葛底斯堡演说里"民有、民治、民享"一句,后来被写进多国宪法,孙中山的"三民主义"也受其影响。1865 年 4 月他在剧院遇刺身亡。',
     'The war killed some 620,000 people, more than any other in American history. The Thirteenth Amendment, abolishing slavery outright, passed months after his death. The phrase from Gettysburg — government of the people, by the people, for the people — has been written into constitutions around the world and shaped Sun Yat-sen\'s Three Principles. He was shot in a theatre in April 1865.'] },
'罗斯福': { g:'state', y:[1882,1945], r:[1933,1945], c:'美国', n:['罗斯福','Franklin D. Roosevelt'],
  t:['39 岁瘫痪,坐着轮椅当了十二年总统——美国唯一连任四届的人。',
     'Paralysed at thirty-nine, he governed twelve years from a wheelchair — the only American elected four times.'],
  a:[['1933 年起推行新政,建立社会保障、失业救济与银行存款保险','From 1933 the New Deal brought social security, unemployment relief and deposit insurance'],
     ['1941 年珍珠港事件后领导美国参战,成为同盟国的兵工厂','Took the US into the war after Pearl Harbor and turned it into the arsenal of the Allies'],
     ['与丘吉尔、斯大林会晤,规划战后秩序与联合国','Met Churchill and Stalin to design the post-war order and the United Nations']],
  s:['新政确立了政府对经济与社会保障负责的原则,美国的社会保障制度沿用至今。他推动创建的联合国 1945 年成立,是二战后国际秩序的核心机构。他去世后,美国 1951 年通过宪法第二十二修正案,把总统任期正式限定为两届。',
     'The New Deal established the principle that government is answerable for the economy and for social security, and its programmes still run. The United Nations he pushed for was founded in 1945 and remains the centre of the post-war order. After his death, the Twenty-Second Amendment fixed presidential terms at two.'] },
'杜桑·卢维杜尔': { g:'state', y:[1743,1803], c:'拉丁美洲诸国', n:['杜桑·卢维杜尔','Toussaint Louverture'],
    t:['他自己就是奴隶出身,后来指挥军队打退了西班牙和英国,逼得拿破仑派大军来抓他。','Born a slave himself, he ended up commanding armies that beat off Spain and Britain, until Napoleon sent a fleet to seize him.'],
    a:[['他 1743 年前后生在圣多明各一座种植园里,是奴隶。20 世纪末发现的档案显示他在 1772 到 1776 年间获得自由,比过去以为的早得多。1791 年奴隶起义爆发后他投身其中,几年里从一名军医做到全岛的实际统治者','He was born enslaved on a plantation in Saint-Domingue about 1743. Records found in the late twentieth century show he was freed some time between 1772 and 1776 — much earlier than used to be thought. He joined the slave rising after it broke out in 1791 and within a few years went from army doctor to the effective ruler of the whole island'],
       ['他打仗打得极好,也很会挑边站:先后与西班牙、法国、英国分别结盟又翻脸,始终围着一件事——废奴不能翻案。1801 年他颁布一部宪法,宣布岛上永远废除奴隶制','He fought very well and chose his sides with care, allying in turn with Spain, France and Britain and breaking with each, always around one point: the abolition must not be undone. In 1801 he issued a constitution declaring slavery abolished on the island forever'],
       ['1802 年拿破仑派大军来重新征服并恢复奴隶制。他被诱捕、押往法国,1803 年死在汝拉山中的茹堡监狱里,时年五十九。他没能看到独立——第二年元旦,他的部下宣布了','In 1802 Napoleon sent an army to reconquer the island and restore slavery. He was taken by a ruse, shipped to France, and died in 1803 at the Fort de Joux in the Jura, aged fifty-nine. He did not live to see independence: his officers declared it on the first day of the next year']],
    s:['他被捕上船时说过一句话,后来被反复引用:你们只是砍倒了自由之树的树干,它的根很深、很多,还会长回来。第二年他的话应验了。这个站里的人物大多出身王室、贵族或士人,他是极少数从最底层一路走到国家层面的——而且是被自己曾经的主人们围攻着走上去的。','A remark he made as he was put aboard ship has been quoted ever since: in overthrowing me you have cut down only the trunk of the tree of liberty, whose roots are many and deep, and it will grow again. Within a year he was proved right. Most of the people in this site began as royalty, nobility or scholars; he is among the very few who came the whole way up from the bottom — and did it with his former owners closing in on him the entire time.'] },
  '玻利瓦尔': { g:'war', y:[1783,1830], c:'拉丁美洲诸国', n:['玻利瓦尔','Simón Bolívar'],
  t:['他解放了六个国家,死的时候身无分文。',
     'He liberated six countries and died with nothing.'],
  a:[['1819 年率军翻越安第斯山突袭波哥大,解放新格拉纳达','Crossed the Andes in 1819 to take Bogotá by surprise and free New Granada'],
     ['先后促成委内瑞拉、哥伦比亚、厄瓜多尔、秘鲁、玻利维亚、巴拿马独立','Freed, in turn, Venezuela, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, Bolivia and Panama'],
     ['试图把西属南美合成一个"大哥伦比亚",1830 年在分裂中辞职','Tried to hold Spanish South America together as Gran Colombia, and resigned in 1830 as it broke apart']],
  s:['西班牙在美洲三百年的统治由此终结。玻利维亚以他的名字命名,是极少数以个人命名的国家之一;委内瑞拉的正式国名是"委内瑞拉玻利瓦尔共和国"。他临终前说"我们耕耘的是大海"——大哥伦比亚的解体让拉美的整合至今仍是未竟之事。',
     'Three centuries of Spanish rule in the Americas ended with him. Bolivia is named after him, one of very few countries named for a person, and Venezuela\'s formal name is the Bolivarian Republic. Near the end he said they had ploughed the sea: Gran Colombia fell apart, and Latin American integration remains unfinished business.'] },
'圣马丁': { g:'war', y:[1778,1850], c:'拉丁美洲诸国', n:['圣马丁','José de San Martín'],
  t:['南美南边是他解放的。见过玻利瓦尔一面之后,他把军队交出去,自己去了欧洲。',
     'He freed the south of the continent. After one meeting with Bolívar he handed over his army and left for Europe.'],
  a:[['1817 年率五千人翻越安第斯山,海拔逾四千米,解放智利','Took 5,000 men over Andean passes above 4,000 m in 1817 and freed Chile'],
     ['1821 年从海路进军秘鲁,宣布秘鲁独立','Sailed north to Peru in 1821 and proclaimed its independence'],
     ['1822 年瓜亚基尔会晤玻利瓦尔后,主动退出,移居法国直至去世','Met Bolívar at Guayaquil in 1822, withdrew from public life, and lived out his years in France']],
  s:['翻越安第斯山被公认为军事史上最艰难的行军之一,可与汉尼拔翻越阿尔卑斯相比。瓜亚基尔会晤的内容至今没有可靠记录,但他随后主动让出全部指挥权,以避免与玻利瓦尔内斗——这一选择使南美独立战争避免了一场内战。阿根廷称他为"国父"。',
     'The Andes crossing is reckoned among the hardest marches in military history, comparable to Hannibal\'s Alps. What was said at Guayaquil has never been reliably recorded, but he gave up his entire command afterwards rather than contest leadership with Bolívar — and that choice spared South America a civil war among its liberators. Argentina calls him the father of the nation.'] },

'郭守敬': { g:'sci', y:[1231,1316], c:'元', n:['郭守敬','Guo Shoujing'],
  t:['元朝的天文学家。他算出的一年有多长,和今天用的公历一模一样,却早了三百年。',
     'A Yuan astronomer whose measurement of the year matches the calendar we use today — three centuries early.'],
  a:[['1276 年起主持全国天文观测,在从西伯利亚到南海的二十七个点同时测量','From 1276 he ran a nationwide survey, measuring simultaneously at twenty-seven stations from Siberia to the South China Sea'],
     ['1281 年颁行《授时历》,定一年为 365.2425 日','Issued the Shoushi calendar in 1281, fixing the year at 365.2425 days'],
     ['主持开通惠河,把大运河直接接进大都城内','Cut the Tonghui canal, bringing the Grand Canal right into the capital']],
  s:['365.2425 日与 1582 年才启用的公历完全相同,早了三百零一年,与今测回归年仅差约 26 秒。《授时历》在中国行用三百六十四年,是中国使用时间最长的历法。月球背面有环形山以他命名。',
     'That figure is exactly the one the Gregorian calendar adopted in 1582 — 301 years later — and is about 26 seconds off the modern tropical year. His calendar stayed in use for 364 years, longer than any other in China. A crater on the far side of the moon carries his name.'] },
'善德女王': { g:'king', y:[632,647], yk:'r', c:'三国与统一新罗', n:['善德女王','Queen Seondeok'],
  t:['父亲没有儿子,于是新罗有了第一位女王——而这在当时的东亚几乎没有先例。','Her father had no son, so Silla got its first queen — something with almost no precedent in the East Asia of her day'],
  a:[['632 年即位,是朝鲜半岛历史上第一位女性君主;新罗后来还有过两位女王,末一位真圣女王已不属最高的圣骨','She took the throne in 632, the first woman to rule in Korean history; Silla had two more queens later, the last of them no longer of the highest rank'],
     ['在位时建瞻星台——一座九米多高的石砌圆台,一般认为是观星与定历用的,是东亚现存最早的天文台建筑之一','She built the Cheomseongdae, a stone tower over nine metres high generally taken to be for watching the sky and fixing the calendar — among the oldest surviving observatory structures in East Asia'],
     ['她在位时新罗被高句丽与百济两面夹击,处境很险;她重用金庾信与金春秋,后者后来促成了与唐朝的同盟','Silla was squeezed between Goguryeo and Baekje throughout her reign; she relied on the general Kim Yu-sin and on Kim Chun-chu, who later brought about the alliance with Tang China']],
  s:['她死后十几年,新罗统一了半岛——用的正是她任内搭起来的那套人马与那条外交路线。瞻星台今天还立在庆州的田野里,是那座城最老的地面建筑之一。','Silla unified the peninsula within two decades of her death, using the men and the diplomacy she had put in place. The Cheomseongdae still stands in the fields at Gyeongju, one of the oldest structures above ground in that city.'] },

'王建': { g:'king', y:[877,943], r:[918,943], c:'高丽', n:['王建','Wang Geon'],
  t:['他打天下的办法是娶亲:一口气娶了二十九位夫人,把各地豪族变成亲戚。','His way of winning the country was to marry it: twenty-nine wives, and the strongmen of every region became his relatives.'],
  a:[['开城一带海商豪族出身,918 年推翻旧主自立,国号取的是两百五十年前那个已经亡了的高句丽','Of a merchant and strongman family near Kaesong, he overthrew his overlord in 918 and named his state after Goguryeo, the kingdom that had fallen two and a half centuries before'],
     ['935 年新罗末代国王主动归附,他以礼相待并与新罗王族联姻;次年才用兵灭掉后百济,半岛重新合一','In 935 the last king of Silla came over of his own accord and was received with honour and married into the new house; only in 936 did Wang Geon take Later Baekje by force, reuniting the peninsula'],
     ['传下《训要十条》告诫子孙:敬佛、立嗣不必拘于长子、莫效契丹之俗、重视西京——这份遗训被高丽历代王反复引用','He left ten injunctions for his heirs — honour the Buddha, do not insist the eldest son succeed, do not copy Khitan ways, attend to the western capital — and Goryeo kings quoted them for centuries']],
  s:['他把敌人变成亲戚的办法保住了统一,代价是留下二十多支有王室血统的外戚,此后高丽的王位之争大多出在这些人之间。制度的好处与麻烦,常常是同一件事的两面。','Turning enemies into relatives preserved the unification, at the cost of leaving more than twenty in-law houses with royal blood; most of the struggles over the Goryeo throne afterwards were fought among them. The advantage of an arrangement and the trouble it makes are often the same thing seen twice.'] },

'世宗大王': { g:'king', y:[1397,1450], r:[1418,1450], c:'朝鲜王朝', n:['世宗大王','Sejong the Great'],
  t:['他给不识字的百姓造了一套字母。今天整个朝鲜半岛都在用它。',
     'He invented an alphabet for people who could not read. The whole Korean peninsula still uses it.'],
  a:[['1443 年创制训民正音,二十八个字母,序言说"愚民有所欲言,而终不得伸其情者多矣"','Created the Korean alphabet in 1443 — twenty-eight letters — explaining that common people had things to say and no way to say them'],
     ['组织编纂农书与医书,把耕作与医疗知识发给地方','Had farming and medical manuals compiled and distributed to the provinces'],
     ['支持工匠蒋英实造测雨器、自击漏与浑天仪','Backed the artisan Jang Yeong-sil, who built a rain gauge, a striking water clock and an armillary sphere']],
  s:['谚文是世界上少数有明确发明者、发明年份和设计说明书的文字——字母形状直接模拟发音时的口腔与舌位,语言学界常称它是设计最科学的字母之一。《训民正音》解例本 1997 年列入世界记忆遗产,10 月 9 日是韩国的韩文日。',
     'Hangul is one of the very few scripts with a known inventor, a known date and a written explanation of its design: the letter shapes model the position of the tongue and mouth. Linguists routinely call it the most rationally designed alphabet in use. The manual explaining it entered UNESCO\'s Memory of the World in 1997, and 9 October is Hangul Day in South Korea.'] },
'李舜臣': { g:'war', y:[1545,1598], c:'朝鲜王朝', n:['李舜臣','Yi Sun-sin'],
  t:['他打了二十三场海战,一场没输。最后一场他中弹身亡,临死下令别声张。',
     'Twenty-three naval battles, twenty-three victories. Shot in the last one, he ordered his death kept quiet until it was won.'],
  a:[['1592 年日本入侵,他以少量战船连续击败日军水师,切断其海上补给','When Japan invaded in 1592 he broke their fleets one after another and cut the sea supply line'],
     ['改造龟船:上覆铁甲板并插铁锥,使敌军无法跳帮接舷','Rebuilt the turtle ship with an iron-spiked roof so no one could board it'],
     ['1597 年鸣梁海战,以十二艘战船在急流中击退日军一百三十余艘','At Myeongnyang in 1597, twelve ships held a strait against more than a hundred and thirty']],
  s:['二十三战全胜在世界海战史上极为罕见,鸣梁的兵力对比更是海战史上最悬殊的胜利之一。切断海上补给是丰臣秀吉侵朝失败的关键。他是韩国最受尊崇的历史人物,首尔光化门广场的铜像与一百韩元硬币上都是他。',
     'An unbeaten record across twenty-three engagements is almost unheard of, and the odds at Myeongnyang are among the longest ever overcome at sea. Severing the sea supply was what broke Hideyoshi\'s invasion. He is the most revered figure in Korean history — his statue stands in Gwanghwamun Square and his face is on the 100-won coin.'] },
'朴正熙': { g:'state', y:[1917,1979], r:[1963,1979], c:'韩国', n:['朴正熙','Park Chung-hee'],
  t:['军人政变上台,统治十八年。韩国的经济起飞和高压统治都发生在他手上。',
     'He took power in a coup and held it eighteen years. Korea\'s economic take-off and its harshest repression both happened under him.'],
  a:[['1961 年发动军事政变夺权,此后连任总统直至遇刺','Seized power in 1961 and stayed president until he was shot'],
     ['推行出口导向工业化,连续五个五年计划,扶植现代、三星等企业集团','Drove export-led industrialisation through five consecutive plans, building up Hyundai, Samsung and the other chaebol'],
     ['1970 年发起新村运动,改造农村道路、屋顶与供水','Launched the New Village Movement in 1970 to rebuild rural roads, roofs and water supply']],
  s:['1961 年韩国人均 GDP 约 90 美元,低于当时的加纳;1979 年他遇刺时已达约 1700 美元,这段增长被称为"汉江奇迹"。同一时期他颁布维新宪法、镇压异见,最终被自己的情报部长枪杀。韩国社会对他的评价至今两极分化。',
     'In 1961 South Korea\'s GDP per head was about $90, below Ghana\'s; by his assassination in 1979 it was around $1,700 — the Miracle on the Han. The same years brought the Yushin constitution and the crushing of dissent, and he was shot dead by his own intelligence chief. Korean opinion on him remains sharply split.'] },
'金大中': { g:'state', y:[1924,2009], r:[1998,2003], c:'韩国', n:['金大中','Kim Dae-jung'],
  t:['被判过死刑、被绑架过、流亡过,最后当上总统,还拿了诺贝尔和平奖。',
     'Sentenced to death, kidnapped, exiled — and then elected president, and given the Nobel Peace Prize.'],
  a:[['1973 年在东京被本国情报机构绑架,险些被抛入海中,因外部干预获救','Kidnapped in Tokyo by his own country\'s intelligence service in 1973 and nearly thrown into the sea; outside pressure saved him'],
     ['1980 年光州事件后被判死刑,后改判并流亡美国','Condemned to death after the Gwangju uprising in 1980, then reprieved and exiled to the United States'],
     ['1998 年就任总统,推行"阳光政策",2000 年赴平壤与金正日会晤','Took office in 1998, launched the Sunshine Policy, and went to Pyongyang in 2000']],
  s:['2000 年他获诺贝尔和平奖,至今是韩国唯一的诺贝尔奖得主。执政期间韩国完成 1997 年金融危机后的经济重整,并解除了对日本流行文化的进口禁令——今天韩流的对外输出正建立在那一轮开放之上。',
     'The 2000 Nobel Peace Prize remains Korea\'s only Nobel. His government pulled the country through the aftermath of the 1997 financial crisis and lifted the ban on importing Japanese popular culture — the opening on which the later Korean wave was built.'] },
'范蔓': { g:'war', y:[205,225], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'扶南', n:['范蔓','Fan Shiman'],
  t:['中国史书里第一个留下名字的东南亚国王。',
     'The first Southeast Asian king whose name appears in the Chinese records.'],
  a:[['3 世纪初造大船,征服周边十余国,自号"扶南大王"','Built a fleet in the early third century, took a dozen neighbouring states and styled himself Great King of Funan'],
     ['打通从湄公河三角洲到马来半岛的贸易通道','Opened the route from the Mekong delta across to the Malay peninsula'],
     ['事迹见于吴国使者康泰、朱应的出使报告','What we know comes from the report of two envoys sent by the kingdom of Wu']],
  s:['关于他的记载全部来自中国——东南亚早期几乎没有本地文献,中国史书的转述至今是研究扶南最重要的文字材料。扶南的港口遗址奥高出土过罗马金币与印度饰物,从实物一侧印证了这条贸易通道确实存在。',
     'Everything known about him is Chinese: early Southeast Asia left almost no records of its own, so those Chinese summaries remain the primary written source on Funan. At the port site of Oc Eo, Roman coins and Indian ornaments confirm from the ground that the trade route was real.'] },
'巴拉普特拉': { g:'king', y:[850,870], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'三佛齐', n:['巴拉普特拉','Balaputradewa'],
  t:['他在印度出钱建了一座僧院,那块石碑后来成了三佛齐存在的关键证据。',
     'He paid for a monastery in India, and the stone recording it became the key proof that his empire existed.'],
  a:[['9 世纪中叶统治三佛齐,控制马六甲海峡的过路贸易','Ruled Srivijaya in the mid-ninth century, controlling the traffic through the Strait of Malacca'],
     ['出资在印度那烂陀寺兴建僧院,当地国王为此立铜牌铭文','Funded a monastery at Nalanda in India; the local king had a copperplate cut to record it'],
     ['铭文里记载了他的世系,称其为苏门答腊的统治者','That inscription names his lineage and calls him ruler of Suvarnadvipa']],
  s:['三佛齐几乎没有本土文献,长期只见于中国与阿拉伯的转述,一度被怀疑是否真实存在;直到学者把那烂陀铭文与中国史料中的"室利佛逝"对上,这个海上帝国才被确认。一块印度的石碑,证明了一个苏门答腊帝国。',
     'Srivijaya left almost nothing of its own and survived only in Chinese and Arab mentions, to the point that scholars doubted it had existed. It was matching this Indian inscription against the Chinese name for it that established the empire as real — a stone in India proving a state in Sumatra.'] },
'苏利耶跋摩二世': { g:'king', y:[1113,1150], yk:'r', c:'高棉·吴哥', n:['苏利耶跋摩二世','Suryavarman II'],
  t:['吴哥窟是他建的,一般认为那是世界上最大的宗教建筑。',
     'He built Angkor Wat — the largest religious structure in the world.'],
  a:[['1113 年即位,多次出兵占婆与大越','Took the throne in 1113 and campaigned repeatedly against Champa and Dai Viet'],
     ['兴建吴哥窟,供奉毗湿奴,同时作为自己的陵庙','Built Angkor Wat for Vishnu, and as his own funerary temple'],
     ['主动遣使中国,《宋史》记其国名"真腊"','Sent embassies to Song China, which recorded his kingdom as Chenla']],
  s:['吴哥窟占地约 162 公顷,一般认为是世界上面积最大的宗教建筑,1992 年列入世界遗产。它印在柬埔寨国旗正中——柬埔寨是世界上唯一把一座建筑画进国旗的国家。',
     'Angkor Wat covers about 162 hectares, the largest religious complex anywhere, and became World Heritage in 1992. It sits at the centre of Cambodia\'s flag: no other country puts a building on its national flag.'] },
'阇耶跋摩七世': { g:'king', y:[1122,1218], ca:1, r:[1181,1218], c:'高棉·吴哥', n:['阇耶跋摩七世','Jayavarman VII'],
  t:['将近六十岁才即位。他在全国修了一百多所医院。',
     'He came to the throne at nearly sixty, and built over a hundred hospitals.'],
  a:[['1177 年占婆攻陷吴哥,他起兵反攻,四年后即位','After Champa sacked Angkor in 1177 he fought back and took the throne four years later'],
     ['建巴戎寺,塔上刻出二百余张数米高的人脸','Built the Bayon, with over two hundred giant stone faces on its towers'],
     ['碑文记载他在全国建 102 所医院、121 处驿站','His own inscriptions record 102 hospitals and 121 rest houses across the kingdom']],
  s:['他把国教从印度教改为大乘佛教,巴戎寺的微笑人脸成为吴哥最著名的形象。医院与驿站的记载出自他自己所立的碑,是前现代罕见的国家公共医疗系统记录。他在位时的吴哥城人口估计达数十万,是当时世界上最大的城市之一。',
     'He switched the state religion from Hinduism to Mahayana Buddhism, and the smiling faces of the Bayon became the emblem of Angkor. The hospitals and rest houses are recorded on his own stelae — a rare pre-modern account of a state medical system. Angkor in his reign held perhaps several hundred thousand people, among the largest cities on earth.'] },
'李太祖': { g:'king', y:[974,1028], r:[1009,1028], c:'大越', n:['李太祖','Ly Thai To'],
  t:['越南李朝的开国皇帝。今天的河内是他挑的地方。',
     'Founder of Vietnam\'s Ly dynasty — and the man who chose the site of Hanoi.'],
  a:[['1009 年被拥立为王,建立李朝,越南第一个长期稳定的本土王朝','Was raised to the throne in 1009, founding the first durable native dynasty in Vietnam'],
     ['1010 年迁都并改名升龙,即今天的河内,留下《迁都诏》','Moved the capital in 1010 and renamed it Thang Long — today\'s Hanoi — in a famous edict'],
     ['建文庙、办科举,确立以儒学取士','Built a temple of literature and began recruiting officials by examination']],
  s:['升龙建都至今已逾千年,2010 年河内举行了建都一千年纪念。李朝延续二百一十六年,越南由此从中国的郡县彻底转为独立国家,并同时保留了汉字、科举与儒制——这套"政治独立、文化承继"的组合是越南历史的基本形态。',
     'Hanoi has been a capital for over a thousand years, and marked its millennium in 2010. The Ly lasted 216 years, and with them Vietnam changed from a Chinese province into an independent state that nonetheless kept Chinese characters, examinations and Confucian government — the combination that has defined Vietnamese history since.'] },
'陈兴道': { g:'war', y:[1228,1300], ca:1, c:'大越', n:['陈兴道','Tran Hung Dao'],
  t:['蒙古人三次打越南,三次被他打了回去。',
     'The Mongols invaded Vietnam three times. He threw them out three times.'],
  a:[['1258、1285、1288 年三次抗击蒙元入侵,均获胜','Defeated Mongol invasions in 1258, 1285 and 1288'],
     ['1288 年白藤江之战,在江底埋下铁头木桩,趁退潮击沉元军船队','At the Bach Dang in 1288 he planted iron-tipped stakes in the riverbed and sank the fleet on the falling tide'],
     ['写《檄将士文》,是越南最早的军事文献之一','Wrote a proclamation to his officers, among the earliest Vietnamese military texts']],
  s:['蒙古帝国横扫欧亚,越南是极少数三次击退它的国家之一。白藤江的木桩战术复刻了 938 年吴权对南汉的同一战法,今天出土的木桩仍陈列在博物馆里。他被越南尊为"兴道大王",各地建有祠庙。',
     'The Mongols overran most of Eurasia; Vietnam is one of the very few places that beat them back three times. The stake trap repeated a tactic used on the same river in 938, and the excavated stakes are on display in museums today. Vietnam honours him as Grand Prince Hung Dao, with shrines across the country.'] },
'加查·马达': { g:'state', y:[1290,1364], ca:1, c:'满者伯夷', n:['加查·马达','Gajah Mada'],
  t:['他发过一个誓:不统一群岛,就不吃有调料的食物。',
     'He swore an oath: no spiced food until the archipelago was one.'],
  a:[['1334 年立"巴拉巴誓言",誓言征服整个努山达拉才享安逸','Took the Palapa oath in 1334, forswearing comfort until Nusantara was united'],
     ['任宰相期间,满者伯夷的势力扩及今印尼与马来西亚大部','As chief minister he extended Majapahit\'s reach over most of modern Indonesia and Malaysia'],
     ['主持编订法典,整顿全国行政','Codified law and reorganised the administration']],
  s:['他提出的"努山达拉"(群岛)概念被 20 世纪印尼民族主义者直接继承,成为现代印尼国家版图的历史依据。印尼的加查马达大学、军事学院与第一颗通信卫星都以他命名——他是印尼国家认同的核心历史符号。',
     'His word for the archipelago, Nusantara, was taken up by twentieth-century Indonesian nationalists as the historical warrant for the country\'s modern borders. Indonesia named a university, a military academy and its first communications satellite after him; he is a cornerstone of the national story.'] },
'拜里米苏拉': { g:'king', y:[1344,1414], ca:1, c:'马六甲及诸苏丹国', n:['拜里米苏拉','Parameswara'],
  t:['一个逃亡的王子,在一棵树下建了座城。那里后来经手了全世界一半的香料。',
     'A prince on the run founded a town under a tree. Half the world\'s spice trade later passed through it.'],
  a:[['原为巨港王子,被满者伯夷驱逐,辗转逃至马来半岛','A prince of Palembang, driven out by Majapahit and forced across to the Malay peninsula'],
     ['约 1400 年建马六甲,城名相传来自他歇脚时靠的那棵树','Founded Malacca around 1400; the name is said to come from the tree he rested under'],
     ['1405 年遣使明朝,郑和多次到访,借明朝之力抵御暹罗','Sent envoys to Ming China in 1405, and used Zheng He\'s visits as a shield against Siam']],
  s:['马六甲扼守东西航路最窄处,成为香料贸易总汇,也是伊斯兰教进入马来世界的门户——今天马来西亚与印尼的伊斯兰化多经由此地。1511 年葡萄牙攻占马六甲,这是欧洲在东南亚的第一个据点。',
     'Malacca sits at the narrowest point of the route between east and west, and became the clearing house for the spice trade — and the door through which Islam entered the Malay world, from which most of Malaysia\'s and Indonesia\'s conversion followed. When Portugal took it in 1511, it was Europe\'s first foothold in Southeast Asia.'] },
'纳黎萱': { g:'war', y:[1555,1605], r:[1590,1605], c:'暹罗', n:['纳黎萱','Naresuan'],
  t:['他小时候是缅甸的人质。长大以后他把缅甸赶了出去。',
     'He grew up a hostage in Burma. He came home and drove the Burmese out.'],
  a:[['少年时被作为人质送往缅甸东吁王朝','Sent to the Burmese court as a boy hostage'],
     ['1584 年宣布独立,此后连年与缅甸作战','Declared independence in 1584 and fought Burma for the rest of his life'],
     ['1593 年在农萨莱与缅甸王储象背单挑,将其击杀','In 1593 he killed the Burmese crown prince in single combat, both men on elephants']],
  s:['他确立了阿瑜陀耶的独立地位,泰国由此避免被缅甸长期兼并。象背决斗是泰国最著名的历史场景,反复出现在教科书与电影里。1 月 18 日是泰国的纳黎萱大帝日。',
     'He secured Ayutthaya\'s independence and spared Siam a long Burmese occupation. The elephant duel is the most retold scene in Thai history, in textbooks and on film alike. Thailand keeps 18 January as King Naresuan Day.'] },
'朱拉隆功': { g:'king', y:[1853,1910], r:[1868,1910], c:'暹罗', n:['朱拉隆功','King Chulalongkorn'],
  t:['暹罗是东南亚唯一没被殖民的国家,很大程度上靠的是他。',
     'Siam was the only country in Southeast Asia never colonised, and largely because of him.'],
  a:[['1874 年起分阶段废除奴隶制,历时三十余年,不流一滴血完成','Abolished slavery in stages from 1874, taking thirty years and shedding no blood'],
     ['建铁路、邮政与学校,派王子赴欧留学,改革官制与法律','Built railways, a postal service and schools, sent his sons to study in Europe, and rewrote the administration and the law'],
     ['两次出访欧洲,以割让边缘领土换取核心地区的独立','Toured Europe twice, and traded peripheral territory to keep the centre free']],
  s:['泰国是东南亚唯一未被殖民的国家,他在英法之间保持平衡并主动现代化的策略是关键。10 月 23 日是泰国的朱拉隆功纪念日,他的画像至今普遍挂在泰国的家庭与店铺里,泰国最著名的大学也以他命名。',
     'Thailand alone in the region was never colonised, and his balancing act between Britain and France — combined with reforming before he was forced to — is the main reason. Thailand marks 23 October as Chulalongkorn Day, his portrait still hangs in homes and shops, and the country\'s most prestigious university carries his name.'] },
'莱佛士': { g:'state', y:[1781,1826], c:'欧洲殖民东南亚', n:['莱佛士','Stamford Raffles'],
  t:['新加坡是他挑的地方。他挑中它的时候,那儿只有一个小渔村。',
     'He picked the site of Singapore when there was nothing there but a fishing village.'],
  a:[['1819 年代表英国东印度公司在新加坡设立自由港','Set up a free port at Singapore for the East India Company in 1819'],
     ['任爪哇副总督期间下令测绘并清理婆罗浮屠','As lieutenant-governor of Java he ordered Borobudur surveyed and cleared'],
     ['写《爪哇史》,并在返英后创办伦敦动物学会','Wrote a History of Java, and founded the Zoological Society of London after returning home']],
  s:['新加坡今天是全球最大的转口港之一,起点就是 1819 年那份协议。婆罗浮屠 1991 年列入世界遗产,它重见天日始于他任内的清理。新加坡的莱佛士坊、莱佛士酒店与莱佛士书院都以他命名——他同时也是殖民扩张的执行者,当地对他的评价从来不是单一的。',
     'Singapore is now among the largest transshipment ports on earth, and it starts with that 1819 agreement. Borobudur, World Heritage since 1991, came back into view because of the clearance he ordered. Singapore named a district, a hotel and a school after him — and he was also an agent of colonial expansion, which local assessments have never treated as a single story.'] },
'苏加诺': { g:'state', y:[1901,1970], r:[1945,1967], c:'现代东南亚', n:['苏加诺','Sukarno'],
  t:['印尼的开国总统。1955 年他把二十九个亚非国家请到了万隆。',
     'Indonesia\'s founding president, who brought twenty-nine African and Asian countries to Bandung in 1955.'],
  a:[['1945 年 8 月 17 日宣布印尼独立,随后与荷兰打了四年独立战争','Declared independence on 17 August 1945 and fought the Dutch for four years to keep it'],
     ['提出建国五原则,作为一个多民族多宗教国家的立国基础','Set out the Pancasila, five principles to hold a country of many peoples and faiths together'],
     ['1955 年主办万隆会议,亚非国家第一次集体登场','Hosted the Bandung Conference in 1955, the first collective appearance of the newly independent world']],
  s:['万隆会议是不结盟运动的直接源头,刚独立的亚非国家第一次作为一支力量出现在国际政治里,也是新中国第一次大规模多边外交。印尼今天是世界第四人口大国和最大的穆斯林国家,其国家框架仍是他那一套。',
     'Bandung was the seed of the Non-Aligned Movement — the first time the newly decolonised world acted as a bloc, and also the first major multilateral outing of the new China. Indonesia is now the fourth most populous country and the largest Muslim-majority state, still running on the framework he laid down.'] },
'李光耀': { g:'state', y:[1923,2015], r:[1959,1990], c:'现代东南亚', n:['李光耀','Lee Kuan Yew'],
  t:['一个没有资源、没有腹地、连水都要买的小岛,他把它变成了发达国家。',
     'An island with no resources, no hinterland and no fresh water of its own — and he made it a developed country.'],
  a:[['1965 年新加坡被马来西亚逐出,被迫独立,他在电视上落泪','In 1965 Malaysia expelled Singapore into unwanted independence, and he wept on television'],
     ['推行组屋制度、双语教育与强制公积金,并大力引进外资','Built public housing, bilingual schooling and compulsory savings, and courted foreign investment'],
     ['治理严格,对反对派与媒体的压制长期受到批评','Governed strictly, and was long criticised for how he treated opponents and the press']],
  s:['1965 年新加坡人均 GDP 约五百美元,2015 年他去世时已超过五万美元。他的治理模式被许多发展中国家研究借鉴,同时也一直是"经济发展与政治自由能否分开"这一争论最常被引用的案例。',
     'Singapore\'s GDP per head was about $500 in 1965 and over $50,000 when he died in 2015. His model has been studied by developing countries everywhere, and remains the single most cited case in the argument over whether prosperity and political freedom can be separated.'] },
'波你尼': { g:'mind', y:[-520,-460], ca:1, c:'吠陀时代', n:['波你尼','Panini'],
  t:['他用不到四千条规则,把整个梵语的语法写完了。',
     'In fewer than four thousand rules, he finished the grammar of an entire language.'],
  a:[['著《八章书》,以约 3959 条规则完整描述梵语的构词与句法','Wrote the Ashtadhyayi: some 3,959 rules covering the whole word-formation and syntax of Sanskrit'],
     ['规则高度形式化,用符号与"规则的规则"层层压缩','Formalised them with symbols and meta-rules, compressing the system layer by layer'],
     ['全书极短,整套语法设计成可以口头背诵传承','Kept it short enough to be memorised and transmitted by mouth']],
  s:['《八章书》被公认为 20 世纪以前对任何一种语言最完整、最严密的语法描述。计算语言学兴起后,学者发现他的规则体系与形式文法高度相似,他因此常被称为最早的形式语言学家。',
     'The Ashtadhyayi is generally reckoned the most complete and rigorous description of any language written before the twentieth century. When formal grammars appeared in computer science, linguists found his rule system closely parallel to them, and he is now often called the first formal linguist.'] },
'迦腻色伽一世': { g:'king', y:[127,150], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'贵霜帝国', n:['迦腻色伽一世','Kanishka I'],
  t:['佛像开始有人的样子,是在他的时代。',
     'What a Buddha looks like was settled in his reign.'],
  a:[['统治横跨今阿富汗、巴基斯坦与印度北部,都城在白沙瓦','Ruled from Afghanistan across Pakistan into northern India, with his capital at Peshawar'],
     ['召集第四次佛教结集,推动大乘佛教的整理与外传','Convened the fourth Buddhist council and pushed Mahayana Buddhism outward'],
     ['所铸钱币上同时出现希腊、波斯、印度与佛教的神祇','His coins carry Greek, Persian, Indian and Buddhist deities side by side']],
  s:['犍陀罗艺术在他这一朝成熟——用希腊雕塑的手法造佛像。在此之前,佛陀只能用脚印、法轮或菩提树来表示,不作人形。东亚寺庙里佛像的样子,大体可以追到这个时代。他派出的僧侣沿丝绸之路东行,佛教由此传入中国。',
     'Gandharan art matured under him: Greek sculptural technique applied to the Buddha. Before this the Buddha was shown only by a footprint, a wheel or a tree, never as a person. The look of a Buddha in an East Asian temple descends largely from that change. The monks he sent east along the Silk Road carried Buddhism into China.'] },
'戒日王': { g:'king', y:[590,647], r:[606,647], c:'中世纪诸王朝', n:['戒日王','Harsha'],
  t:['玄奘在印度见到的那位国王,就是他。',
     'He is the king Xuanzang met in India.'],
  a:[['606 年即位,统一北印度大部,是笈多之后最后一个大帝国','Took the throne in 606 and united most of northern India — the last great empire after the Guptas'],
     ['每五年举办一次大会,把国库积蓄尽数散出施舍','Every fifth year he held an assembly and gave away the entire treasury'],
     ['接待玄奘,并请他参加曲女城的辩论大会','Received Xuanzang and had him take part in the great debate at Kannauj']],
  s:['玄奘的《大唐西域记》是研究 7 世纪印度最重要的文献之一——印度中世纪本土史料稀缺,这本中国人写的游记至今被印度考古界当作定位指南,那烂陀寺遗址就是靠它找到的。他本人还写过三部梵语剧本,是极少数留下文学作品的君主。',
     'Xuanzang\'s account of his travels is among the most important sources for seventh-century India: native records are thin, and Indian archaeologists still use this Chinese traveller\'s book to locate sites — Nalanda was found with it. Harsha himself wrote three Sanskrit plays, making him one of the very few rulers to leave literature behind.'] },
'拉贾拉贾一世': { g:'king', y:[947,1014], r:[985,1014], c:'朱罗王朝', n:['拉贾拉贾一世','Rajaraja I'],
  t:['他建的那座庙全部用石头垒成,塔顶那一块重约八十吨。',
     'He built a temple entirely of stone, and the block on top weighs some eighty tonnes.'],
  a:[['985 年即位,征服今泰米尔纳德、喀拉拉与斯里兰卡北部','Took the throne in 985 and conquered Tamil Nadu, Kerala and northern Sri Lanka'],
     ['1010 年建成坦贾武尔的布里哈迪希瓦拉神庙','Completed the Brihadeeswarar temple at Thanjavur in 1010'],
     ['建立海军,为朱罗此后的远洋扩张打下基础','Built the navy on which Chola sea power would rest']],
  s:['该庙塔高约 66 米,是当时世界上最高的庙宇之一,整座建筑不用任何黏合剂,全靠石块咬合,1987 年列入世界遗产。庙墙上刻满了他的征战与捐赠记录,是研究南印度中世纪社会最丰富的铭文材料。',
     'The tower rises about 66 metres, among the tallest temples of its day, and the whole structure holds together without mortar; it became World Heritage in 1987. Its walls are covered in inscriptions recording his campaigns and endowments — the richest epigraphic source we have for medieval south India.'] },
'罗贞陀罗一世': { g:'sail', y:[988,1044], r:[1014,1044], c:'朱罗王朝', n:['罗贞陀罗一世','Rajendra I'],
  t:['他派舰队跨过孟加拉湾,去打一千八百公里外的苏门答腊。',
     'He sent a fleet across the Bay of Bengal to attack Sumatra, 1,800 km away.'],
  a:[['1017 与 1025 年两次远征三佛齐','Launched two seaborne expeditions against Srivijaya, in 1017 and 1025'],
     ['北伐至恒河,取号"恒河的征服者",并建新都"胜利之城"','Marched north to the Ganges, took the title of its conqueror, and founded a new capital named for the victory'],
     ['与中国宋朝互派使节','Exchanged embassies with Song China']],
  s:['印度历史上极少向海外用兵,这是唯一一次大规模远征。它打断了三佛齐对马六甲海峡的垄断,南印度商人集团由此深入东南亚——今天东南亚各地的印度教遗迹与泰米尔痕迹,有相当一部分是沿这条商路留下的。',
     'India almost never projected force overseas; this was the one large exception. It broke Srivijaya\'s grip on the Strait of Malacca and let south Indian merchant guilds push deep into Southeast Asia — a good deal of the Hindu and Tamil trace across the region came along that route.'] },
'拉齐娅女苏丹': { g:'king', y:[1205,1240], ca:1, r:[1236,1240], c:'德里苏丹国', n:['拉齐娅女苏丹','Razia Sultana'],
  t:['德里苏丹国唯一的女性统治者。她只做了四年。',
     'The only woman ever to rule the Delhi Sultanate. She lasted four years.'],
  a:[['父亲临终指定她继位,越过了所有儿子','Her father named her heir on his deathbed, passing over all his sons'],
     ['放弃女装与面纱,着男装上朝,亲自率军出征','Put aside veil and women\'s dress, held court in men\'s clothes and led armies herself'],
     ['1240 年被突厥贵族推翻并杀害','Was overthrown and killed by the Turkish nobility in 1240']],
  s:['她是德里苏丹国三百二十年间唯一的女苏丹,也是南亚穆斯林政权中极罕见的女性统治者。同时代与后世史家大多认为她的失败源于贵族集团无法接受女性掌权,而非施政本身。',
     'In 320 years of the sultanate she was the only woman on the throne, and one of very few in any Muslim state in South Asia. Historians then and since have generally judged that she fell because the nobility would not accept a woman, not because of how she governed.'] },
'阿拉乌丁·卡尔吉': { g:'king', y:[1266,1316], ca:1, r:[1296,1316], c:'德里苏丹国', n:['阿拉乌丁·卡尔吉','Alauddin Khalji'],
  t:['蒙古人六次打到德里城下,六次被他挡了回去。',
     'Six times the Mongols came to Delhi. Six times he threw them back.'],
  a:[['1296 年杀死叔父夺位,此后六次击退蒙古入侵','Killed his uncle to take the throne in 1296, then beat off six Mongol invasions'],
     ['实行价格管制,规定粮食、布匹与马匹的固定价格并设市场官监督','Fixed the prices of grain, cloth and horses by decree, with inspectors to enforce them'],
     ['南征德干,把苏丹国的势力第一次推进到南印度','Pushed south into the Deccan, taking the sultanate into southern India for the first time']],
  s:['13 至 14 世纪蒙古横扫欧亚,印度是少数没有被征服的大区之一,他的防御是主要原因。他的物价管制是前现代规模最大的一次计划价格实验,细节被同时代史家巴拉尼完整记录下来,至今仍是经济史研究的样本。',
     'The Mongols overran most of Eurasia in those two centuries; India is one of the few large regions they never took, largely because of him. His price controls were the biggest planned-price experiment attempted before modern times, recorded in detail by the contemporary historian Barani, and still studied by economic historians.'] },
'尼赫鲁': { g:'state', y:[1889,1964], r:[1947,1964], c:'印度·南亚诸国', n:['尼赫鲁','Jawaharlal Nehru'],
  t:['独立那天午夜,他说印度"与命运有约"。他做了十七年总理。',
     'At midnight on independence day he said India had a tryst with destiny. He was prime minister for seventeen years.'],
  a:[['1947 年出任印度首任总理,直至去世','Became India\'s first prime minister in 1947 and served until his death'],
     ['建立议会民主制、世俗宪政与计划经济体系','Built a parliamentary democracy, a secular constitution and a planned economy'],
     ['与铁托、纳赛尔共同发起不结盟运动','Founded the Non-Aligned Movement with Tito and Nasser']],
  s:['在同一批获得独立的国家里,印度是少数始终保持议会民主制的。他确立的世俗宪政与不结盟外交至今仍是印度政治的基本框架。他的女儿英迪拉与外孙拉吉夫先后担任总理,这个政治家族延续了数十年。',
     'Of all the countries that became independent in that wave, India is among the few that kept a parliamentary democracy throughout. The secular constitution and non-aligned foreign policy he established remain the frame of Indian politics. His daughter and grandson both became prime minister after him.'] },
'安贝德卡尔': { g:'state', y:[1891,1956], c:'印度·南亚诸国', n:['安贝德卡尔','B. R. Ambedkar'],
  t:['他出生在最低的种姓,上学时不许和同学共用水杯。后来他起草了印度宪法。',
     'Born into the lowest caste and not allowed to share a water cup at school, he went on to draft India\'s constitution.'],
  a:[['达利特出身,靠奖学金在哥伦比亚大学与伦敦政治经济学院取得博士学位','Born a Dalit, he took doctorates at Columbia and the London School of Economics on scholarships'],
     ['任制宪委员会主席,主持起草 1950 年宪法,明文废除不可接触制','Chaired the drafting committee of the 1950 constitution, which abolished untouchability outright'],
     ['1956 年率约五十万达利特集体皈依佛教','In 1956 he led some half a million Dalits into Buddhism in a single ceremony']],
  s:['印度宪法是世界上篇幅最长的成文宪法,其中的平权条款与保留名额制度沿用至今,直接关系数亿人。他发起的新佛教运动让佛教在其发源地重新出现——今天印度的佛教徒多为达利特。2012 年一项全国民调把他选为"最伟大的印度人"。',
     'India\'s is the longest written constitution in the world, and the equality clauses and reserved quotas he wrote into it still govern the lives of hundreds of millions. His mass conversion brought Buddhism back to the country of its birth; most Indian Buddhists today are Dalits. A 2012 national poll voted him the greatest Indian.'] },
'真纳': { g:'state', y:[1876,1948], c:'印度·南亚诸国', n:['真纳','Muhammad Ali Jinnah'],
  t:['他曾是印穆统一最坚定的支持者,最后成了巴基斯坦的国父。',
     'He was once the firmest advocate of Hindu-Muslim unity, and he ended as the founder of Pakistan.'],
  a:[['早年任国大党要员,被称为"印穆团结的使者"','A leading Congress figure in his early career, hailed as the ambassador of Hindu-Muslim unity'],
     ['1940 年提出两个民族理论,主张穆斯林建立独立国家','Advanced the two-nation theory in 1940, arguing Muslims needed a state of their own'],
     ['1947 年出任巴基斯坦首任总督,次年病逝','Became Pakistan\'s first governor-general in 1947 and died the following year']],
  s:['1947 年印巴分治造成约一千二百万至一千五百万人迁徙,是人类历史上规模最大的一次非战争性人口迁移,并伴随大规模流血。巴基斯坦今天人口逾两亿,是世界第二大穆斯林国家;他被尊为"伟大领袖",巴基斯坦的纸币上印的是他。',
     'Partition in 1947 moved somewhere between twelve and fifteen million people, the largest non-wartime migration in human history, and it was extremely bloody. Pakistan now has over 200 million people and is the second-largest Muslim country. It calls him the Great Leader, and his face is on its banknotes.'] },
'帕卡尔大帝': { g:'king', y:[603,683], r:[615,683], c:'玛雅', n:['帕卡尔大帝','Pakal the Great'],
  t:['十二岁继位,在位六十八年。他的墓在地下埋了一千三百年没人知道。',
     'King at twelve, on the throne sixty-eight years — and his tomb lay undiscovered for thirteen centuries.'],
  a:[['615 年即位,把战败后的帕伦克重建为玛雅西部最强的城邦','Took the throne in 615 and rebuilt a defeated Palenque into the strongest city in the western Maya world'],
     ['大兴土木,建王宫与铭文神庙','Built the palace and the Temple of the Inscriptions'],
     ['1952 年考古学家在铭文神庙下发现他的墓室、石棺与玉石面具','In 1952 archaeologists found his burial chamber, sarcophagus and jade mask beneath that temple']],
  s:['铭文神庙的阶梯下藏着一条通往墓室的秘密通道,清理花了四年——这是美洲第一次在金字塔内部发现完整王墓,证明了玛雅金字塔和埃及金字塔一样也可以是陵墓。他石棺盖上的浮雕是玛雅艺术最著名的作品。帕伦克 1987 年列入世界遗产。',
     'A hidden stairway under the temple floor took four years to clear. It was the first intact royal tomb ever found inside an American pyramid, and it proved that Maya pyramids, like Egyptian ones, could be tombs. The carved lid of his sarcophagus is the single most famous work of Maya art. Palenque became World Heritage in 1987.'] },
'蒙特祖马二世': { g:'king', y:[1466,1520], ca:1, r:[1502,1520], c:'阿兹特克', n:['蒙特祖马二世','Moctezuma II'],
  t:['阿兹特克最后一位实权皇帝。西班牙人来的时候,他先把他们请进了城。',
     'The last Aztec emperor with real power — and he invited the Spaniards into his capital.'],
  a:[['1502 年即位,帝国版图达到最大,治下约五百万人','Came to the throne in 1502 with the empire at its largest, some five million subjects'],
     ['1519 年科尔特斯抵达,他以礼相待并让其进入特诺奇蒂特兰','Received Cortés with honours in 1519 and let him into Tenochtitlan'],
     ['1520 年在西班牙人手中死去,死因至今说法不一','Died in Spanish hands in 1520; how, is still disputed']],
  s:['特诺奇蒂特兰建在湖中,人口估计二十万以上,超过当时欧洲任何一座城市,有堤道、淡水渠与浮田农业。1521 年城破后被夷平,西班牙人在废墟上建起墨西哥城——今天墨西哥城宪法广场的地下,就是大神庙的遗址。',
     'Tenochtitlan stood in a lake, with an estimated population above 200,000 — larger than any city in Europe at the time — served by causeways, an aqueduct and floating farm plots. After it fell in 1521 the Spaniards levelled it and built Mexico City on top; the ruins of its great temple lie under the main square today.'] },
'帕查库特克': { g:'king', y:[1438,1471], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'印加', n:['帕查库特克','Pachacuti'],
  t:['印加从一个山谷小部落变成大帝国,是从他开始的。',
     'The Inca went from one valley to an empire starting with him.'],
  a:[['1438 年击退强敌昌卡人,随即开始大规模扩张','Beat off a Chanca invasion in 1438 and immediately began expanding'],
     ['重建库斯科,把城市规划成一头美洲豹的形状','Rebuilt Cusco, laying the city out in the shape of a puma'],
     ['一般认为马丘比丘是他的行宫','Machu Picchu is generally taken to be his country estate']],
  s:['印加最盛时纵贯南美西部约四千公里,是前哥伦布时代美洲最大的国家。它没有文字、没有轮子、没有铁器,却建起两万五千公里的道路网和不用灰浆而严丝合缝的石构建筑。马丘比丘 1983 年列入世界遗产,2007 年入选新世界七大奇迹。',
     'At its height the Inca empire ran some 4,000 km down the western side of South America, the largest state in the pre-Columbian Americas — built without writing, without the wheel and without iron, yet with 25,000 km of roads and stonework fitted so tightly it needs no mortar. Machu Picchu became World Heritage in 1983 and one of the new seven wonders in 2007.'] },
'阿塔瓦尔帕': { g:'king', y:[1502,1533], ca:1, r:[1532,1533], c:'印加', n:['阿塔瓦尔帕','Atahualpa'],
  t:['他刚打赢内战当上皇帝,几个月后就被一百多个西班牙人抓住了。',
     'He had just won a civil war and taken the throne. Months later, a hundred-odd Spaniards captured him.'],
  a:[['1532 年击败兄长瓦斯卡尔,结束印加内战','Defeated his brother Huascar in 1532, ending the Inca civil war'],
     ['同年在卡哈马卡被皮萨罗率一百六十余人伏击俘获','Was ambushed and seized at Cajamarca that same year by Pizarro and about 160 men'],
     ['以填满一间屋子的黄金作赎金,交付之后仍被处死','Paid a roomful of gold as ransom, and was executed anyway']],
  s:['一百六十余人俘获一个数百万人口帝国的皇帝,是欧洲征服美洲最具象征性的一幕。原因包括火器与马匹、刚结束的内战造成的分裂,以及此前已随人流传入并削弱了印加统治层的天花。他的赎金约合十三吨金银,是有记载以来最大的一笔赎金。',
     'A hundred and sixty men taking the emperor of a state of millions is the emblematic moment of the European conquest of the Americas. Firearms and horses were part of it; so was a country freshly split by civil war; and so was smallpox, which had already run ahead of the Spaniards and killed much of the Inca leadership. His ransom came to some thirteen tonnes of gold and silver — the largest ever recorded.'] },
'科尔特斯': { g:'war', y:[1485,1547], c:'西葡殖民美洲', n:['科尔特斯','Hernán Cortés'],
  t:['他带着不到六百个西班牙人,推翻了一个几百万人的帝国。',
     'With fewer than six hundred Spaniards he brought down an empire of millions.'],
  a:[['1519 年登陆墨西哥,凿沉自己的船以绝退路','Landed in Mexico in 1519 and scuttled his own ships so no one could turn back'],
     ['联合特拉斯卡拉等被阿兹特克压迫的部族,组成数万人的联军','Allied with Tlaxcala and other peoples the Aztecs had subjugated, fielding tens of thousands'],
     ['1521 年攻陷特诺奇蒂特兰,阿兹特克灭亡','Took Tenochtitlan in 1521, and the Aztec empire ended']],
  s:['他真正的兵力主要来自当地盟军而非西班牙人,这一点常被忽略。随之而来的天花在数年内使墨西哥中部人口锐减,这是征服得以成功最重要的因素之一。西班牙由此建立起延续三百年的美洲殖民体系,新大陆的白银改变了全球贸易格局。',
     'Most of his army was indigenous allies, not Spaniards — a point usually left out. The smallpox that came with him cut the population of central Mexico drastically within a few years, and was among the decisive factors. Spain built a colonial system on the result that lasted three centuries, and New World silver reshaped global trade.'] },
'拉斯·卡萨斯': { g:'faith', y:[1484,1566], c:'西葡殖民美洲', n:['拉斯·卡萨斯','Bartolomé de las Casas'],
  t:['他自己当过奴隶主,后来花了五十年替印第安人说话。',
     'He owned forced labourers himself, and then spent fifty years speaking for them.'],
  a:[['早年在古巴拥有庄园与印第安劳工,1514 年放弃全部财产','Held an estate and Indian labourers in Cuba, and gave everything up in 1514'],
     ['1542 年写《西印度毁灭述略》,逐地记录殖民者的暴行','Wrote A Short Account of the Destruction of the Indies in 1542, cataloguing the atrocities region by region'],
     ['1550 年在巴利亚多利德公开辩论"印第安人是否为完全的人"','Argued in public at Valladolid in 1550 over whether Indians were fully human']],
  s:['他的证词直接促成 1542 年西班牙《新法律》,禁止奴役印第安人。他被视为最早系统主张原住民权利的欧洲人之一,也是国际人权观念的先声。他早年曾建议用非洲奴隶替代印第安劳工,后来公开忏悔——这段自我否定被完整写进了他自己的著作。',
     'His testimony produced the New Laws of 1542, which forbade the enslavement of Indians. He is regarded as among the first Europeans to argue systematically for indigenous rights, and as a forerunner of the idea of human rights. He had once proposed importing African slaves instead, and later recanted in print — the retraction is in his own books.'] },

'萨尔贡': { g:'war', y:[-2334,-2279], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'苏美尔·阿卡德', n:['萨尔贡','Sargon of Akkad'],
  t:['据他自己的铭文,他是园丁养大的弃婴,后来建立了人类第一个帝国。',
     'By his own inscription he was a foundling raised by a gardener. He built the first empire in human history.'],
  a:[['出身低微,原为基什国王的侍臣,后夺权自立','Rose from the household of the king of Kish and took the throne himself'],
     ['征服苏美尔各城邦,把两河流域第一次置于一个政权之下','Conquered the Sumerian city-states, putting Mesopotamia under one ruler for the first time'],
     ['设常备军、派亲信任各城总督,以阿卡德语为行政语言','Kept a standing army, installed his own men as governors, and made Akkadian the language of administration']],
  s:['这是人类历史上第一个跨越多个城邦的中央集权政权,"帝国"这一政治形式从他开始。他的弃婴传说(放进篮子顺河漂走)与后来摩西的故事高度相似,是已知最早的同类叙事之一。他的女儿恩赫杜安娜是历史上第一位留下姓名的作者。',
     'This was the first centralised state to rule across many cities — the empire as a political form begins with him. His origin story, a baby set adrift in a basket, is the earliest known version of a tale later told of Moses. His daughter Enheduanna is the first author in history known by name.'] },
'乌尔纳姆': { g:'king', y:[-2112,-2095], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'苏美尔·阿卡德', n:['乌尔纳姆','Ur-Nammu'],
  t:['现存最早的成文法典是他的,比汉谟拉比早了三个世纪。',
     'The oldest law code that survives is his — three centuries before Hammurabi.'],
  a:[['建立乌尔第三王朝,重新统一两河南部','Founded the Third Dynasty of Ur and reunified southern Mesopotamia'],
     ['颁布《乌尔纳姆法典》,以罚金而非肉刑处理多数伤害案件','Issued a code that settled most injuries with fines rather than mutilation'],
     ['修建乌尔大金字形神塔,是现存保存最好的苏美尔塔庙','Built the great ziggurat of Ur, the best preserved in Mesopotamia']],
  s:['他的法典比《汉谟拉比法典》早约三百年,是现存最早的成文法。值得注意的是它以赔偿为主而非"以眼还眼"——法律史上"损害赔偿"的思路出现得比"同态复仇"更早。乌尔塔庙今天仍立在伊拉克南部。',
     'His code predates Hammurabi\'s by about three centuries and is the earliest surviving written law. Notably it works mostly by compensation rather than eye-for-eye: in legal history, paying damages appears earlier than matching the injury. His ziggurat still stands in southern Iraq.'] },
'穆瓦塔里二世': { g:'war', y:[-1295,-1272], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'赫梯', n:['穆瓦塔里二世','Muwatalli II'],
  t:['他在卡叠什和拉美西斯二世打了一场,双方都说自己赢了。',
     'He fought Ramesses II at Kadesh, and both sides went home claiming victory.'],
  a:[['前 1274 年卡叠什战役,投入三千五百辆战车迎战埃及','Committed some 3,500 chariots against Egypt at Kadesh in 1274 BCE'],
     ['用假情报把埃及先头部队诱入包围','Fed the Egyptians false intelligence and drew their lead division into a trap'],
     ['战后控制住叙利亚北部,埃及未能北扩','Held northern Syria afterwards; Egypt never pushed further north']],
  s:['卡叠什是古代世界记录最详尽的战役,也是已知规模最大的战车会战。双方的记载都留了下来:埃及刻在神庙墙上宣称大胜,赫梯的泥板则说自己守住了地盘——这是历史学上最早可以做"两方对照"的战例之一。十五年后双方签下现存最早的国际和约。',
     'Kadesh is the best-documented battle of the ancient world and the largest chariot engagement known. Both accounts survive — Egypt carved a triumph on its temple walls, while Hittite tablets record holding the ground — making it one of the earliest battles historians can read from both sides. Fifteen years later the two powers signed the oldest surviving international treaty.'] },
'希兰一世': { g:'king', y:[-980,-947], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'腓尼基', n:['希兰一世','Hiram I'],
  t:['推罗的国王。他派人、派木料,帮所罗门盖了耶路撒冷的第一圣殿。',
     'King of Tyre, who sent the men and the timber for Solomon\'s Temple in Jerusalem.'],
  a:[['把推罗从半岛小城扩建为地中海东岸最大的港口','Expanded Tyre from a small headland town into the leading port of the eastern Mediterranean'],
     ['向所罗门提供黎巴嫩雪松与工匠,共建第一圣殿与王宫','Supplied Solomon with Lebanese cedar and craftsmen for the Temple and the palace'],
     ['与所罗门合股经营红海船队,远航"俄斐"贩运黄金','Ran a joint Red Sea fleet with Solomon, trading as far as the gold country of Ophir']],
  s:['他与所罗门的合作是《圣经》里记载最详细的一次国际商业协议,也是腓尼基"以贸易而非征服立国"模式的样板。腓尼基人随后把二十二个辅音字母带到地中海各地,希腊人加上元音,成了今天欧洲所有字母的祖先。',
     'His partnership with Solomon is the most fully described commercial treaty in the Hebrew Bible, and the model of the Phoenician way of building power by trade rather than conquest. Phoenician ships then carried a twenty-two letter consonantal alphabet around the Mediterranean; the Greeks added vowels, and every European alphabet descends from it.'] },
'希律王': { g:'king', y:[-73,-4], r:[-37,-4], c:'罗马治下近东', n:['希律王','Herod the Great'],
  t:['罗马扶植的犹地亚国王。他建了古代世界最大的宗教建筑群之一。',
     'Rome\'s client king in Judaea, and builder of one of the largest religious complexes in the ancient world.'],
  a:[['前 37 年在罗马支持下夺取犹地亚王位','Took the throne of Judaea in 37 BCE with Roman backing'],
     ['扩建耶路撒冷第二圣殿,平台面积约十四万平方米','Enlarged the Second Temple onto a platform of some 140,000 square metres'],
     ['修建凯撒利亚人工港、马萨达要塞与希律堡','Built the artificial harbour at Caesarea, plus the fortresses of Masada and Herodium']],
  s:['圣殿山的挡土墙至今仍在——西墙(哭墙)就是他那次扩建的遗存,是今天犹太教最神圣的地点。凯撒利亚港用水下混凝土建成,是古代最大的人工港之一。他在《新约》里被写成下令屠婴的暴君,这一记载没有其他史料佐证,但他晚年处死自己三个儿子确有其事。',
     'The retaining walls of his Temple Mount still stand — the Western Wall is part of that expansion, and the holiest site in Judaism today. His harbour at Caesarea, built with underwater concrete, was among the largest artificial ports of antiquity. The New Testament casts him as the king who ordered the killing of infants, a story no other source records; that he executed three of his own sons, however, is well attested.'] },
'芝诺比娅': { g:'war', y:[240,274], ca:1, r:[267,272], c:'罗马治下近东', n:['芝诺比娅','Zenobia'],
  t:['她从一座沙漠绿洲出发,五年内拿下了罗马帝国的整个东方。',
     'From one desert oasis she took the entire Roman East in five years.'],
  a:[['丈夫遇刺后以摄政身份掌权,统治帕尔米拉','Took power at Palmyra as regent after her husband was assassinated'],
     ['269—271 年攻占叙利亚、小亚细亚与埃及,控制罗马的粮仓','Between 269 and 271 she took Syria, Anatolia and Egypt — Rome\'s granary'],
     ['自称奥古斯塔,为儿子铸造带皇帝头衔的钱币','Styled herself Augusta and minted coins giving her son the imperial title']],
  s:['罗马东部三分之一的领土曾短暂脱离帝国,由一个绿洲城邦统治,这在罗马史上绝无仅有。272 年她被奥勒良击败,据说被金链锁着走过罗马城的凯旋式,之后在意大利度过余生。帕尔米拉古城 1980 年列入世界遗产,2015 年遭极端组织严重破坏。',
     'A third of Rome\'s eastern provinces briefly seceded under the rule of a caravan city — nothing like it happened again. Aurelian defeated her in 272 and, by one account, walked her through his triumph in golden chains before she lived out her life in Italy. Palmyra became World Heritage in 1980 and was heavily destroyed by militants in 2015.'] },
'阿尔普·阿尔斯兰': { g:'war', y:[1029,1072], r:[1063,1072], c:'塞尔柱突厥', n:['阿尔普·阿尔斯兰','Alp Arslan'],
  t:['他打赢的那一仗,间接引来了十字军东征。',
     'The battle he won brought the Crusades.'],
  a:[['1071 年曼齐刻尔特战役击溃拜占庭军队,俘获皇帝罗曼努斯四世','Destroyed the Byzantine army at Manzikert in 1071 and captured the emperor'],
     ['战后放还皇帝,只索取赎金与边境城市','Released the emperor for a ransom and some frontier towns'],
     ['以尼扎姆·穆勒克为相,建立起塞尔柱的行政体系','Made Nizam al-Mulk his vizier and built the Seljuk administration on him']],
  s:['曼齐刻尔特之后,拜占庭失去了小亚细亚的兵源与税基,再也没能恢复。突厥各部随即涌入安纳托利亚,这块土地从此走向"土耳其化"——今天的土耳其正是从这里开始的。拜占庭向西方求援,直接促成 1095 年教皇号召第一次十字军东征。',
     'After Manzikert, Byzantium lost Anatolia — its recruiting ground and its tax base — and never got it back. Turkic peoples poured in, and the land began the transformation that made it Turkey. Byzantine appeals west led directly to the Pope\'s call for the First Crusade in 1095.'] },
'尼扎姆·穆勒克': { g:'state', y:[1018,1092], c:'塞尔柱突厥', n:['尼扎姆·穆勒克','Nizam al-Mulk'],
  t:['连任两朝宰相三十年。他建了伊斯兰世界最早的官办大学网络。',
     'Vizier to two sultans for thirty years, and founder of the first state university network in the Islamic world.'],
  a:[['在巴格达、内沙布尔等地创办"尼采米亚"学院,由国家出资供养师生','Founded the Nizamiyya colleges at Baghdad, Nishapur and elsewhere, with state-paid teachers and students'],
     ['写《治国策》,以四十九章讲君主该如何治理','Wrote the Book of Government, forty-nine chapters on how a ruler should rule'],
     ['1092 年被阿萨辛派刺客刺杀','Was stabbed to death by an Assassin in 1092']],
  s:['尼采米亚学院是伊斯兰世界最早由国家系统资助的高等教育机构,固定薪俸、固定课程、颁发教学许可,被不少学者视为欧洲大学制度的一个来源。神学家安萨里就在巴格达尼采米亚任教。《治国策》至今是研究中世纪伊斯兰政治思想的核心文本。',
     'The Nizamiyya were the first systematically state-funded institutions of higher learning in Islam, with salaried teachers, a set curriculum and licences to teach — which a number of scholars treat as one source of the European university. Al-Ghazali taught at the Baghdad branch. His Book of Government remains a core text for medieval Islamic political thought.'] },
'旭烈兀': { g:'war', y:[1218,1265], r:[1256,1265], c:'伊尔汗国', n:['旭烈兀','Hulagu Khan'],
  t:['成吉思汗的孙子。1258 年他攻陷巴格达,五百年的哈里发王朝结束了。',
     'Genghis\' grandson. In 1258 he took Baghdad, and five centuries of the caliphate ended.'],
  a:[['1256 年攻灭阿萨辛派在阿拉穆特的山中堡垒','Destroyed the Assassins\' mountain fortress at Alamut in 1256'],
     ['1258 年围攻巴格达,城破后末代哈里发被处死','Besieged Baghdad in 1258; the last caliph was executed when it fell'],
     ['1260 年阿音扎鲁特之战,其部将败于埃及马穆鲁克','His detachment was beaten by the Egyptian Mamluks at Ain Jalut in 1260']],
  s:['巴格达陷落终结了阿拔斯哈里发,智慧宫的藏书被投入底格里斯河——阿拉伯世界近五百年的学术中心地位就此中断,通常被视为伊斯兰黄金时代的终点。阿音扎鲁特则是蒙古西进第一次被真正挡住,埃及与北非因此未被征服。',
     'The fall of Baghdad ended the Abbasid caliphate, and the books of the House of Wisdom went into the Tigris — the Arab world\'s five centuries as the centre of learning stopped there, and the sack is usually taken as the end of the Islamic Golden Age. Ain Jalut, two years later, was the first real check on the Mongol advance west, and it saved Egypt and North Africa.'] },
'拉施特丁': { g:'mind', y:[1247,1318], c:'伊尔汗国', n:['拉施特丁','Rashid al-Din'],
  t:['犹太医生出身,做到伊尔汗国宰相,写出了世界上第一部真正的世界史。',
     'A Jewish physician who became chief minister — and wrote the first true world history.'],
  a:[['皈依伊斯兰教后任合赞汗与完者都的宰相','Converted to Islam and served as vizier to two Ilkhans'],
     ['主编《史集》,写蒙古、中国、印度、突厥、犹太与法兰克各族的历史','Directed the Compendium of Chronicles, covering Mongols, Chinese, Indians, Turks, Jews and Franks'],
     ['1318 年被政敌构陷处死,时年七十','Was framed by rivals and executed in 1318, at seventy']],
  s:['《史集》是已知第一部有意识地把欧亚各文明并列叙述的史书——此前的史书都只写"我们"。它借助蒙古帝国横跨欧亚的信息网络才可能写成,书中关于中国与印度的部分取自当地学者的口述。这本书今天被公认为世界史学的开端之一。',
     'The Compendium is the first history known to have set the civilisations of Eurasia deliberately side by side; everything before it wrote only about "us". It was possible because the Mongol empire spanned the continent, and its Chinese and Indian sections came from scholars of those countries in person. It is now regarded as one of the beginnings of world history as a discipline.'] },
'伊斯玛仪一世': { g:'king', y:[1487,1524], r:[1501,1524], c:'萨法维·波斯', n:['伊斯玛仪一世','Ismail I'],
  t:['十四岁攻下大不里士,当场宣布全国改信什叶派。',
     'He took Tabriz at fourteen and declared the whole country Shia on the spot.'],
  a:[['1501 年即位,建立萨法维王朝','Founded the Safavid dynasty in 1501'],
     ['宣布十二伊玛目什叶派为国教,从黎巴嫩等地引进教法学者推行','Made Twelver Shia Islam the state religion, importing jurists from Lebanon to enforce it'],
     ['1514 年查尔迪兰战役败于奥斯曼的火枪与火炮','Lost to Ottoman guns at Chaldiran in 1514']],
  s:['伊朗此前以逊尼派为主,他这一举把它变成了世界上唯一以什叶派为国教的大国,这一格局延续至今,也是此后五百年中东教派政治的基本盘。查尔迪兰之败则划定了奥斯曼与波斯的边界,大致就是今天土耳其与伊朗的边界。',
     'Iran had been mostly Sunni; he made it the only major Shia state in the world, and it has stayed that way — the underlying fault line of Middle Eastern sectarian politics for five centuries since. Chaldiran fixed the Ottoman-Persian frontier roughly where the Turkish-Iranian border runs today.'] },
'阿拔斯一世': { g:'king', y:[1571,1629], r:[1588,1629], c:'萨法维·波斯', n:['阿拔斯一世','Abbas the Great'],
  t:['他把首都搬到伊斯法罕,当时人说"伊斯法罕半天下"。',
     'He moved his capital to Isfahan, and people said Isfahan was half the world.'],
  a:[['改组军队,建立火枪与炮兵部队,收复被奥斯曼夺去的领土','Rebuilt the army around muskets and artillery and won back what the Ottomans had taken'],
     ['1598 年迁都伊斯法罕,营建伊玛目广场与一系列清真寺、宫殿','Moved the capital to Isfahan in 1598 and laid out its great square, mosques and palaces'],
     ['引入亚美尼亚商人经营丝绸出口,与英国、荷兰东印度公司直接通商','Settled Armenian merchants to run the silk export, trading directly with the English and Dutch companies']],
  s:['伊斯法罕的伊玛目广场面积约八点九万平方米,是世界上最大的城市广场之一,1979 年列入世界遗产。萨法维波斯在他手上成为与奥斯曼、莫卧儿并立的三大伊斯兰火药帝国之一,波斯细密画、地毯与建筑都在这一朝达到顶峰。',
     'The square he laid out at Isfahan covers some 89,000 square metres, among the largest urban squares in the world, and became World Heritage in 1979. Under him Safavid Persia stood alongside the Ottomans and Mughals as one of the three Islamic gunpowder empires, and Persian miniature painting, carpets and architecture all reached their height.'] },
'凯末尔': { g:'state', y:[1881,1938], r:[1923,1938], c:'现代中东', n:['凯末尔','Mustafa Kemal Atatürk'],
  t:['奥斯曼帝国解体后,他从废墟里造出了一个新国家,连字母都换了。',
     'Out of the wreck of the Ottoman Empire he made a new country — and changed even its alphabet.'],
  a:[['1919—1922 年领导独立战争,击退希腊军队,废除苏丹制','Led the war of independence, drove out the Greek army and abolished the sultanate'],
     ['1924 年废除哈里发制度,政教分离;1928 年改用拉丁字母','Abolished the caliphate in 1924, separated mosque and state, and switched to the Latin alphabet in 1928'],
     ['1934 年赋予妇女选举权与被选举权,早于法国十年','Gave women the vote and the right to stand in 1934, ten years before France']],
  s:['哈里发制度自 632 年延续了近一千三百年,到他这里终止。文字改革后土耳其识字率在二十年内从约一成升至三成以上。土耳其是穆斯林占多数的国家中最早实行世俗宪政的,这条路线至今仍是土耳其国内政治争论的核心。"阿塔图尔克"意为"土耳其人之父",是议会授予他的姓氏。',
     'The caliphate had run since 632, nearly thirteen centuries, and ended with him. After the script reform, literacy rose from around ten per cent to over thirty within twenty years. Turkey was the first Muslim-majority country to adopt secular constitutional rule, and that choice is still the central argument in Turkish politics. Atatürk — father of the Turks — was a surname voted him by parliament.'] },
'纳赛尔': { g:'state', y:[1918,1970], r:[1954,1970], c:'现代中东', n:['纳赛尔','Gamal Abdel Nasser'],
  t:['他把苏伊士运河收归国有,英法出兵,结果是英法输了。',
     'He nationalised the Suez Canal. Britain and France invaded — and Britain and France lost.'],
  a:[['1952 年参与推翻埃及国王,结束君主制','Took part in the 1952 coup that ended the Egyptian monarchy'],
     ['1956 年宣布苏伊士运河国有化,引发英法以三国出兵','Nationalised the canal in 1956, bringing British, French and Israeli forces down on him'],
     ['修建阿斯旺高坝,推行土地改革与免费教育','Built the Aswan High Dam and pushed through land reform and free education']],
  s:['苏伊士危机中英法在美苏共同压力下被迫撤军,这通常被视为大英帝国作为世界强权的终结点。他由此成为阿拉伯民族主义的象征,影响力遍及整个阿拉伯世界。阿斯旺高坝为埃及提供了防洪与电力,同时淹没了努比亚遗址——阿布辛贝神庙因此被整体切割搬迁。',
     'Under joint American and Soviet pressure the invaders withdrew, and Suez is usually taken as the moment Britain ceased to be a world power. He became the emblem of Arab nationalism across the region. The Aswan dam gave Egypt flood control and electricity, and drowned much of Nubia — which is why Abu Simbel was cut apart and moved to higher ground.'] },
'阿提亚斯': { g:'war', y:[-429,-339], ca:1, c:'斯基泰', n:['阿提亚斯','Ateas'],
  t:['斯基泰唯一有确切事迹的国王,九十岁还在战场上,死于亚历山大父亲之手。',
     'The only Scythian king with a firm record: still fighting at ninety, and killed by Alexander\'s father.'],
  a:[['统一黑海北岸的斯基泰各部,铸造自己的钱币','United the Scythian tribes north of the Black Sea and minted his own coinage'],
     ['向多瑙河下游扩张,与希腊城邦既交易又冲突','Pushed toward the lower Danube, trading with and fighting the Greek cities'],
     ['前 339 年与马其顿腓力二世交战,战死,时年约九十','Died in battle against Philip II of Macedon in 339 BCE, aged about ninety']],
  s:['斯基泰没有文字,关于他们的记载几乎全部来自希腊人,而这位国王是少数能与考古发现相互印证的具体人物之一。斯基泰墓葬出土的黄金饰品做工极精,其中不少由希腊工匠打造——草原与地中海之间的往来,由此有了实物证据。',
     'The Scythians left no writing, and almost everything known of them comes from Greek pens; he is one of the few individuals whose record can be cross-checked against archaeology. The gold from Scythian burial mounds is extraordinarily fine, and much of it was made by Greek craftsmen — hard evidence of the traffic between the steppe and the Mediterranean.'] },
'迪瓦什提奇': { g:'state', y:[706,722], yk:'r', c:'粟特', n:['迪瓦什提奇','Divashtich'],
  t:['他逃进山里时带走了全部公文。一千二百年后,这批文件被找到了。',
     'He fled into the mountains with his entire archive. Twelve hundred years later, it was found.'],
  a:[['任片治肯特(今塔吉克斯坦)统治者,阿拉伯军队东进时组织抵抗','Ruled Panjikent, in modern Tajikistan, and organised resistance as the Arab armies came east'],
     ['722 年退守穆格山城堡,兵败被处死','Retreated to the fortress on Mount Mugh in 722, and was executed after his defeat'],
     ['他随身带走的粟特语文书 1932 年在穆格山被发现','The Sogdian documents he took with him were discovered on Mount Mugh in 1932']],
  s:['穆格山文书是粟特语最重要的一批一手材料——契约、书信、账目、婚书都有,让人第一次看到丝绸之路商人日常怎么做生意。粟特人是丝路的实际经营者,他们的语言曾是中亚的通用商业语言;这批文件出土前,粟特语几乎只能靠零星词汇拼凑。',
     'The Mount Mugh papers are the single most important cache of Sogdian material — contracts, letters, accounts, even a marriage agreement — and the first clear view of how Silk Road merchants actually did business. The Sogdians ran that trade, and their language was the commercial lingua franca of Central Asia; before this find, it was known mostly from scattered words.'] },
'头罗曼': { g:'war', y:[493,515], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'嚈哒·白匈奴', n:['头罗曼','Toramana'],
  t:['他从中亚南下,把印度的笈多王朝打垮了。',
     'He came down out of Central Asia and broke the Gupta empire.'],
  a:[['率嚈哒(白匈奴)部众攻入印度西北,占领马尔瓦与旁遮普','Led the Hephthalites into northwestern India, taking Malwa and the Punjab'],
     ['铸造钱币并立铭文,自称"大王中之王"','Struck coins and inscriptions styling himself great king of kings'],
     ['其子米希拉古拉继续南侵,以摧毁佛教寺院著称','His son Mihirakula pressed further south and became notorious for destroying Buddhist monasteries']],
  s:['笈多王朝是印度的黄金时代,零、十进制与梵语古典文学都出自那一朝;它的崩溃直接源于嚈哒的连续入侵,印度此后进入六百年的分裂。嚈哒同时压制着萨珊波斯,一度让波斯纳贡——同时按住两个大帝国,这在中亚历史上仅此一次。',
     'The Guptas were India\'s golden age — zero, the decimal system and classical Sanskrit literature all came from it — and its collapse followed directly from these invasions, after which India stayed divided for six centuries. The Hephthalites were pressing Sasanian Persia at the same time, even collecting tribute from it: holding down two great empires at once happened only that one time in Central Asian history.'] },
'布民可汗': { g:'king', y:[551,552], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'突厥汗国', n:['布民可汗','Bumin Khagan'],
  t:['他起兵的那一年就打垮了旧主,建立了突厥汗国。他当可汗只当了几个月。',
     'In the year he rebelled he destroyed his overlords and founded the Turkic Khaganate. He was khagan for a few months.'],
  a:[['原为柔然的属部,以炼铁为业,被称为"锻奴"','His people had been vassal ironsmiths of the Rouran, called their forge-slaves'],
     ['552 年起兵大败柔然,自立为伊利可汗','Rose in 552, crushed the Rouran and took the title Il Khagan'],
     ['与弟弟室点密分治东西,汗国迅速扩张至中亚','Split the realm with his brother, who pushed the western wing deep into Central Asia']],
  s:['"突厥"这个名字第一次作为一个政权出现,就是从他开始。此后一千五百年,从中亚到安纳托利亚的突厥语民族都上溯至这个汗国。汗国鼎盛时东起辽海、西抵里海,是第一个同时与中国、波斯和拜占庭直接通使的草原政权。',
     'The name Türk first appears as a state with him. For fifteen centuries afterwards, Turkic peoples from Central Asia to Anatolia have traced themselves to this khaganate. At its height it ran from Manchuria to the Caspian, and was the first steppe power to deal directly with China, Persia and Byzantium at the same time.'] },
'毗伽可汗': { g:'king', y:[683,734], r:[716,734], c:'突厥汗国', n:['毗伽可汗','Bilge Khagan'],
  t:['他立的那块碑,是突厥语最早的成篇文字记录。',
     'The stone he set up carries the earliest extended text in any Turkic language.'],
  a:[['716 年即位,重振第二突厥汗国','Took the throne in 716 and restored the Second Turkic Khaganate'],
     ['在鄂尔浑河畔为弟弟阙特勤与自己立碑,用突厥如尼文与汉文双语刻写','Raised stelae on the Orkhon for his brother and himself, in both Turkic runes and Chinese'],
     ['碑文告诫族人不要迁入中原的城市与丝绸中,否则必被吞没','The inscription warns his people not to move into Chinese towns and silks, or they will be swallowed']],
  s:['鄂尔浑碑铭是突厥语最早的成篇文献,也是极少数由游牧民族自己书写、而非由定居邻邦转述的历史记录——它让人第一次直接听到草原一方的声音。碑文中"我为突厥人民不眠不休"一段至今被土耳其与中亚各国当作民族记忆的源头。',
     'The Orkhon inscriptions are the oldest substantial texts in Turkic and one of the very few histories written by nomads about themselves rather than recorded by settled neighbours — the first time the steppe speaks in its own voice. Passages from them are still treated across Turkey and Central Asia as the founding text of national memory.'] },
'骨力裴罗': { g:'king', y:[744,747], yk:'r', c:'回鹘', n:['骨力裴罗','Kutluk Bilge Kul Khagan'],
  t:['他推翻突厥汗国,建立回鹘,并接受了唐朝的册封。',
     'He overthrew the Turkic Khaganate, founded the Uyghur one, and accepted a Chinese title for it.'],
  a:[['744 年联合各部灭后突厥汗国,建回鹘汗国','Destroyed the Second Turkic Khaganate in 744 with allied tribes and founded the Uyghur Khaganate'],
     ['接受唐玄宗册封为"怀仁可汗",与唐建立同盟','Was invested by the Tang emperor and entered into alliance with China'],
     ['定牙帐于鄂尔浑河畔,即后来的哈剌巴剌哈孙城','Set his court on the Orkhon, at the site later known as Ordu-Baliq']],
  s:['他建立的同盟关系在十一年后派上用场:安史之乱中回鹘出兵助唐收复长安、洛阳,唐朝由此得以延续。回鹘后来成为唯一以摩尼教为国教的政权,西迁后由游牧转为定居农耕——这是草原民族极少见的转型,今天新疆的维吾尔族即由此而来。',
     'The alliance mattered eleven years later: Uyghur cavalry helped the Tang retake both its capitals during the An Lushan rebellion, and the dynasty survived because of it. The Uyghurs later became the only state ever to adopt Manichaeism as its religion, and after migrating west they turned from herding to settled farming — a rare transition on the steppe, and the origin of today\'s Uyghurs in Xinjiang.'] },
'萨图克·博格拉汗': { g:'faith', y:[901,955], ca:1, c:'喀喇汗王朝', n:['萨图克·博格拉汗','Satuq Bughra Khan'],
  t:['第一个皈依伊斯兰教的突厥可汗。整个中亚的信仰版图由此改变。',
     'The first Turkic khan to become Muslim. The religious map of Central Asia turned on it.'],
  a:[['青年时秘密皈依伊斯兰教,后起兵夺取汗位','Converted in secret as a young man, then took the throne by force'],
     ['宣布伊斯兰教为国教,据记载有二十万帐部众随之皈依','Made Islam the state religion; the sources speak of 200,000 tents converting with him'],
     ['以喀什噶尔为中心,向东传教','Made Kashgar his base and pushed the faith eastward']],
  s:['在他之前,突厥人多信萨满教、摩尼教或佛教;他这一皈依起了头,此后几百年间突厥语世界的大半换了信仰。这一转变的影响一直延伸到今天——从土耳其到中亚五国再到新疆,伊斯兰教的分布大体沿着当年突厥人西迁与皈依的路线。',
     'Before him the Turks were mostly shamanist, Manichaean or Buddhist; his conversion set it moving, and over the centuries that followed most of the Turkic-speaking world changed faith. The consequences run to the present: from Turkey through the five Central Asian republics to Xinjiang, the distribution of Islam still broadly follows the route of Turkic migration and conversion.'] },
'麻赫穆德·喀什噶里': { g:'mind', y:[1005,1102], ca:1, c:'喀喇汗王朝', n:['麻赫穆德·喀什噶里','Mahmud al-Kashgari'],
  t:['他走遍突厥各部,把听到的词一个个记下来,编成了一部词典和一张地图。',
     'He walked among the Turkic tribes writing down every word he heard, and made a dictionary and a map out of it.'],
  a:[['游历中亚各地,实地采录各部落的方言与口语','Travelled across Central Asia recording tribal dialects and everyday speech in the field'],
     ['1072—1074 年编成《突厥语大词典》,收词七千五百余条,用阿拉伯语解释','Compiled the Compendium of the Turkic Dialects, over 7,500 entries explained in Arabic'],
     ['书中附一幅圆形世界地图,以喀什噶尔为中心','Included a circular world map with Kashgar at its centre']],
  s:['这是突厥语最早的词典,也是最早的比较方言学著作之一——他记录了各部落发音的差异并加以对比,方法上领先当时。书里保存的谚语、诗歌与民歌是 11 世纪突厥社会唯一的完整文字快照。附图是已知最早由突厥人绘制的世界地图。',
     'It is the first Turkic dictionary and one of the earliest works of comparative dialectology anywhere — he recorded how pronunciation differed between tribes and set the forms against each other, a method ahead of its time. The proverbs, poems and songs it preserves are the only complete written snapshot of eleventh-century Turkic society, and the map is the earliest known to have been drawn by a Turk.'] },
'摩诃末二世': { g:'king', y:[1169,1220], ca:1, r:[1200,1220], c:'花剌子模', n:['摩诃末二世','Muhammad II of Khwarezm'],
  t:['他杀了成吉思汗派来的商队和使者。这个决定毁掉了他的国家。',
     'He killed Genghis Khan\'s caravan and then his envoys. That decision destroyed his country.'],
  a:[['扩张至今伊朗、阿富汗与中亚大部,自称"第二亚历山大"','Expanded across Iran, Afghanistan and most of Central Asia, calling himself the second Alexander'],
     ['1218 年其边将扣杀蒙古商队四百五十人,他拒绝交出责任者并处死来使','In 1218 his governor killed a 450-man Mongol caravan; he refused to hand the man over and executed the envoys sent to demand it'],
     ['蒙古入侵后分兵守城,被逐个击破,最后死于里海一座小岛','Split his forces among fortified cities, was destroyed piecemeal, and died on an island in the Caspian']],
  s:['成吉思汗本无西征计划,是这次事件把蒙古军队引向了中亚与波斯。撒马尔罕、玉龙杰赤、内沙布尔等城被屠,中亚的灌溉系统遭到破坏,一些地区数百年未恢复。一次外交处置引发的后果,规模在历史上罕有其匹。',
     'Genghis had no plan to march west; this affair brought the Mongol armies into Central Asia and Persia. Samarkand, Urgench and Nishapur were put to the sword, the irrigation systems were wrecked, and parts of the region did not recover for centuries. Few diplomatic decisions in history have cost so much.'] },
'扎兰丁': { g:'war', y:[1199,1231], c:'花剌子模', n:['扎兰丁','Jalal al-Din Mingburnu'],
  t:['国破家亡后他一个人打了十一年。成吉思汗说,做父亲的该有这样的儿子。',
     'He fought on alone for eleven years after his country fell. Genghis said a father should have such a son.'],
  a:[['1221 年在帕尔万击败蒙古一支军队,是成吉思汗西征中少见的败绩','Beat a Mongol force at Parwan in 1221, one of the few defeats of the western campaign'],
     ['同年印度河之战失败后,策马跃入印度河泅渡逃生','After losing on the Indus that same year he rode his horse off the bank and swam across'],
     ['此后转战印度、波斯、高加索十年,1231 年在库尔德山区被杀','Fought on through India, Persia and the Caucasus for a decade, and was killed in the Kurdish hills in 1231']],
  s:['成吉思汗亲眼看到他泅渡印度河,下令不许射箭,并对儿子们说做父亲的该有这样的儿子——这段记载出自波斯史家志费尼,是蒙古方面对敌手最高的一次评价。他的抵抗虽未改变结局,却成为中亚与伊朗抵抗叙事的核心形象,至今被反复书写。',
     'Genghis watched him swim the Indus, ordered his archers to hold fire, and told his sons that a father should have such a son — the account comes from the Persian historian Juvayni, and it is the highest compliment the Mongols paid any opponent. His resistance changed nothing, but it became the central image of resistance in Central Asian and Iranian memory, retold ever since.'] },
'耶律大石': { g:'king', y:[1087,1143], r:[1132,1143], c:'西辽·哈剌契丹', n:['耶律大石','Yelu Dashi'],
  t:['辽朝灭亡时他带着二百骑西走,几年后在中亚重建了一个帝国。',
     'When the Liao fell he rode west with two hundred men, and a few years later he had an empire in Central Asia.'],
  a:[['辽朝进士出身,又能领兵,是契丹少见的文武兼备之人','A Liao examination graduate who could also command an army — rare among the Khitan'],
     ['1124 年辽亡前夕率二百骑北走可敦城,再从那里西行,收拢旧部与草原诸族','Rode north to Khatun City with two hundred horsemen in 1124, then on west, gathering up scattered Khitan and steppe tribes'],
     ['1141 年卡特万之战击溃塞尔柱苏丹桑贾尔的十万大军','Destroyed the Seljuk sultan Sanjar\'s army of 100,000 at Qatwan in 1141']],
  s:['卡特万是伊斯兰世界第一次被非穆斯林政权重创,消息传到欧洲后被误认为是东方基督教君主"祭司王约翰"打赢了穆斯林——这个传说影响了此后三百年的欧洲东方想象,并间接推动了寻找东方盟友的地理探索。西辽疆域一度横跨中亚,存续近百年。',
     'Qatwan was the first heavy defeat the Islamic world suffered from a non-Muslim power, and when word reached Europe it was taken to mean that a Christian king in the east — Prester John — had beaten the Muslims. That legend shaped European ideas about Asia for three centuries and helped drive the search for allies beyond it. His state spanned Central Asia and lasted nearly a hundred years.'] },
'阿布赉汗': { g:'king', y:[1711,1781], r:[1771,1781], c:'哈萨克汗国', n:['阿布赉汗','Ablai Khan'],
  t:['他同时向清朝和俄国称臣,靠在两个帝国之间周旋保住了哈萨克。',
     'He submitted to both China and Russia at once, and kept the Kazakhs by playing one against the other.'],
  a:[['青年时以孤儿牧马为生,在抗击准噶尔的战争中崭露头角','Grew up an orphan herding horses, and made his name fighting the Dzungars'],
     ['同时接受清朝与俄国的册封,在两大帝国之间维持独立','Accepted titles from both the Qing and the Russians while keeping his own hand free'],
     ['统一三个玉兹的大部,是哈萨克汗国最后一位有实权的可汗','United most of the three Kazakh hordes — the last khan with real power']],
  s:['准噶尔被清朝灭掉后,哈萨克草原直接暴露在两大帝国之间,他的双重效忠策略为哈萨克争取到几十年的实际自治。他是哈萨克斯坦最重要的民族英雄,首都的机场以他命名,纸币上也有他的形象。',
     'Once the Qing destroyed the Dzungars, the Kazakh steppe lay open between two empires, and his double allegiance bought several decades of real autonomy. He is Kazakhstan\'s foremost national hero; the capital\'s airport carries his name and his face is on the currency.'] },
'昔班尼汗': { g:'war', y:[1451,1510], r:[1500,1510], c:'布哈拉·希瓦·浩罕三汗国', n:['昔班尼汗','Muhammad Shaybani'],
  t:['他把帖木儿的子孙赶出中亚。被赶走的那个人后来去印度建了莫卧儿帝国。',
     'He drove Timur\'s descendants out of Central Asia. The one he drove out went to India and founded the Mughal empire.'],
  a:[['率乌兹别克部众南下,1500 年攻占撒马尔罕','Led the Uzbeks south and took Samarkand in 1500'],
     ['击败帖木儿后裔巴布尔,迫使其退往阿富汗','Beat Babur, Timur\'s descendant, and pushed him back into Afghanistan'],
     ['1510 年在梅尔夫败于萨法维的伊斯玛仪一世,战死','Was killed at Merv in 1510, defeated by Ismail I of Persia']],
  s:['他把乌兹别克人带进河中地区并定居下来,今天乌兹别克斯坦的民族与国名由此而来。被他赶走的巴布尔南下印度,1526 年建立莫卧儿帝国——中亚的一次改朝换代,间接决定了印度此后三百年的历史。',
     'He brought the Uzbeks into Transoxiana to stay, and modern Uzbekistan takes its people and its name from that. Babur, the man he expelled, went south and founded the Mughal empire in 1526 — a change of dynasty in Central Asia that settled the next three centuries of Indian history.'] },
'噶尔丹': { g:'war', y:[1644,1697], r:[1671,1697], c:'准噶尔', n:['噶尔丹','Galdan Boshugtu Khan'],
  t:['他本来在西藏当喇嘛,还俗回草原后,成了康熙一生最大的对手。',
     'He was a lama in Tibet. He returned to the steppe, and became the Kangxi emperor\'s greatest opponent.'],
  a:[['幼年被认定为活佛送往西藏学经,兄长遇害后还俗返回','Sent to Tibet as a recognised incarnation, he left the order and came home when his brother was murdered'],
     ['统一卫拉特诸部,东征喀尔喀蒙古,兵锋直逼北京数百里外','United the Oirat tribes, drove the Khalkha east, and came within a few hundred li of Beijing'],
     ['1696 年昭莫多之战大败于清军,次年身死','Was smashed at Jao Modo in 1696 and died the following year']],
  s:['康熙三次亲征才把他击败,这是清朝立国后规模最大的几次军事行动之一。准噶尔是欧亚大陆上最后一个游牧帝国,它的覆灭标志着延续两千余年的草原政权与农耕帝国拉锯就此终结——此后再没有哪个游牧势力能威胁定居国家。',
     'The Kangxi emperor took the field in person three times to beat him, among the largest campaigns the Qing ever mounted. The Dzungars were the last nomadic empire in Eurasia, and their destruction ended a two-thousand-year contest between steppe and farmland: no pastoral power ever threatened a settled state again.'] },
'阿拜': { g:'art', y:[1845,1904], c:'俄国治下中亚', n:['阿拜','Abai Qunanbaiuly'],
  t:['哈萨克现代文学是他一个人开的头。',
     'Modern Kazakh literature begins with one man.'],
  a:[['出身部落贵族,自学俄语与俄国文学','Born into a tribal notable family, he taught himself Russian and read Russian literature'],
     ['把普希金、莱蒙托夫、歌德译成哈萨克语,并创作大量诗歌与歌曲','Translated Pushkin, Lermontov and Goethe into Kazakh, and wrote poems and songs of his own'],
     ['写散文集《箴言录》四十五篇,直言批评本民族的陋习与惰性','Wrote forty-five prose "Words", bluntly criticising his own people\'s habits and complacency']],
  s:['他把书面哈萨克语从口头传统中确立起来,是哈萨克现代文学的奠基者。《箴言录》主张学习包括俄国在内的外部世界,同时保住本民族的语言与尊严——这种"既开放又自守"的立场至今是哈萨克民族认同的核心文本。哈萨克斯坦有以他命名的城市、大学与国家歌剧院。',
     'He turned Kazakh from an oral into a written literature and stands as its founder. The Words argue for learning from the outside world, Russia included, while holding on to language and dignity — a stance that remains the core text of Kazakh identity. A city, a university and the national opera house are named after him.'] },
'纳扎尔巴耶夫': { g:'state', y:[1940,2019], yk:'r', c:'现代中亚', n:['纳扎尔巴耶夫','Nursultan Nazarbayev'],
  t:['苏联解体时他手上有一千四百枚核弹头。他把它们全部交了出去。',
     'When the Soviet Union broke up he held 1,400 nuclear warheads. He gave every one of them up.'],
  a:[['1991 年苏联解体,哈萨克斯坦独立,他成为首任总统','Became the first president of an independent Kazakhstan in 1991'],
     ['1991 年关闭塞米巴拉金斯克核试验场,1995 年前销毁或移交全部核武器','Closed the Semipalatinsk test site in 1991 and had all warheads removed or destroyed by 1995'],
     ['1997 年迁都至北部草原新城,并长期执政至 2019 年辞职','Moved the capital to a new city on the northern steppe in 1997, and governed until resigning in 2019']],
  s:['哈萨克斯坦当时是世界第四大核武库,它的自愿弃核是核不扩散史上最重要的案例之一,《不扩散核武器条约》体系至今以此为范例。塞米巴拉金斯克曾进行过四百多次核试验,当地居民的健康影响持续至今。他执政二十八年,选举的竞争性长期受到国际批评。',
     'Kazakhstan held the fourth-largest nuclear arsenal in the world, and its voluntary disarmament is among the most important cases in the history of non-proliferation, still cited as the model. Semipalatinsk had absorbed more than four hundred tests, and the health effects on people living nearby persist. He governed for twenty-eight years, and the competitiveness of his elections was long criticised abroad.'] },
'格劳秀斯': { g:'mind', y:[1583,1645], c:'荷兰共和国', n:['格劳秀斯','Hugo Grotius'],
  t:['十一岁上大学,十五岁拿学位。他被判无期徒刑后,藏在一只书箱里逃了出去。',
     'At university at eleven, graduated at fifteen, sentenced to life — and escaped hidden in a book chest.'],
  a:[['1609 年写《海洋自由论》,主张海洋不属于任何国家,人人可通航','Argued in 1609 that the sea belongs to no state and is open to all'],
     ['1625 年写《战争与和平法》,系统提出战争也应受法律约束','Set out in 1625 that even war is bound by law'],
     ['1621 年被判终身监禁后,由妻子安排藏在书箱中运出监狱','Was smuggled out of prison in 1621 in a chest his wife had arranged']],
  s:['他被公认为国际法之父。"公海自由"原则至今写在《联合国海洋法公约》里;"战争也要守法"的思路是日内瓦公约与现代战争法的源头。他写《海洋自由论》本是替荷兰东印度公司的一次劫掠辩护——现代国际法的第一块基石,起点是一场商业官司。',
     'He is regarded as the father of international law. Freedom of the high seas is still written into the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea, and the idea that war itself is governed by rules is the origin of the Geneva Conventions. He wrote the sea treatise to justify a Dutch East India Company seizure — the first stone of modern international law was laid in a commercial lawsuit.'] },
'伦勃朗': { g:'art', y:[1606,1669], c:'荷兰共和国', n:['伦勃朗','Rembrandt'],
  t:['他画了近百幅自画像,从春风得意一直画到破产潦倒。',
     'He painted himself close to a hundred times, from prosperous young man to bankrupt old one.'],
  a:[['1642 年画《夜巡》,把集体肖像画成一个正在发生的场面','Painted the Night Watch in 1642, turning a group portrait into a scene in motion'],
     ['以强烈的明暗对比塑造人物,光只照在该照的地方','Modelled his figures in sharp light and deep shadow, lighting only what mattered'],
     ['1656 年破产,财产被拍卖,晚年在贫困中继续作画','Went bankrupt in 1656, saw his possessions auctioned, and painted on in poverty']],
  s:['《夜巡》是阿姆斯特丹国立博物馆的镇馆之作。他的自画像系列跨度四十年,是西方艺术史上最完整的一次自我记录——一个人用画笔留下自己一生的容貌与处境变化,此前没有先例。荷兰黄金时代的绘画产量惊人,估计留下数百万幅作品,他是其中的顶点。',
     'The Night Watch is the centrepiece of the Rijksmuseum. His self-portraits span forty years and are the most complete record of a single life in Western art — nobody had used the brush to document their own face and circumstances that way before. The Dutch Golden Age produced paintings in the millions, and he is its summit.'] },
'塔哈尔卡': { g:'king', y:[-690,-664], yk:'r', c:'库施·努比亚', n:['塔哈尔卡','Taharqa'],
  t:['他是从苏丹北上、统治了整个埃及的黑人法老。',
     'A Nubian pharaoh who came up from Sudan and ruled all of Egypt.'],
  a:[['统治埃及与努比亚,是第二十五王朝最强盛的时期','Ruled Egypt and Nubia at the height of the twenty-fifth dynasty'],
     ['大兴土木,在卡纳克神庙前立柱,并在努比亚各地建金字塔式陵墓','Built widely, adding a colonnade at Karnak and pyramid tombs across Nubia'],
     ['与亚述作战多年,最终被逐出埃及,退回努比亚','Fought the Assyrians for years, was driven out of Egypt, and withdrew to Nubia']],
  s:['第二十五王朝是埃及历史上唯一由努比亚人统治的时期,他们自视为埃及传统的复兴者,重修神庙、恢复古王国的艺术样式。努比亚境内今存金字塔约两百座,数量超过埃及全境——但知道这一点的人不多。他的名字也出现在《圣经·列王纪》里。',
     'The twenty-fifth dynasty is the only period when Nubians ruled Egypt, and they saw themselves as restorers of Egyptian tradition, rebuilding temples and reviving Old Kingdom styles. Sudan contains around two hundred pyramids, more than Egypt does — a fact few people know. His name also appears in the Book of Kings.'] },
'埃扎纳': { g:'faith', y:[320,360], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'阿克苏姆', n:['埃扎纳','Ezana of Axum'],
  t:['他让阿克苏姆成为世界上最早以基督教为国教的国家之一。',
     'Under him Axum became one of the first states anywhere to adopt Christianity officially.'],
  a:[['4 世纪皈依基督教,钱币上的图案从新月改为十字架','Converted in the fourth century; his coins changed from a crescent to a cross'],
     ['出兵灭掉尼罗河上游的库施-麦罗埃王国','Campaigned up the Nile and ended the Kushite kingdom of Meroe'],
     ['立多语石碑,以吉兹语、萨巴语与希腊语三种文字刻写','Set up stelae inscribed in Ge\'ez, Sabaean and Greek']],
  s:['他的钱币是这次改宗最直接的物证——从新月到十字架的变化可以精确断代,这在早期基督教史上极为罕见。埃塞俄比亚正教会自此延续一千七百年,是世界上最古老的基督教会之一,也是非洲唯一未被殖民中断的本土宗教传统。阿克苏姆遗址 1980 年列入世界遗产。',
     'His coinage is the hard evidence for that conversion: the switch from crescent to cross can be dated precisely, which is rare in early Christian history. The Ethiopian Orthodox Church has run unbroken for seventeen centuries since, one of the oldest in the world and the only African religious tradition never interrupted by colonisation. Axum became World Heritage in 1980.'] },
'通卡·曼宁': { g:'king', y:[1063,1068], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'加纳帝国', n:['通卡·曼宁','Tunka Manin'],
  t:['一位阿拉伯地理学家写下了他上朝的样子,那段文字成了加纳帝国最生动的记录。',
     'An Arab geographer described his court, and that passage is the most vivid record the Ghana Empire left.'],
  a:[['统治加纳帝国鼎盛期,控制跨撒哈拉的黄金与食盐贸易','Ruled at the empire\'s height, controlling the trans-Saharan gold and salt trade'],
     ['据记载可动员二十万军队,其中四万是弓箭手','Could reportedly field 200,000 men, 40,000 of them archers'],
     ['其形象见于安达卢斯地理学家巴克里 1068 年的著作','His court is described in the 1068 work of the Andalusian geographer al-Bakri']],
  s:['巴克里从未到过加纳,他的记述来自往返商人的口述,却详细到能写出国王坐在饰金的帐幕里、身旁拴着金链的狗、马匹披着金饰。西非早期历史几乎没有本地文献,阿拉伯地理学家的转述是主要材料——这也提醒我们:一个文明"有没有名字留下",往往取决于邻居有没有写字的习惯。',
     'Al-Bakri never went to Ghana; he compiled his account from returning merchants, yet it is detailed enough to describe the king in a gold-hung pavilion, dogs on golden chains beside him, horses in gold trappings. Early West Africa left almost no records of its own, and Arab geographers are the main source — a reminder that whether a civilisation leaves names behind often depends on whether its neighbours wrote things down.'] },
'哈桑·本·苏莱曼': { g:'king', y:[1310,1333], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'斯瓦希里城邦', n:['哈桑·本·苏莱曼','al-Hasan ibn Sulaiman'],
  t:['伊本·白图泰到过他的城,说那是他见过最美的城市之一。',
     'Ibn Battuta visited his city and called it one of the most beautiful he had seen.'],
  a:[['统治基尔瓦,当时东非海岸最富庶的城邦','Ruled Kilwa, the wealthiest of the East African coastal city-states'],
     ['控制来自津巴布韦内陆的黄金出口','Controlled the export of gold coming up from the Zimbabwean interior'],
     ['建胡苏尼库布瓦宫,是撒哈拉以南非洲当时最大的石构建筑','Built Husuni Kubwa, then the largest stone building in sub-Saharan Africa']],
  s:['基尔瓦的繁荣建立在印度洋季风贸易上——黄金、象牙向东,中国瓷器、印度棉布向西;基尔瓦遗址至今出土大量中国青瓷。斯瓦希里语正是在这一系列港口城邦里成型的,今天是东非数千万人的通用语。基尔瓦遗址 1981 年列入世界遗产。',
     'Kilwa\'s wealth rested on the monsoon trade of the Indian Ocean — gold and ivory east, Chinese porcelain and Indian cotton west; Chinese celadon still turns up in its ruins. Swahili took shape in this chain of ports and is now the common language of tens of millions across East Africa. The site became World Heritage in 1981.'] },
'桑尼·阿里': { g:'war', y:[1464,1492], yk:'r', c:'桑海帝国', n:['桑尼·阿里','Sonni Ali'],
  t:['他建了一支内河舰队,靠尼日尔河把西非最大的帝国连了起来。',
     'He built a river navy, and used the Niger to hold together the largest empire in West Africa.'],
  a:[['1468 年攻取廷巴克图,1473 年攻取杰内','Took Timbuktu in 1468 and Djenné in 1473'],
     ['组建尼日尔河舰队,把军队与粮食沿河快速投送','Assembled a fleet on the Niger to move troops and grain quickly'],
     ['与廷巴克图的伊斯兰学者集团长期冲突,史书对他评价两极','Clashed for years with Timbuktu\'s Muslim scholars, who wrote about him accordingly']],
  s:['桑海在他手上取代马里,成为当时西非最大的帝国。关于他的记载几乎全部出自与他敌对的廷巴克图学者之手,把他写成暴君;而口传史诗里他是英雄——同一个人在两套史料里判若两人,这是非洲史研究里最常被举出的史料立场问题。',
     'Under him Songhai replaced Mali as the largest state in West Africa of its day. Almost everything written about him comes from the Timbuktu scholars he fought, who cast him as a tyrant; the oral epics make him a hero. The same man in two bodies of source material — the standard example, in African historiography, of why who is writing matters.'] },
'阿斯基亚·穆罕默德': { g:'king', y:[1493,1528], yk:'r', c:'桑海帝国', n:['阿斯基亚·穆罕默德','Askia Muhammad'],
  t:['他把桑海从征服的军营变成了一个有制度的国家。',
     'He turned Songhai from a war camp into a state with institutions.'],
  a:[['1493 年推翻桑尼·阿里之子夺位','Overthrew Sonni Ali\'s son in 1493'],
     ['分设行省与统一度量衡,建立中央财政与法官系统','Created provinces, standard weights and measures, a central treasury and a corps of judges'],
     ['1496 年率庞大队伍朝觐麦加,重建桑科雷大学的学术声望','Made a great pilgrimage to Mecca in 1496 and rebuilt Sankoré\'s scholarly standing']],
  s:['廷巴克图在他这一朝成为伊斯兰世界的重要学术中心,桑科雷大学的学生一度数以千计,手抄本产业兴盛——今天廷巴克图仍藏有数十万份中世纪手稿,2012 年当地居民冒险把大批手稿偷运出城,躲过了极端组织的焚毁。',
     'Timbuktu became a serious centre of Islamic scholarship in his reign, with thousands of students at Sankoré and a thriving manuscript trade. The city still holds hundreds of thousands of medieval manuscripts; in 2012 local families smuggled much of the collection out under the noses of militants who meant to burn it.'] },
'利奥波德二世': { g:'king', y:[1835,1909], r:[1865,1909], c:'欧洲殖民非洲', n:['利奥波德二世','Leopold II'],
  t:['他把一块相当于西欧面积的非洲土地,变成了自己的私人财产。',
     'He made an area of Africa the size of western Europe his personal property.'],
  a:[['1885 年柏林会议上以人道与科学为名,取得刚果自由邦的私人所有权','Won personal ownership of the Congo Free State at the 1885 Berlin Conference, in the name of humanity and science'],
     ['以配额制强征橡胶,完不成者被断手、扣押家属或处死','Imposed rubber quotas, punishing failure by mutilation, hostage-taking and killing'],
     ['1908 年在国际舆论压力下,被迫将刚果移交比利时政府','Was forced in 1908 to hand the Congo over to the Belgian state']],
  s:['他一生从未踏足刚果。学界对该时期人口损失的估计通常在数百万,常被引用的数字是约一千万。英国外交官凯斯门特的调查报告与摩雷尔发起的运动,构成了历史上最早的一次现代国际人权运动。2020 年后比利时多地拆除或移走了他的塑像。',
     'He never once set foot in the Congo. Scholarly estimates of the population loss in that period run into the millions, with ten million a widely cited figure. The investigation by the British consul Roger Casement and the campaign E. D. Morel built around it amounted to the first modern international human rights movement. Since 2020 a number of Belgian cities have taken down or removed his statues.'] },
'塞西尔·罗兹': { g:'state', y:[1853,1902], c:'欧洲殖民非洲', n:['塞西尔·罗兹','Cecil Rhodes'],
  t:['他说过想把非洲从开普敦到开罗全部涂成英国的红色。',
     'He said he wanted Africa painted British red from the Cape to Cairo.'],
  a:[['创办戴比尔斯公司,一度控制世界九成的钻石产量','Founded De Beers, which at one point controlled ninety per cent of the world\'s diamonds'],
     ['以特许公司名义占领赞比西河两岸,该地被命名为"罗得西亚"','Took the lands on both sides of the Zambezi through a chartered company; they were named Rhodesia after him'],
     ['遗嘱设立罗兹奖学金,资助各国学生赴牛津就读','Left his fortune to endow the Rhodes Scholarship at Oxford']],
  s:['以个人名字命名两个殖民地(南北罗得西亚,即今津巴布韦与赞比亚),在殖民史上仅此一例。罗兹奖学金至今是世界上最著名的奖学金之一,已资助逾八千人。2015 年南非开普敦大学的学生运动要求移走他的塑像并获成功,此后"罗兹必须倒下"扩散到牛津等地,成为全球去殖民化讨论的标志性事件。',
     'Two colonies named after one private individual — Northern and Southern Rhodesia, now Zambia and Zimbabwe — has no parallel in colonial history. The scholarship remains among the most prestigious in the world and has funded over eight thousand people. In 2015 students at the University of Cape Town forced his statue down; "Rhodes Must Fall" then spread to Oxford and elsewhere, and became the emblem of the global argument over decolonisation.'] },
'恩克鲁玛': { g:'state', y:[1909,1972], r:[1957,1966], c:'现代非洲', n:['恩克鲁玛','Kwame Nkrumah'],
  t:['他领导的加纳是撒哈拉以南非洲第一个独立的国家。',
     'The Ghana he led was the first country in sub-Saharan Africa to win independence.'],
  a:[['以"立即自治"为口号发动非暴力不合作,坐过牢,在狱中赢得选举','Campaigned for self-government now by non-violent means, went to prison, and won an election from his cell'],
     ['1957 年加纳独立,他宣布"加纳的独立没有意义,除非与整个非洲的解放联系起来"','At independence in 1957 he said Ghana\'s freedom was meaningless unless linked to the liberation of all Africa'],
     ['1963 年推动成立非洲统一组织;1966 年在出访途中被军事政变推翻','Helped found the Organisation of African Unity in 1963, and was overthrown by a coup in 1966 while abroad']],
  s:['加纳独立后的六年里,又有二十多个非洲国家相继独立。他推动成立的非洲统一组织是今天非洲联盟的前身,成员五十五国。泛非主义作为一种政治思想,他是最重要的实践者——尽管他自己的执政后期转向一党制,并以政变收场。',
     'In the six years after Ghana, more than twenty African countries became independent. The organisation he helped found became today\'s African Union, with fifty-five members. He was the foremost practitioner of pan-Africanism as working politics — though his own rule turned to one-party government and ended in a coup.'] },
'曼德拉': { g:'state', y:[1918,2013], r:[1994,1999], c:'现代非洲', n:['曼德拉','Nelson Mandela'],
  t:['他坐了二十七年牢。出狱四年后当选总统,没有清算任何人。',
     'Twenty-seven years in prison. Four years after walking out, he was president — and he settled no scores.'],
  a:[['1964 年因组织武装斗争被判终身监禁,在罗本岛服刑十八年','Sentenced to life in 1964 for organising armed resistance, and held eighteen years on Robben Island'],
     ['1990 年获释,与德克勒克谈判和平过渡,共获 1993 年诺贝尔和平奖','Freed in 1990, he negotiated the transition with de Klerk; they shared the 1993 Nobel Peace Prize'],
     ['1994 年南非首次全民选举当选总统,设真相与和解委员会','Won the first universal election in 1994 and set up the Truth and Reconciliation Commission']],
  s:['南非从种族隔离到多数人统治的转变没有演变成内战,这在当时被普遍认为几乎不可能。真相与和解委员会以"讲出真相换取赦免"取代审判,此后被卢旺达、东帝汶等三十余个国家借鉴。他只做一届总统即主动交权。联合国把他的生日 7 月 18 日定为"曼德拉国际日"。',
     'South Africa moved from apartheid to majority rule without the civil war almost everyone expected. The Truth and Reconciliation Commission traded amnesty for testimony instead of holding trials, and more than thirty countries — Rwanda and Timor-Leste among them — have since borrowed the model. He served one term and handed over power. The UN keeps his birthday, 18 July, as Nelson Mandela International Day.'] },

'西潘王': { g:'king', y:[250,300], yk:'a', ca:1, c:'莫切', n:['西潘王','Lord of Sipán'],
  t:['约三世纪莫切的一位统治者。没有任何文字记下他,我们知道的一切,都是考古学家从他的墓里「读」出来的。','A Moche ruler of about the third century. No text records him; everything we know was read out of his tomb.'],
  a:[['1987 年,盗墓贼先挖进了西潘村旁的土坯金字塔;考古学家瓦尔特·阿尔瓦闻讯赶到,在警察看守下抢救发掘,找到了第一座完整出土、未被盗掘的莫切王墓。','In 1987 looters broke into an adobe pyramid by the village of Sipán; archaeologist Walter Alva rushed in to excavate under police guard and found the first Moche royal tomb ever recovered intact.'],
     ['他戴着金银头饰,项链是二十颗花生形状的珠子——金银各十颗;陪葬的还有武士、女子、孩童、一条狗,还有两头美洲驼。','He wore gold and silver regalia, with a necklace of twenty peanut-shaped beads — ten gold, ten silver — and was buried with warriors, women, a child, a dog and two llamas.'],
     ['他的整套装束,与莫切陶器上反复出现的「武士祭司」形象对得上——学者由此确认:陶画里主持仪式的那种人物,真实存在过。','His full regalia matches the "warrior priest" who appears again and again on Moche pottery — confirming that the figure presiding over those painted ceremonies really existed.']],
  s:['这座墓被称作「美洲的图坦卡蒙」;同一座金字塔后来又发掘出年代更早的「老西潘王」等多座王墓。出土文物如今收藏在专为它们建造的西潘王室陵墓博物馆里,是秘鲁最重要的博物馆之一——一个没有文字的文明,靠一座没被盗走的墓,让世界记住了它的王。','The find has been called an American Tutankhamun; the same pyramid later yielded the earlier "Old Lord of Sipán" and other royal tombs. The treasures now fill the Royal Tombs of Sipán Museum, built for them and among the most important museums in Peru — a civilisation without writing, remembered through the one tomb the looters never reached.'] },
'火之生': { g:'war', y:[374,396], yk:'a', ca:1, c:'特奥蒂瓦坎', n:['火之生','Siyaj K\'ak\''],
  t:['我们知道他,全靠一千公里外的玛雅人把他写进了石碑。',
     'We know him only because the Maya, a thousand kilometres away, carved him into stone.'],
  a:[['378 年 1 月 16 日抵达玛雅城邦蒂卡尔,同一天蒂卡尔的国王死了','Arrived at the Maya city of Tikal on 16 January 378; Tikal\'s king died the same day'],
     ['此后蒂卡尔换上与特奥蒂瓦坎有关的新王朝,建筑与武器样式随之改变','A new dynasty with Teotihuacan ties took over, and the city\'s architecture and weapons changed with it'],
     ['他的名字与事迹见于蒂卡尔、瓦哈克通等多座玛雅城市的碑铭','His name and deeds appear on inscriptions at Tikal, Uaxactun and other Maya sites']],
  s:['特奥蒂瓦坎鼎盛时人口约十至二十万,是当时美洲最大的城市,但它留下的那些符号至今几乎无法解读,连统治者自称什么都不知道。关于它唯一有名有姓的历史记载,来自被它影响的玛雅人——这和加纳帝国只见于阿拉伯地理学家笔下是同一种处境:一个文明能否留下名字,常常取决于邻居写不写字。',
     'Teotihuacan held perhaps 100,000 to 200,000 people at its height, the largest city in the Americas — yet its script remains essentially undeciphered, and we do not even know what its rulers called themselves. The one named episode in its history comes from the Maya it influenced, exactly as the Ghana Empire survives only in Arab geography: whether a civilisation leaves names behind often depends on whether its neighbours wrote things down.'] },

'红发埃里克': { g:'sail', y:[950,1003], ca:1, c:'维京·北欧', n:['红发埃里克','Erik the Red'],
  t:['他在冰岛杀了人被判流放三年,就往西开船去找传说里的陆地——找到了,还给它起了个骗人的名字。',
     'Outlawed from Iceland for three years for killing a man, he sailed west to look for a land people spoke of — found it, and gave it a name meant to attract settlers.'],
  a:[['他本是挪威人,父亲因杀人被逐,全家迁到冰岛;他自己后来又因械斗致人死被冰岛的集会判处三年流放。',
      'Born in Norway, he came to Iceland when his father was outlawed for killing; he was later outlawed himself for three years, again over a killing.'],
     ['流放期间他向西航行,沿一片大陆的西南岸考察了三年,回冰岛后把它称作「绿地」(Grønland,即格陵兰)——萨迦说他起这个名字是因为「名字好听,人才愿意去」。',
      'During those three years he explored the south-west coast of a great land, and on his return called it Greenland — the sagas say he chose the name because people would be readier to go somewhere that sounded good.'],
     ['约 986 年他带着一支船队回去定居,据萨迦记载出发时二十五条船、到达的只有十四条;这几处定居点在格陵兰住了将近五百年,15 世纪消失。',
      'About 986 he led a fleet back to settle; the sagas say twenty-five ships set out and fourteen arrived. The settlements lasted nearly five hundred years, and died out in the fifteenth century.']],
  s:['格陵兰的北欧定居点是维京人向西扩张的最远一站,也是他儿子莱夫再往西走的跳板。定居点在 15 世纪消失,原因至今没有定论——气候转冷、与因纽特人的关系、与挪威的贸易断绝都被提出过。今天格陵兰南部还能看到当年的教堂与农庄石基。',
     'The Norse settlements in Greenland were the farthest west the Vikings held, and the springboard for his son Leif to go farther still. Why they vanished in the fifteenth century is still argued over — a cooling climate, relations with the Inuit, the loss of trade with Norway have all been proposed. The stone foundations of their churches and farms can still be seen in southern Greenland.'] },

'莱夫·埃里克森': { g:'sail', y:[970,1020], ca:1, c:'维京·北欧', n:['莱夫·埃里克森','Leif Erikson'],
  t:['他上岸的年份精确到 1021 年——不是猜的,是从树轮里算出来的。',
     'The year he came ashore is known exactly: 1021 — not a guess, but read out of tree rings.'],
  a:[['他是红发埃里克的儿子,在格陵兰长大。萨迦说他约 1000 年向西航行,先后看到三片地方,给最南边一片起名「文兰」(Vinland,葡萄之地),在那里过了一冬。',
      'Son of Erik the Red, he grew up in Greenland. The sagas say that about the year 1000 he sailed west, saw three lands in turn, named the southernmost Vinland — the land of vines — and wintered there.'],
     ['1960 年,挪威人英斯塔夫妇在纽芬兰岛北端找到兰塞奥兹牧草地遗址:八座草皮房屋、铁匠炉与船钉,是格陵兰以外美洲唯一得到确证的维京聚落,1978 年列入世界遗产。',
      'In 1960 the Norwegians Helge and Anne Stine Ingstad found L\'Anse aux Meadows at the northern tip of Newfoundland: eight turf buildings, a smithy and boat nails — the only confirmed Norse site in the Americas outside Greenland, and a World Heritage site since 1978.'],
     ['2021 年一项研究用树木年轮里一次已知年份的太阳事件,把遗址上砍下的三块木头定在公元 1021 年——欧洲人在美洲活动的第一个确切年份。',
      'In 2021 a study used a solar event of known date recorded in tree rings to fix three pieces of wood cut at the site to the year 1021 — the first exact date for Europeans in the Americas.']],
  s:['文兰没有留下来:遗址只住了很短时间,萨迦说与当地人(萨迦称之为 skrælingjar)起了冲突,补给线又太长。它证明的不是「发现」而是「到达」——真正改变世界的相遇要再等五百年。美国把 10 月 9 日定为莱夫·埃里克森日。',
     'Vinland did not last: the site was occupied only briefly, the sagas tell of clashes with the people already there, and the supply line from Greenland was far too long. What it proves is not discovery but arrival — the meeting that changed the world was still five centuries off. The United States marks 9 October as Leif Erikson Day.'] },

'克努特大帝': { g:'king', y:[995,1035], ca:1, r:[1016,1035], c:'维京·北欧', n:['克努特大帝','Cnut the Great'],
  t:['一个丹麦人同时当着英格兰、丹麦和挪威三国的国王——维京时代的最高点。',
     'A Dane who was at once king of England, Denmark and Norway — the high-water mark of the Viking age.'],
  a:[['1016 年他打赢了英格兰的王位之争,成为英格兰国王;1018 年继承丹麦,1028 年又拿下挪威,史家称这三国为「北海帝国」。',
      'He won the fight for England in 1016, inherited Denmark in 1018 and took Norway in 1028; historians call the three together the North Sea Empire.'],
     ['他不是以征服者的方式统治英格兰:沿用英格兰的法律与货币,颁布以他名义写成的法典(实际执笔的是约克大主教伍尔夫斯坦),大笔捐给英格兰教会。',
      'He did not rule England as a conqueror: he kept its law and its coinage, issued law codes in his own name (actually drafted by Wulfstan, archbishop of York), and gave generously to the English church.'],
     ['1027 年他到罗马参加皇帝康拉德二世的加冕,顺便替英格兰的大主教减免了受职费,又替朝圣者和商人谈妥了沿途的通行条件。',
      'In 1027 he went to Rome for the coronation of Emperor Conrad II, and while there got the fees for English archbishops reduced and safer passage agreed for pilgrims and merchants.']],
  s:['「海水不会因为国王下令就退回去」这个故事出自他死后一百年的记载:他把王座搬到海边命令潮水停下,水照样涨上来——原意是他借此告诉臣下,国王的权力有限。1035 年他一死,三国立刻分开,他的儿子们十年内相继去世,北海帝国没有留下来。',
     'The story of the king commanding the tide comes from a chronicle written a century after his death: he had his throne carried to the shore and ordered the sea to stop, and the sea came on regardless — the point, as told, was to show his courtiers how little a king can do. When he died in 1035 the three kingdoms came apart at once; his sons were all dead within a decade, and the North Sea Empire did not outlive them.'] },

'玛格丽特一世': { g:'king', y:[1353,1412], c:'北欧诸王国', n:['玛格丽特一世','Margaret I'],
  t:['十岁出嫁、三十五岁上手,她把北欧三个王国合成了一个——而她自己从来没有戴上过女王的冠。',
     'Married at ten, in charge at thirty-five, she brought the three Scandinavian kingdoms under one crown — and was never herself crowned queen.'],
  a:[['她是丹麦国王瓦尔德马四世的女儿,1363 年十岁嫁给挪威国王哈康六世。1387 年独子奥拉夫十六岁猝死,次年她被丹麦与挪威推为摄政。',
      'Daughter of Valdemar IV of Denmark, she was married at ten in 1363 to Haakon VI of Norway. When her only son Olaf died suddenly at sixteen in 1387, both Denmark and Norway made her regent the next year.'],
     ['丹麦与挪威到手靠的是继承和联姻,瑞典是她亲手打下来的:1389 年瑞典国王阿尔贝特兵败被俘,在她的城堡里一关就是六年。',
      'Denmark and Norway came by inheritance and marriage; Sweden she won herself: in 1389 King Albert was beaten and taken, and spent six years locked in one of her castles.'],
     ['1397 年她在卡尔马为甥孙波美拉尼亚的埃里克加冕,三个王国从此共戴一君——卡尔马联盟,北欧史上最大的国家。她自己用的头衔是「女主与监护人」一类的称呼,始终没有正式加冕为女王。',
      'In 1397 at Kalmar she had her great-nephew Eric of Pomerania crowned, and the three kingdoms shared one king — the Kalmar Union, the largest state Scandinavia has ever had. Her own title was something like "sovereign lady and guardian"; she was never formally crowned queen regnant.']],
  s:['联盟维持了一百多年,1523 年瑞典脱离而散,丹麦与挪威则一直到 1814 年。1412 年她死在停泊于弗伦斯堡港的船上,死因不明,葬在罗斯基勒大教堂——那口石棺今天还在。她被认为是欧洲中世纪最有能力的统治者之一,而她的权力全部来自「代理」:先替儿子,再替甥孙。',
     'The union held for over a century, breaking when Sweden left in 1523; Denmark and Norway stayed together until 1814. She died in 1412 aboard a ship in Flensburg harbour, of causes unknown, and lies in Roskilde Cathedral, where her stone sarcophagus can still be seen. She is reckoned among the ablest rulers of medieval Europe — and all her power was held on someone else\'s behalf: first her son\'s, then her great-nephew\'s.'] },

'腓特烈二世': { g:'king', y:[1712,1786], r:[1740,1786], c:'勃兰登堡·普鲁士', n:['腓特烈二世','Frederick II (the Great)'],
  t:['他年轻时想逃出这个国家,后来把它变成了欧洲强权;他吹长笛、写法文书,也打了一辈子仗。',
     'As a young man he tried to run away from this country; later he made it a European power. He played the flute, wrote in French, and spent his life at war.'],
  a:[['十八岁时他与好友卡特一起出逃未遂,父亲把他关起来,并强迫他在窗前看着卡特被处死。',
      'At eighteen he tried to flee with his friend Katte; his father imprisoned him and made him watch from a window while Katte was executed.'],
     ['1740 年即位当年就出兵夺取奥地利的西里西亚,此后三次战争守住了它;1756—1763 年的七年战争里普鲁士以一敌数国,几度濒临崩溃。',
      'In 1740, his first year on the throne, he seized Silesia from Austria and then fought three wars to keep it; in the Seven Years\' War of 1756–63 Prussia stood against several great powers at once and more than once came close to collapse.'],
     ['他在波茨坦建无忧宫,自称「国家的第一公仆」,废除了刑讯逼供,推广土豆以防饥荒;1747 年巴赫到波茨坦见他,回去写成《音乐的奉献》。',
      'He built Sanssouci at Potsdam, called himself the first servant of the state, abolished judicial torture, and pushed the potato as insurance against famine; when Bach visited him at Potsdam in 1747 the meeting produced the Musical Offering.']],
  s:['他把一个中等邦国变成能与奥地利、法国、俄国并列的强权,西里西亚也从此归了普鲁士——一百多年后德意志由普鲁士统一,起点在这里。他的名声在后世被反复借用:19 世纪把他当民族英雄,20 世纪的德国政权又拿他做宣传,与他本人写在纸上的那套开明专制主张相去甚远。他要求死后葬在无忧宫的葡萄园阶地上、和他的狗在一起,这个愿望到 1991 年才实现。',
     'He turned a middling state into a power ranked with Austria, France and Russia, and Silesia stayed Prussian — the unification of Germany by Prussia a century later begins here. His name was borrowed again and again after him: as a national hero in the nineteenth century, and by twentieth-century German regimes for propaganda, far from the enlightened absolutism he set out on paper. He asked to be buried on the vine terrace at Sanssouci beside his dogs; that wish was carried out only in 1991.'] },

'加里波第': { g:'war', y:[1807,1882], c:'现代欧洲诸国', n:['加里波第','Giuseppe Garibaldi'],
  t:['他带着一千个穿红衬衫的人出发,几个月后把半个意大利交给了国王。',
     'He set out with a thousand men in red shirts, and a few months later handed half of Italy to a king.'],
  a:[['早年流亡南美十二年,在乌拉圭内战中带一支意大利志愿军作战,红衬衫就是那时穿起来的。',
      'He spent twelve years exiled in South America, leading an Italian legion in Uruguay\'s civil war; the red shirts came from those years.'],
     ['1860 年 5 月他率约一千一百人从热那亚附近的夸尔托出海,登陆西西里,几个月内打下西西里与那不勒斯——两西西里王国有近千万人口,而他的出发点只有两条船。',
      'In May 1860 he sailed from Quarto near Genoa with about eleven hundred men, landed in Sicily, and within months had taken Sicily and Naples — the Kingdom of the Two Sicilies had millions of subjects; he had started with two ships.'],
     ['1860 年 10 月他在特亚诺把打下来的南部交给撒丁国王维托里奥·埃马努埃莱二世,自己回到卡普雷拉岛上种地,没有要官职。',
      'In October 1860 at Teano he handed the conquered south to Victor Emmanuel II of Sardinia, then went back to farm on the island of Caprera, taking no office.']],
  s:['1861 年意大利王国宣告成立,他这一趟是关键的一步。他不是唯一的功臣——加富尔的外交与撒丁的军队同样决定性,而他和加富尔互相看不上。美国内战时林肯政府曾试探请他带兵,他没有接受。今天意大利几乎每座城市都有一条加里波第街。',
     'The Kingdom of Italy was proclaimed in 1861, and his campaign was a decisive step towards it. He was not the only maker of it — Cavour\'s diplomacy and the Sardinian army mattered as much, and he and Cavour could not stand each other. During the American Civil War Lincoln\'s government sounded him out about a command; he did not take it. Nearly every town in Italy now has a Via Garibaldi.'] },

'玛丽·居里': { g:'sci', y:[1867,1934], c:'现代欧洲诸国', n:['玛丽·居里','Marie Curie'],
  t:['两次诺贝尔奖,两个不同的学科——至今只有她一个人做到。',
     'Two Nobel Prizes in two different sciences — still the only person to have done it.'],
  a:[['她生在被俄国统治的华沙,当时波兰的大学不收女生,她一边做家庭教师一边攒钱,二十四岁去巴黎读书。',
      'She was born in Warsaw under Russian rule, where the universities took no women; she worked as a governess to save money and went to Paris to study at twenty-four.'],
     ['1898 年她与丈夫皮埃尔从沥青铀矿里分离出两种新元素,其中一种以她的祖国命名为钋(polonium),另一种是镭;为提炼出零点一克镭盐,他们处理了数吨矿渣。',
      'In 1898 she and her husband Pierre isolated two new elements from pitchblende — one she named polonium after her homeland, the other radium; to get a tenth of a gram of radium salt they worked through tons of ore.'],
     ['1903 年获物理学奖(与皮埃尔、贝克勒尔同获),1911 年独得化学奖;第一次世界大战中她改装了约二十辆载 X 光机的汽车开上前线,士兵管它们叫「小居里」。',
      'The physics prize came in 1903, shared with Pierre and Becquerel, and the chemistry prize alone in 1911; in the First World War she fitted out some twenty vans carrying X-ray equipment for the front, and the soldiers called them "little Curies".']],
  s:['她是巴黎大学第一位女教授,女儿伊雷娜后来也得了诺贝尔化学奖。她拒绝为镭的提炼方法申请专利,认为那属于所有人。1934 年她死于再生障碍性贫血,一般认为与长期接触辐射有关——她的笔记本至今仍有放射性,存放在铅盒里。',
     'She was the first woman to hold a professorship at the University of Paris, and her daughter Irène later won a Nobel in chemistry too. She refused to patent the process for isolating radium, holding that it belonged to everyone. She died in 1934 of aplastic anaemia, generally attributed to her years of exposure to radiation — her notebooks are still radioactive and are kept in lead-lined boxes.'] },

'诺贝尔': { g:'sci', y:[1833,1896], c:'现代欧洲诸国', n:['诺贝尔','Alfred Nobel'],
  t:['他发明了炸药,又用炸药挣来的钱设了一个奖,奖给「为人类作出最大贡献」的人。',
     'He invented dynamite, and with the money it made set up a prize for those who confer the greatest benefit on humankind.'],
  a:[['硝化甘油威力大但一碰就炸,他把它吸附在硅藻土里做成可以安全搬运的炸药,1867 年取得专利;一生共有 355 项专利。',
      'Nitroglycerine was powerful but went off at a knock; he soaked it into diatomaceous earth to make something that could be carried safely, and patented dynamite in 1867. He held 355 patents in all.'],
     ['1895 年 11 月 27 日他在巴黎的瑞典-挪威俱乐部签下遗嘱,把约百分之九十四的财产(三千一百二十多万瑞典克朗)拿出来设立五个奖项,并写明不分国籍。',
      'On 27 November 1895, at the Swedish-Norwegian Club in Paris, he signed a will leaving about ninety-four per cent of his fortune — over 31 million Swedish kronor — to endow five prizes, to be given without regard to nationality.'],
     ['流传很广的说法是:1888 年他哥哥去世,一家法国报纸误登了他的讣告并称他为「死亡商人」,让他决定改变身后的名声。这份误登的讣告确实存在(1888 年 4 月),但「死亡商人」这个说法史家一直无法证实。',
      'The often-told story is that in 1888, when his brother died, a French paper printed Alfred\'s obituary by mistake and called him a merchant of death, which made him think about how he would be remembered. The misprinted obituary is real — April 1888 — but historians have never been able to verify the famous phrase.']],
  s:['首届诺贝尔奖 1901 年颁发。和平奖按他的遗嘱由挪威的委员会评选,其余在瑞典——那时挪威与瑞典还是同一个联合王国。102 号元素锘(nobelium)以他命名。一个靠军火与炸药起家的人,把名字留成了世界上最有名的奖。',
     'The first prizes were awarded in 1901. By his will the peace prize is decided by a Norwegian committee and the rest in Sweden — at the time Norway and Sweden were still one united kingdom. Element 102, nobelium, is named after him. A man who made his fortune in explosives left his name to the best-known prize in the world.'] },

'布尔纳布里亚什二世': { g:'king', y:[-1359,-1333], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'加喜特巴比伦', n:['布尔纳布里亚什二世','Burna-Buriash II'],
  t:['他写给埃及法老的信留到了今天,内容大半是抱怨:金子成色不足,使者被扣了两年。',
     'His letters to the pharaoh survive, and most of them are complaints: the gold was underweight, and his messenger had been held for two years.'],
  a:[['他在位约二十七年,是加喜特王朝最强的时候。1887 年埃及阿马尔那出土的一批外交泥板里,有九封是他写的(编号 EA 6—14),用阿卡德语——当时中东各国通用的外交语言。',
      'He reigned some twenty-seven years, at the height of the Kassite dynasty. Among the diplomatic tablets found at Amarna in Egypt in 1887, nine are his (EA 6–14), written in Akkadian, the diplomatic language of the day.'],
     ['信里他与法老互称「兄弟」,讨价还价:埃及送来的金子分量不够,女儿出嫁时只派了五辆车来接,他生病时法老没有派人问候。',
      'In them he and the pharaoh call each other brother and haggle: the gold Egypt sent was short weight, only five carriages came to fetch his daughter for her wedding, and when he was ill the pharaoh sent no word.'],
     ['他最不高兴的是亚述人也派使者去了埃及——在他看来那是自己的属国。他送给埃及的礼物主要是青金石,换回象牙、乌木和黄金。',
      'What annoyed him most was that Assyrian envoys had gone to Egypt too — in his view they were his vassals. What he sent Egypt was mostly lapis lazuli, in exchange for ivory, ebony and gold.']],
  s:['这批阿马尔那书信是青铜时代晚期国际关系最直接的证据:埃及、巴比伦、赫梯、亚述、米坦尼的君主互称兄弟,用联姻和送礼维持一个多国体系,和后世的外交没什么两样。他死后不久王位发生动乱,亚述王阿淑尔-乌巴里特一世出兵干预、扶立新王——那个他看不起的邻居,已经反过来能决定巴比伦的王位了。',
     'The Amarna letters are the plainest evidence we have of international relations in the late Bronze Age: the kings of Egypt, Babylon, Hatti, Assyria and Mitanni addressed one another as brothers and held a multi-state system together by marriage and gift-exchange, not so differently from diplomacy since. Soon after his death the succession broke down and the Assyrian king Ashur-uballit I intervened to put his own candidate on the throne — the neighbour he had looked down on was now deciding who ruled Babylon.'] },

'伊奢那跋摩一世': { g:'king', y:[616,637], ca:1, yk:'r', c:'真腊', n:['伊奢那跋摩一世','Isanavarman I'],
  t:['把自己的名字给了国都的王:伊奢那补罗,意思是「伊奢那之城」。','The king who gave the capital his name: Ishanapura, the city of Isana.'],
  a:[['《隋书》记大业十二年(616 年)真腊遣使入贡,一般系于他在位初年;隋炀帝「礼之甚厚」,此后往来断了','The Book of Sui records the Chenla embassy of 616, generally placed early in his reign; the emperor received it handsomely, and then the exchanges lapsed'],
     ['兼并扶南在他手里收尾,疆域推到湄公河下游;都城伊奢那补罗就是今天的三坡布雷古','The absorption of Funan was finished under him and the realm reached the lower Mekong; his capital Ishanapura is today\'s Sambor Prei Kuk'],
     ['《隋书》记他的都城「郭下二万余家」,又记国王三日一听朝,坐五香七宝床——一座 7 世纪东南亚都城的排场,被中国史官记了下来','The Book of Sui counts over twenty thousand households below the walls, and describes the king holding audience every third day on a couch of five scents and seven jewels — the style of a seventh-century Southeast Asian capital, noted down by Chinese historians']],
  s:['他的名字随都城一起留了下来:考古学界至今用「伊奢那补罗」称呼三坡布雷古的都城遗址。真腊自己的碑铭与中国的史书在他身上对上了号——东南亚早期历史里,能两头都查到的王并不多。','His name survived with his city: archaeologists still call the Sambor Prei Kuk capital Ishanapura. On him, Chenla\'s own inscriptions and the Chinese histories agree — among early Southeast Asian kings, not many can be checked from both ends.'] },

'宗喀巴': { g:'faith', y:[1357,1419], c:'西藏诸政权', n:['宗喀巴','Tsongkhapa'],
  t:['一位改革僧人:他整顿了戒律,身后长出一个教派、两大活佛系统。','A reformer monk: he restored the discipline, and after him grew a school and two great lines of rebirth.'],
  a:[['生在青海湟水一带,「宗喀巴」意思就是「宗喀地方的人」;十六岁入卫藏求学,遍访各派名师','Born by the Huangshui in Qinghai — Tsongkhapa simply means the man from Tsongkha — he went to central Tibet at sixteen and studied under masters of every school'],
     ['他针对的是当时僧团的松弛:重申戒律、重立学制,让僧人从显到密按次第修学;他和弟子都戴黄帽,人称「黄帽派」','What he set himself against was the laxity of the clergy of his day: discipline restated, a curriculum rebuilt, monks to study in ordered stages from open to esoteric teaching; he and his disciples wore yellow hats, and the yellow hat became the name'],
     ['1409 年在拉萨首办传昭大法会,同年建甘丹寺——格鲁派从这一年起步,后来成为藏传佛教最大的教派','In 1409 he held the first Great Prayer Festival at Lhasa and founded Ganden monastery the same year — the Gelug school starts from that year, and grew into the largest in Tibetan Buddhism']],
  s:['他身后,弟子一系发展出达赖与班禅两大转世系统;而他自己的法座走了另一条路——甘丹寺座主「甘丹赤巴」不看出身、不认转世,由考出来的学问僧轮流继承,一任七年,六百年接了近百任。转世的和考上的,两条继承的路都从他门下走出。今天塔尔寺就建在他的出生地。','After him his disciples\' lines grew into the Dalai and Panchen successions; his own throne went another way — the Ganden Tripa, holder of his seat, is neither born nor reincarnated into it but earned by examination, one scholar-monk after another for a seven-year term, nearly a hundred holders across six centuries. Succession by rebirth and succession by merit both walked out of his school. Kumbum monastery stands today on his birthplace.'] },

'阇耶波罗': { g:'king', y:[964,1001], yk:'r', c:'喀布尔沙希', n:['阇耶波罗','Jayapala'],
  t:['联合诸邦对抗加兹尼的老王;战败被俘赎回后,他选择了柴堆。','The old king who led the coalition against Ghazni — beaten, captured and ransomed, he chose the pyre.'],
  a:[['先联合北印诸邦迎战萨布克特勤,后又独力迎战其子马哈茂德——每一仗都败给快进快出的突厥骑兵','He led a coalition of northern kings against Sabuktigin, then faced his son Mahmud with his own forces — beaten each time by cavalry that struck and withdrew'],
     ['1001 年在白沙瓦附近再败被俘,以重金赎回','Beaten and captured again near Peshawar in 1001, he was ransomed at a heavy price'],
     ['他把王冠交给儿子阿难陀波罗,随后自焚——败而被俘的王,按那个时代的规矩不能再戴王冠','He handed the crown to his son Anandapala and gave himself to the fire — a king once taken captive could not, by the rules of that age, wear a crown again']],
  s:['此后每一代沙希王都接着打,每一代都再退一步,直到退无可退。几十年后为这一家写下身后评语的,正是征服者宫廷里的那位学者——他的话,本带的鼎盛段里可以读到。','Each Shahi king after him fought on, and each fell back another step, until there was nowhere left to fall. The man who wrote this house its verdict decades later was the scholar of the conquerors\' own court — his words can be read in this band\'s golden-age panel.'] },

'马哈茂德': { g:'king', y:[998,1030], yk:'r', c:'加兹尼王朝', n:['马哈茂德','Mahmud of Ghazni'],
  t:['三十二年里一再南下印度的苏丹;他抢来的金子,养出了一座文学之都。','The sultan who raided India for thirty-two years — and fed a capital of letters on the gold.'],
  a:[['「苏丹」这个王号在他手里叫响(通常认为他是先例);他一生不称哈里发,反而去巴格达讨来一纸册封','The royal style of sultan rang out with him (commonly held the precedent); he never claimed the caliphate, and fetched a deed of investiture from Baghdad instead'],
     ['南征的次数,旧史算作十七,今人各有各的数;最响的一击落在古吉拉特海边——索姆纳特','The old histories count seventeen expeditions south and modern counts vary; the loudest blow fell on the Gujarat coast, at Somnath'],
     ['他的宫廷把战利品折成了文名:诗人有赏,学者是掳来的,《列王纪》是献来的','His court converted plunder into letters: the poets rewarded, the scholar carried off, the Shahnameh presented']],
  s:['在伊斯兰世界的记忆里他是护教的雄主,在印度的记忆里他是毁庙的劫掠者——同一个人,两份记忆,至今都没有淡。他真正留下的是一个模板:波斯语宫廷加突厥武力,后来统治印度七百年的政权,大都照这个样子搭。','In Islamic memory a champion of the faith, in Indian memory the temple-wrecking raider — one man, two memories, neither faded yet. What he really left was a template: a Persian court on Turkic arms, and most of the powers that ruled India for the next seven hundred years were built to the pattern.'] },

'马武拉': { g:'king', y:[1629,1652], yk:'r', c:'穆塔帕与托尔瓦', n:['马武拉','Mavura'],
  t:['靠葡萄牙人的枪坐上王位的王;坐上去那天,也把国家签了出去。','A king set on the throne by Portuguese guns — and the day he sat down, he signed the kingdom away.'],
  a:[['1629 年,他在葡萄牙人助战下击败争位的卡帕拉里泽登上王位,并受洗为「菲利佩」——受洗的确切年份各家记载不一','In 1629, with Portuguese help in the fight, he beat his rival Kapararidze to the throne and was baptised Filipe — the date of the baptism is variously reported'],
     ['同年签下的条约里:葡萄牙商人与传教士通行免税,金矿对他们开放,斯瓦希里商人被逐出境','The treaty he signed that year gave Portuguese traders and missionaries free passage untaxed, opened the mines to them, and expelled the Swahili merchants'],
     ['此后二十多年他一直在位,名义上仍是「穆韦内·穆塔帕」,实际上王庭的废立常凭葡萄牙人的火枪','He reigned on for over twenty years, still Mwene Mutapa in name; in practice the making and unmaking of kings ran on Portuguese muskets']],
  s:['他成了一个类型的开头:此后两个多世纪,非洲不少王位都要靠欧洲人的承认与军火才坐得稳——先是贸易,再是条约,最后是废立。1629 年那纸条约,常被史家当作这条路最早的完整样本之一。','He was the start of a pattern: for the next two centuries and more, many African thrones would need European recognition and firearms to hold — trade first, then treaty, then the making of kings. Historians often cite the treaty of 1629 as one of the earliest complete specimens of that road.'] },

'设赏迦': { g:'king', y:[600,625], ca:1, yk:'r', c:'早期孟加拉', n:['设赏迦','Shashanka'],
  t:['孟加拉的第一位大王;关于他的记载,全部出自敌人之手。','Bengal\'s first great king — every surviving account of him written by his enemies.'],
  a:[['约 600 年在金耳城称王,在位年代各家考订出入较大;金币上铸着卧牛与湿婆,是孟加拉最早的本地王朝铸币之一','Crowned at Karnasubarna about 600, his dates much debated; his gold coins, stamped with Shiva and the reclining bull, are among Bengal\'s earliest royal issues'],
     ['《戒日王传》说他骗杀了戒日王的哥哥——作者是戒日王的御用文人;另一面的说法,一个字也没有传下来','The Harshacharita says he lured Harsha\'s brother to his death — its author was Harsha\'s court poet, and not one word from the other side survives'],
     ['玄奘几十年后路过,记他砍倒了菩提迦耶的菩提树;这条是转述,又出自敌对阵营,考古上没有印证——但「灭佛者」的形象就此定了型','Xuanzang, passing decades later, records that he cut down the Bodhi tree at Bodh Gaya; the report is second-hand, from the hostile camp, with no archaeological confirmation — but the image of the persecutor stuck']],
  s:['他一死王国就散了,名声却走了两条路:敌人的书里他是奸雄与灭佛者,后世孟加拉史家把他追认为第一位本土大王。两种形象用的其实是同一批史料——史料是谁写的,常常比史料写了什么更要紧。','His kingdom fell apart at his death, but his name went two ways: villain and persecutor in his enemies\' books, first great native king to later Bengali historians. Both portraits rest on the same few sources — and who wrote a source often matters more than what it says.'] },

'贝尼尼': { g:'art', y:[1598,1680], c:'教皇国', n:['贝尼尼','Gian Lorenzo Bernini'],
  t:['先后为八任教皇干活的艺术家;今天的罗马长什么样,有一半是他的主意。','Artist to eight popes in succession; how Rome looks today is half his doing.'],
  a:[['二十多岁就名动罗马:《阿波罗与达芙妮》把「人正在变成月桂树」的一瞬刻进大理石,指尖化作叶子,石头薄得透光','Famous in his twenties: his Apollo and Daphne fixes in marble the instant of a girl turning into a laurel, fingertips becoming leaves, the stone carved thin enough to glow'],
     ['也栽过大跟头:他给圣彼得大教堂加建的钟塔出现裂缝,1646 年教皇下令整座拆掉,声名跌到谷底;几年后他靠四河喷泉翻了身','He also fell hard: cracks appeared in the bell tower he added to St Peter\'s, in 1646 the pope ordered it demolished, and his standing hit bottom — a few years later the Four Rivers fountain won it back'],
     ['1656 年起主持圣彼得广场,他把柱廊设计成环抱的双臂——按他自己的说法,是教会张开手臂迎接世人;工程做了十一年','From 1656 he directed St Peter\'s Square, designing the colonnade as two embracing arms — in his own words, the church reaching out to gather the world in; the work took eleven years']],
  s:['他死后巴洛克退潮,19 世纪的评论家一度看不起他;20 世纪重新翻案,如今常与米开朗基罗并提为雕塑史的高峰。而每天在他的广场上拍照的游客,多数并不知道他的名字——作品比名字有名,对建城的人来说不算坏结局。','After his death the Baroque went out of fashion and nineteenth-century critics looked down on him; the twentieth century reversed the verdict, and he now stands with Michelangelo among the peaks of sculpture. Most of the visitors photographing his square each day do not know his name — the work more famous than the man, which is not a bad ending for a city-builder.'] },

'克罗伊斯': { g:'king', y:[-560,-547], yk:'r', c:'吕底亚', n:['克罗伊斯','Croesus'],
  t:['他问天下谁最幸福,得到的答案当时没听懂——听懂的时候,人在火刑堆上。','He asked who was the happiest of men and did not understand the answer — until he stood on the pyre.'],
  a:[['给以弗所的阿尔忒弥斯神庙捐过整批石柱,其中几件构件刻着他的名字,今天存于大英博物馆','Gave a whole set of columns to the temple of Artemis at Ephesus; several pieces carry his name and are in the British Museum today'],
     ['希罗多德记他问来访的雅典贤人梭伦:你见过比我更幸福的人吗?梭伦答:人没到最后一天,说不上幸福——这段对话的年代其实对不上,后人多当寓言读','Herodotus has him ask the visiting Athenian sage Solon whether he had ever seen a happier man; Solon answered that no man should be called happy before his last day — the chronology does not quite work, and it is mostly read as a parable'],
     ['王国亡后,希罗多德版本的结局是:他在火刑堆上喊出梭伦的名字,居鲁士问明原委,把他放了下来留在身边——另一路古代记载里没有火刑堆','In Herodotus\' version of the end he cried out Solon\'s name on the pyre, and Cyrus, once he heard why, had him taken down and kept him close — other ancient accounts have no pyre at all'],],
  s:['他死后,吕底亚人做了两百年波斯臣民;而他传下的那句话越走越远:命运没有走完,先别急着下结论——此后两千多年,西方人一想到「盛极而衰」,常常就想起他。','After him the Lydians spent two centuries as Persian subjects, while the sentence he passed on travelled further and further: judge no life before it is finished. For two thousand years and more, when the West has thought of fortune overturned, it has often thought of him.'] },

'檀石槐': { g:'king', y:[156,181], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'鲜卑', n:['檀石槐','Tanshihuai'],
  t:['爸爸不肯认的孩子,长大把整片草原捏进了一只手里。','A child his father refused to own grew up to close one hand around the whole steppe.'],
  a:[['《后汉书》记的出身带着传奇色彩:父亲从军三年回来,见家里多了个儿子,不认,弃之;他由外祖家养大,十四五岁单骑追回被抢走的牛羊,部落自此服他','The Book of the Later Han gives him a storybook start: his father came home from three years with the army, found a son he would not own, and cast him out; raised by his mother\'s family, at fourteen or fifteen he rode out alone and took back the clan\'s stolen herds — and the clan followed him from that day'],
     ['东汉遣使送来王印,「封檀石槐为王,欲与和亲」,他不肯受,寇边反而更勤——王号是别人给的,草原是自己打下的','The Han sent envoys with a royal seal, offering to make him a king and bind it with a marriage; he refused, and raided the frontier harder than before — a crown is granted, but a steppe is taken'],
     ['据记载他大约活了四十五岁,在位二十多年——这个年纪放在草原霸主里算短的,而他建起来的东西比他的寿命还短','He is recorded as living to about forty-five, some twenty-five of them in power — a short life for a steppe overlord, and what he built proved shorter still'],],
  s:['草原上后来每一个想把各部拧成一股绳的人,都要面对他留下的那道题:靠威望拢起来的联盟,怎么活过那个有威望的人。一千年后,成吉思汗用千户制和一部叫「大扎撒」的法回答了它。','Every steppe leader who later tried to twist the clans into one rope faced the problem he left behind: how does a confederation held together by prestige outlive the man with the prestige? A thousand years on, Genghis Khan answered it with decimal households and the code called the Great Yasa.'] },

'曹议金': { g:'state', y:[914,935], yk:'r', c:'归义军', n:['曹议金','Cao Yijin'],
  t:['莫高窟有一窟被文书叫作「大王窟」——修窟的这位大王,一辈子没真敢称王。','One Mogao cave is called the Great King\'s Cave in the old documents — and the great king who built it never quite dared be king.'],
  a:[['接掌十年后才等到中原的正式册命:924 年后唐的旌节送到沙州——他的使团为此要穿过回鹘与吐蕃各部的地界,路上时有折损','His formal patent from China came ten years after he took charge: in 924 the insignia of Later Tang reached Shazhou — carried by missions that crossed Uyghur and Tibetan country, and not all of them made it'],
     ['第 98 窟是他的功德窟:两百多身供养人像连排而立,曹家、姻亲与僚属画成一支队伍——一座窟,就是一册画出来的家谱加官册','Cave 98 is his merit cave: over two hundred donor figures stand in ranks — family, in-laws and officers painted as one procession. A cave that is a genealogy and a register of office, done in paint'],
     ['他的回鹘夫人以「天公主」的名号与他并列出现在题记与壁画上——在归义军的文书里,这位夫人有自己的政治身份','His Uyghur wife appears beside him in inscriptions and murals under her own title of Heavenly Princess — in the circuit\'s documents she holds standing of her own'],],
  s:['学界另有一说:曹氏可能出自入华粟特人的后裔(依据是婚姻圈与命名习惯,争议未定)。若真如此,替河西守了一百二十年汉家旗号的,是一个胡商移民家族——放在丝绸之路上,这倒是最合适不过的一个结局。','One school holds that the Cao family may have descended from Sogdian settlers in China (the evidence lies in marriage circles and naming habits; the question is open). If so, the house that kept a Chinese banner over Hexi for a hundred and twenty years was itself a family of immigrant caravan traders — and on the Silk Road no ending could fit better.'] },

'米特里达梯六世': { g:'king', y:[-120,-63], yk:'r', c:'本都王国', n:['米特里达梯六世','Mithridates VI'],
  t:['罗马人打了二十五年才打倒的国王;他每天服毒防毒,最后毒药果真毒不死他。','It took Rome twenty-five years to bring him down; he dosed himself against poison daily, and in the end poison indeed could not kill him.'],
  a:[['据老普林尼记载,他能说二十二种语言,接见治下各族都不用翻译','Pliny records that he spoke twenty-two languages and needed no interpreter with any people he ruled'],
     ['前 88 年那场同日发难出自他的密令;亚细亚各城多数照办了——后世史家常以此说明行省对罗马收税人的怨恨之深','The same-day killings of 88 BC were done on his sealed orders; most cities of Asia complied — long read as a measure of how the province hated Rome\'s tax collectors'],
     ['前 63 年兵败众叛,服毒自尽而毒药无效,请随行军官动手——各家记载版本不一','Defeated and deserted in 63 BC, he took poison and it failed; he asked an officer of his guard to finish it — the accounts differ']],
  s:['解毒方冠着他的名字进了欧洲的药房;连「习惯了就不怕」这层意思,西方语言里也用他的名字来说。在罗马人自己的记忆里,他与汉尼拔并列,是共和国最难缠的对手之一。','The antidote that bears his name entered the pharmacies of Europe, and Western languages still reach for his name to say that what you are used to cannot hurt you. In Rome\'s own memory he stands with Hannibal among the republic\'s most stubborn opponents.'] },

'迈达斯': { g:'king', y:[-738,-696], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'弗里吉亚', n:['迈达斯','Midas'],
  t:['同一个国王留下两份记录:希腊人的神话,和亚述人的泥板——彼此认不出对方笔下的他。',
     'One king, two records: Greek myth and Assyrian clay — neither would recognise the other\'s Midas.'],
  a:[['亚述萨尔贡二世时期的泥板记着一位「穆什基人的米塔」,袭扰亚述东部各省,后来又与亚述缔约——史家一般认为这就是希腊人说的迈达斯。',
      'Tablets from the reign of Sargon II of Assyria record a Mita, king of the Mushki, raiding Assyria\'s eastern provinces and later coming to terms — historians generally take him to be the Midas the Greeks wrote about.'],
     ['希腊人说他在辛梅里安人入侵时喝公牛血自尽,时间约在前 696 年;戈尔迪翁确实烧过一场大火,但发掘方现在把那一层定在更早的约前 800 年、认为是失控的意外——同一层灰,两种读法。',
      'Greek writers say he killed himself by drinking bull\'s blood when the Cimmerians invaded, about 696 BC; Gordion did burn, but the excavators now date that layer earlier, to about 800 BC, and read it as an accident that got out of hand — one layer of ash, two readings.'],
     ['1957 年宾夕法尼亚大学的罗德尼·扬打开戈尔迪翁那座最大的封土墓,里面有木家具、上百件青铜器和铁器时代最好的一批饮酒器皿;墓室的木料测出砍伐于约前 740 年,所以今天学者多认为墓主是迈达斯的父亲,不是他本人。',
      'In 1957 Rodney Young of the University of Pennsylvania opened the great tumulus at Gordion: wooden furniture, over a hundred bronze vessels and the finest set of Iron Age drinking gear ever found. The timbers were cut about 740 BC, so most scholars now think the man buried there was Midas\'s father rather than Midas.']],
  s:['点石成金的故事最有名的版本出自罗马诗人奥维德的《变形记》,已经离他的年代七百多年——一个真实的国王,被传说盖住了。今天到土耳其的戈尔迪翁还能爬上那座封土,墓里的东西在安卡拉的博物馆。',
     'The best-known version of the golden touch is in Ovid\'s Metamorphoses, seven centuries after his time — a real king buried under a story. The mound at Gordion in Turkey can still be climbed, and what was found inside it is in the museum at Ankara.'] },

'伊本·白图泰': { g:'sail', y:[1304,1369], ca:1, c:'摩洛哥诸王朝', n:['伊本·白图泰','Ibn Battuta'],
  t:['二十一岁出门去麦加朝觐,回来时已经过了近三十年,走过的路比同时代任何人都长。',
     'He left at twenty-one to make the pilgrimage to Mecca and came home nearly thirty years later, having travelled farther than anyone else of his day.'],
  a:[['他是丹吉尔的法官世家出身,1325 年独自骑一头驴上路。此后走遍北非、阿拉伯、东非、小亚细亚、金帐汗国、印度、马尔代夫、锡兰、东南亚,据他自述还到过中国;学者估算行程约十一万七千公里。',
      'He came of a family of judges in Tangier and set out alone in 1325 on a donkey. He went on through North Africa, Arabia, East Africa, Anatolia, the Golden Horde, India, the Maldives, Ceylon and South-East Asia, and by his own account China; the distance is reckoned at some 117,000 km.'],
     ['他不是游客:凭伊斯兰法学的学历,他在德里苏丹国当了几年法官,又在马尔代夫做过法官,还被派往中国出使——中途遇海难和叛乱,任务没完成。',
      'He did not travel as a tourist: his training in Islamic law got him years as a judge at the Delhi sultanate and again in the Maldives, and an appointment as envoy to China — a mission wrecked by shipwreck and revolt.'],
     ['1354 年回到摩洛哥,马林王朝的苏丹派书记伊本·朱扎伊记录他的口述,1355 年成书《游记》(Rihla)。书里有些段落被后世学者怀疑是抄别人的或记错了,尤其中国那一段。',
      'He got back to Morocco in 1354, and the Marinid sultan set a secretary, Ibn Juzayy, to take down his account; the Rihla was finished in 1355. Some passages are doubted by later scholars as borrowed or misremembered, the China part especially.']],
  s:['《游记》是了解 14 世纪伊斯兰世界最重要的一份材料:泉州的港口、基尔瓦的珊瑚石城、霍尔木兹的过路税、马里的宫廷,都由他记下来——站里好几座城的段落用的就是他的记述。他走得比马可·波罗远,而他从来不是「探险」:整个伊斯兰世界对他来说是一片可以凭同一套法律、同一门语言通行的地方。',
     'The Rihla is the single most important source for the fourteenth-century Islamic world: the port of Quanzhou, the coral city of Kilwa, the tolls of Hormuz, the court of Mali all come down through him, and several city entries on this site rest on his account. He went farther than Marco Polo — and never as an explorer: the whole Islamic world was, to him, a place he could cross on one law and one language.'] },

'穆莱·伊斯玛仪': { g:'king', y:[1672,1727], yk:'r', c:'摩洛哥诸王朝', n:['穆莱·伊斯玛仪','Moulay Ismail'],
  t:['在位五十五年,把一座小城改建成自己的都城,城墙里圈的地方比凡尔赛还大。',
     'Fifty-five years on the throne, and he rebuilt a small town into his own capital, walling in more ground than Versailles.'],
  a:[['他是阿拉维王朝的第二代君主,1672 年即位,靠一支叫「布哈里黑军」的常备军统一全国——这支部队由黑人奴隶及其后代组成,世代当兵,不属于任何部落,因此只忠于苏丹。',
      'The second ruler of the Alaouite dynasty, he came to the throne in 1672 and united the country with a standing army, the Black Guard — men of slave descent who served from father to son, belonging to no tribe and so loyal only to the sultan.'],
     ['他把梅克内斯建成都城:宫殿、城墙、粮仓与马厩连成一大片,直到今天还叫「摩洛哥的凡尔赛」,1996 年列入世界遗产。',
      'He made Meknes his capital: palaces, walls, granaries and stables running on and on — still called the Versailles of Morocco, and a World Heritage site since 1996.'],
     ['1684 年英国人撤出丹吉尔、他随即进城,1689 年又从西班牙人手里打下拉腊什,又与路易十四通信往来、互派使节;有个流传很广的说法是他向法国求娶一位公主,被婉拒。',
      'The English pulled out of Tangier in 1684 and he moved in, and in 1689 he took Larache from the Spanish; and exchanged letters and embassies with Louis XIV; a much-repeated story has him asking for a French princess and being politely refused.']],
  s:['他在位期间摩洛哥没有被并入奥斯曼帝国,也顶住了欧洲人在沿海的据点——马格里布唯一保持独立的一块。他的名声两面:一面是把国家从内战里拉出来的强君,一面是以残暴著称;关于他子女数以百计的记载常被引用,但那些数字出自当时欧洲人的记述,可靠程度有限。他建立的阿拉维王朝统治摩洛哥至今。',
     'Under him Morocco stayed out of the Ottoman empire and pushed the Europeans off its coastal footholds — the one part of the Maghreb to keep its independence. His reputation runs both ways: the strong ruler who pulled the country out of civil war, and a byword for cruelty. The often-quoted figures for his hundreds of children come from European accounts of the time and are hard to verify. The dynasty he built still rules Morocco.'] },

'马克图姆·本·布蒂': { g:'state', y:[1833,1852], yk:'r', c:'海湾诸邦', n:['马克图姆·本·布蒂','Maktoum bin Butti'],
  t:['1833 年他带着一族人离开阿布扎比,在一条海湾边住下——那条海湾今天叫迪拜河。',
     'In 1833 he led his people away from Abu Dhabi and settled on a creek — the creek is now Dubai.'],
  a:[['他是巴尼亚斯部落联盟里布法拉萨一支的首领。阿布扎比发生政变、原酋长被废之后,这一支不认新酋长,1833 年采珠季由他与欧拜德·本·赛义德一同带着族人出走,迁到迪拜河口的辛达加一带;当年秋天,留下的亲族大批跟了过去。两人共同统治迪拜,1836 年欧拜德去世后由他独掌。',
      'He led the Al Bu Falasah section of the Bani Yas. After a coup at Abu Dhabi deposed its sheikh, his people would not accept the new one, and in the pearling season of 1833 he and Obeid bin Said led them out, to Shindagha at the mouth of the Dubai creek; that autumn the bulk of their relatives followed. The two ruled Dubai together until Obeid died in 1836, after which he held it alone.'],
     ['他统治迪拜到 1852 年。当时的迪拜只是辛达加一带二百多户人家的港口,靠采珍珠和转口贸易过活,一年最重要的事是六月到九月的采珠季。',
      'He ruled Dubai until 1852. It was then a port of some two hundred and fifty houses at Shindagha, living on pearling and transhipment, its year turning on the diving season from June to September.'],
     ['这一带的小邦当时都已与英国签有海上休战条约,英国管海上、不管岸上——「休战诸国」这个名字就是这么来的,直到 1971 年才合成阿拉伯联合酋长国。',
      'The small states along this coast had by then signed maritime truces with Britain, which policed the sea and left the shore alone — hence the name Trucial States, until they became the United Arab Emirates in 1971.']],
  s:['他这一支就是马克图姆家族,统治迪拜至今。19 世纪末到 20 世纪初迪拜两次免税,吸引波斯与印度商人迁来,才慢慢超过邻近的港口;石油要到 1966 年才发现,而迪拜的石油一直不多——今天这座城靠的是转口、航空与地产,与他那时靠的转口贸易,其实是同一条思路。',
     'His line is the Al Maktoum family, which rules Dubai still. Around the turn of the twentieth century Dubai twice lifted its customs duties and drew Persian and Indian merchants away from neighbouring ports, and only then began to outgrow them; oil was not found until 1966 and there was never much of it — the city today lives on transhipment, aviation and property, which is the same idea he started with.'] },

'达延汗': { g:'king', y:[1474,1517], ca:1, c:'北元·蒙古诸部', n:['达延汗','Dayan Khan'],
  t:['他即位那年才几岁,几十年后才真正把散掉的蒙古各部重新拢到一起。',
     'He was a small boy when he was raised up as khan; the reuniting of the Mongols took him decades more.'],
  a:[['元朝退回草原之后,大汗的位子长期被权臣与瓦剌把持。他是忽必烈一系的后裔,幼年由夫人满都海哈屯扶立并摄政——满都海本人带兵出征,是这段历史里绕不开的人物。',
      'After the Yuan withdrew to the steppe, the khanship was long in the hands of powerful ministers and of the Oirats. A descendant of Kublai\'s line, he was raised up as a child by his wife Mandukhai Khatun, who ruled for him and led armies herself — she is impossible to leave out of this story.'],
     ['他用了几十年打服右翼各部,一般认为到 1510 年前后才真正统一漠南漠北,把蒙古重新编为左右两翼共六个万户,分给自己的儿子们。',
      'It took him decades to bring the right-wing tribes to heel; the reunification is usually put around 1510. He then reorganised the Mongols into six tümens in two wings and gave them to his sons.'],
     ['他的生卒与在位年份史料出入很大,不同来源相差十几年;明朝史书叫他「小王子」。',
      'His dates are badly disputed — sources differ by more than a decade — and the Ming histories call him simply the Little Prince.']],
  s:['这次重编决定了此后几百年蒙古的样子:六个万户成了后来各部的祖源,俺答汗、林丹汗都出自他的子孙。清朝把蒙古编为盟旗时,依据的仍是这套分封留下的部落格局。他没有恢复元朝,但让「大汗」这个位子重新有了实际内容——直到 1634 年林丹汗死在青海路上为止。',
     'That reorganisation set the shape of Mongolia for centuries: the six tümens became the ancestors of the later tribes, and both Altan Khan and Ligdan Khan descend from him. When the Qing later organised Mongolia into leagues and banners, the tribal map they worked from was still his. He did not restore the Yuan, but he made the title of khan mean something again — until Ligdan Khan died on the road in Qinghai in 1634.'] },

'俺答汗': { g:'king', y:[1508,1582], c:'北元·蒙古诸部', n:['俺答汗','Altan Khan'],
  t:['他抢了明朝二十多年,最后换来一纸和议:长城沿线开市,用马换茶和布。',
     'He raided the Ming for twenty years and ended by making a deal: markets along the Great Wall, horses for tea and cloth.'],
  a:[['他是达延汗的孙子,统领右翼土默特部。1550 年他一路打到北京城下,焚掠城郊三日而退,明军闭门不战,史称「庚戌之变」——蒙古人要的其实是通商。',
      'A grandson of Dayan Khan, he led the Tümed of the right wing. In 1550 he rode to the walls of Beijing, stayed three days and withdrew — what the Mongols actually wanted was trade.'],
     ['1571 年双方达成隆庆和议:明朝封他为顺义王,在长城沿线开设马市,边境安静了几十年。他在今呼和浩特一带筑城,明朝赐名「归化」。',
      'In 1571 the two sides came to terms: the Ming made him Prince Shunyi and opened horse markets along the Wall, and the frontier was quiet for decades. He built a city at what is now Hohhot, which the Ming named Guihua.'],
     ['1578 年他在青海会见西藏格鲁派的索南嘉措,给了他「达赖喇嘛」这个称号——索南嘉措被追认为三世,这个称号一直用到今天;蒙古人也从此大批改信藏传佛教。',
      'In 1578 he met the Tibetan lama Sönam Gyatso in Qinghai and gave him the title Dalai Lama — Sönam Gyatso is counted the third, and the title has been used ever since; from then on the Mongols turned in large numbers to Tibetan Buddhism.']],
  s:['他做的两件事都比打仗影响远:开市让长城从战场变回一条边界,几十年不打仗;给达赖喇嘛的称号则把蒙古与西藏绑在了一起——后来卫拉特蒙古入藏、清朝介入西藏事务,线索都能追到这里。呼和浩特今天还有他建的大召寺。',
     'Both the things he did outlasted his wars: the markets turned the Great Wall from a battlefield back into a border for decades, and the title he gave tied Mongolia to Tibet — the later Oirat interventions in Tibet, and the Qing\'s own involvement there, all trace back through this. The Da Zhao temple he built still stands in Hohhot.'] },

'林丹汗': { g:'king', y:[1592,1634], r:[1604,1634], c:'北元·蒙古诸部', n:['林丹汗','Ligdan Khan'],
  t:['最后一位蒙古大汗。他想把各部重新收回手里,结果把他们推到了后金那一边。',
     'The last Mongol great khan. He set out to bring the tribes back under his hand, and drove them to the Manchus instead.'],
  a:[['他是达延汗的后裔、察哈尔部之主,1604 年即大汗位时十三岁,名义上是全蒙古的共主,实际只管得住察哈尔。',
      'A descendant of Dayan Khan and lord of the Chakhar, he became great khan in 1604 at thirteen — nominally overlord of all the Mongols, in practice master only of his own tribe.'],
     ['他用武力压服其他各部,反而使科尔沁、喀喇沁等部转投正在兴起的后金;皇太极几次西征,1632 年他被迫西走。',
      'He tried to force the other tribes into line, and pushed the Khorchin and Kharchin over to the rising Manchu state instead; after several campaigns by Hong Taiji he was driven west in 1632.'],
     ['1634 年他病死在甘肃的大草滩,一般记为出痘。次年他的儿子额哲降后金,献出据说是元朝传下来的传国玉玺;皇太极随即于 1636 年改国号为大清。',
      'He died in 1634 on the Dalan Tala steppe in Gansu, of smallpox by most accounts. The next year his son Ejei submitted and handed over a seal said to have come down from the Yuan; Hong Taiji proclaimed the Great Qing in 1636.']],
  s:['他一死,成吉思汗直系的大汗位就此终结,蒙古各部先后编入清朝的盟旗体系。他做过一件与打仗无关的事:主持把藏文《甘珠尔》译成蒙古文,这部译经至今是蒙古文佛教典籍的基础。史书对他多是负面评价,但他面对的局面——各部离心、后金崛起、白灾频仍——换谁都难。',
     'With his death the line of great khans descended from Genghis came to an end, and the Mongol tribes were absorbed one after another into the Qing system of leagues and banners. He did one thing that had nothing to do with war: he had the Tibetan Kanjur translated into Mongolian, and that translation is still the foundation of Mongolian Buddhist literature. The histories treat him harshly, though the hand he was dealt — tribes pulling away, the Manchus rising, winter disasters — would have been hard for anyone.'] },

'秃黑鲁帖木儿': { g:'king', y:[1329,1363], ca:1, c:'东察合台·叶尔羌', n:['秃黑鲁帖木儿','Tughlugh Timur'],
  t:['他改信伊斯兰教,据说还带着十六万部众一起改——天山南北的信仰格局从这里转弯。',
     'He became a Muslim, and by tradition brought a hundred and sixty thousand of his people with him — the turn that set the faith of this region.'],
  a:[['1348 年他被蒙古贵族拥立为汗,察合台汗国从此分成东西两半,东边这一半后世称为「蒙兀儿斯坦」。',
      'In 1348 the Mongol nobles raised him up as khan, and the Chagatai realm split into two halves; the eastern half came to be called Moghulistan.'],
     ['他是东察合台第一位皈依伊斯兰教的汗,传统记载说他 1354 年前后受教于谢赫,并带动大批部众改信。',
      'He was the first khan of the eastern Chagatai line to embrace Islam; tradition puts his conversion around 1354 at the hands of a sheikh, with great numbers of his people following.'],
     ['1360—1361 年他两次西征河中,一度占领撒马尔罕——年轻的帖木儿当时正是在他手下起家的。',
      'In 1360–61 he twice campaigned west into Transoxiana and briefly held Samarkand — and it was in his service that the young Timur got his start.']],
  s:['他的陵墓在今新疆霍城,砖砌穹顶、外贴蓝色琉璃砖,是新疆现存最早的伊斯兰建筑之一。他这一支的后裔在天山南北当了三百五十多年的汗,到 1705 年才断;而他手下起家的帖木儿,后来建起了横跨中亚的帝国。这段历史今天几乎全靠一本书传下来——1546 年米尔咱·海答儿流亡克什米尔时写的《拉失德史》。',
     'His tomb at Huocheng in Xinjiang, a brick dome faced with blue glazed tile, is among the oldest Islamic buildings in the region. His line ruled here for over three hundred and fifty years, ending in 1705; and Timur, who began in his service, went on to build an empire across Central Asia. Nearly all of this history comes down through one book — the Tarikh-i-Rashidi, written in 1546 by Mirza Haidar in exile in Kashmir.'] },

'赛义德汗': { g:'king', y:[1487,1533], r:[1514,1533], c:'东察合台·叶尔羌', n:['赛义德汗','Sultan Said Khan'],
  t:['他 1514 年在叶尔羌立国,这个汗国管着塔里木盆地一圈绿洲,一直到 1705 年。',
     'In 1514 he founded a khanate at Yarkand that held the ring of oases round the Tarim basin until 1705.'],
  a:[['他是东察合台汗室的后裔,早年颠沛流离,投奔过表兄巴布尔(后来莫卧儿帝国的开国者),1514 年击败当地统治者,以叶尔羌(今新疆莎车)为都建国。',
      'A prince of the eastern Chagatai house, he spent his early years a fugitive and took refuge for a time with his cousin Babur, the future founder of the Mughal empire; in 1514 he beat the local ruler and set up his state with its capital at Yarkand, today\'s Shache in Xinjiang.'],
     ['汗国治下有喀什噶尔、和田、阿克苏、库车等绿洲城市,靠丝路商道与绿洲农业为生,是塔里木盆地最后一个由成吉思汗后裔统治的政权。',
      'The khanate held Kashgar, Khotan, Aksu and Kucha, living by the Silk Road and by oasis farming — the last state in the Tarim basin ruled by descendants of Genghis Khan.'],
     ['1532—1533 年他远征西藏西部的拉达克与克什米尔,回程翻越高原时死于高原反应。',
      'In 1532–33 he campaigned into Ladakh and Kashmir, and died of altitude sickness on the way back across the plateau.']],
  s:['他的表弟米尔咱·海答儿是这次远征的将领,后来流亡克什米尔时写下《拉失德史》——这三百年的历史几乎全靠这一本书。叶尔羌汗国的宫廷养出了十二木卡姆这套维吾尔古典音乐的雏形——相传是他儿子拉失德汗一朝的王妃阿曼尼莎汗整理成集的,不过提到她名字的文献要晚到 1854 年;今天喀什与莎车的木卡姆,源头就在这里。',
     'His cousin Mirza Haidar commanded on that campaign and later, exiled in Kashmir, wrote the Tarikh-i-Rashidi — nearly all we know of these three centuries. The court at Yarkand nurtured the beginnings of the Twelve Muqam, the classical music of the Uyghurs, said to have been gathered by Amannisa Khan, consort of his son Rashid Khan — though the text that names her is three centuries later, from 1854. The muqam heard today in Kashgar and Shache begins here.'] },

'苏赫巴托尔': { g:'state', y:[1893,1923], c:'蒙古国', n:['苏赫巴托尔','Damdin Sükhbaatar'],
  t:['他三十岁就死了,而首都的中心广场、纸币和一座省份都以他命名。',
     'He died at thirty, and the capital\'s central square, the banknotes and a whole province carry his name.'],
  a:[['他出身贫苦,当过博克多汗政权机枪连的排长。1919 年中国北洋政府出兵取消外蒙古自治,次年他与乔巴山等人组织人民党,赴俄求援。',
      'Born poor, he was a platoon leader in a machine-gun company of the Bogd Khan\'s army. After Chinese troops ended Outer Mongolia\'s autonomy in 1919, he and Choibalsan organised the People\'s Party and went to Russia for help.'],
     ['1921 年 3 月他率部攻下中蒙边境的买卖城(恰克图),7 月在苏俄红军配合下进入库伦(今乌兰巴托),建立人民政府,博克多汗留任为虚位君主。',
      'In March 1921 he took the border town of Maimaicheng (Kyakhta), and in July, with Soviet Red Army support, entered Urga — today Ulaanbaatar — and set up a people\'s government, with the Bogd Khan left on as a figurehead.'],
     ['1923 年 2 月他突然病死,年仅三十。死因至今有争议,后来的官方叙述曾指为被人下毒。',
      'He died suddenly in February 1923, aged thirty. The cause is still argued over; later official accounts claimed he had been poisoned.']],
  s:['1924 年博克多汗去世后蒙古人民共和国成立,是世界上第二个共产党执政的国家。苏赫巴托尔被塑造成建国者,乌兰巴托的中心广场以他命名(2013 年一度改名成吉思汗广场,2016 年改回)。他没有活到看见后来的事:1930 年代的大清洗毁掉了几乎所有寺院,数万人被处决;1990 年蒙古和平转向多党制。',
     'The Mongolian People\'s Republic was proclaimed in 1924 after the Bogd Khan\'s death — the second communist-ruled state in the world. Sükhbaatar was made its founding figure, and the main square in Ulaanbaatar bears his name (renamed Chinggis Khaan Square in 2013, changed back in 2016). He did not live to see what followed: the purges of the 1930s destroyed almost every monastery and executed tens of thousands, and in 1990 Mongolia turned peacefully to multi-party politics.'] },

'艾哈迈德·沙·杜兰尼': { g:'king', y:[1722,1772], ca:1, r:[1747,1772], c:'阿富汗', n:['艾哈迈德·沙·杜兰尼','Ahmad Shah Durrani'],
  t:['一场部落长老会开了几天,选了这个二十来岁的军官当王——阿富汗这个国家从那次会议算起。',
     'A council of tribal elders sat for days and chose this young officer as king — Afghanistan counts itself from that meeting.'],
  a:[['他本是波斯君主纳迪尔沙的近卫军官。1747 年纳迪尔沙遇刺后,普什图各部在坎大哈开长老会议(支尔格),推举他为王,称杜兰尼。',
      'He had been an officer in the guard of Nadir Shah of Persia. When Nadir Shah was murdered in 1747, the Pashtun tribes met in council — a jirga — at Kandahar and chose him as their king, with the title Durrani.'],
     ['他向东多次用兵,1761 年在帕尼帕特大破马拉塔联军,那是 18 世纪规模最大的会战之一,马拉塔人的北进就此止步。',
      'He campaigned east again and again, and in 1761 at Panipat shattered the Maratha army — one of the largest battles of the eighteenth century, and the end of the Maratha advance north.'],
     ['他把德里、克什米尔、信德、旁遮普一度纳入版图,但从不长驻:打完仗带着战利品回坎大哈,把地方交给当地人管。',
      'Delhi, Kashmir, Sind and the Punjab all came under him at one time or another, but he never stayed: he fought, took the plunder back to Kandahar, and left the locals to run things.']],
  s:['他建立的杜兰尼王朝统治阿富汗一百多年,今天阿富汗人称他「阿赫马德·沙·巴巴」(父亲)。他打赢帕尼帕特却没能坐收其利:马拉塔垮了,填补空缺的是英国东印度公司——1757 年普拉西之战后,南亚的赢家已经换了人。他的陵墓在坎大哈,是那座城的地标。',
     'The Durrani dynasty he founded ruled Afghanistan for over a century, and Afghans call him Ahmad Shah Baba, the father. He won at Panipat but did not collect the winnings: the Marathas fell, and what filled the gap was the East India Company — after Plassey in 1757 the winner in South Asia was already someone else. His tomb in Kandahar is a landmark of the city.'] },

'普沙密多罗·巽伽': { g:'king', y:[-185,-149], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'巽伽与恒河诸国', n:['普沙密多罗·巽伽','Pushyamitra Shunga'],
  t:['他本是孔雀王朝的将领,在阅兵时杀了自己的国王,印度第一个大帝国就此结束。',
     'He was a Mauryan general who killed his own king at a parade, and with that India\'s first great empire ended.'],
  a:[['前 185 年前后,他在检阅军队时杀掉孔雀王朝末代君主巨车王(Brihadratha),自立为王,建巽伽王朝。',
      'Around 185 BC he killed Brihadratha, the last Mauryan king, while reviewing the army, and made himself king, founding the Shunga dynasty.'],
     ['他守住的只是恒河中游一带,远小于孔雀王朝;北面要对付印度-希腊人的南下,西面有德干的百乘。他举行了古老的马祭(阿湿婆弥陀),这是在宣告自己是名正言顺的王。',
      'What he held was the middle Ganges and no more, a fraction of the Mauryan realm; he had the Indo-Greeks pressing from the north-west and the Satavahanas in the Deccan. He performed the ancient horse sacrifice — a way of announcing that he was a king by right.'],
     ['佛教文献说他大规模迫害佛教徒、毁坏佛塔;但同一时期桑奇大塔正在扩建,巴尔胡特的石栏楯也是巽伽时期立的,所以现代学者多认为那些记载有夸大。',
      'Buddhist texts accuse him of persecuting Buddhists and destroying stupas; but the Great Stupa at Sanchi was being enlarged in these same years and the Bharhut railing is Shunga work, so most modern scholars think the accusations are overdrawn.']],
  s:['巽伽王朝传了十代、约一百一十年,末代君主被大臣所杀,取而代之的甘婆王朝更短。他本人留下的实物证据极少:没有他的钱币,只有巴尔胡特石栏楯上一段自记「巽伽王治下」的题记,和《往世书》里的一份王表。他的名字之所以还被记得,一半是因为他终结了孔雀王朝,一半是因为那些指控他的佛教文献。',
     'The Shunga line ran ten kings and about a hundred and ten years, until the last was killed by a minister and the shorter-lived Kanvas took over. Of the man himself very little physical evidence survives: no coins of his, only an inscription on the Bharhut railing that dates itself to the reign of the Shungas, and a king-list in the Puranas. He is remembered half for ending the Mauryas, and half because of the Buddhist texts that accuse him.'] },

'帕坦伽利': { g:'mind', y:[-150,-100], yk:'a', ca:1, c:'巽伽与恒河诸国', n:['帕坦伽利','Patanjali'],
  t:['他给一部四百年前的语法书写了注解,把梵语的规则变成了此后两千年不许乱改的标准。',
     'He wrote a commentary on a grammar four centuries old, and turned the rules of Sanskrit into a standard no one was to alter for two thousand years.'],
  a:[['他的《大疏》(Mahābhāṣya)是为波你尼《八章书》所作的注,逐条讨论前人对波你尼的解释哪些站得住——梵语语法学的三大家(波你尼、迦旃延、帕坦伽利)以他收尾。',
      'His Mahābhāṣya is a commentary on Panini\'s Ashtadhyayi, going rule by rule through earlier interpretations and testing which hold up; of the three great names in Sanskrit grammar — Panini, Katyayana, Patanjali — he is the last.'],
     ['他写作时用来举例的句子,顺便留下了那个时代的实况:书里提到「刚才希腊人围了萨凯塔」,史家用它来给印度-希腊人的东进定年。',
      'The sentences he made up as examples happen to record his own times: one of them says the Greeks were besieging Saketa, and historians use it to date the Indo-Greek advance eastwards.'],
     ['传统把《瑜伽经》也算作他写的,但那部书的年代一般定在公元 2 至 4 世纪,与语法家相差三四百年;现代学者多认为是两个人,11 世纪以前也没有哪部书把两人算作一个。',
      'Tradition also credits him with the Yoga Sutras, but that work is usually dated to the second to fourth centuries AD, three or four hundred years after the grammarian; most modern scholars take them for two different men, and no text before the eleventh century treats them as one.']],
  s:['波你尼把梵语的规则写成约四千条,帕坦伽利的注解则把这套规则钉死:此后梵语基本不再变化,成了一门「标准语」——这也是为什么两千年前的梵语文本今天还能一字不差地读。至于《瑜伽经》那一百九十来条格言,今天全世界练瑜伽的人多少都听过它的开头,而它跟这位语法家是不是同一个人,还没有定论。',
     'Panini set out the rules of Sanskrit in some four thousand aphorisms; Patanjali\'s commentary nailed them down. Sanskrit hardly changed afterwards — it became a standard language, which is why texts two thousand years old can still be read word for word today. As for the hundred and ninety-odd aphorisms of the Yoga Sutras, anyone who practises yoga has heard their opening; whether their author is this grammarian is still unsettled.'] },

'米南德一世': { g:'king', y:[-165,-130], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'印度-希腊诸王', n:['米南德一世','Menander I (Milinda)'],
  t:['一位希腊国王和一位佛教僧人辩论了一整部书——这本书今天还是南传佛教的必读。',
     'A Greek king and a Buddhist monk argue their way through an entire book — and that book is still read in Theravada monasteries today.'],
  a:[['他是印度-希腊诸王里版图最大、留下钱币最多的一位,都城在舍羯罗(今巴基斯坦锡亚尔科特),势力一度东进到恒河流域。',
      'He held the largest realm and left the most coins of any Indo-Greek king, with his capital at Sagala, today Sialkot in Pakistan, and campaigns that reached east into the Ganges valley.'],
     ['巴利文经典《弥兰陀王问经》(Milindapañha)记他与僧人那先(Nagasena)的问答:什么是「我」、车拆开之后车在哪里、人死后什么在轮回——最后国王皈依。',
      'The Pali text Milindapañha records his questions to the monk Nagasena: what is the self, where is the chariot once you take it apart, what is reborn when a man dies — and at the end the king takes refuge in the Buddha.'],
     ['他的钱币一面是希腊文与他的头像,另一面是佉卢文与法轮;古希腊作家普鲁塔克说他死后各城争抢他的骨灰,最后分掉——这个说法与佛陀舍利八分的故事一模一样。',
      'His coins carry Greek and his own portrait on one side, Kharoshthi and the wheel of the law on the other; Plutarch writes that when he died the cities quarrelled over his ashes and divided them — the same story told of the Buddha\'s relics.']],
  s:['他是希腊化世界与印度思想真正对上话的那个点:一个用希腊语思考的国王,拿逻辑问题去问一位佛教僧人,而对方用比喻一一化解。此后犍陀罗的佛像带上希腊式的衣褶与面容,那是同一次相遇的另一半。至于他到底皈没皈依,佛教文献说得肯定,希腊罗马那边不置一词。',
     'He is the point where the Hellenistic world and Indian thought actually talked to each other: a king who thought in Greek putting logical questions to a Buddhist monk, and the monk answering each with an image. Afterwards the Buddha figures of Gandhara took on Greek drapery and Greek faces — the other half of the same meeting. Whether he really converted, the Buddhist texts are sure and the Greek and Roman sources say nothing.'] },

'普拉巴瓦蒂古普塔': { g:'state', y:[390,410], yk:'a', ca:1, c:'伐卡塔卡与德干诸国', n:['普拉巴瓦蒂古普塔','Prabhavatigupta'],
  t:['她是笈多王朝的公主,嫁到德干,丈夫早死,她替儿子摄政二十年——用的是娘家的名义。',
     'A Gupta princess married into the Deccan; her husband died young and she governed for her sons for twenty years — in her own family\'s name.'],
  a:[['她是笈多王旃陀罗笈多二世的女儿,嫁给伐卡塔卡王鲁陀罗塞纳二世。丈夫在位仅五年左右去世,两个儿子还小,国政由她一手执掌了约二十年(约 390—410),自己活到 443 年前后。',
      'Daughter of the Gupta king Chandragupta II, she married Rudrasena II of the Vakatakas. He reigned only about five years; with her sons still small she held the government in her own hands for some twenty years, about 390 to 410, and lived on to about 443.'],
     ['她自己颁发铜板敕令——这在当时的印度极少见。敕令里她列的是自己父系笈多家族的世系,而不是夫家的,史家由此看出笈多在德干的影响有多深。',
      'She issued copper-plate charters in her own name, which was very rare in India then. In them she gives her own Gupta ancestry rather than her husband\'s house — from which historians read how deep Gupta influence in the Deccan ran.'],
     ['她信毗湿奴,敕令里自称「至上薄伽梵的信女」;她与娘家的紧密关系,通常被认为帮助笈多王朝在西边对付塞人时稳住了侧翼。',
      'She was a devotee of Vishnu, styling herself in her charters a worshipper of the Lord; and her close tie to her father\'s house is generally thought to have secured the Gupta flank while they fought the Shakas in the west.']],
  s:['古代印度有名字、有政绩、还留下自己文书的女性统治者极少,她是其中最清楚的一个。她的敕令是研究 4—5 世纪德干的一手材料:土地怎么授、村庄怎么免税、王室怎么自称,都写在那些铜板上。她的儿子之后,王朝传到哈里塞纳手里,阿旃陀石窟最精美的那一批洞窟就在那时开凿。',
     'Women rulers of ancient India who are known by name, by what they did, and by documents of their own are very few; she is the clearest of them. Her charters are first-hand material for the fourth- and fifth-century Deccan: how land was granted, which villages were freed from tax, how the royal house styled itself, all set down on copper. After her sons the throne passed to Harishena, in whose reign the finest of the Ajanta caves were cut.'] },

'哈里塞纳': { g:'king', y:[460,477], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'伐卡塔卡与德干诸国', n:['哈里塞纳','Harishena'],
  t:['阿旃陀石窟里最好的那批洞窟,是在他在位的二十来年里凿出来的——然后突然停工。',
     'The finest caves at Ajanta were cut in the twenty-odd years of his reign — and then the work suddenly stopped.'],
  a:[['他是伐卡塔卡王朝最后一位大王,统治德干中部,版图一度从阿拉伯海延伸到孟加拉湾。',
      'The last great king of the Vakatakas, he ruled the central Deccan, and his realm at one point stretched from the Arabian Sea to the Bay of Bengal.'],
     ['阿旃陀的洞窟分两期:第一期在公元前后,第二期就在他这一朝。第 16 窟的题记记着出资人是他的大臣伐罗诃提婆,那位大臣在题记里说他造这座石窟是为了纪念亡弟;隔壁 17 窟出钱的是另一个人,当地的藩王乌彭陀笈多。',
      'Ajanta was cut in two phases: the first around the turn of the era, the second in his reign. The inscription in cave 16 names the donor as his minister Varahadeva, who says he made it in memory of a dead brother; cave 17 next door was paid for by someone else, the local prince Upendragupta.'],
     ['艺术史家沃尔特·斯平克把第二期洞窟的年代压缩到 462—480 年这不到二十年里,并指出许多洞窟半途而废:柱子刻了一半、壁画只上了底色——工程随着王朝崩溃戛然而止。',
      'The art historian Walter Spink compressed the second phase into under twenty years, 462–480, and pointed out how many caves were abandoned in mid-work: pillars half carved, murals only underpainted — the work stopping dead as the dynasty fell.']],
  s:['阿旃陀 1819 年被一队英国军官打猎时偶然发现,当时已被森林盖了一千多年,1983 年列入世界遗产。里面的壁画是印度古代绘画保存最完整的一批——佛本生故事、宫廷、乐舞、外国使节,连人物的手势都清清楚楚。它保存下来的原因恰恰是那次戛然而止:王朝倒了,人走了,洞窟被遗忘,反而没有被后来的人改动。',
     'Ajanta was stumbled on in 1819 by British officers out hunting, after more than a thousand years under forest, and became a World Heritage site in 1983. Its murals are the best-preserved body of ancient Indian painting there is — Jataka stories, courts, music and dance, foreign envoys, down to the gestures of the hands. The reason they survive is precisely that sudden stop: the dynasty fell, the people left, the caves were forgotten — and so no one came along to alter them.'] },

'天爱帝须': { g:'king', y:[-247,-207], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'斯里兰卡诸王国', n:['天爱帝须','Devanampiya Tissa'],
  t:['阿育王派儿子渡海来传法,他在打猎时遇见了这位僧人——斯里兰卡从这一天起是佛教国家。',
     'Ashoka sent his son across the sea to preach; the king met the monk while out hunting — and Sri Lanka has been Buddhist ever since.'],
  a:[['他与孔雀王朝的阿育王互通使节,关系友好。他的在位年代有两套:《大史》的传统纪年作前 307—前 267,盖格尔修订后的年表作前 247—前 207,现在学者多用后者。传说阿育王之子摩哂陀(Mahinda)率僧团到岛上,在弥沙迦山(今米欣特莱)遇见正在打猎的国王,当场问答,国王皈依。',
      'He exchanged envoys with Ashoka of the Mauryas and the two were on good terms. His dates come in two sets: the traditional chronology of the Mahavamsa puts him at 307–267 BC, Geiger\'s revised list at 247–207 BC, and most scholars now use the latter. Tradition has it that Ashoka\'s son Mahinda came with a party of monks and met the king out hunting at Mihintale; they talked there and then, and the king took refuge.'],
     ['他把都城阿努拉德普勒的御园献出建大寺(Mahavihara),此后一千多年这里是南传佛教的中心。',
      'He gave up the royal park at his capital Anuradhapura for the Mahavihara, the Great Monastery, which for over a thousand years was the centre of Theravada Buddhism.'],
     ['摩哂陀的妹妹僧伽蜜多(Sanghamitta)随后带来菩提伽耶那棵菩提树的分枝,种在阿努拉德普勒——今天还活着,是世界上有确切种植年代记载的最老的树。',
      'Mahinda\'s sister Sanghamitta then brought a cutting from the Bodhi tree at Bodh Gaya and planted it at Anuradhapura, where it still lives — the oldest tree in the world with a recorded planting date.']],
  s:['南传佛教后来传遍缅甸、泰国、柬埔寨、老挝,起点是这座岛;而佛经第一次从口传写成文字(公元前 1 世纪,巴利文,写在贝叶上),也是在这里。这段历史记在《大史》(Mahavamsa)里——那是一部从公元 5 世纪起持续编写的编年史,斯里兰卡因此拥有南亚最连贯的一份古代王统记录。',
     'Theravada Buddhism later spread to Burma, Thailand, Cambodia and Laos, and this island is where it started; it is also where the canon was first written down, in Pali on palm leaves, in the first century BC. The story is told in the Mahavamsa, a chronicle kept up from the fifth century AD onward — which gives Sri Lanka the most continuous record of ancient kings in South Asia.'] },

'波罗迦罗摩巴忽一世': { g:'king', y:[1153,1186], yk:'r', c:'斯里兰卡诸王国', n:['波罗迦罗摩巴忽一世','Parakramabahu I'],
  t:['《小史》记他说过一句话:「一滴雨水也不能不为人所用就流进海里。」他照这句话修了一辈子水库。',
     'The chronicle records him saying that not even a little water from the rain should reach the sea without first being made useful to man — and he built to that rule all his reign.'],
  a:[['他统一全岛,定都波隆纳鲁沃。《大史》记他修建、修复了上千座水库与灌溉渠——干旱区的农业靠的就是这套系统。',
      'He united the island and ruled from Polonnaruwa. The Mahavamsa credits him with building or repairing a thousand-odd tanks and channels — the irrigation on which farming in the dry zone depended.'],
     ['其中最大的一座是「波罗迦罗摩海」(Parakrama Samudra):把几座旧水库连成一片,堤坝长十多公里,今天仍在灌溉。',
      'The largest is the Parakrama Samudra, the Sea of Parakrama: several older tanks joined into one sheet of water behind a dam ten-odd kilometres long, and still irrigating today.'],
     ['他也整顿僧团、重修佛寺,并向外用兵——据僧伽罗史书记载他出兵缅甸的蒲甘,又插手南印度朱罗与潘地亚之争;这些远征耗费极大,他一死国家就衰下去。',
      'He also reformed the monastic order and rebuilt temples, and he made war abroad — an expedition to Pagan in Burma, as the Sinhalese chronicles have it, and an intervention in the quarrel between the Cholas and the Pandyas in south India. Those campaigns cost dearly, and the kingdom weakened as soon as he died.']],
  s:['波隆纳鲁沃的遗址今天是世界遗产:石雕的卧佛、砖砌的佛殿、王宫的墙基,和那片仍在用的水库。斯里兰卡古代的水利工程在同时代世界上少有其匹——早在公元前后,这里的工程师就会用一种叫「biso-kotuwa」的闸室控制出水压力。他的国家在他身后没能维持,而水还在流。',
     'The ruins of Polonnaruwa are a World Heritage site: the reclining Buddha cut from rock, brick shrine halls, the footings of the palace — and the reservoir, still in use. Ancient Sri Lanka\'s hydraulics had few equals anywhere: as early as the turn of the era its engineers were using a sluice chamber, the biso-kotuwa, to control the pressure of water let out. The kingdom did not outlast him. The water still runs.'] },

'信修浮': { g:'king', y:[1453,1471], yk:'r', c:'阿瓦·勃固', n:['信修浮','Shin Sawbu'],
  t:['东南亚少有的女性君主:她把自己体重的黄金捐给大金塔,又亲自挑了继承人。',
     'A rare female sovereign in South-East Asia: she gave the great pagoda her own weight in gold, and chose her successor herself.'],
  a:[['她是勃固(汉达瓦底)王室之女,早年曾被送到北方的阿瓦朝廷,后来在两位僧人帮助下逃回南方;1453 年即位为王;1460 年前后她已把日常政务交给达摩悉提。',
      'A daughter of the royal house of Pegu, she was sent north to the court at Ava as a young woman and later escaped south with the help of two monks; she came to the throne in 1453, and by about 1460 had handed the day-to-day government to Dhammazedi.'],
     ['她这一朝是勃固最太平的一段:海港贸易兴盛,与斯里兰卡、南印度往来密切。',
      'Her reign was the most peaceful the kingdom knew: the ports flourished, and there was close traffic with Sri Lanka and south India.'],
     ['她重修仰光的瑞大光大金塔,把塔身加高,并按传统捐出与自己体重相等的黄金贴在塔上;她晚年退位,把王位传给僧人出身的女婿达摩悉提。',
      'She rebuilt the Shwedagon at Rangoon, raising its height, and by tradition gave her own weight in gold to gild it; late in life she abdicated in favour of her son-in-law Dhammazedi, who had been a monk.']],
  s:['瑞大光大金塔今天仍是缅甸最重要的圣地,历代君主捐金贴塔是延续几百年的传统——她这一次最有名。缅甸史上女性掌权极罕见,她与继承人达摩悉提这三十来年,常被称作勃固的黄金时代;此后战乱又起,1555 年勃固被北方的东吁王朝并吞。',
     'The Shwedagon is still the holiest place in Burma, and gilding it with gifts of gold was a tradition kept up by rulers for centuries — hers is the most famous. Women holding power are very rare in Burmese history, and the thirty years of her reign and Dhammazedi\'s are often called Pegu\'s golden age. War came back afterwards, and in 1555 Pegu was swallowed by the Toungoo kingdom to the north.'] },

'达摩悉提': { g:'faith', y:[1471,1492], yk:'r', c:'阿瓦·勃固', n:['达摩悉提','Dhammazedi'],
  t:['他当过和尚,还俗做了国王,然后回过头来整顿僧团——办法是让所有和尚重新受一次戒。',
     'He had been a monk, left the robe to be king, and then set about reforming the order — by having every monk ordained all over again.'],
  a:[['他本是僧人,做过信修浮的老师,还俗后娶其女,1471 年继位。',
      'He was a monk and had been Shin Sawbu\'s teacher; he left the order, married her daughter, and succeeded her in 1471.'],
     ['他派使团到斯里兰卡,在凯拉尼亚依大寺一系的戒统受戒,回国后要求全国僧人一律依这一派重新受戒,统一了教团——此事刻在勃固的《甘露戒坛碑》(Kalyani inscriptions)上,碑今天还在。',
      'He sent a mission to Sri Lanka, ordained at Kelaniya in the lineage of the Mahavihara, and on its return required every monk in the country to be re-ordained in that line, unifying the order. The whole affair is cut into the Kalyani inscriptions at Pegu, which still stand.'],
     ['他与阿拉伯、印度、马六甲通商,以善于用外交而非战争解决争端著称。他还铸过一口巨钟捐给大金塔,1608 年葡萄牙人德布里托想把它运走,钟沉入河中至今没找到。',
      'He traded with the Arabs, India and Malacca, and was known for settling quarrels by diplomacy rather than war. He also cast a huge bell for the Shwedagon; in 1608 the Portuguese adventurer de Brito tried to carry it off, and it sank in the river, where it has never been found.']],
  s:['他这次僧团改革影响远超缅甸:此后缅甸、泰国的僧团都以斯里兰卡大寺一系为正统,一直到今天。他与信修浮这三十年是勃固最好的时候——一个航海贸易的王国,靠戒律和外交而不是打仗立足。那口沉在仰光河底的钟,几百年来被找过许多次,至今仍是缅甸最有名的一桩悬案。',
     'His reform of the order mattered far beyond Burma: the monastic lineages of Burma and Thailand have traced themselves to that Sri Lankan line ever since. The thirty years of his reign and Shin Sawbu\'s were Pegu at its best — a seafaring trading kingdom that held its place by discipline and diplomacy rather than war. The bell at the bottom of the Rangoon river has been searched for many times over the centuries, and remains Burma\'s best-known unsolved mystery.'] },

'金日成': { g:'state', y:[1912,1994], c:'朝鲜', n:['金日成','Kim Il Sung'],
  t:['他从抗日游击队出身,建立了朝鲜民主主义人民共和国,掌权四十六年。',
     'He came out of the anti-Japanese guerrilla movement, founded the Democratic People\'s Republic of Korea and held power for forty-six years.'],
  a:[['他生于平壤附近,1930 年代在中国东北参加抗日武装,1940 年前后转入苏联境内接受整编,1945 年日本投降后随苏军回到朝鲜。',
      'Born near Pyongyang, he fought with anti-Japanese partisans in north-east China in the 1930s, crossed into Soviet territory around 1940 and was reorganised into a Soviet unit, and returned to Korea with the Soviet army after Japan surrendered in 1945.'],
     ['1948 年朝鲜民主主义人民共和国成立,他任内阁首相;1950 年 6 月北方军队越过三八线南下,战争打了三年,他此后重建国家,1960 年代北方的工业与人均产值一度高于南方。',
      'The DPRK was established in 1948 with him as premier; in June 1950 the northern army crossed the parallel and the war ran three years, after which he rebuilt the country, and in the 1960s the North\'s industry and output per head were for a time ahead of the South\'s.'],
     ['他提出「主体思想」作为国家的指导思想,强调一切自主自立;国家后来的种种安排,都从这套思想出发。1994 年去世后由儿子金正日继任,2011 年再传金正恩。',
      'He put forward Juche, the doctrine of self-reliance in all things, as the state ideology; everything the state later arranged was built on it. On his death in 1994 his son Kim Jong Il succeeded him, and in 2011 Kim Jong Un.']],
  s:['朝鲜宪法称他为「共和国永远的主席」,国家纪年以他出生的 1912 年为主体元年。1970 年代后经济停滞,1991 年苏联解体后援助断绝,加上连年水旱,1990 年代中期发生饥荒,估计死亡数十万人。半岛至今没有和平条约,只有 1953 年的停战协定;南北的经济差距是今天世界上最大的之一。',
     'The DPRK constitution calls him the eternal president, and the state calendar counts from 1912, the year of his birth, as year one. The economy stalled after the 1970s; when Soviet aid ended with the collapse of the USSR in 1991, and floods and drought followed, famine in the mid-1990s is estimated to have killed hundreds of thousands. The peninsula still has no peace treaty, only the armistice of 1953, and the gap between the two Koreas is among the widest in the world today.'] },

'拉利贝拉': { g:'faith', y:[1181,1221], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'扎格维王朝', n:['拉利贝拉','Lalibela'],
  t:['耶路撒冷去不了了,他就在自己的都城里凿了一座——从整块岩石上向下挖出来的。',
     'Jerusalem was out of reach, so he cut one at home — carved downwards out of solid rock.'],
  a:[['他在位大约 1181 到 1221 年,正是萨拉丁 1187 年夺回耶路撒冷、基督徒朝圣路被切断之后。',
      'He reigned about 1181 to 1221, in the years after Saladin retook Jerusalem in 1187 and the pilgrim road was cut.'],
     ['他在都城罗哈从整块红色火山岩里向下凿出十一座教堂:先在岩体上凿出深沟把一块石头四面分离,再从上往下掏空成殿堂,门窗、柱子、屋顶全是同一块石头。最有名的圣乔治堂平面是一个正十字,深十二米。',
      'At his capital Roha he had eleven churches cut down into the red volcanic rock: first trenches to free a block on all four sides, then hollowing it out from the top, so that doors, pillars and roof are all one stone. The best known, Bete Giyorgis, is a cross in plan and twelve metres deep.'],
     ['他还把旁边一条小河命名为「约旦河」,山丘叫「各各他」,又造了一座「圣墓」——整座城是按耶路撒冷的地形重排的。',
      'He named the stream beside it the Jordan and a hill Golgotha, and built a Holy Sepulchre — the whole town laid out to the map of Jerusalem.']],
  s:['这些教堂不是遗址:八百年来一直在做礼拜,门口排着朝圣的人,1978 年列入首批世界遗产。1270 年扎格维被推翻,新王朝自称所罗门与示巴女王的后裔,官方史书把扎格维写成篡位者——而拉利贝拉本人被埃塞俄比亚正教会封为圣人,那座城也改叫了他的名字。当地传说说教堂是天使夜里帮着凿的:白天人凿,晚上天使接着凿。',
     'These are not ruins: services have been held in them for eight hundred years, pilgrims still queue at the doors, and they were among the first World Heritage sites in 1978. When the Zagwe were overthrown in 1270 the new dynasty claimed descent from Solomon and Sheba, and the official histories wrote the Zagwe down as usurpers — yet Lalibela himself was made a saint by the Ethiopian church, and the town took his name. Local tradition says angels did the cutting at night: men by day, angels after dark.'] },

'基里亚科斯': { g:'king', y:[747,768], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'努比亚诸王国', n:['基里亚科斯','Kyriakos'],
  t:['埃及的总督把科普特教会的主教关了起来,这位努比亚国王就带兵北上,一直开到福斯塔特城下。',
     'When the governor of Egypt jailed the Coptic patriarch, this Nubian king marched north and camped outside Fustat.'],
  a:[['他是马库里亚的国王。据《亚历山大城主教史》记载,约 748 年埃及的倭马亚总督囚禁了科普特正教的宗主教米海尔一世,他随即率军北上问罪。',
      'He was king of Makuria. The History of the Patriarchs of Alexandria records that when the Umayyad governor of Egypt imprisoned the Coptic patriarch Michael I about 748, he marched north to answer for it.'],
     ['努比亚军队一路推进到埃及首府福斯塔特(今开罗一带)附近,总督放人求和,他才退兵。',
      'The Nubian army came up to Fustat, near today\'s Cairo, and only when the patriarch was released did he turn back.'],
     ['这件事发生在双方的 baqt 之约之下:641 年与 652 年阿拉伯军队两次南下都被努比亚弓箭手挡回去——阿拉伯史料称他们为「瞳孔射手」——打不下来才改签条约。',
      'This happened under the baqt, the pact between them: Arab armies had come south in 641 and 652 and both times were turned back by Nubian archers — the Arab sources call them the pupil-smiters — and the treaty was what came of not being able to conquer them.']],
  s:['在他手里,baqt 那纸约定显出了护身符的一面:约在,王国就在。它断断续续维持了六百年,在伊斯兰向外扩张的历史上是个罕见的例外——一个基督教王国在伊斯兰世界的边上又存续了六百多年。努比亚教堂的壁画今天保存在喀土穆与华沙的博物馆里,那是 1960 年代阿斯旺水坝蓄水前抢救出来的。',
     'In his hands the baqt showed its other face — a charm of protection: while the treaty held, the kingdom held. It held, on and off, for six hundred years — a rare exception in the history of Islamic expansion, a Christian kingdom lasting six more centuries on the edge of the Islamic world. The wall paintings of the Nubian churches are now in museums in Khartoum and Warsaw, rescued before the Aswan dam flooded the valley in the 1960s.'] },

'阿马拉·敦卡斯': { g:'king', y:[1504,1534], yk:'r', ca:1, c:'努比亚诸王国', n:['阿马拉·敦卡斯','Amara Dunqas'],
  t:['基督教的努比亚落幕之后,他在青尼罗河边建起一个苏丹国,统治了三百年。',
     'After Christian Nubia ended, he founded a sultanate on the Blue Nile that lasted three hundred years.'],
  a:[['他是丰吉人的首领,1504 年在森纳尔立国,地盘沿青尼罗河展开;这一年通常被当作丰吉苏丹国的起点。',
      'He was a chief of the Funj and in 1504 founded a state at Sennar on the Blue Nile; that year is usually taken as the beginning of the Funj sultanate.'],
     ['阿尔瓦——努比亚最后一个基督教王国——在这前后覆灭;一说是他与从北方南下的阿拉伯部族联手打下的,一说是阿拉伯部族先自己攻破的。',
      'Alwa, the last Christian kingdom of Nubia, fell about this time; by one account he and the Arab tribes from the north took it together, by another the Arabs had already done it themselves.'],
     ['有一派学者认为丰吉人最初不信伊斯兰教、后来才改宗;能确定的是 1523 年一位犹太旅行家见到他时,他已经是穆斯林。丰吉王室的信仰转向,是苏丹地区伊斯兰化的关键一步。',
      'One school holds that the Funj were not Muslims at first and converted later; what is certain is that when a Jewish traveller met him in 1523 he was already a Muslim. The turn of the ruling house to Islam was a decisive step in the Islamisation of the Sudan.']],
  s:['丰吉苏丹国存续到 1821 年,被埃及的穆罕默德·阿里征服。森纳尔一度是红海与内非洲之间的商路枢纽,黄金、象牙与奴隶经它北运。今天苏丹的阿拉伯-伊斯兰面貌大体成型于这三百年——而在它之前,尼罗河上游是一千年的基督教努比亚,更早还有库施与麦罗埃的金字塔。',
     'The Funj sultanate lasted until 1821, when Muhammad Ali of Egypt conquered it. Sennar was for a time the hinge of the routes between the Red Sea and inner Africa, with gold, ivory and slaves passing north through it. The Arab and Muslim character of Sudan today largely took shape in those three centuries — and before them the upper Nile had a thousand years of Christian Nubia, and before that the pyramids of Kush and Meroe.'] },

'塔卡伊纳莫': { g:'king', y:[900,950], yk:'a', ca:1, c:'奇穆', n:['塔卡伊纳莫','Taycanamu'],
  t:['传说里他坐着一条木筏从海上来,在这片没有雨的海岸上开国。',
     'In the tradition he came from the sea on a raft, and founded a kingdom on a coast where it does not rain.'],
  a:[['这个名字来自 1604 年一份西班牙人记下的特鲁希略王统传说:一位叫塔卡伊纳莫的人乘轻木筏漂到莫切河谷登陆,建立奇穆的王朝。',
      'The name comes from a dynastic tradition written down by the Spanish at Trujillo in 1604: a man called Taycanamu drifted ashore in the Moche valley on a balsa raft and founded the line of Chimor.'],
     ['这份传说列出十来位国王,考古能对上的只有后半段;前面几位没有任何独立证据,他本人属于建国传说的部分。',
      'The tradition lists ten or eleven kings, of whom only the later ones can be matched to the archaeology; for the earliest there is no independent evidence, and he belongs to the founding story.'],
     ['都城昌昌确实在 9—10 世纪开始建造:十个各带围墙的宫城依次排开,占地约二十平方公里,是美洲最大的土坯城(全世界排第二)。',
      'The capital of Chan Chan was indeed begun in the ninth or tenth century: ten walled palace compounds laid out one after another over some twenty square kilometres, the largest adobe city in the Americas and the second largest in the world.']],
  s:['把「乘筏从海上来」当作开国故事,在秘鲁北岸不止这一处——传说里的另一位英雄纳伊拉普也是这样登陆的。这类故事未必是史实,却透露出这片海岸的人怎么看自己:雨不下、河有限,能来的东西多半从海上来。1470 年前后印加切断昌昌的引水渠,围了几个月才破,城里的国王和匠人被带去库斯科当差——从此金银手艺替新主人干活。昌昌 1986 年列入世界遗产,同年因土坯遇雨溶蚀被列入濒危名单。',
     'A founder arriving by raft is told of more than one kingdom on the north coast of Peru — the hero Naylamp in another tradition comes ashore the same way. Such stories need not be history, but they show how the people of this coast saw themselves: no rain, few rivers, and whatever comes, comes off the sea. About 1470 the Inca cut Chan Chan\'s water channel and took the city after a siege of some months; the king and his craftsmen were taken off to Cuzco — from then on their skill worked for new masters. Chan Chan became a World Heritage site in 1986, and was put on the endangered list the same year — adobe dissolves in rain.'] },

'塞·阿卡特尔·托皮尔岑': { g:'king', y:[920,950], yk:'a', ca:1, c:'托尔特克与谷地诸邦', n:['塞·阿卡特尔·托皮尔岑','Ce Acatl Topiltzin'],
  t:['传说里的图拉之王,后来和羽蛇神合成了一个人——阿兹特克人一直等着他从东边回来。',
     'The legendary king of Tula, later merged with the feathered serpent god — and the Aztecs went on waiting for him to come back from the east.'],
  a:[['阿兹特克人的传说说他是图拉的国王兼祭司,把「羽蛇」(克察尔科阿特尔)这个神名当作自己的称号,教人耕作、织布与历法,禁止活人祭祀。',
      'Aztec tradition makes him king and priest at Tula, taking the god\'s name Quetzalcoatl as his own title, teaching farming, weaving and the calendar, and forbidding human sacrifice.'],
     ['传说又说他被对手用计灌醉、犯了戒,羞愧出走,一路向东到海边,乘蛇筏离去,并说有一天会回来。',
      'The story goes on that his rivals tricked him into drink, he broke his vows, left in shame, went east to the sea and sailed away on a raft of serpents, saying he would return.'],
     ['这些说法都出自西班牙征服之后由传教士记录的口传材料,写下来时已经距他的年代五六百年;史家至今无法判定他是不是一个真实的人。',
      'All of this comes from oral traditions written down by friars after the Spanish conquest, five or six centuries after his supposed time; historians still cannot say whether he was a real person.']],
  s:['「他会从东边回来」这个预言常被说成让阿兹特克人误认科尔特斯为神——但现代学者普遍认为,那种说法主要是征服之后西班牙人与本地精英各自的追述,不能当作 1519 年当时的实况。一个可能真存在过的祭司王,死后被并进了羽蛇神的名字里——人和神从此再也拆不开。',
     'The prophecy of a return from the east is often said to have made the Aztecs mistake Cortés for a god — but modern scholars generally hold that this account was shaped after the conquest, by Spaniards and by indigenous elites alike, and cannot be taken for what people thought in 1519. A priest-king who may once have lived was folded after death into the name of the feathered serpent god — and man and god have never come apart since.'] },

'卡美哈梅哈一世': { g:'king', y:[1758,1819], ca:1, c:'夏威夷王国', n:['卡美哈梅哈一世','Kamehameha I'],
  t:['他把几个互相打了几百年的岛合成一个王国,还立下一条保护路人的法律。',
     'He made one kingdom of islands that had fought each other for centuries, and laid down a law to protect anyone travelling the road.'],
  a:[['他是夏威夷大岛的酋长,靠夏威夷自己的战法加上从欧洲船上得来的火枪与火炮、还有两名不列颠顾问,1795 年瓦胡岛努乌阿努一役打通了最后一关,大部分岛屿归他统辖;考艾岛 1810 年以协议归附。',
      'A chief of the island of Hawaii, he used Hawaiian tactics together with muskets and cannon got from European ships, and two British advisers; the battle of Nuʻuanu on Oahu in 1795 opened the last of it, and most of the islands came under him; Kauai came in by agreement in 1810.'],
     ['他颁布「碎桨法」(Māmalahoe Kānāwai):老人、妇女、儿童可以在路边安睡而不受伤害。传说这条法来自他自己——早年他追赶渔民时脚卡在礁石缝里,被对方用船桨打在头上,桨断了,他活了下来;多年后他没有报复,反而立了这条法。',
      'He proclaimed the Law of the Splintered Paddle: the old, women and children may lie down to sleep by the roadside unharmed. The story is his own — as a young man chasing fishermen he caught his foot in the reef and was struck on the head with a paddle, which broke; years later, instead of taking revenge, he made this law.'],
     ['他统一后没有闭关:与来往的商船做檀香木生意,派人学航海,王国也保留了自己的祭祀制度,他死后半年,夏威夷人自己把它废掉了。',
      'After unification he did not close the islands: he traded sandalwood with the ships that called, had men taught navigation, and kept the old system of temple worship, which the Hawaiians themselves abolished six months after his death.']],
  s:['「碎桨法」1978 年写进了夏威夷州宪法,是第九条第十款。他死后不到一百年,王国就没了——先被种植园主架空,再被推翻、并入美国。而对岛上的人来说,更大的打击是疾病:库克船长来时的几十万人,一个多世纪后只数得出约四万。每年 6 月 11 日是夏威夷的卡美哈梅哈日,他的铜像上会挂满花环。',
     'The Law of the Splintered Paddle was written into the constitution of the state of Hawaii in 1978, as article IX, section 10. Less than a century after his death the kingdom was gone — hollowed out by the planters, then overthrown and annexed. But the heaviest blow to the islanders was disease: the hundreds of thousands alive when Captain Cook arrived had, a century and more later, become some forty thousand. Every 11 June is Kamehameha Day, and his statues are hung with garlands.'] },

'莉莉乌欧卡拉尼': { g:'king', y:[1838,1917], r:[1891,1893], c:'夏威夷王国', n:['莉莉乌欧卡拉尼','Liliʻuokalani'],
  t:['夏威夷最后一位君主,被推翻后写下的那首歌,今天全世界都在唱。',
     'The last monarch of Hawaii — and the song she wrote is sung all over the world.'],
  a:[['她 1891 年继兄长即位。1887 年的「刺刀宪法」已在武力下削去了王权,她着手起草新宪法要收回来;1893 年,种植园主们发难,军舰上的陆战队「维持秩序」地上了岸,王座到此为止。',
      'She succeeded her brother in 1891. The Bayonet Constitution of 1887 had already stripped the crown of power at gunpoint; when she moved to draft a new one to take it back, the planters struck in 1893 — marines came ashore to "keep order", and that was the end of the throne.'],
     ['为避免流血,她当时把王位「让与美国政府」而非那个委员会,并声明是在抗议之下。1895 年支持者起事失败,她被控知情,在自己的王宫里被软禁八个月。',
      'To avoid bloodshed she yielded not to the committee but to the government of the United States, and said plainly that she did so under protest. After an attempted counter-revolt in 1895 she was charged with knowing of it and held for eight months under house arrest in her own palace.'],
     ['她是作曲家,一生写了一百多首歌;《Aloha ʻOe》(《告别夏威夷》)是她最有名的作品,软禁期间她还写下《Queen\'s Prayer》。',
      'She was a composer and wrote over a hundred songs; Aloha ʻOe is the best known, and during her confinement she wrote the Queen\'s Prayer.']],
  s:['美国总统克利夫兰调查后认定推翻不合法、要求复位,国会没有照办,1898 年正式兼并夏威夷。1993 年美国国会通过决议,为一百年前那次推翻正式道歉。她的王宫伊奥拉尼宫今天是博物馆,那间软禁她的房间保留原样——墙上挂着她在里面用碎布拼的被子。',
     'President Cleveland investigated, found the overthrow unlawful and called for her restoration; Congress did not comply, and annexed Hawaii in 1898. In 1993 Congress passed a resolution formally apologising for the overthrow a century before. Iolani Palace is now a museum, and the room where she was held is kept as it was — on the wall hangs the quilt she pieced together there.'] },

'乔治·图普一世': { g:'king', y:[1797,1893], r:[1845,1893], c:'汤加王国', n:['乔治·图普一世','George Tupou I'],
  t:['他在位四十七年,给汤加立了一部宪法,把平民从对酋长的人身依附里解出来。',
     'Forty-seven years on the throne: he gave Tonga a constitution and freed the commoners from bondage to their chiefs.'],
  a:[['他本名陶法阿豪,是哈派群岛的酋长,从 1820 年代起一片一片地结束了各岛几十年的内战;1831 年受洗,取教名西奥西(即乔治),1845 年接过最高头衔。',
      'Born Tāufaʻāhau, a chief of Haʻapai, from the 1820s he ended decades of civil war island by island; he was baptised in 1831, taking the name Siaosi — George — and assumed the paramount title in 1845.'],
     ['1862 年的法典解除了平民对酋长的人身依附,规定每个成年男子有权租得一块土地;1875 年颁布宪法,设立议会,这部宪法至今仍是汤加的根本法。',
      'His code of 1862 released commoners from personal obligation to the chiefs and gave every adult man the right to a plot of land; the constitution of 1875 set up a parliament, and it is still Tonga\'s basic law.'],
     ['他一生的另一半工作是把汤加留在自己手里:与欧洲各国签友好条约、争取承认。他身后王国虽一度把对外事务托付给英国,但王冠和家门里的事始终没有易手。',
      'The other half of his work was keeping Tonga his own: treaties of friendship with the European powers, and recognition. After him the kingdom did for a time hand its foreign affairs to Britain, but the crown and the running of the house never changed hands.']],
  s:['汤加始终自己管自己,也是太平洋上唯一保住了君主制的国家——「太平洋岛国里唯一没被殖民」这个说法,依据就在这里;今天在位的还是同一家。他把「立宪」当成保住独立的办法——一个有宪法、有议会、有条约的国家,列强不好下手。这套算盘在 19 世纪的太平洋上很少有人打成。',
     'Tonga always governed itself and is the one Pacific nation to have kept its monarchy — which is what lies behind the saying that it was never colonised; the family on the throne today is still his. He treated constitution-making as a way of keeping his independence: a state with a constitution, a parliament and treaties is harder to take. Few in the nineteenth-century Pacific managed to make that reasoning work.'] },

'萨洛特·图普三世': { g:'king', y:[1900,1965], r:[1918,1965], c:'汤加王国', n:['萨洛特·图普三世','Sālote Tupou III'],
  t:['1953 年伦敦大雨,别的君主都关上车篷,只有这位汤加女王一路敞着——从此全英国都认识她。',
     'London, 1953: in the rain every other monarch closed the carriage, and the queen of Tonga rode the whole way open — and all Britain knew who she was.'],
  a:[['她十八岁即位,在位四十七年多,是汤加在位最久的君主。她着力于公共卫生与教育:她在位期间汤加的结核大幅下降,免费义务教育推开,识字率达到太平洋岛国前列。',
      'She came to the throne at eighteen and reigned forty-seven years and more, the longest in Tongan history. She worked at public health and schooling: tuberculosis fell sharply in her reign, free schooling was extended, and literacy reached among the highest in the Pacific.'],
     ['她把分裂了几十年的汤加两个教会重新合一,又推动整理与保存汤加的口传诗歌和舞蹈——她自己就写了上百首歌词。',
      'She reunited the two Tongan churches that had been split for decades, and pushed for the collecting and keeping of Tongan poetry and dance — she wrote a hundred-odd song texts herself.'],
     ['1953 年她到伦敦参加伊丽莎白二世加冕,途中下雨,按汤加的礼节,在尊长面前不可遮挡,她始终没有合上敞篷马车——英国人记了几十年。',
      'At Elizabeth II\'s coronation in 1953 it rained, and by Tongan courtesy one does not cover oneself before someone to be honoured, so she kept the carriage open the whole way — and the British remembered it for decades.']],
  s:['同一年伊丽莎白二世回访汤加,是英国君主第一次踏上这个王国。她 1965 年去世时,汤加举国服丧;她写的歌至今在葬礼与庆典上唱。汤加本土约十万人,住在海外(新西兰、澳大利亚、美国)的差不多同样多,汇款是重要收入——这个跨太平洋的汤加人网络,在她那一代就已经开始。',
     'Elizabeth II visited Tonga the same year, the first time a British monarch had set foot in the kingdom. When she died in 1965 the whole kingdom went into mourning, and her songs are still sung at funerals and feasts. Tonga has about a hundred thousand people at home and roughly as many abroad — in New Zealand, Australia and the United States — and remittances matter greatly; that trans-Pacific Tongan network began in her generation.'] },

};
